{
  post: {
    title: 'Inspirations',
    content: '<h2>Similar libraries that do secure UI</h2>\n' +
      '<p><a href="https://github.com/Shopify/remote-ui">Remote UI by Shopify</a></p>\n' +
      '<h2>State Management</h2>\n' +
      '<p>HyperApp - <a href="https://blog.asayer.io/hyperapp-is-it-the-lightweight-react-killer">Blog post</a>\n' +
      '<a href="https://medium.com/@veeralpatel/things-ive-learned-about-state-management-for-react-apps-174b8bde87fb">6 things I wish I know ... react state management</a></p>\n' +
      '<h2>CSS only components</h2>\n' +
      '<p>charts using CSS only - <a href="https://chartscss.org/">chartcss</a></p>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
