{
  post: {
    title: 'Hydrate Conditional Creation Fallback',
    content: '<h1>Design Log 100 — Hydrate Conditional Creation Fallback</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>DL93 defined three levels of hydration complexity:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Level 1</strong>: Static HTML with dynamic text/attribute points</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Level 2</strong>: Conditionals that are true at SSR — adopt existing DOM, toggle on/off</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Level 3</strong>: Conditionals that are false at SSR — element doesn&#39;t exist in DOM, needs creation code</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>DL93/94 implemented Levels 1 and 2. Level 3 was left as future work. DL99 fixed coordinate alignment bugs but exposed Level 3 as a real problem on the whisky-store products page.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>When a conditional is false at SSR time, the server doesn&#39;t render the element. The hydrate target generates:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token function">hydrateConditional</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>productSearch<span class="token operator">?</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>isSearching<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token function">adoptElement</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'3'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><code>adoptElement(&quot;3&quot;, ...)</code> fails (coordinate &quot;3&quot; doesn&#39;t exist in DOM), returns noop. <code>hydrateConditional</code> sees <code>!adopted.dom</code>, returns noop. The element can <strong>never appear</strong>, even when the condition becomes true at interactive time.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Example: the loading overlay <code>&lt;div class=&quot;loading-overlay&quot; if=&quot;productSearch.isSearching&quot;&gt;</code> never shows because <code>isSearching</code> is false on initial page load.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This affects ALL conditionals that are false at SSR — not just this one.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Approach: creation fallback in <code>hydrateConditional</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add an optional <code>createFallback</code> parameter to <code>hydrateConditional</code>. When adoption fails and a create callback exists, set up lazy creation similar to the standard <code>conditional()</code> / <code>mkUpdateCondition</code> pattern.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> hydrateConditional<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  condition<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token operator">:</span> ViewState<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> boolean<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  adoptExisting<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> BaseJayElement<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  createFallback<span class="token operator">?:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> BaseJayElement<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// NEW</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> BaseJayElement<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>How it works</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>hydrateConditional</code> already handles the conditional logic — it IS the adoption of the conditional itself. The adopt callback tries to find and adopt the element. When adoption fails (false at SSR), the create callback provides the element creation code as a fallback.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token function">hydrateConditional</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>productSearch<span class="token operator">?</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>isSearching<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token function">adoptElement</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'3'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// adopt (existing)</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token function">e</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'div'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token keyword">class</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'loading-overlay'</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token comment">// create (fallback)</span>\n' +
      `      <span class="token function">e</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'div'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token keyword">class</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'loading-spinner'</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>True at SSR</strong>: adopt callback finds the element → existing toggle behavior, create callback ignored</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>False at SSR</strong>: adopt callback returns noop → create callback stored, called lazily when condition first becomes true</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The create callback uses the standard element target (<code>e()</code>, <code>dt()</code>, <code>da()</code> etc.), same pattern as <code>hydrateForEach</code>&#39;s create callback.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Why not split into <code>hydrateConditionalTrue</code> / <code>hydrateConditionalFalse</code>?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Considered splitting into two methods to reduce client script size. Doesn&#39;t help because the compiler can&#39;t determine at compile time whether a condition is true or false at SSR — conditions like <code>if=&quot;productSearch.isSearching&quot;</code> depend on fast/interactive-phase data resolved at request time. The hydrate compiler must generate code for both outcomes; the runtime decides based on whether adoption succeeds.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The one exception is <strong>slow-phase conditions</strong>: the value IS known at compile time (baked into pre-rendered jay-html). If true → only adoption needed. If false → no code needed (slow data doesn&#39;t change). These are already handled implicitly.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>DOM insertion position</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When the condition was false at SSR and toggles true, the created element needs a position in the DOM. Solution: <code>hydrateConditional</code> creates a comment anchor node as a position marker. The parent <code>adoptElement</code> inserts anchors for children that returned <code>dom: undefined</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Challenge: <code>adoptElement</code> evaluates children before resolving its own element (JS argument evaluation order). Workaround: <code>adoptElement</code> post-processes children after resolving — scans for comment-anchor DOMs and appends them to the parent in order.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Runtime — <code>hydrateConditional</code> with createFallback</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add optional third parameter <code>createFallback</code> to <code>hydrateConditional</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>When <code>!adopted.dom</code> and <code>createFallback</code> exists:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Create a comment anchor node</li>\n' +
      '<li>Return a <code>BaseJayElement</code> with <code>dom: anchor</code> and an <code>update</code> function that:<ul>\n' +
      '<li>On first true condition → call <code>createFallback()</code>, insert created element before anchor</li>\n' +
      '<li>On subsequent toggles → remove/re-insert before anchor (same as true-at-SSR path)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Runtime — <code>adoptElement</code> anchor insertion</h3>\n' +
      '<p>After <code>adoptElement</code>'... 6169 more characters,
