{
  post: {
    title: 'Validate Tag Coverage Report',
    content: '<h1>Validate Tag Coverage Report</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> February 27, 2026\n' +
      '<strong>Related:</strong> Design Log #73 (jay-stack validate command), #38 (Contract File), #85 (agent kit)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>jay-stack validate</code> command validates <code>.jay-html</code> and <code>.jay-contract</code> files for parse and compile errors. AI agents run this command after generating pages to verify correctness. However, validation currently only checks for errors — it doesn&#39;t tell the agent whether it used the contract&#39;s data effectively.</p>\n' +
      '<p>An agent generating a product page might successfully compile a page that only uses 3 of 12 available contract tags, missing important data like price, images, or stock status. The agent has no feedback that it left data on the table.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>After generating a jay-html page, an agent needs a sanity check:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Which contract tags did I use?</li>\n' +
      '<li>Which tags did I miss?</li>\n' +
      '<li>Are any <strong>required</strong> tags missing?</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>This feedback lets the agent decide whether to iterate on the page or move on.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: Should this be a separate command or part of <code>validate</code>?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Part of <code>validate</code> — always runs. The agent gets errors + coverage in one command.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: How do we detect which tags are &quot;used&quot; in a jay-html file?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> HTML tree traversal. Walk the parsed DOM tree returned by <code>parseJayFile()</code> (a <code>node-html-parser</code> HTMLElement), tracking the current scope (key + forEach nesting). Extract tag references from:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>{key.tagName}</code> text expressions</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>if=&quot;key.tagName&quot;</code> condition attributes</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>ref=&quot;key.tagName&quot;</code> ref attributes</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>forEach=&quot;key.tagName&quot;</code> forEach attributes</li>\n' +
      '<li>Attribute values with <code>{expression}</code> bindings</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Source text search was considered but rejected — it can&#39;t distinguish same-named child tags under different forEach scopes (e.g., <code>name</code> under <code>options</code> vs <code>name</code> under <code>variants</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: How should we handle sub-contract tags inside <code>forEach</code> scopes?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Track forEach scopes. When entering <code>forEach=&quot;key.items&quot;</code>, record that we&#39;re now inside <code>items</code> scope. Child references like <code>name</code> map to contract path <code>items.name</code>. The contract tells us which tags are repeated sub-contracts, so we know when a forEach introduces a new scope.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: What should the output look like?</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Tag Coverage:\n' +
      '  src/pages/products/[slug]/page.jay-html\n' +
      '    productPage (product-page): 8/12 tags used\n' +
      '      Unused: ribbons, breadcrumbs, sku, additionalInfo\n' +
      '    cartIndicator (cart-indicator): 3/3 tags used</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>When there are required unused tags:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">      ⚠ Required unused: productName, price</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Q5: Should we report on <code>jay:instance</code> tags (no key) or only key-based headless components?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Both. Key-based use <code>key.tagPath</code> references. Instance tags (<code>&lt;jay:contract-name&gt;</code>) use bare tag names inside their inline template. We can detect these by walking <code>&lt;jay:*&gt;</code> elements and checking child content against the contract.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q6: What counts as a &quot;required&quot; tag?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Only explicit <code>required: true</code> on contract tags.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Tree traversal approach</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Walk the parsed <code>body: HTMLElement</code> tree. Maintain a scope stack that tracks the current variable context:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Start with root scope — tag references are prefixed with headless keys (e.g., <code>productPage.name</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>When entering <code>forEach=&quot;key.items&quot;</code>, push a new scope where bare names resolve to <code>items.childTag</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>When entering <code>&lt;jay:contract-name&gt;</code>, push a scope for that contract&#39;s tags (bare names)</li>\n' +
      '<li>When entering <code>&lt;with-data accessor=&quot;path&quot;&gt;</code>, push scope for nested sub-contract</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>At each element, extract tag references from:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>forEach</code> attribute value — marks the repeated tag as used</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>if</code> attribute value — parse the condition expression for tag references</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>ref</code> attribute value — marks the interactive tag as used</li>\n' +
      '<li>Text content <code>{expr}</code> — parse for tag references</li>\n' +
      '<li>Any attribute value containing <code>{expr}</code> — parse for tag references</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Collecting used tags</h3>\n' +
      '<p>For each headless import (with or without key), maintain a <code>Set&lt;string&gt;</code> of used tag paths. After traversal, compare against the flattened contract tag list.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Flattening contract tags</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Recursively flatten <code>Contract.tags</code> into a list of paths:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>{ tag: &quot;name&quot;, type: data }</code> → path <code>&quot;name&quot;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>{ tag: &quot;options&quot;, type: sub-contract, tags: [{ tag: &quot;_id&quot; }, { tag: &quot;name&quot; }] }</code> → paths <code>&quot;options&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;options._id&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;options.name&quot;</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Output</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add <code>coverage: FileCoverage[]</code> to <code>ValidationResult</code>. Print after errors/warnings.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Tag coverage analysis function</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Add <code>analyzeTagCoverage(jayHtml: JayHtmlSourceFile)</code> function in <code>validate.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Implement contract tag flattening: <code>flattenContractTags(tags: ContractTag[], prefix?: string): TagInfo[]</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Implement DOM tree walker that collects used tag paths per headless import</li>\n' +
      '<li>Return <code>FileCoverage</code> with used/unused/required-unused per contract</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Integration with validate</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Add <code>FileCoverage</code> and related types to <code>ValidationResult</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Call <code>analyzeTagCoverage()</code> for each successfully parsed jay-html file</li>\n' +
      '<li>Update <code>printJayValidationResult()</code> to print coverage report</li>\n' +
      '<li>Include coverage in <code>--json</code> output</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification Criteria</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Running <code>jay-stack validate</code> on the whisky-store shows tag coverage per page per contract</li>\n' +
      '<li>Unused tags are listed by name</li>\n' +
      '<li>Required unused tags are highlighted with ⚠</li>\n' +
      '<li>Existing validation behavior (errors/warnings) is unchanged</li>\n' +
      '<li>Output is clear enough for an AI agent to act on</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Results</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>What was implemented</h3>\n' +
      '<p>All changes in <code>packages/jay-stack/stack-cli/lib/validate.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Types</strong>: <code>ContractCoverage</code>, <code>FileCoverage</code> (exported), <code>TagInfo</code>, <code>TagScope</code> (internal). Added <code>coverage: FileCoverage[]</code> to <code>ValidationResult</code>.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>flattenContractTags(tags, prefix?)</code></strong>: Recursively flattens contract tags into <code>{path, required}</code> entries. Sub-contract children get dotted paths (e.g., <code>priceData.formatted.price</code>).</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>extractExpressions(text)</code></strong>: Extracts <code>{expr}</code> patterns from text/attribute values.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>extractTagPath(expr)</code></strong>: Parses expressions and conditions (<code>!tag</code>, <code>tag === value</code>) into dotted tag paths.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>collectUsedTags(jayHtml)</code></strong>: Walks DOM tree with scope tracking. Handles key-based (<code>key.tagPath</code>), instance-based (<code>&lt;jay:contract-name&gt;</code>), forEach, and with-data scoping. Returns <code>Map&lt;importIndex, Set&lt;tagPath&gt;&gt;</code>.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>analyzeTagCoverage(jayHtml, file)</code></strong>: Orchestrates flatten → collect → compare. Marks parent sub-contract paths as implicitly used when children are used.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Integration</strong>: Called after successful parse, before generate. Coverage printed after errors/warnings. Included in <code>--json</code> output automatically.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Deviations from design</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Used import index (<code>Map&lt;number, Set&lt;string&gt;&gt;</code>) instead of direct object references for tracking used tags per headless import — avoids Map identity issues.</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>if</code> and <code>ref</code> attributes on elements resolve in the parent scope (before forEach), while text content and child elements resolve in the child scope (after forEach). This matches the semantic meaning: <code>if</code> conditions and <code>ref</code> bindings on an element apply to the element itself in its parent context.</li>\n' +
      '<li>Attributes on <code>&lt;jay:*&gt;</code> elements (props like <code>productId=&quot;{_id}&quot;</code>) resolve in the parent scope, not the instance scope — correct since prop values come from the outer context.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Test results</h3>\n' +
      '<p>All existing tests pass: 61/61 (6 test files). Type checking passes.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Validate Tag Coverage Report","number":101}'
  }
}
