{
  post: {
    title: 'Headless Instance SSR And Hydration Compilation',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #102 — Headless Instance SSR and Hydration Compilation</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The compiler has three code generation targets for jay-html files:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Element target</strong> (<code>generated-element.ts</code>) — client-side DOM creation</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Server-element target</strong> (<code>generated-server-element.ts</code>) — SSR streaming HTML</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Hydrate target</strong> (<code>generated-element-hydrate.ts</code>) — client-side DOM adoption after SSR</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Headless component instances (<code>&lt;jay:contract-name&gt;</code>) are fully supported in the element target (DL#84, DL#90) but <strong>not implemented</strong> in the server-element or hydrate targets. This means pages with headless instances cannot be server-rendered or hydrated.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The runtime infrastructure is complete — <code>makeHeadlessInstanceComponent</code>, <code>hydrateCompositeJayComponent</code>, <code>__headlessInstances</code> ViewState, and the coordinate system all work. The gap is strictly in the compiler&#39;s code generation.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Current Behavior: Try-Catch Fallback to Client Rendering</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The dev-server (<code>sendResponse()</code>, line ~810-854) wraps the SSR attempt in a try-catch. When the server-element compiler generates broken code for <code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code> tags (treating them as literal HTML), the error is caught and the dev-server falls back to <code>generateClientScript()</code> — pure client-side rendering with no SSR.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This means pages with headless instances (like <code>fake-shop/src/pages/page.jay-html</code> which uses <code>product-widget</code> and <code>stock-status</code> instances) <strong>always</strong> fall back to client-only rendering. The runtime infrastructure works (instance discovery, slow/fast phases, <code>__headlessInstances</code> ViewState), but the compiled <code>renderToStream()</code> function can&#39;t handle the <code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code> tags.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The fallback is silent except for a warning: <code>&quot;[SSR] Failed, falling back to client rendering: {error}&quot;</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Five scenarios need support in both server-element and hydrate targets:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Page-level headless component</strong> — old-style <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;&gt;</code> with <code>key</code> (SSR works, hydration missing)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Nested headless instance</strong> — <code>&lt;jay:product-card productId=&quot;prod-hero&quot;&gt;</code> with inline template</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Conditional headless instance</strong> — <code>&lt;jay:product-card if=&quot;showPromo&quot;&gt;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>forEach headless instance</strong> — <code>&lt;jay:product-card&gt;</code> inside <code>forEach</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>slowForEach headless instance</strong> — <code>&lt;jay:product-card&gt;</code> inside <code>slowForEach</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Compiler Gaps</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Server-element target:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>ServerContext</code> has no <code>headlessContractNames</code>, <code>headlessImports</code>, or <code>headlessInstanceDefs</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>renderServerElement()</code> has no check for <code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code> component tags</li>\n' +
      '<li>A headless instance tag gets treated as literal HTML (<code>&lt;jay:product-card&gt;</code>) — broken</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Hydrate target:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>HydrateContext</code> has <code>headlessContractNames</code> but <code>renderHydrateElement()</code> doesn&#39;t distinguish <code>headless-instance</code> from <code>headful</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Emits <code>childComp(product-card, ...)</code> where <code>product-card</code> is undefined — broken</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Key Insight: Server-Element vs Element/Hydrate Divergence</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The server-element target is fundamentally different from element and hydrate targets:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Element/hydrate generate <strong>component definitions</strong> (<code>makeHeadlessInstanceComponent</code>) that are instantiated at runtime via <code>childComp()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Server-element generates <strong>streaming HTML</strong> — there are no components, no <code>childComp()</code>, no <code>makeHeadlessInstanceComponent</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>For server-element, the headless instance&#39;s inline template should be <strong>inlined directly</strong> into the <code>renderToStream</code> function. The only change needed is switching the ViewState context from the page&#39;s <code>vs</code> to the instance&#39;s ViewState within <code>vs.__headlessInstances[coordinate]</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>For the hydrate target, the approach mirrors the element target — generate inline template render functions using hydrate APIs (<code>adoptElement</code>, <code>adoptText</code>, etc.) plus <code>makeHeadlessInstanceComponent</code> definitions and <code>childComp()</code> calls.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Server-Element Target Design</h3>\n' +
      '<h4>ViewState Access Pattern</h4>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>renderToStream(vs, ctx)</code> function receives the full merged ViewState. The headless instance&#39;s data is at <code>vs.__headlessInstances[coordinateKey]</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>For a headless instance, the compiler needs to:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Compute the coordinate key (same logic as element target)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Create a local variable for the instance&#39;s ViewState</li>\n' +
      '<li>Render the inline template children using that local variable</li>\n' +
      '<li>Assign coordinates to dynamic elements within the inline template</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h4>Coordinate Keys</h4>\n' +
      '<p>Same as element target:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Static instance</strong>: <code>&#39;product-card:0&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;product-card:hero&#39;</code> (if ref is provided)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Inside slowForEach</strong>: <code>&#39;p1/product-card:0&#39;</code> (jayTrackBy prefix)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Inside forEach</strong>: runtime expression using trackBy value</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Example: Simple Instance</h4>\n' +
      '<p>Input:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;jay</span>:product-card <span class="token attribute">productId</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;prod-hero&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;article</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;hero-card&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;h2</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{name}<span class="token tag">&lt;/h2</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;span</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;price&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{price}<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;addToCart&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>Add to Cart<span class="token tag">&lt;/button</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/article</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/jay</span>:product-card<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Server-element output (within <code>renderToStream</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Headless instance: product-card (coordinate: product-card:0)</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">const</span> vs_pc0 <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs as any<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>__headlessInstances<span class="token operator">?</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'product-card:0'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> as\n` +
      '  <span class="token operator">|</span> ProductCardViewState\n' +
      '  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token keyword">undefined</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs_pc0<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'&lt;article'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
