[Build] 20/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=106-hydrate-dynamic-element-with-kindergarten)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Dev Server Consistency And Phase Optionality',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #107 — Dev Server Consistency and Phase Optionality</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>During integration testing of DL#106 (hydration with Kindergarten), multiple inconsistencies were discovered in how the dev server handles different component configurations. These cause hard-to-debug failures when component phase combinations differ from the tested paths.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problems</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Slow render cache on/off produces different behavior</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The dev server has a <code>dontCacheSlowly</code> option. When the slow render cache is enabled, a full pre-render pipeline runs: <code>slowRenderTransform</code> → <code>discoverHeadlessInstances</code> → <code>resolveHeadlessInstances</code> → <code>assignCoordinates</code> → <code>renderFastChangingDataForInstances/ForEachInstances</code>. When disabled, much of this pipeline is skipped, and headless instances inside forEach are never discovered or rendered server-side.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Expected:</strong> The dev server should produce the same output regardless of the cache setting. The cache should only affect performance (avoid re-running slow render on every request), not correctness.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>2. Component phases are optional but the pipeline assumes specific combinations</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A full-stack component can have any combination of phases:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Slow only: <code>withSlowlyRender()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Fast only: <code>withFastRender()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Slow + fast: <code>withSlowlyRender().withFastRender()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Slow + fast + interactive: all three</li>\n' +
      '<li>Fast + interactive: <code>withFastRender().withInteractive()</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Current issues:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A fast-only component (no slow phase) inside a forEach is never discovered because discovery runs on the slow-rendered HTML and only finds instances whose slow bindings were resolved.</li>\n' +
      '<li>If no fast phase, the carry forward for the interactive phase should be empty (<code>{}</code>), but some code paths don&#39;t handle this.</li>\n' +
      '<li>If no slow phase, <code>fastRender</code> receives <code>(props, ...services)</code> instead of <code>(props, carryForward, ...services)</code> — this is correct but fragile and inconsistent with the slow+fast case.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>3. Client script should work with or without fast/slow parts</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A component with an interactive phase should work on the client regardless of whether it has slow or fast server phases. Currently:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Without <code>withInteractive()</code>, no client code is needed — this works.</li>\n' +
      '<li>With <code>withInteractive()</code> but without <code>withFastRender()</code>, the composite component&#39;s <code>hasFastRendering</code> is false, so it doesn&#39;t pass <code>fastViewState</code> signals to parts. The interactive constructor then receives wrong parameters.</li>\n' +
      '<li>The <code>HEADLESS_INSTANCES</code> context is only provided when <code>__headlessInstances</code> data exists in the viewState. If the server didn&#39;t produce it (e.g., no slow cache), the context is missing and <code>useContext</code> throws.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>4. No option to disable SSR</h3>\n' +
      '<p>For development, it would be useful to disable SSR entirely and only serve client scripts without hydration. The page would render entirely on the client via the element target (not the hydrate target). This simplifies debugging when SSR/hydration issues are blocking development.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Proposed:</strong> A global dev server setting <code>ssr: false</code> that:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Serves an empty <code>&lt;div id=&quot;target&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code> instead of SSR HTML</li>\n' +
      '<li>Uses the element target (not hydrate target) for the client script</li>\n' +
      '<li>Skips all server rendering phases</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>5. Build folder not cleared on dev server start</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>build/</code> directory (containing pre-rendered HTML, server-element files, coordinate debug output) persists between dev server restarts. Stale artifacts from previous runs can cause hydration mismatches when code changes.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Proposed:</strong> Clear the <code>build/</code> directory on dev server startup.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>6. <code>loadParams</code> called on every request</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>loadParams</code> function (which resolves route parameters) is called on every request and every page. The result should be cached for the lifecycle of the dev server, since route params don&#39;t change during a session.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Proposed:</strong> Cache <code>loadParams</code> result in the dev server instance. Invalidate only on file changes that affect route definitions.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Build folder cleanup</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Clear <code>build/</code> directory on <code>mkDevServer()</code> startup</li>\n' +
      '<li>Low risk, immediate value</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: loadParams caching</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Cache in the dev server instance</li>\n' +
      '<li>Invalidate on route file changes</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 3: SSR disable option</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Add <code>ssr: boolean</code> to dev server options (default <code>true</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>When <code>false</code>: empty target div, element target script, skip server rendering</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 4: Phase optionality consistency</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Ensure <code>HEADLESS_INSTANCES</code> context is always provided (even if empty)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Handle missing fast/slow phases gracefully in all code paths</li>\n' +
      '<li>Test matrix: all phase combinations × static/forEach/slowForEach instances</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 5: Extract coordinate pre-processing from compiler targets</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Currently <code>assignCoordinates</code> runs inside <code>generateServerElementFile</code> and <code>renderHydrate</code> independently, and <code>discoverHeadlessInstances</code> auto-generates refs independently too. This causes synchronization issues (DL#106: counter mismatch, <code>buildCoordinatePrefix</code> vs <code>assignCoordinates</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Refactoring:</strong> Extract into a single pre-processing stage in the dev server:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Always runs</strong> — regardless of slow render cache setting</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Single pass:</strong> auto-generate refs for all <code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code> elements, then <code>assignCoordinates</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Output:</strong> jay-html with <code>ref</code> attributes and <code>jay-coordinate-base</code> attributes</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Cached:</strong> saved to <code>build/pre-processed/page.jay-html</code> (distinct from slow render cache at <code>build/pre-rendered/page.jay-html</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Both compiler targets read it</strong> — server-element and hydrate compile from the pre-processed file, never running <code>assignCoordinates</code> themselves</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>This subsumes phases 4 and 5:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Phase 4 (phase optionality):</strong> pre-processing runs for all pages, so headless instances are always discovered even without slow cache</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Phase 5 (slow cache parity):</strong> one pipeline, one output — both cached and uncached paths are identical</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The pipeline becomes:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">jay-html → [pre-process: refs + coordinates] → pre-processed.jay-html\n' +
      '                                                    ↓\n' +
      '                                              [slow render (if enabled)] → pre-rendered.jay-html\n' +
      '                                                    ↓\n' +
      '                                              [discover headless instances]\n' +
      '                                              [resolve slow bindings]\n' +
      '                                              [fast render for instances]\n' +
      '                                                    ↓\n' +
      '                                              server-element compiler ← reads pre-rendered or pre-processed\n' +
      '                                              hydrate compiler        ← reads pre-rendered or pre-processed</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification Criteria</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>All 6a–6e hydration tests pass with both <code>useSlowRenderCache: true</code> and <code>false</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Fake-shop example works correctly (mood tracker, static widgets, forEach widgets)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>yarn test</code> passes for all 68 packages</li>\n' +
      '<li>Dev server starts with clean build directory</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>loadParams</code> called once per dev server lifecycle</li>\n' +
      '<li>Compiler targets never call <code>assignCoordinates</code> — they read pre-assigned coordinates from the input HTML</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Progress</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Completed</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong><code>HEADLESS_INSTANCES</code> context always provided</strong> — Both <code>hydrateCompositeJayComponent</code> and <code>makeCompositeJayComponent</code> now always push the <code>HEADLESS_INSTANCES</code> context to <code>provideContexts</code>, even when <code>__headlessInstances</code> is empty. Previously, <code>useContext(HEADLESS_INSTANCES)</code> would throw when no server data existed (e.g., no slow cache, fast-only page). Now headless instance constructors gracefully fall back to <code>clientDefaults</code> or empty data.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong><code>adoptText</code> DOM reconciliation</strong> — <code>adoptText</code> now initializes <code>content</code> from the DOM text (not the accessor) so the first update detects SSR-to-hydration ViewState mismatches. Fixes interactive-only pages where SSR renders &quot;undefined&quot; but the interactive constructor provides real values.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong><code>assignCoordinates</code> auto-generates refs</strong> — When a <code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code> element has no <code>ref</code> attribute, <code>assignCoordinates</code> auto-generates one using an <code>AR</code> prefix with a global counter per contract (e.g., <code>AR0</code>, <code>AR1</code>). This matches <code>discoverHeadlessInstances</code>&#39;s counter scoping and ensures both systems produce the same refs. Eliminates the counter synchronization '... 18084 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Dev Server Consistency And Phase Optionality","number":107}'
  }
}
[Build] 21/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=107-dev-server-consistency-and-phase-optionality)
{
  post: {
    title: 'No-Contract Phase Defaults For Jay-Stack',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #108 — No-Contract Phase Defaults for Jay Stack</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack components use three-phase rendering: slow (build time), fast (SSR request time), fast+interactive (SSR + client reactive). When a <code>.jay-contract</code> exists, each field has an explicit phase annotation. When no contract exists (inline <code>jay-data</code>), the framework must decide which phase each binding belongs to.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Two conflicting decisions exist:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>DL#51</strong> (type generation): Without a contract, all data is <code>interactive</code> → <code>SlowViewState = {}</code>, <code>FastViewState = {}</code>, <code>InteractiveViewState = PageViewState</code>. Rationale: backward compatibility with client-only Jay.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>DL#107</strong> (<code>noMainContract</code> flag): Without a contract, slow render treats all bindings as slow → resolves them from the slow ViewState. Rationale: practical fix so SSR produces HTML.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>This contradiction causes test 4b to fail: the component puts data in <code>withFastRender</code>, but the slow render resolves bindings from an empty slow ViewState → &quot;undefined&quot;.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Jay Stack requires <code>fast+interactive</code>, not <code>interactive</code> alone</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack always renders SSR. SSR requires data at request time (fast phase). A binding that is only <code>interactive</code> (client-only) has no server-side value — SSR renders &quot;undefined&quot;.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Client-only Jay (no SSR) can have <code>interactive</code>-only bindings because there&#39;s no server render. But Jay Stack pages always go through SSR.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Therefore: in Jay Stack, the minimum phase for data is <code>fast+interactive</code>, never <code>interactive</code> alone.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>2. No-contract pages should not have a slow phase</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Without a contract, there&#39;s no way to distinguish slow vs fast bindings. The <code>noMainContract</code> flag in DL#107 treats everything as slow, but this only works if the slow ViewState actually contains the data. If the component puts data in <code>withFastRender</code> (which the types currently allow), slow render produces &quot;undefined&quot;.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The safest option: without a contract, all data is <code>fast+interactive</code>. No slow phase. If a component without a contract defines <code>withSlowlyRender</code> that returns data, that&#39;s an error — there&#39;s no contract to tell the framework which bindings are slow.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Tests 2b and 3b currently put all data in <code>withSlowlyRender</code>. After this fix, slow render resolves nothing without a contract — don&#39;t those tests need to move data to <code>withFastRender</code>?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: Yes. Tests 2b, 3b, and 4b all need updating. 2b and 3b move data from <code>withSlowlyRender</code> to <code>withFastRender</code>. 4b already uses <code>withFastRender</code> but has a no-op <code>withSlowlyRender</code> that should be removed.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: DL#107 added 3 tests in <code>describe(&#39;No contract&#39;)</code> for the slow-render-transform. Removing <code>noMainContract</code> will break those — what happens to them?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: The three affected tests are 2b, 3b, and 4b in the dev-server hydration tests. We fix them as part of this change.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: Should <code>withSlowlyRender</code> returning data without a contract be a warning or an error?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: Error. Without a contract, there&#39;s no way to know which bindings are slow. Data returned from <code>withSlowlyRender</code> would be silently ignored, which is always a bug.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q4: Does the phase-aware hydration fix (interactivePaths) need changes?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: No. Without a contract, <code>interactivePaths</code> is empty, so the guard <code>size &gt; 0</code> prevents any skipping — all bindings are treated as dynamic. This is correct: all data is <code>fast+interactive</code>, so all bindings need client adoption.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q5: What about <code>slowForEach</code> without a contract? If slow render resolves nothing, the <code>forEach</code> won&#39;t be unrolled.</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: There is no <code>slowForEach</code> without a slow phase. The slow render creates <code>slowForEach</code> items by unrolling forEach elements whose array is slow. Without a contract, no arrays are slow, so no unrolling happens. The forEach stays intact for the server-element target to iterate at SSR time.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q6: Fix 1 changes type defaults for all jay-html files. Does this affect client-only Jay (non-stack)?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: No. Client-only Jay uses the same <code>.d.ts</code> files (e.g., <code>examples/jay/async-counter/src/counter.jay-html.d.ts</code>). Jay&#39;s client-only component is exactly the same as the Jay Stack interactive part — Jay is the client component of Jay Stack. The client-only component just ignores the fast ViewState type. Having <code>FastViewState = PageViewState</code> is harmless for client-only usage.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix 1: Change no-contract type defaults to <code>fast+interactive</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>When generating phase-specific types for a jay-html without a contract:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Current (DL#51 — wrong for Jay Stack)</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> type PageSlowViewState <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> type PageFastViewState <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> type PageInteractiveViewState <span class="token operator">=</span> PageViewState<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// New</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> type PageSlowViewState <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> type PageFastViewState <span class="token operator">=</span> PageViewState<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> type PageInteractiveViewState <span class="token operator">=</span> PageViewState<span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This tells the component author: put all data in <code>withFastRender</code>. The data is available at SSR and reactive on the client.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Files:</strong> <code>jay-html-compiler.ts</code> — <code>generatePhaseSpecificTypes</code> (or the section that generates the default types when no contract exists).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix 2: Remove <code>noMainContract</code> slow render behavior</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Remove the <code>noMainContract</code> flag from <code>slowRenderTransform</code>. Without a contract, <code>isSlowPhase()</code> returns <code>false</code> for all bindings → slow render resolves nothing → bindings pass through to the fast/server-element phase.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This aligns with Fix 1: no-contract pages have no slow data, so slow render is a no-op.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Files:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>slow-render-transform.ts</code> — remove <code>noMainContract</code> from <code>isSlowPhase</code>, <code>resolveTextBindings</code>, <code>transformElement</code>, <code>transformChildren</code>, <code>SlowRenderContext</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>expression-parser.pegjs</code> — remove <code>noMainContract</code> from <code>isSlowPhase</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>expression-compiler.ts</code> — remove <code>noMainContract</code> from <code>SlowRenderContext</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix 3: Error on slow data without contract</h3>\n' +
      '<p>If a Jay Stack component without a contract returns non-empty data from <code>withSlowlyRender</code>, emit an error. Without a contract, the slow render has no way to know which bindings to resolve — data from <code>withSlowlyRender</code> would be silently ignored, which is always a bug.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Where:</strong> In the dev server pipeline, when <code>slowRenderTransform</code> receives data but has no contract.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix 4: Update no-contract test components</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>2b</strong> (<code>page-dynamic-text-no-contract</code>): Move data from <code>withSlowlyRender</code> to <code>withFastRender</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>3b</strong> (<code>page-conditional</code>): Move data from <code>withSlowlyRender</code> to <code>withFastRender</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>4b</strong> (<code>page-foreach</code>): Remove no-op <code>withSlowlyRender</code>, keep <code>withFastRender</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Regenerate <code>expected-ssr.html</code> and <code>expected-hydrate.ts</code> fixtures for all three</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Test 2b passes — dynamic text with no contract renders correctly via fast phase</li>\n' +
      '<li>Test 3b passes — conditionals with no contract render correctly via fast phase</li>\n' +
      '<li>Test 4b passes — forEach with no contract renders correctly via fast phase</li>\n' +
      '<li>Tests with contracts (2a, 3a, 4a) unaffected — contract phases still work</li>\n' +
      '<li>Generated <code>.d.ts</code> for no-contract pages shows <code>FastViewState = PageViewState</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>compiler-jay-html tests all pass (including DL#107 <code>No contract</code> slow-render tests updated)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Error emitted when <code>withSlowlyRender</code> returns data without a contract</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Results</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Completed</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Fix 1</strong> — Changed <code>generatePhaseSpecificTypes</code> in <code>jay-html-compiler.ts</code>: when <code>jayFile.hasInlineData</code> (no contract), '... 2957 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"No-Contract Phase Defaults For Jay-Stack","number":108}'
  }
}
