[Build] 25/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=110-filesystem-based-slow-render-cache)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Nested Headfull Full-Stack Components',
    content: '<h1>Nested Headfull Full-Stack Components</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay-stack supports three-phase rendering: <strong>slow</strong> (build/SSG), <strong>fast</strong> (SSR per-request), <strong>interactive</strong> (client).</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Current component landscape:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Layer</th>\n' +
      '<th>Type</th>\n' +
      '<th>Builder</th>\n' +
      '<th>Slow/Fast</th>\n' +
      '<th>Interactive</th>\n' +
      '<th>Import type</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Page</td>\n' +
      '<td>Headfull</td>\n' +
      '<td>makeJayStackComponent</td>\n' +
      '<td>✓</td>\n' +
      '<td>✓</td>\n' +
      '<td>route (page.ts)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Page</td>\n' +
      '<td>Headless</td>\n' +
      '<td>makeJayStackComponent</td>\n' +
      '<td>✓</td>\n' +
      '<td>✓</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>jay-headless</code> with key</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Nested</td>\n' +
      '<td>Headless</td>\n' +
      '<td>makeJayStackComponent</td>\n' +
      '<td>✓</td>\n' +
      '<td>✓</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>jay-headless</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Nested</td>\n' +
      '<td>Headfull</td>\n' +
      '<td>makeJayComponent</td>\n' +
      '<td>—</td>\n' +
      '<td>✓</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>jay-headfull</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>Without a contract, headfull, headless, and page components default to interactive-only.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Headless nested components have complete full-stack support — including instance-based rendering (<code>&lt;jay:contract-name&gt;</code>), slow/fast phase execution, SSR server-element compilation, hydration, and interactive client composition. This was built through DL#84, DL#102, DL#107, DL#109.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Headfull nested</strong> (imported via <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headfull&quot;&gt;</code>) use <code>makeJayComponent</code> — they are client-only. They have no slow/fast phases and no SSR. They can also import CSS files which need to be included in the page.</p>\n' +
      '<p>On the client, headless and page-level full-stack components are all compiled to headfull components — headfull nested components are the client-side implementation target for all component types.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Prior Attempt (Failed Branch)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>DL#102 from the <code>jay-stack-headfull-components</code> branch attempted to add headfull full-stack support <strong>before</strong> headless instance support was complete. That approach proposed:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Adding a <code>contract</code> attribute to <code>application/jay-headfull</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>A &quot;post-slow merge&quot; step that injects the headfull component&#39;s compiled jay-html into the page after slow render</li>\n' +
      '<li>Treating the merged result like headless from that point on</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>That approach was abandoned. Since then, headless instances gained complete SSR and hydration support (DL#102 on main, DL#106, DL#109). We now need to revisit headfull full-stack design with the mature headless infrastructure in mind.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>We need <strong>nested headfull full-stack components</strong> — components that:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Include their own UI</strong> (headfull = have a jay-html file)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Can render on the server</strong> (slow and/or fast phases)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Continue interactively</strong> on the client</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Can be reused</strong> across multiple pages (shared layout: header, footer, sidebar)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Example use case</strong>: A site header shared across pages. Today you either duplicate the header markup in every page&#39;s jay-html, or accept that the header is client-only and won&#39;t SSR.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Key difference from headless</strong>: Headless components delegate their UI to the parent page&#39;s jay-html (inline template inside <code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code>). Headfull components <strong>bring their own jay-html</strong> — the UI is part of the component, not the page.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q: How does this differ from nested headless?</strong>\n' +
      'A: Headless provides data + behavior; the parent provides the UI template inline. Headfull brings its own jay-html file. A header/footer/sidebar has fixed UI that belongs to the component, not the page.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q: Can a nested headfull full-stack component be in a plugin/package?</strong>\n' +
      'A: Not initially. Plugins provide headless components. Headfull FS components are project-local only, because they bundle UI.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q: Does this affect existing client-only nested headfull?</strong>\n' +
      'A: No. Existing <code>makeJayComponent</code> nested headfull components (no <code>contract</code> attribute) stay as-is.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q: Does a headfull FS component have its own contract?</strong>\n' +
      'A: Yes. Like headless, it needs a <code>.jay-contract</code> for phase annotations. The contract defines what data is slow vs fast vs interactive. The jay-html provides the UI.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q: Can headfull FS components be nested inside forEach?</strong>\n' +
      'A: Yes, following the same patterns as headless instances (DL#84, DL#90).</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q: Can the page pass props to a headfull FS component?</strong>\n' +
      'A: Yes, via attributes on <code>&lt;jay:Name itemId=&quot;1&quot;&gt;</code>, same as headless instances.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Approach: Reuse the Headless Instance Pipeline</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The key insight: <strong>a headfull full-stack component is a headless component whose inline template comes from its own jay-html file instead of the parent page&#39;s markup.</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>Instead of inventing a new rendering pipeline, we compile the headfull component&#39;s jay-html into the same structure as a headless inline template, and then the existing headless instance pipeline (slow render → fast render → SSR server-element → hydration → interactive) handles everything.</p>\n' +
      '<div class="md-mermaid"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1202.1170000000002 264.5" width="1202.1170000000002" height="264.5">\n' +
      '<style>\n' +
      '  svg {\n' +
      '    /* Derived from --bg and --fg (overridable via --line, --accent, etc.) */\n' +
      '    --_text:          var(--fg);\n' +
      '    --_text-sec:      var(--muted, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 60%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_text-muted:    var(--muted, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 40%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_text-faint:    color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 25%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '    --_line:          var(--line, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 50%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_arrow:         var(--accent, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 85%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_node-fill:     var(--surface, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 3%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_node-stroke:   var(--border, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 20%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_group-fill:    var(--bg);\n' +
      '    --_group-hdr:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 5%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '    --_inner-stroke:  color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 12%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '    --_key-badge:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 10%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '  }\n' +
      '</style>\n' +
      '<defs>\n' +
      '  <marker id="arrowhead" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="5" refX="7" refY="2.5" orient="auto">\n' +
      '    <polygon points="0 0, 8 2.5, 0 5" fill="var(--_arrow)" stroke="var(--_arrow)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-linejoin="round" />\n' +
      '  </marker>\n' +
      '  <marker id="arrowhead-start" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="5" refX="1" refY="2.5" orient="auto-start-reverse">\n' +
      '    <polygon points="8 0, 0 2.5, 8 5" fill="var(--_arrow)" stroke="var(--_arrow)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-linejoin="round" />\n' +
      '  </marker>\n' +
      '</defs>\n' +
      '<g class="subgraph" data-id="Headless" data-label="Headless Instance (current)">\n' +
      '  <rect x="660.931" y="40" width="501.18600000000004" height="158.60000000000002" rx="0" ry="0" fill="var(--_group-fill)" stroke="var(--_node-stroke)" stroke-width="1" />\n' +
      '  <rect x="660.931" y="40" width="501.18600000000004" height="28" rx="0" ry="0" fill="var(--_group-hdr)" stroke="var(--_node-stroke)" stroke-width="1" />\n' +
      '  <text x="672.931" y="54" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--_text-sec)" dy="4.199999999999999">Headless Instance (current)</text>\n' +
      '</g>\n' +
      '<g class="subgraph" data-id="Headfull" data-label="Headfull FS (new)">\n' +
      '  <rect x="40" y="110.70000000000002" width="560.931" height="113.80000000000001" rx="0" ry="0" fill="var(--_group-fill)" stroke="var(--_node-stroke)" stroke-width="1" />\n' +
      '  <rect x="40" y="110.70000000000002" width="560.931" height="28" rx="0" ry="0" fill="var(--_group-hdr)" stroke="var(--_node-stroke)" stroke-width="1" />\n' +
      '  <text x="52" y="124.70000000000002" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--_text-sec)" dy="4.199999999999999">Headfull FS (new)</text>\n' +
      '</g>\n' +
      '<polyline class="edge" data-from="I" data-to="P" data-style="solid" data-arrow-start="false" data-arrow-end="true" points="584.931,181.60000000000002 962.2040000000001,181.60000000000002 962.2040000000001,160.85000000000002 998.2040000000001,160.85000000000002" fill="none" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)" />\n' +
      '<polyline class="edge" data-from="A" data-to="P" data-style="solid" data-arrow-start="false" data-arrow-end="true" data-label="inline template" points="827.808,127.80000000000001 962.2040000000001,127.80000000000001 962.2040000000001,148.55 998.2040000000001,148.55" fill="none" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)" />\n' +
      '<polyline class="edge" data-from="B" data-to="I" data-style="solid" data-arrow-start="false" data-arrow-end="true" data-label="template from file" points="267.639,181.60000000000002 448.13300000000004,181.60000000000002" fill="none" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)" />\n' +
      '<g class="edge-label" data-from="A" data-to="P" data-label="inline template">\n' +
