[Build] 26/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=111-nested-headfull-full-stack-components)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Hydration View State Consistency',
    content: '<h1>Hydration ViewState Consistency</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay-stack hydration assumes the ViewState used during hydration matches the DOM produced by SSR. This invariant is critical for:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>hydrateConditional</code>: checks <code>condition(currData)</code> to decide whether to adopt (element exists) or skip (element absent)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>hydrateForEach</code>: uses the array from the ViewState to match existing DOM items by trackBy</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>adoptText</code>/<code>adoptElement</code>: resolves coordinates expecting specific DOM structure</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The current flow in <code>makeJayComponent</code> (component.ts:170-181):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">1. preRender()         → [refs, render]     (sets up hydrate functions)\n' +
      '2. comp(props, refs)   → interactive core   (runs interactive constructors)\n' +
      '3. renderViewState()   → viewState          (materializes from signals)\n' +
      '4. render(viewState)   → element            (hydrates DOM with THIS viewState)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Step 2 runs interactive constructors which receive the SSR ViewState as signals. But constructors can modify these signals based on client-local data (localStorage, cookies, client-only API calls). By step 3, the ViewState may differ from what SSR produced.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Step 4 hydrates using the modified ViewState — breaking the invariant.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Components that use client-local data produce a different initial ViewState than the server:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Cart indicator</strong>: server has <code>hasItems: false</code> (no cookie access), client reads cookie → <code>hasItems: true</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>User preferences</strong>: server has defaults, client reads localStorage → different values</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Auth state</strong>: server has anonymous, client checks session → logged in</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>When the client ViewState differs from SSR:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>hydrateConditional</code> with <code>wasTrue = true</code> tries to adopt an element that doesn&#39;t exist (SSR rendered false)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>hydrateConditional</code> with <code>wasTrue = false</code> skips adoption of an element that DOES exist</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>hydrateForEach</code> tries to adopt items with trackBy values that don&#39;t match the DOM</li>\n' +
      '<li>Warnings, broken positioning, orphaned DOM nodes</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Approach: Hydrate with SSR ViewState, then update</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The SSR ViewState (<code>defaultViewState</code>) is already serialized in the HTML and passed to <code>hydrateCompositeJayComponent</code>. Use it for the hydration render, then immediately update with the client&#39;s actual ViewState.</p>\n' +
      '<div class="md-mermaid"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 917.3734999999999 420" width="917.3734999999999" height="420">\n' +
      '<style>\n' +
      '  svg {\n' +
      '    /* Derived from --bg and --fg (overridable via --line, --accent, etc.) */\n' +
      '    --_text:          var(--fg);\n' +
      '    --_text-sec:      var(--muted, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 60%, var(--bg)));\n' +
