{
  post: {
    title: 'Explicit Route Params For Static Overrides',
    content: '<h1>Explicit Route Params for Static Overrides</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>DL#69 introduced route priority ordering (static routes match before dynamic). DL#70 added automatic param inference so static override routes like <code>/products/ceramic-flower-vase</code> get <code>{ slug: &#39;ceramic-flower-vase&#39; }</code> by matching against sibling dynamic routes like <code>/products/[slug]</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The inference logic (<code>inferParamsForStaticRoutes</code> in route-scanner.ts) works by:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Finding all fully static routes</li>\n' +
      '<li>For each, searching for a dynamic sibling route where static segments align</li>\n' +
      '<li>Mapping static segment values to param names from the dynamic route</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The automatic inference is too complex and collision-prone:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Multiple dynamic routes at different nesting levels can match the same static route</li>\n' +
      '<li>Catch-all routes (<code>[...path]</code>) and optional params (<code>[[id]]</code>) add matching ambiguity</li>\n' +
      '<li>The inference happens at scan time with no visibility to the developer — params appear &quot;magically&quot;</li>\n' +
      '<li>When routes are reorganized, inference results change silently</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Explicit params via <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-params&quot;&gt;</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>Replace automatic inference with an explicit declaration in the override route&#39;s jay-html:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token comment">&lt;!-- /products/ceramic-flower-vase/page.jay-html --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;html</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;head</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-params&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      slug: ceramic-flower-vase\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-data&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;./page.jay-contract&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/head</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    ...\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/html</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The tag body is YAML (consistent with <code>application/jay-data</code>). Keys are param names, values are param values.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Route scanner changes</h3>\n' +
      '<p>During <code>scanDirectory</code>, when a <code>page.jay-html</code> is found:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Read the file content</li>\n' +
      '<li>Parse <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-params&quot;&gt;</code> if present</li>\n' +
      '<li>Parse the YAML body as <code>Record&lt;string, string&gt;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Store as <code>route.inferredParams</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Remove:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>inferParamsForStaticRoutes()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>dynamicRouteCouldMatch()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>isFullyStaticRoute()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>hasDynamicSegments()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>ParamInferenceResult</code> type</li>\n' +
      '<li>The inference logging at lines 289-297</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>What stays the same</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>JayRoute.inferredParams</code> field — same type, same usage</li>\n' +
      '<li>Dev server merge: <code>{ ...route.inferredParams, ...req.params }</code> — unchanged</li>\n' +
      '<li>Slow render cache keying with params hash — unchanged</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>loadParams</code> validation — unchanged</li>\n' +
      '<li>Route priority sorting — unchanged</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Parsing approach</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add a <code>parseJayHtmlHead</code> utility that uses <code>node-html-parser</code> (same HTML parser as <code>parseJayFile</code>, <code>slowRenderTransform</code>, and <code>assignCoordinates</code>) to extract metadata from jay-html <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> script tags. This is lighter than the full <code>parseJayFile</code> (which does type analysis, contract loading, etc.) but uses a real parser — no fragile regex.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Returns <code>WithValidations&lt;T&gt;</code> to report errors (duplicate tags, YAML parse failures).</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> parse <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'node-html-parser'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> YAML <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'yaml'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> WithValidations <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/compiler-shared'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">/**\n' +
      " * Parse a jay-html file's &lt;head&gt; and extract &lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-params&quot;&gt; content.\n" +
      ' * Uses the same HTML parser as the compiler (node-html-parser).\n' +
      ' */</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">parseJayParams</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  jayHtmlContent<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> WithValidations<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token keyword">undefined</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> root <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">parse</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>jayHtmlContent<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    comment<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">true</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    blockTextElements<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> script<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">true</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> style<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">true</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token keyword">const</span> head <span class="token operator">=</span> root<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">querySelector</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>'head<span class="token string">');\n` +
      '  if (!head) return new WithValidations(undefined, []);\n' +
      '\n' +
      `  const paramScripts = head.querySelectorAll('</span>script<span class="token punctuation">[</span>type<span class="token operator">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-params&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token string">');\n` +
      '  if (paramScripts.length === 0) return new WithValidations(undefined, []);\n' +
      '  if (paramScripts.length &gt; 1) {\n' +
      '    return new WithValidations(undefined, [\n' +
      `      '</span>Multiple <span class="token operator">&lt;</span>script type<span class="token operator">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-params&quot;</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span> tags found — expected at most one'<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> body <span class="token operator">=</span> paramScripts<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token number">0</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>textContent<span class="token operator">?</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">trim</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token operator">!</span>body<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token keyword">new</span> <span class="token function">WithValidations</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token keyword">undefined</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">try</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token keyword">new</span> <span class="token function">WithValidations</span><span class="token punctuation">(</s'... 20296 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
