{
  post: {
    title: 'Client Import Rewriting In Library Builds',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #116 — Client Import Rewriting in Library Builds</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay plugins have dual entry points: main (<code>index.ts</code>) for server code and <code>/client</code> (<code>index.client.ts</code>) for browser code. The <code>jayStackCompiler</code> plugin handles code splitting — removing server code from client builds and vice versa — but import specifiers pointing to other plugins need rewriting from bare (<code>@jay-framework/wix-cart</code>) to client subpath (<code>@jay-framework/wix-cart/client</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Related</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>compiler-jay-stack/lib/plugin-client-import-resolver.ts</code> — the rewriting plugin</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>compiler-jay-stack/lib/index.ts</code> — <code>jayStackCompiler()</code> orchestration</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>When building a Jay plugin library (e.g., <code>wix-stores</code>) with <code>vite build</code> (client build, <code>ssr: false</code>), bare <code>@jay-framework/*</code> imports are <strong>not rewritten</strong> to <code>/client</code> subpaths in the output.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Example output</strong> (<code>wix-stores/dist/index.client.js</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-javascript"><span class="token comment">// Line 1 — correct (manually written as /client in index.client.ts)</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> WIX_CART_CONTEXT <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/wix-cart/client'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Line 7 — WRONG (bare import from wix-stores-context.ts, not rewritten)</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> WIX_CART_CONTEXT as WIX_CART_CONTEXT2 <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/wix-cart'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p><strong>Source</strong> (<code>wix-stores-context.ts</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  WIX_CART_CONTEXT<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  type CartState<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  type CartOperationResult as CartResult<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/wix-cart'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>This file is shared between server and client builds. The bare import is correct for server; needs <code>/client</code> for client.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>How it breaks</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In the monorepo dev-server, Vite&#39;s middleware intercepts imports at serve time, masking the bug. In a standalone project, Vite&#39;s dependency pre-bundling (esbuild) follows the bare import into <code>dist/index.js</code> (server entry), which contains <code>module.createRequire</code> — a Node-only API:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Uncaught TypeError: (0, import_module.createRequire) is not a function</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Analysis</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The existing <code>createPluginClientImportResolver</code> used a <code>transform</code> hook with regex-based import rewriting. The regex used <code>.+?</code> which does not match across newlines, silently skipping multi-line imports like:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> WIX_CART_CONTEXT<span class="token punctuation">,</span> type CartState <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/wix-cart'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>Single-line imports (manually written as <code>/client</code> in <code>index.client.ts</code>) worked fine. Multi-line imports (common in shared context files) were silently skipped.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix the regex in <code>transform</code> hook</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Change <code>.+?</code> to <code>[\\s\\S]+?</code> in both <code>IMPORT_REGEX</code> and <code>EXPORT_FROM_REGEX</code> to match across newlines.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Rejected approach: <code>resolveId</code> hook</h3>\n' +
      '<p>We initially tried replacing <code>transform</code> with a <code>resolveId</code> hook (<code>this.resolve()</code> to re-resolve with <code>/client</code> suffix). This approach was theoretically cleaner (no regex needed — Rollup provides each import specifier individually) but caused the Vite dev-server to crash during hydration tests. The <code>resolveId</code> hook runs for every import in every module, and even with synchronous <code>null</code> returns for non-plugin imports, the added overhead in the Vite dev-server resolution pipeline caused process crashes during test suite execution. The root cause was not fully diagnosed but appeared related to how Vite&#39;s dev-server handles plugin hooks during concurrent module resolution.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>transform</code> hook approach works reliably because:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>It runs once per file (not per import)</li>\n' +
      '<li>The regex fix handles multi-line imports correctly</li>\n' +
      '<li>In dev serve mode, Vite serves the transformed source directly</li>\n' +
      '<li>In build mode, Rollup processes the transformed source and preserves the rewritten specifiers for externals</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Fix regex</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Change <code>.+?</code> to <code>[\\s\\S]+?</code> in <code>IMPORT_REGEX</code> and <code>EXPORT_FROM_REGEX</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Add multi-line test</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add test case for multi-line import rewriting.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 3: Verify</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Build wix-stores client bundle — check output has <code>/client</code> imports</li>\n' +
      '<li>Run in standalone project — no <code>createRequire</code> error</li>\n' +
      '<li>Run dev-server tests — no regressions</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification Criteria</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><code>wix-stores/dist/index.client.js</code> has <code>@jay-framework/wix-cart/client</code> (not bare)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Standalone project <code>yarn dev</code> loads without <code>createRequire</code> error</li>\n' +
      '<li>Dev-server tests pass</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Results</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Fixed <code>IMPORT_REGEX</code> and <code>EXPORT_FROM_REGEX</code> to use <code>[\\s\\S]+?</code> for multi-line matching. Added multi-line import test case.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Files changed</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>compiler-jay-stack/lib/plugin-client-import-resolver.ts</code> — fixed regex patterns for multi-line imports</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>compiler-jay-stack/test/plugin-client-import-resolver.test.ts</code> — added multi-line import test</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Test results</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>61/61 compiler-jay-stack tests pass (including new multi-line test)</li>\n' +
      '<li>68/68 packages build successfully</li>\n' +
      '<li>Dev-server tests pass</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Future: replace regex with AST-based transformation</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The regex approach is fragile — it can break on edge cases like import specifiers inside comments, string literals, or unusual formatting. A proper AST-based transformation (e.g., using TypeScript&#39;s compiler API or a lightweight parser like <code>es-module-lexer</code>) would be more robust. The <code>resolveId</code> approach was the ideal solution (no parsing needed at all) but was blocked by Vite dev-server stability issues. If those are resolved upstream, <code>resolveId</code> should be revisited.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Client Import Rewriting In Library Builds","number":116}'
  }
}
