[Build] 33/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=118-jay-html-compiler-refactor)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Async Data SSR And Hydration',
    content: '<h1>Async Data SSR and Hydration</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay contracts support async data tags (<code>async: true</code>) which generate <code>Promise&lt;T&gt;</code> types in ViewState. The jay-html template uses <code>when-loading</code>, <code>when-resolved</code>, and <code>when-rejected</code> directives to render different UI for each promise state.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The <strong>client-side runtime</strong> handles async elements correctly — <code>pending()</code>, <code>resolved()</code>, <code>rejected()</code> in <code>element.ts</code> react to promise state changes. The <strong>compiler</strong> generates correct code for the standard element target and the server element target. The <strong>SSR pipeline</strong> (<code>generate-ssr-response.ts</code>) awaits all promises before sending the response.</p>\n' +
      '<p>However, <strong>no integration test exists for async data flowing through SSR → swap → hydration</strong>. Creating one (test <code>11a-async-data</code>) revealed three gaps that prevent async data from working end-to-end.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 1: SSR swap scripts not generated</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>generate-ssr-response.ts</code> collects resolved template HTML via <code>onAsync()</code> but never wraps it with <code>asyncSwapScript()</code>. The resolved HTML is appended as raw text after <code>&lt;div id=&quot;target&quot;&gt;</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Current output:\n' +
      '  &lt;div id=&quot;target&quot;&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;0&quot;&gt;\n' +
      '      &lt;h1&gt;Async Data Test&lt;/h1&gt;\n' +
      '      &lt;div jay-async=&quot;message:pending&quot;&gt;        ← pending placeholder stays\n' +
      '        &lt;p class=&quot;loading&quot;&gt;Loading...&lt;/p&gt;\n' +
      '      &lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '  &lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '  &lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;0/1&quot;&gt;                   ← resolved HTML dumped outside target\n' +
      '    &lt;p class=&quot;resolved&quot;&gt;Hello from async!&lt;/p&gt;\n' +
      '  &lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><code>asyncSwapScript()</code> exists in <code>ssr-runtime</code> and is unit-tested, but is never called by the SSR pipeline.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 2: Hydrate compiler doesn&#39;t generate async elements</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The hydrate compiler uses <code>checkAsync()</code> only to decide <code>de()</code> vs <code>e()</code> for parent elements. It does NOT generate <code>pending()</code>, <code>resolved()</code>, <code>rejected()</code> runtime calls. Instead, it generates <code>adoptText</code> for coordinates inside <code>when-resolved</code> and <code>when-rejected</code> elements:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Current hydrate output — tries to adopt text at coordinates that don't exist</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token function">adoptElement</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>'<span class="token number">0</span><span class="token string">', {}, [\n` +
      `  adoptText('</span><span class="token number">0</span><span class="token operator">/</span><span class="token number">1</span><span class="token operator">/</span><span class="token number">0</span><span class="token string">', (vs) =&gt; vs), // resolved text — not in DOM\n` +
      '  adoptText(\'</span><span class="token number">0</span><span class="token operator">/</span><span class="token number">3</span><span class="token operator">/</span><span class="token number">0</span>\'<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token string">`Error: ${vs.message}`</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// rejected text — not in DOM</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Hydration warnings:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">[jay hydration] adoptText coordinate &quot;0/1/0&quot; not found in DOM\n' +
      '[jay hydration] adoptText coordinate &quot;0/3/0&quot; not found in DOM</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 3: Promise values lost in hydration script serialization</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The hydration script serializes ViewState via <code>JSON.stringify(defaultViewState)</code>. Promises serialize to <code>{}</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-javascript"><span class="token comment">// Generated hydration script</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">const</span> viewState <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> title<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'Async Data Test'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> message<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Promise → {}</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>Even if the hydrate compiler generated <code>resolved(vs =&gt; vs.message, ...)</code>, calling <code>.then()</code> on <code>{}</code> would throw.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Intended data flow</h3>\n' +
      '<div class="md-mermaid"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 933.2495 825" width="933.2495" height="825">\n' +
      '<style>\n' +
      '  svg {\n' +
      '    /* Derived from --bg and --fg (overridable via --line, --accent, etc.) */\n' +
      '    --_text:          var(--fg);\n' +
      '    --_text-sec:      var(--muted, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 60%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_text-muted:    var(--muted, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 40%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_text-faint:    color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 25%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '    --_line:          var(--line, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 50%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_arrow:         var(--accent, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 85%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_node-fill:     var(--surface, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 3%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_node-stroke:   var(--border, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 20%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_group-fill:    var(--bg);\n' +
      '    --_group-hdr:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 5%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '    --_inner-stroke:  color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 12%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '    --_key-badge:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 10%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '  }\n' +
      '</style>\n' +
      '<defs>\n' +
      '  <marker id="seq-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="5" refX="8" refY="2.5" orient="auto-start-reverse">\n' +
      '    <polygon points="0 0, 8 2.5, 0 5" fill="var(--_arrow)" />\n' +
      '  </marker>\n' +
      '  <marker id="seq-arrow-open" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="5" refX="8" refY="2.5" orient="auto-start-reverse">\n' +
      '    <polyline points="0 0, 8 2.5, 0 5" fill="none" stroke="var(--_arrow)" stroke-width="1" />\n' +
      '  </marker>\n' +
      '</defs>\n' +
      '<line class="lifeline" data-actor="SR" x1="91.8055" y1="70" x2="91.8055" y2="795" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />\n' +
      '<line class="lifeline" data-actor="HTML" x1="275.4235" y1="70" x2="275.4235" y2="795" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />\n' +
      '<line class="lifeline" data-actor="SWAP" x1="469.786" y1="70" x2="469.786" y2="795" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />\n' +
      '<line class="lifeline" data-actor="HYD" x1="647.1055" y1="70" x2="647.1055" y2="795" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />\n' +
      '<g class="message" data-from="SR" data-to="SR" data-label="renderToStream(viewState) with promises" data-line-style="solid" data-arrow-head="filled" data-self="true">\n' +
      '  <polyline points="91.8055,90 121.8055,90 121.8055,110 91.8055,110" fill="none" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#seq-arrow)" />\n' +
      '  <text x="129.8055" y="100" font-size="11" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" fill="var(--_text-muted)" dy="3.8499999999999996">renderToStream(viewState) with promises</text>\n' +
      '</g>\n' +
      '<g class="message" data-from="SR" data-to="SR" data-label="render pending content inline" data-line-style="solid" data-arrow-head="filled" data-self="true">\n' +
      '  <polyline points="91.8055,160 121.8055,160 121.8055,180 91.8055,180" fill="none" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#seq-arrow)" />\n' +
      '  <text x="129.8055" y="170" font-size="11" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" fill="var(--_text-muted)" dy="3.8499999999999996">render pending content inline</text>\n' +
      '</g>\n' +
      '<g class="message" data-from="SR" data-to="SR" data-label="collect promises via onAsync()" data-line-style="solid" data-arrow-head="filled" data-self="true">\n' +
      '  <polyline points="91.8055,230 121.8055,230 121.8055,250 91.8055,250" fill="none" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#seq-arrow)" />\n' +
