{
  post: {
    title: 'Secure Architecture',
    content: '<h1>Secure Architecture</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>as noted in <a href="02-jay-element-vs-component">02 - Jay Element and Component</a>\n' +
      'and in <a href="09-safe-events">09 - save events</a>, the main architecture idea\n' +
      'for securing Jay Components is to run the Component in a worker, while the Element runs in the main window.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This document explores this architecture.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Basic Architecture</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The basic architecture of a jay application is a tree of elements and components as in the following diagram</p>\n' +
      '<p><img src="/content/design-log/jay/12-secure-architecture-1.png" alt="Jay Basic architecture 1" loading="lazy" /></p>\n' +
      '<p>We note that a component has only one child element, while an element may have one or more\n' +
      'child components. The child components of an element can be static, under condition, or under for each.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The secure architecture is</p>\n' +
      '<p><img src="/content/design-log/jay/12-secure-architecture-2.png" alt="Jay Basic architecture 2" loading="lazy" /></p>\n' +
      '<p>We note in this diagram a few additional things</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>we have two root components - the <code>main root</code> and the <code>worker root</code>, which\n' +
      'are responsible for the creation of the Jay component and element structure\n' +
      'and establishing a <code>communication channel</code>.</li>\n' +
      '<li>on the worker, we replace each element with an <code>element bridge</code> or <code>element stab</code>.</li>\n' +
      '<li>The <code>element bridge</code> is generated by the compiler and acts like the element,\n' +
      'except it does not render DOM. instead, it records the input <code>ViewState</code> and\n' +
      'creates instances of child components when needed</li>\n' +
      '<li>The <code>element stab</code> only role is to record the input <code>ViewState</code> and need not\n' +
      'be compiler generated</li>\n' +
      '<li>The <code>Null Component</code> is in the position of the root component in the main thread\n' +
      'and passes the recorded <code>ViewState</code> of the root component to the first element</li>\n' +
      '<li>The <code>Component Bridge</code> receives the <code>ViewState</code> from the worker and passes it\n' +
      'into the Element.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>The Communication Challenge</h2>\n' +
      '<p>In order to facilitate communication between the main and worker instances, we have to\n' +
      'create some language that identifies the relationships of elements and components,\n' +
      'in three aspects</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>identify element -&gt; component relation (1:N) in both main and worker</li>\n' +
      '<li>identify component -&gt; element relation (1:1) in both main and worker</li>\n' +
      '<li>identify component &lt;-&gt; component relation (1:1) between the worker and main</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Mapping Challenges 1,2</h3>\n' +
      '<p><img src="/content/design-log/jay/12-secure-architecture-3.png" alt="First two mapping challenges" loading="lazy" /></p>\n' +
      '<p>The first two can be easily solved using a unique id generated by the first element <code>childComp</code> construct\n' +
      'for each child component, and passing that id also for the component child element. Those ids\n' +
      'can be generated by the element bridges in the worker as global ids for uniqueness between components.</p>\n' +
      '<p>We can denote those ids as <code>tree id</code> as those ids are mapping the relations element -&gt; component -&gt; element</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Mapping Challenge 3</h3>\n' +
      '<p><img src="/content/design-log/jay/12-secure-architecture-4.png" alt="Third mapping challenge" loading="lazy" /></p>\n' +
      '<p>The third challenge is to sync the element in the main with the element in the worker and how they correlate\n' +
      'to one another. The element in main and the element bridge in the worker can be generated with unique\n' +
      '<code>coordinates</code> that are in sync, used to create the <code>tree id</code>s in sync.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>The algorithm</h2>\n' +
      '<p>We use the <code>ConstructionContext</code> (internal to runtime) as the storage for <code>coordinates</code> as the nested\n' +
      'structure of <code>ConstructionContext</code>s makes it simple to create coordinates built from the matchBy ids\n' +
      'of collection with an id on the <code>ChildComp</code> member. So for a nested component under two collections, the\n' +
      'coordinate will be <code>[{first forEach matchBy},{second forEach matchBy},{ChildComp coordinates}]</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>coordinates</code>s are then guaranteed to be unique and consistent, defined during component creation.\n' +
      'Keep in mind that the <code>coordinates</code>s are only unique within the scope of a single element.</p>\n' +
      '<p>We then exchange the <code>coordinates</code>s with <code>tree id</code>s (<code>tree id</code>s are globally unique).\n' +
      'During component creation in the worker, the element bridge has the <code>coordinates</code>.\n' +
      'we generate a new unique <code>tree id</code> and pass the mapping <code>coordinates -&gt; tree id</code> to the main.</p>\n' +
      '<p>On the main, the component bridge gets the <code>coordinates</code> from the parent element,\n' +
      'and is using the <code>coordinates -&gt; tree id</code> mapping to get its data.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Secure Architecture","number":12}'
  }
}
[Build] 35/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=12-secure-architecture)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Record Type In Jay-Action',
    content: '<h1>Design Log 120 — <code>record(T)</code> Type in Jay-Action</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay-actions need to express <code>Record&lt;string, T&gt;</code> as output types. A real use case: <code>VariantStockMap</code> — variant IDs → option IDs → in-stock booleans (<code>Record&lt;string, Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;&gt;</code>). The existing type notation had no way to express typed record/map types. Empty objects <code>{}</code> produce <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code>, but there was no notation for typed values.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Add <code>record(T)</code> keyword to the compact type notation, following the <code>enum(a | b | c)</code> pattern. Supports nesting and all existing inner types via recursive parsing.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">outputSchema</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  stock<span class="token punctuation">:</span> record(boolean) <span class="token comment"># Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  variants<span class="token punctuation">:</span> record(record(boolean)) <span class="token comment"># Record&lt;string, Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  labels<span class="token punctuation">:</span> record(string) <span class="token comment"># Record&lt;string, string&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  items<span class="token punctuation">:</span> record(productCard) <span class="token comment"># Record&lt;string, ProductCardViewState&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Changes</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>compiler-shared/lib/jay-type.ts</code></strong> — Added <code>record</code> to <code>JayTypeKind</code>, <code>JayRecordType</code> class (mirrors <code>JayArrayType</code>), <code>isRecordType()</code> guard, <code>equalJayTypes()</code> case</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>compiler-shared/lib/jay-type-to-json-schema.ts</code></strong> — Added <code>additionalProperties</code> to <code>JsonSchemaProperty</code>, record → <code>{ type: &#39;object&#39;, additionalProperties: ... }</code> conversion</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>compiler-jay-html/lib/action/action-parser.ts</code></strong> — <code>record(...)</code> detection in <code>resolveStringType()</code> with recursive inner type parsing</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>compiler-jay-html/lib/action/action-compiler.ts</code></strong> — <code>renderType()</code> renders <code>Record&lt;string, T&gt;</code>, <code>collectImportedAliases()</code> recurses into record items</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Documentation</strong> — Added <code>record(T)</code> row to type notation tables in <code>server-actions.md</code>, <code>plugins.md</code>, <code>contracts-and-plugins.md</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Test Results</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
