{
  post: {
    title: 'Enum Name Collision Across Linked Contracts',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #122 — Enum Name Collision Across Linked Contracts</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>In jay-html, headless contracts define enums via <code>dataType: enum(A | B)</code>. The compiler generates a TypeScript enum name using <code>pascalCase(tag)</code> — e.g., tag <code>optionRenderType</code> → <code>OptionRenderType</code>. When a page transitively imports multiple contracts that define enums with the same tag name but different values, the generated imports collide.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Related Design Logs</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>#93 — Client hydration</li>\n' +
      '<li>#118 — Hydrate compilation target extraction</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Reproduction</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Page <code>products/kitan/[[category]]/page.jay-html</code> imports <code>product-search</code> contract (key: <code>search</code>). The linking chain:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">product-search\n' +
      '├── filters.optionFilters.optionRenderType: enum(TEXT_CHOICES | SWATCH_CHOICES)\n' +
      '└── searchResults (link: ./product-card)\n' +
      '    └── quickOption, secondQuickOption (link: ./product-options)\n' +
      '        └── optionRenderType: enum(TEXT_CHOICES | COLOR_SWATCH_CHOICES)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Both enums produce <code>OptionRenderType</code> via <code>pascalCase(&#39;optionRenderType&#39;)</code> in <code>contract-parser.ts:78</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Generated output (broken)</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// page.jay-html.d.ts</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> OptionRenderType<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">&quot;.../product-search.jay-contract&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> OptionRenderType<span class="token punctuation">,</span> ChoiceType<span class="token punctuation">,</span> OptionRenderType<span class="token punctuation">,</span> ChoiceType <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">&quot;.../product-options.jay-contract&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Three bugs visible:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Shadowing</strong>: two <code>import { OptionRenderType }</code> from different modules; second shadows first at runtime</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Duplicate within import</strong>: <code>product-card</code> links <code>product-options</code> twice (for <code>quickOption</code> and <code>secondQuickOption</code>), so <code>OptionRenderType, ChoiceType</code> appear twice in the same import</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Validation false-negative</strong>: compiler validates <code>SWATCH_CHOICES</code> against the correct enum (product-search&#39;s, via the type tree), raises no error, but at runtime <code>OptionRenderType</code> is the product-options version which doesn&#39;t have <code>SWATCH_CHOICES</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Root cause trace</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><code>contract-parser.ts:78</code> — <code>new JayEnumType(pascalCase(tag), parseEnumValues(dataType))</code> derives name solely from tag name, no scoping by contract or path</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>contract-to-view-state-and-refs.ts:92,103</code> — enums from linked sub-contracts bubble up via <code>enumsToImport</code> without deduplication</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-html-parser.ts:657-701, 951-992</code> — enum import links are built without collision detection; same enum can appear multiple times from multiply-linked contracts</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-html-compile-imports.ts:22-25</code> — <code>renderImports</code> generates <code>import {symbols}</code> using <code>symbol.name</code>, producing duplicate bindings</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>expression-parser.pegjs:570</code> — <code>enumCondition</code> uses <code>head.resolvedType.name</code> for code generation; the type tree correctly resolves to the right enum, but the generated identifier matches the wrong runtime object due to shadowing</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Why validation doesn&#39;t catch it</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The expression parser resolves <code>optionRenderType</code> via <code>Variables.resolveAccessor</code>, which walks the type tree: <code>search → filters → optionFilters[] → optionRenderType</code>. This correctly lands on the product-search JayEnumType with values <code>[TEXT_CHOICES, SWATCH_CHOICES]</code>. Validation passes. But the generated code references <code>OptionRenderType.SWATCH_CHOICES</code>, and at runtime <code>OptionRenderType</code> is the product-options version (due to import shadowing) which has <code>[TEXT_CHOICES, COLOR_SWATCH_CHOICES]</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Approach: Import-level aliasing with JayEnumType.alias</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Keep <code>JayEnumType.name</code> as the canonical contract-defined name (used in <code>.d.ts</code> generation). Add an optional <code>alias</code> field that the expression parser checks first. Import uses <code>import { Name as Alias }</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Generated output (fixed)</h3>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> OptionRenderType <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./product-search.jay-contract'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> OptionRenderType as OptionRenderType$<span class="token number">1</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> ChoiceType <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./product-options.jay-contract'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>Expression for <code>search.filters.optionFilters</code>:\n' +
      '→ <code>vs1.optionRenderType === OptionRenderType.SWATCH_CHOICES</code> ✓</p>\n' +
      '<p>Expression for <code>search.searchResults.quickOption</code> (if used):\n' +
      '→ <code>vs1.optionRenderType === OptionRenderType$1.COLOR_SWATCH_CHOICES</code> ✓</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Step 1: Add <code>alias</code> field to JayEnumType</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>packages/compiler/compiler-shared/lib/jay-type.ts</code></p>\n' +
      '<p>Add <code>public alias?: string</code> to <code>JayEnumType</code>. This is a page-local override — set only when a collision is detected during page compilation. Contract <code>.d.ts</code> generation is unaffected (never sets alias).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Step 2: Use alias in expression parser</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>packages/compiler/compiler-jay-html/lib/expressions/expression-parser.pegjs</code></p>\n' +
      '<p>In the <code>enumCondition</code> rule (line 566-575), replace <code>head.resolvedType.name</code> with <code>(head.resolvedType.alias || head.resolvedType.name)</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Rebuild parser (<code>yarn build</code> regenerates <code>expression-parser.cjs</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Step 3: Deduplicate enums within a single headless import</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>packages/compiler/compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-html-parser.ts</code></p>\n' +
      '<p>In both enum collection blocks (lines ~679-701 and ~970-992), deduplicate <code>enumsFromOtherContracts</code> by <code>(declaringModule, type.name)</code> before building <code>enumImportLinks</code>. Fixes the <code>{X, Y, X, Y}</code> duplication from multiply-linked sub-contracts.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Step 4: Resolve cross-contract collisions in parseJayFile</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>packages/compiler/compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-html-parser.ts</code></p>\n' +
      '<p>After <code>allHeadlessImports</code> is assembled (line ~1254), before <code>parseTypes</code> is called:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Collect all enum-typed <code>JayImportName</code> entries from all <code>contractLinks</code> across all headless imports</li>\n' +
      '<li>Group by <code>name</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>For groups with &gt;1 entry from different modules:<ul>\n' +
      '<li>First occurrence: unchanged</li>\n' +
      '<li>Subsequent: set <code>enumType.alias = name + &#39;$&#39; + counter</code>, set <code>importName.as = alias</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li>Always alias across different modules — even same values in different order would produce different numeric indices</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Must happen before <code>parseTypes</code> because the type tree is built from the same JayEnumType instances — the alias field propagates automatically.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><code>cd packages/compiler/compiler-jay-html &amp;&amp; yarn vitest run</code> — all tests pass</li>\n' +
      '<li>Golf page <code>.d.ts</code> has no duplicate OptionRenderType imports</li>\n' +
      '<li>Expression output uses aliased name for the colliding enum</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Enum Name Collision Across Linked Contracts","number":122}'
  }
}
