[Build] 41/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=125-plugin-agent-kit)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Coordinate Assignment Rules',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #126 — Scoped Coordinate System</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The coordinate system ensures SSR and hydration consistently resolve elements in the DOM tree. Coordinates are assigned at compile/pre-render time, written to <code>jay-coordinate</code> attributes in SSR HTML, and resolved at runtime during hydration.</p>\n' +
      '<p>DL#103 introduced coordinate pre-processing. DL#106 added Kindergarten for dynamic elements. DL#123 added headfull FS components. This design log addresses a fundamental inconsistency in how coordinates are computed and proposes a scoped coordinate system to replace the current approach.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>The Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The current system has two inconsistent mechanisms:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>SSR (assign-coordinates + server element):</strong> Writes coordinates that mix absolute paths with relative segments depending on context. slowForEach items use a separate <code>slowForEachPrefix</code> chain that skips headless instance segments.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Hydrate compiler:</strong> Strips prefixes from coordinates to produce relative coordinates, then relies on the runtime&#39;s <code>coordinateBase</code> accumulation (<code>forInstance</code>/<code>forItem</code>) to reconstruct the full path.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>These two mechanisms produce different results when slowForEach items are nested inside headless instances:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>SSR writes:</strong> <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;001de78a-...&quot;</code> (trackBy value only — no parent prefix)\n' +
      '<strong>Hydrate resolves:</strong> <code>0/kitanheader:AR0/0/category-list:AR0/001de78a-...</code> (full accumulated path)</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Root Cause</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The inconsistency comes from coordinate stripping in the hydrate compiler that has no equivalent in the SSR path. The hydrate compiler strips prefixes when entering headless instances, forEach, and slowForEach — producing relative coordinates that the runtime rebuilds via <code>forInstance</code>/<code>forItem</code>. But the SSR assigns coordinates using <code>assign-coordinates.ts</code> which has its own independent prefix tracking (<code>slowForEachPrefix</code>) that doesn&#39;t match the hydrate&#39;s stripping rules.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The more nesting levels (headfull FS → headless plugin → slowForEach), the more the two systems diverge.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Current Rules (Status Quo)</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Element Types and Coordinates</h3>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Element Type</th>\n' +
      '<th>Coordinate Format</th>\n' +
      '<th>Example</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Regular HTML element</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>parentCoord/childIndex</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>0/1/2</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>slowForEach item</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>slowForEachPrefix/jayTrackBy</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>p1/p2</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Headless instance <code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>parentCoord/contractName:ref</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>0/widget:AR0</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>forEach item</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>$trackBy/childIndex</code> (template)</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>$_id/0</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h3>The Two Coordinate Chains</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Chain A — <code>parentCoord</code> (full DOM path):</strong>\n' +
      'Includes every nesting level: element indices, headless instance identifiers, and slowForEach trackBy values.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Chain B — <code>slowForEachPrefix</code> (trackBy-only chain):</strong>\n' +
      'Only includes <code>jayTrackBy</code> values. Skips element indices and headless instance coordinates.</p>\n' +
      '<p>For page-level slowForEach, both chains produce the same result. For nested cases (headless instance → slowForEach), Chain A has extra segments that Chain B skips — causing the mismatch.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Runtime Resolution</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The runtime maintains <code>coordinateBase</code> that mirrors Chain A:</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Method</th>\n' +
      '<th>Adds to coordinateBase</th>\n' +
      '<th>Used by</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>forItem(id)</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>[...base, id]</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>forEach, slowForEach</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>forInstance(coord)</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>[...base, ...segments]</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>headless instances</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>Resolution: <code>fullKey = coordinateBase.join(&#39;/&#39;) + &#39;/&#39; + localCoordinate</code></p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design: Scoped Coordinates</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Core Idea</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Define <strong>coordinate scopes</strong>. Each scope is a self-contained coordinate namespace. Coordinates within a scope are relative to the scope root. Scopes are either <strong>static</strong> (compile-time, shared between SSR and hydrate) or <strong>DOM-relative</strong> (runtime, for dynamic forEach).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Scope Boundaries</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Three element types define scope boundaries:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Headless instance</strong> (<code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code>) — each instance starts a new scope</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>forEach item</strong> — each iteration starts a new scope</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>slowForEach item</strong> — each concrete item starts a new scope</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>The page root is the initial scope (<code>S0</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<p>Scope IDs are assigned by a depth-first counter in <code>assign-coordinates</code>: <code>S0</code>, <code>S1</code>, <code>S2</code>, ... Both SSR and hydrate compilers process the same template in the same order, so they produce the same IDs.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>The Universal Rule</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Every scope is resolved against its own DOM subtree, not a global map.</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>When entering a scope boundary, the runtime builds a local coordinate map from that element&#39;s subtree. All coordinate lookups within the scope search this local map. This is the same mechanism used for the page root (<code>withHydrationRootContext</code> builds a map from the root element&#39;s descendants).</p>\n' +
      '<p>This means scope IDs CAN repeat — for example, a forEach body compiled once always uses the same scope IDs (<code>S3</code>, <code>S4</code>, ...). Each forEach iteration builds its own local map from its own DOM branch, so <code>S3/0</code> in iteration A resolves to a different element than <code>S3/0</code> in iteration B. No collisions because different local maps.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Coordinate Format</h3>\n' +
      '<p>All coordinates use the same format:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">jay-coordinate=&quot;S&lt;n&gt;/&lt;relativeCoord&gt;&quot;</code></pre>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>S&lt;n&gt;</code>: Scope ID (e.g., <code>S0</code>, <code>S1</code>, <code>S2</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;relativeCoord&gt;</code>: Position within the scope (e.g., <code>0</code>, <code>0/1</code>)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Example: Golf Project Structure</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Page root (scope S0):\n' +
      '  &lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;S0/0&quot;&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;jay:kitanheader&gt;  → defines scope S1\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Kitanheader (scope S1):\n' +
      '  &lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;S1/0&quot;&gt;              ← wrapper for multi-child body\n' +
      '    &lt;div class=&quot;top-bar&quot;&gt;                  ← S1/0/0\n' +
      '      &lt;div class=&quot;top-bar-actions&quot;&gt;        ← S1/0/0/1\n' +
      '        &lt;jay:cart-indicator&gt;  → defines scope S2\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Cart-indicator (scope S2):\n' +
      '  &lt;a jay-coordinate=&quot;S2/0&quot;&gt;               ← cart link\n' +
      '    &lt;span jay-coordinate=&quot;S2/0/0&quot;&gt;        ← count (conditional)\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Back in Kitanheader (scope S1):\n' +
      '    &lt;jay:category-list&gt;  → defines scope S3\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Category-list (scope S3):\n' +
      '  &lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;S3/0&quot;&gt;             ← category bar wrapper\n' +
      '    &lt;div slowForEach jayTrackBy=&quot;001de78a&quot;&gt;  → defines scope S4\n' +
      '\n' +
      'SlowForEach item (scope S4):\n' +
      '  &lt;a jay-coordinate=&quot;S4/0&quot;&gt;               ← category link</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Example: forEach with Nested Component</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Page (scope S0):\n' +
      '  &lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;S0/0&quot;&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;div forEach=&quot;items&quot; trackBy=&quot;_id&quot;&gt;      ← scope S1 (per item)\n' +
      '\n' +
      'forEach item (scope S1, local map per iteration):\n' +
      '  &lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;S1/0&quot;&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;jay:widget&gt;  → scope S2\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Widget (scope S2, local map per iteration):\n' +
      '  &lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;S2/0&quot;&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;span jay-coordinate=&quot;S2/0/1&quot;&gt;</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The forEach body is compiled once. Every iteration uses the same scope IDs (<code>S1</code>, <code>S2</code>). This works because each iteration builds its own local coordinate map from its own DOM subtree. <code>S2/0</code> in iteration A resolves to a different element than <code>S2/0</code> in iteration B — different local maps, no collisions.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Comparison with Current System</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Current:</strong> <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;0/kitanheader:AR0/0/0/1/cart-indicator:AR0/0&quot;</code>\n' +
      '<strong>Scoped:</strong> <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;S2/0&quot;</code></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Current:</strong> <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;001de78a&quot;</code> (broken — missing parent prefix)\n' +
      '<strong>Scoped:</strong> <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;S4/0&quot;</code> (always correct — scope is self-contained)</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Current forEach:</strong> <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;$_id/0/widget:AR0/0&quot;</code>\n' +
      '<strong>Scoped forEach:</strong> item root has <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;S1/0&quot;</code>, widget has <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;S2/0&quot;</code></p>\n' +
      '<h3>How Scope Resolution Works</h3>\n' +
      '<p>All scopes work the same way — no static vs dynamic distinction:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><code>assign-coordinates</code> assigns <code>jay-scope=&quot;S&lt;n&gt;&quot;</code> on the boundary element and <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;S&lt;n&gt;/...&quot;</code> on descendants within that scope</li>\n' +
      '<li>SSR writes these attributes to the HTML</li>\n' +
      '<li>At hydration time, when entering a scope:\n' +
      'a. Locate the scope boundary element in the parent scope\n' +
      'b. Build a <strong>local coordinate map</strong> from that element&#39;s <code>jay-coordinate</code> descendants\n' +
      'c. Create a scoped context with this local map\n' +
      'd. Adopt children using scoped coordinates (<code>S&lt;n&gt;/...</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>This is the same mechanism used fo'... 15244 more characters,
