{
  post: {
    title: 'SEO Head Injection',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #127 — SEO Head Injection</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay-html templates have a <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> and a <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>. The compiler processes <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> for dynamic bindings (data, conditionals, forEach, refs). The <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> is used for static content: headless imports, stylesheets, and static <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;meta&gt;</code> tags. Dynamic bindings like <code>{value}</code> in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> elements are not supported.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This means there is no way to render SEO data (title, meta description, Open Graph tags, canonical URLs, etc.) from ViewState into the page&#39;s <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> during SSR.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The Wix Stores product page contract defines an <code>seoData</code> structure:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> seoData\n' +
      '  type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> sub<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contract\n' +
      '  tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> tags\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> sub<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contract\n' +
      '      repeated<span class="token punctuation">:</span> true\n' +
      '      trackBy<span class="token punctuation">:</span> position\n' +
      '      tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> position, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> type, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token comment"># element name: meta, title, link, etc.</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> props\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> sub<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contract\n' +
      '          repeated<span class="token punctuation">:</span> true\n' +
      '          trackBy<span class="token punctuation">:</span> key\n' +
      '          tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '            <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> key, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token comment"># attribute name</span>\n' +
      '            <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> value, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token comment"># attribute value</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> meta\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> sub<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contract\n' +
      '          repeated<span class="token punctuation">:</span> true\n' +
      '          trackBy<span class="token punctuation">:</span> key\n' +
      '          tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '            <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> key, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '            <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> value, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> children, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token comment"># inner text (e.g. for &lt;title&gt;)</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> settings\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> sub<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contract\n' +
      '      tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> preventAutoRedirect, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> keywords\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> sub<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contract\n' +
      '          repeated<span class="token punctuation">:</span> true\n' +
      '          trackBy<span class="token punctuation">:</span> term\n' +
      '          tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '            <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> term, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '            <span class="token punctuation">-</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> isMain, type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data, dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean <span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This structure represents serialized HTML elements for the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>type</code> is the element name (<code>meta</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>link</code>, <code>script</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>props</code> are the attributes (<code>name</code>/<code>content</code>, <code>property</code>/<code>content</code> for OG, <code>rel</code>/<code>href</code> for canonical)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>children</code> is inner text (e.g., the text inside <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>An AI agent tried to bind this in the template body:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;p.seoData.tags&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">trackBy</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;position&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;meta</span> <span class="token attribute">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;props&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">trackBy</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;key&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">name</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;{key}&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">content</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;{value}&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This doesn&#39;t work because:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;meta&gt;</code> tags must be in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, not <code>&lt;body&gt;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Jay-html doesn&#39;t support dynamic element names (the <code>type</code> field determines the tag name)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Jay-html doesn&#39;t support dynamic attribute names (<code>name=&quot;{key}&quot;</code> — the attribute name itself is dynamic)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Even if these were supported, <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> wrapping <code>&lt;meta&gt;</code> is semantically wrong</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Should SEO data be rendered by the jay-html compiler or by the SSR pipeline?</strong>\n' +
      '<strong>A:</strong> By the jay-html compiler, rendered as part of <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> during SSR. Head elements are static — rendered only in SSR, never hydrated. They support <code>slow</code> and <code>fast</code> phases only, no <code>interactive</code>. They must be part of the initial HTML response for optimal SEO (not injected after).</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Should we support a general mechanism for dynamic <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> content, or a specific SEO-focused one?</strong></p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Should this be slow-phase only, or also support fast phase?</strong>\n' +
      '<strong>A:</strong> Both slow and fast. No interactive — head elements are SSR-only.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: How does hydration work for head elements?</strong>\n' +
      '<strong>A:</strong> It doesn&#39;t. Head elements are rendered during SSR and left as-is. No hydration, no client-side updates.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Should the seoData contract structure be generic (any HTML tag) or typed (specific SEO tag types)?</strong>\n' +
      '<strong>A:</strong> Jay&#39;s philosophy is that components provide data and templates decide how to render it. The template should control the head structure — what <code>&lt;meta&gt;</code> tags, what <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, what attributes. This keeps us forward-compatible with any new header structure. The compon'... 31573 more characters,
