{
  post: {
    title: 'Unfolded Variant View',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #127 — Page Freeze</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The editor needs tools for designers to inspect all visual states of a page. The original idea was an &quot;unfolded variant view&quot; that renders all conditional branches side by side. Through design iteration, a simpler and more powerful concept emerged: <strong>page freeze</strong>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Related design logs: #50 (rendering phases), #75 (slow render conditionals), #112 (hydration ViewState consistency).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Designers working on jay-html pages need to:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>See what the page looks like in different data states (variant values, different data)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Preserve specific states for comparison while editing the jay-html</li>\n' +
      '<li>Embed frozen page views in design board applications</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Today they must manually toggle states, reload, and remember which combinations they&#39;ve checked.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design: Page Freeze</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Core Concept</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A <strong>freeze</strong> captures the current ViewState of a live page. The frozen page is rendered as pure SSR — the server element compiler produces static HTML from the saved ViewState. No component logic runs, no client scripts are included.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Flow</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>User navigates to a page and interacts until reaching the desired state</li>\n' +
      '<li>User presses <strong>Alt+S</strong> (Option+S on Mac) to trigger freeze</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Visual feedback</strong>: full-page white flash overlay (like a camera flash) + camera shutter sound effect — confirms the freeze was captured</li>\n' +
      '<li>The client captures the current ViewState via <code>window.__jay.automation.getPageState().viewState</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Client POSTs the ViewState to the dev-server → server stores it, returns an ID</li>\n' +
      '<li>Client opens a new tab at the same route with <code>?_jay_freeze=&lt;id&gt;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Server loads the saved ViewState, SSR-renders the jay-html with it, returns static HTML</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>What Freeze Gives You</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Multiple states side by side</strong>: freeze with <code>stockStatus=IN_STOCK</code>, navigate back, change state, freeze again. Two tabs showing both states.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Any state is freezable</strong>: slow-only, fast, interactive, client-only states — whatever the automation API can capture.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Pseudo-classes still work</strong>: <code>:hover</code>, <code>:focus</code>, <code>:active</code> are CSS — they work on the static HTML. The frozen page is fully responsive and supports breakpoints.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No special rendering mode</strong>: pure SSR with fixed data.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Output Formats</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Frozen pages can be served in two formats:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>1. Full page</strong> — complete HTML document with <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>. Opens in a browser tab. Includes inlined CSS.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>2. HTML fragment</strong> — just the rendered body content with scoped styles, suitable for embedding in a shadow DOM inside a design board application. For shadow DOM to work correctly:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>CSS is inlined (scoped to the fragment)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Fonts are inlined as base64 data URIs (prevents cross-origin/relative URL issues)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Images are inlined or use absolute URLs (prevents relative path mismatches)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Named Freezes</h3>\n' +
      '<p>After creating a freeze, the user can rename it (e.g., &quot;in-stock&quot;, &quot;out-of-stock&quot;, &quot;empty-cart&quot;). Rename is a post-save operation to keep the freeze flow fast.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>API Architecture</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The freeze system spans two layers:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Dev-server</strong> (HTTP) — handles the two core operations that need direct access to the rendering pipeline:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>POST /_jay/freeze</code> — save ViewState, return ID (the freeze operation itself)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>GET /route?_jay_freeze=&lt;id&gt;</code> — serve frozen page (full page format)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>GET /route?_jay_freeze=&lt;id&gt;&amp;format=fragment</code> — serve frozen page (shadow DOM fragment)</li>\n' +
      '<li>CORS headers on fragment endpoint for cross-origin design board access</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Editor protocol</strong> (Socket.IO) — exposes freeze management for design board applications:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>listFreezes(route)</code> — list saved freezes for a route</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>renameFreeeze(id, name)</code> — rename a freeze</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>deleteFreeze(id)</code> — delete a freeze</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>onFreezeChanged(callback)</code> — notify design board when jay-html changes so it can refresh its embedded frozen views</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The socket notification replaces HMR for shadow DOM embedded views — the design board application listens for change events and re-fetches the fragment.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Storage</h3>\n' +
      '<p>JSON files in <code>build/freezes/</code>. Each freeze:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;id&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;abc123&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;name&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;in-stock&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;route&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;/products/kitan&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;viewState&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> ... <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;createdAt&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;2026-04-16T10:00:00Z&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Persists across server restarts so designers build up a library of states.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: How does the frozen page render?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Pure SSR — no client scripts. The server element compiler produces HTML from the saved ViewState. For full-page format: complete HTML document with inlined CSS. For fragment format: body content with scoped styles, inlined fonts/images for shadow DOM compatibility.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Does <code>getPageState()</code> capture nested headless component ViewState?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Keyed headless components (<code>key=&quot;w&quot;</code>) — yes, merged under <code>viewState.w</code> by the composite <code>render()</code>. Non-keyed instances and headfull FS components — <strong>no</strong>. Their ViewState lives in the <code>HEADLESS_INSTANCES</code> context (keyed by coordinate, e.g., <code>S0/0/widget:AR0</code>), extracted and deleted from the ViewState in <code>composite-component.ts</code> before it reaches the automation API. Fix: the composite component&#39;s <code>render()</code> should re-inject <code>__headlessInstances</code> with each instance&#39;s current ViewState.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: How does the design board know when to refresh?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Via the editor protocol socket. When jay-html or CSS changes, the dev-server emits a <code>freezeChanged</code> event. The design board re-fetches the fragment endpoint to get the updated render.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Dev-server freeze endpoints</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add to the dev-server:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>POST /_jay/freeze</code> — body: <code>{ route, viewState }</code> → store, return <code>{ id }</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Frozen page rendering: detect <code>?_jay_freeze=&lt;id&gt;</code> in route handler<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Load saved ViewState</li>\n' +
      '<li>SSR-render jay-html with it (skip slow/fast phases)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>format=fragment</code>: return body HTML with scoped styles, inlined fonts/images, CORS headers</li>\n' +
      '<li>Default: return full-page HTML document</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li>Storage: <code>build/freezes/&lt;id&gt;.json</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Client-side: register <code>Alt+S</code> / <code>Option+S</code> keyboard shortcut on dev pages (in the automation setup script, not a plugin) to trigger freeze and open new tab</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Complete ViewState capture for non-keyed instances</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Problem:</strong> Non-keyed headless instances and headfull FS components store their ViewState in the <code>HEADLESS_INSTANCES</code> context, not in the composite component&#39;s ViewState. The <code>__headlessInstances</code> object is extracted and deleted from the ViewState in <code>composite-component.ts</code> (lines 44-49) before hydration. It is never re-injected into the ViewState that <code>render()</code> returns, so the automation API never sees it.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Fix:</strong> In the composite component&#39;s <code>render()</code> function, after merging all keyed and unkeyed parts, re-inject <code>__headlessInstances</code> with each instance component&#39;s current ViewState (from their interactive <code>render()</code> output).</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>packages/jay-stack/stack-client-runtime/lib/composite-component.ts</code></p>\n' +
      '<p>In the <code>render()</code> closure (around line 96-117):</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>After the existing merge loop that handles keyed and unkeyed parts</li>\n' +
      '<li>Collect each instance component&#39;s current ViewState by its coordinate key</li>\n' +
      '<li>Add <code>viewState.__headlessInstances = { [coordKey]: instanceVS, ... }</code> to the returned ViewState</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Test:</strong> Add a test to <code>packages/runtime/runtime-automation/test/integration.test.ts</code> that:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Creates a composite component with a non-keyed headless instance</li>\n' +
      '<li>Wraps with automation</li>\n' +
      '<li>Verifies <code>g'... 21113 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Unfolded Variant View","number":128}'
  }
}
