{
  post: {
    title: 'Plugin Routes And Templates',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #130 — Plugin Routes and Templates</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins currently provide headless components, actions, services, and contexts — but not pages. Some plugins need to provide complete page experiences with a boxed design that doesn&#39;t need per-site visual customization. The primary use case is <strong>backoffice / tooling applications</strong> — admin panels, editors, dashboards — where the UI is functional, not brand-specific.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Example: the <strong>AIditor</strong> — a visual editor for Jay projects. It needs routes like <code>/aiditor</code>, <code>/aiditor/pages/[route]</code>, <code>/aiditor/contracts</code>, etc. These pages have their own UI, their own components, and their own page code. Packaging it as a Jay plugin means any Jay project can install it and get the editor at <code>/aiditor</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Related design logs: #39 (plugin package), #60 (plugin system), #69 (route priority), #111 (headfull FS components), #128 (page freeze).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>A backoffice plugin like the AIditor needs to provide full pages — jay-html templates with styling, page components with three-phase rendering, and routes. Today, the project developer must:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Manually create route pages in <code>src/pages/</code> for each tool screen</li>\n' +
      '<li>Wire up the plugin&#39;s components and actions</li>\n' +
      '<li>Maintain these pages as the plugin evolves</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>This doesn&#39;t scale. The plugin author should ship the complete page experience — routes, templates, components, and styles — as part of the plugin package. The project just installs the plugin and the routes appear.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Where do plugin pages live?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> A plugin is just an NPM package with <code>package.json</code>. Page files (jay-html, CSS) are exported via <code>package.json</code> exports. The component is referenced by its exported name (same pattern as contracts and actions).</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: How are plugin routes discovered and registered?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> From <code>plugin.yaml</code> — the <code>routes</code> array declares each route&#39;s path, jay-html export, and component name. The dev server reads these during startup.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: What happens when a project defines the same route as a plugin?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Project route takes precedence. Plugin routes are only registered when no project route matches the same path.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Can the project customize a plugin page&#39;s template without ejecting?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Not for now. A project can override by creating the same route in <code>src/pages/</code>. In theory, the project could also use the plugin&#39;s component as a keyed headless component and create its own jay-html around it.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: How do plugin routes work with route params and loadParams?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Same as any other page — the plugin page component supports <code>withLoadParams</code>, route params (<code>[slug]</code>), and three-phase rendering. A plugin route is essentially a headless component + jay-html + route path.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: How do plugin pages work with NPM packages vs local plugins?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Same as other headless components — resolved via <code>package.json</code> exports for NPM, relative paths for local plugins.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Key Insight</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A plugin route is a <strong>headless component + jay-html template + route path</strong>. The component is declared the same way as any headless component (exported member name, contract, services). The jay-html is the inline template. The route is just the URL at which the dev server serves it. No new rendering concepts — just a new way to deliver an existing pattern.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Plugin Pages in plugin.yaml</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins declare routes in <code>plugin.yaml</code>. Page files use <code>package.json</code> exports (same as contracts). The component uses the exported member name (same as headless components):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> aiditor\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">global</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> true\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">routes</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> path<span class="token punctuation">:</span> /aiditor\n' +
      '    jayHtml<span class="token punctuation">:</span> aiditor<span class="token punctuation">-</span>dashboard.jay<span class="token punctuation">-</span>html\n' +
      '    css<span class="token punctuation">:</span> aiditor<span class="token punctuation">-</span>dashboard.css\n' +
      '    component<span class="token punctuation">:</span> aiditorDashboard\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> AIditor main dashboard — page list, freeze manager\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> path<span class="token punctuation">:</span> /aiditor/pages/<span class="token punctuation">[</span>route<span class="token punctuation">]</span>\n' +
      '    jayHtml<span class="token punctuation">:</span> aiditor<span class="token punctuation">-</span>page<span class="token punctuation">-</span>editor.jay<span class="token punctuation">-</span>html\n' +
      '    css<span class="token punctuation">:</span> aiditor<span class="token punctuation">-</span>page<span class="token punctuation">-</span>editor.css\n' +
      '    component<span class="token punctuation">:</span> aiditorPageEditor\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> AIditor page editor — visual editing with freeze and variant views\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> path<span class="token punctuation">:</span> /aiditor/contracts\n' +
      '    jayHtml<span class="token punctuation">:</span> aiditor<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contracts.jay<span class="token punctuation">-</span>html\n' +
      '    component<span class="token punctuation">:</span> aiditorContracts\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> AIditor contract browser — view all contracts and their tags\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">actions</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> generateJayHtml\n' +
      '    action<span class="token punctuation">:</span> generate<span class="token punctuation">-</span>jay<span class="token punctuation">-</span>html.jay<span class="token punctuation">-</span>action</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Package.json Exports</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The plugin&#39;s <code>package.json</code> exports the page files (same pattern as contracts):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;exports&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;.&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/index.js&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;./plugin.yaml&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./plugin.yaml&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;./aiditor-dashboard.jay-html&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/pages/dashboard/page.jay-html&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;./aiditor-dashboard.css&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/pages/dashboard/page.css&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;./aiditor-page-editor.jay-html&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/pages/page-editor/page.jay-html&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;./aiditor-page-editor.css&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/pages/page-editor/page.css&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;./aiditor-contracts.jay-html&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/pages/contracts/page.jay-html&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;./generate-jay-html.jay-action&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/actions/generate-jay-html.jay-action&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The component (<code>aiditorDashboard</code>) is an exported member from the package&#39;s main module — resolved the same way as headless component names.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Route Resolution</h3>\n' +
      '<p>For each route in <code>plugin.yaml</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>jayHtml</strong>: Resolved via <code>package.json</code> exports → <code>&quot;./&lt;jayHtml&gt;&quot;</code> → actual file path</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>css</strong>: Same — resolved via exports (optional)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>component</strong>: Exported member name from the module (resolved via <code>index.ts</code> export chain, same as <code>resolveComponentSourcePath</code>)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>This is the same resolution chain used for contracts (DL#124) — <code>plugin.yaml</code> → <code>package.json</code> exports → file on disk.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Validation (validate-plugin)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>validate-plugin</code> should check:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Each route&#39;s <code>jayHtml</code> is exported in <code>package.json</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Each route&#39;s <code>css</code> (if '... 21075 more characters,
    description: '',
