    content: '<h1>Design Log #131 — Multipart File Upload in Actions</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay actions (<code>makeJayAction</code>, <code>makeJayStream</code>) currently accept JSON-only input. The client serializes with <code>JSON.stringify()</code>, sets <code>Content-Type: application/json</code>, and the server body parser calls <code>JSON.parse()</code>. There is no path for binary data.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The AIditor plugin (golf project DL#08) needs to upload screenshots, video frames, and file attachments as part of agent task submissions. Today this is handled by a separate HTTP server on port 8787 — the goal is to eliminate that and route everything through Jay actions.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Related design logs: #63 (server actions), #129 (streaming actions), #130 (plugin routes).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>An AIditor &quot;submit task&quot; action needs to receive:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Screenshots (PNG, ~100KB–2MB each)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Video recordings or frame sequences</li>\n' +
      '<li>Text metadata (annotations, notes, target selectors)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Binary files can&#39;t go through <code>JSON.stringify()</code>. The options are base64 encoding (33% size overhead, memory pressure for large files) or proper multipart form handling.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Approach: FormData-aware actions</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add multipart/form-data support to the existing action pipeline. Actions opt in by declaring file fields. The framework handles parsing on the server and FormData construction on the client.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Action Declaration</h3>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">const</span> submitTask <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">makeJayAction</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'aiditor.submitTask'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withFiles</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token comment">// marks this action as accepting files</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withHandler</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token function">async </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>input<span class="token operator">:</span> SubmitTaskInput<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>services<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">// input.screenshots is JayFile[]</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">// input.notes is string (text field)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><code>withFiles()</code> on the builder sets a flag (<code>acceptsFiles: true</code>) on the action definition. No schema needed — the handler&#39;s input type declares which fields are files.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>File Type</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">/** A file received by a multipart action */</span>\n' +
      'interface JayFile <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Original filename */</span>\n' +
      '  name<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** MIME type */</span>\n' +
      '  type<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** File size in bytes */</span>\n' +
      '  size<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Absolute path to the temp file on disk */</span>\n' +
      '  path<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Files are written to disk by the parser (not buffered in memory). The handler receives paths, not buffers. Temp files are cleaned up after the handler returns.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Client Side</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When calling an action marked with <code>acceptsFiles</code>, the client caller detects <code>File</code> or <code>Blob</code> instances in the input and builds <code>FormData</code> instead of JSON:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Client build transform produces:</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">const</span> submitTask <span class="token operator">=</span> createActionCaller<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>SubmitTaskInput<span class="token punctuation">,</span> Result<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'aiditor.submitTask'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'POST'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n` +
      '  acceptsFiles<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">true</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// When called:</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">submitTask</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  notes<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'Fix the header alignment'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '  screenshots<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>file1<span class="token punctuation">,</span> file2<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// File objects from input or canvas</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The caller:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Creates a <code>FormData</code> object</li>\n' +
      '<li>Appends <code>File</code>/<code>Blob</code> values as file fields</li>\n' +
      '<li>Appends non-file values as a single <code>_json</code> field (<code>JSON.stringify</code> of the remaining data)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Omits <code>Content-Type</code> header (browser sets it with boundary)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Server Side</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The body parser middleware (<code>actionBodyParser</code> in <code>action-router.ts</code>) checks <code>Content-Type</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>application/json</code> → existing JSON parse path (unchanged)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>multipart/form-data</code> → parse with <code>busboy</code> (streaming multipart parser, no dependencies beyond Node built-ins since Node 18+)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>File fields → write to temp dir, produce <code>JayFile</code> objects</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>_json</code> field → parse as JSON, merge with file fields</li>\n' +
      '<li>Result: <code>req.body = { ...jsonFields, ...fileFields }</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Stream Actions with Files</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>makeJayStream</code> can also use <code>.withFiles()</code>. The input parsing is the same — multipart for the request, NDJSON for the response stream. This is the AIditor&#39;s primary use case: upload screenshots, stream agent output back.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Why not just base64 encode?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: Screenshots are typically 500KB–2MB. Base64 adds 33% overhead. For video frames (multiple images), this compounds quickly. Multipart streaming writes directly to disk — constant memory regardless of file size.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Why <code>busboy</code> and not <code>multer</code> or <code>formidable</code>?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: <code>busboy</code> is the lowest-level streaming parser. <code>multer</code> wraps <code>busboy</code> with Express middleware conventions we don&#39;t need (we have our own middleware). <code>formidable</code> is larger. <code>busboy</code> has zero dependencies and is battle-tested (used internally by <code>multer</code>, <code>express-fileupload</code>, etc.). Alternatively, since Node 18+ includes <code>Blob</code> and <code>FormData</code> natively, we could explore using the built-in <code>Request</code> API, but Express doesn&#39;t expose it.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Where do temp files go?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: <code>{buildFolder}/.tmp/actions/</code> — cleaned up after handler returns. The build folder is already gitignored and cleaned by <code>yarn clean</code>.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Does the build transform need changes?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: Yes. The client-side replacement of <code>makeJayAction</code> must pass <code>{ acceptsFiles: true }</code> to <code>createActionCaller</code> when the action uses <code>.withFiles()</code>. This is a flag on the action definition that the compiler reads.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: What about file size limits?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: Default 10MB per file, configurable via <code>withFiles({ maxFileSize: ... })</code>. The parser rejects files exceeding the limit before writing them fully to disk.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Server-side multipart parsing</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File: <code>dev-server/lib/action-router.ts</code></strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p>Update <code>actionBodyParser()</code> (lines 213–251):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Check <code>Content-Type</code> header</li>\n' +
      '<li>If <code>multipart/form-data</code>: parse with <code>busboy</code><ul>\n' +
      '<li>File fields → write to <code>{buildFolder}/.tmp/actions/{requestId}/</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>_json</code> field → parse as JSON</li>\n' +
      '<li>Merge into <code>req.body</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li>If <code>application/json</code>: existing path (unchanged)</li>\n' +
      '<li>After handler completes: delete temp directory</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</l'... 11102 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Multipart File Upload In Actions","number":131}'
  }
}
