{
  post: {
    title: 'Ui-Kit Headless Primitives',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #132 — UI Kit: Headless Primitives</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay separates visual design (jay-html + CSS) from component logic (headless components). Most UI patterns can be built with pure HTML and CSS — modern CSS has <code>scroll-snap</code>, <code>overflow: auto</code>, <code>:hover</code>, <code>details/summary</code>, and the Popover API covers most interactive needs.</p>\n' +
      '<p>But some patterns need a thin JS shim — one or two lines that bridge between a user event and a CSS/HTML state change. These are not &quot;components&quot; in the traditional sense; they&#39;re micro-interactions that complete what HTML/CSS can almost do alone.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Other patterns need <strong>no JS at all</strong> — they&#39;re pure CSS/HTML techniques that designers may not know about. These are documented as <strong>skills</strong> (agent-kit guides) rather than implemented as components.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This plugin (<code>@jay-framework/ui-kit</code>) provides:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Headless components</strong> for the patterns that genuinely need JS</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Designer skills</strong> (agent-kit guides) for patterns that are pure CSS/HTML</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Designers building jay-html pages need common UI patterns. Some need a developer to write JS; others are achievable with pure HTML/CSS but the techniques aren&#39;t widely known:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Needs JS (headless component):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Popover menus</strong> — Popover API requires <code>el.showPopover()</code> for hover triggers</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Scroll carousels</strong> — CSS scroll-snap handles snapping, but prev/next buttons need <code>el.scrollBy()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Copy-to-clipboard</strong> — <code>navigator.clipboard.writeText()</code> is the only option</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Pure CSS/HTML (skill / guide only):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol start="4">\n' +
      '<li><strong>Tabs</strong> — radio inputs + <code>:checked</code> selector + CSS sibling combinators</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Accordions</strong> — <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code> with CSS transitions</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Tooltips</strong> — CSS <code>:hover</code> + <code>::after</code> pseudo-elements or Popover API with <code>popovertarget</code> (click-triggered)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Responsive navigation</strong> — checkbox toggle + CSS media queries</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design Principles</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>What becomes a headless component</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>HTML/CSS handles <strong>90%+</strong> of the behavior</li>\n' +
      '<li>The remaining JS gap is <strong>small and generic</strong></li>\n' +
      '<li>The component adds <strong>no DOM elements</strong> — only attaches behavior to designer-provided refs</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>What becomes a skill (guide)</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>The pattern is <strong>achievable with pure HTML/CSS</strong></li>\n' +
      '<li>Designers may not know the technique</li>\n' +
      '<li>The guide teaches the HTML structure + CSS needed, no component required</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>What does NOT belong</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Components with business logic (cart, search, auth)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Components that generate markup</li>\n' +
      '<li>Patterns that are trivial and well-known</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Headless Components</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Popover Menu (<code>popover-menu</code>)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>HTML/CSS reality:</strong> The Popover API (<code>popover</code> attribute) provides light-dismiss (click outside to close), top-layer rendering, and <code>::backdrop</code>. CSS <code>:popover-open</code> handles show/hide transitions. <code>popovertarget</code> works for click triggers. But <strong>hover triggers</strong> require JS — <code>showPopover()</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What the component does:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>On trigger mouseenter → <code>popover.showPopover()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Light-dismiss handles closing (click outside) — no JS needed for that</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Contract:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> popover<span class="token punctuation">-</span>menu\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">tags</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> trigger\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> interactive\n' +
      '    elementType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLElement\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Element that opens the popover on hover\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> popover\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> interactive\n' +
      '    elementType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLElement\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Element with popover attribute to show/hide</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Designer&#39;s jay-html:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;jay</span>:popover-menu<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;nav</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="token attribute">href</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;/products&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;trigger&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>Products<span class="token tag">&lt;/a</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> popover <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;popover&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;submenu&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="token attribute">href</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;/products/shoes&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>Shoes<span class="token tag">&lt;/a</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="token attribute">href</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;/products/bags&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>Bags<span class="token tag">&lt;/a</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/nav</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/jay</span>:popover-menu<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Interactive code:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">refs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>trigger<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">onmouseenter</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  refs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>popover<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">exec$</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>el<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> el<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">showPopover</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>2. Scroll Carousel (<code>scroll-carousel</code>)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>HTML/CSS reality:</strong> CSS <code>scroll-snap-type</code>, <code>overflow-x: auto</code>, and <code>scroll-snap-align</code> handle snapping. CSS <code>scroll-behavior: smooth</code> handles animation. But prev/next buttons need <code>container.scrollBy()</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What the component does:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Prev button → <code>container.scrollBy({ left: -containerWidth, behavior: &#39;smooth&#39; })</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Next button → <code>container.scrollBy({ left: containerWidth, behavior: &#39;smooth&#39; })</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Tracks <code>atStart</code> / <code>atEnd</code> for disabling buttons</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Contract:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> scroll<span class="token punctuation">-</span>carousel\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">tags</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> container\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> interactive\n' +
      '    elementType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLElement\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Scrollable container with overflow<span class="token punctuation">-</span>x auto and scroll<span class="token punctuation">-</span>snap\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> prev\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> interactive\n' +
      '    elementType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLButtonElement\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Scroll to previous item\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> next\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> interactive\n' +
      '    elementType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLButtonElement\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</spa'... 26825 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Ui-Kit Headless Primitives","number":132}'
  }
}
