[Build] 50/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=133-html-entities-in-text-nodes)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Production Build',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #134 — Production Build</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> May 10, 2026\n' +
      '<strong>Status:</strong> Draft\n' +
      '<strong>Related:</strong> #34 (jay stack), #86 (workflow lifecycle), #94 (SSR streaming), #110 (slow render cache), #52 (code splitting)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack has a working dev server (<code>jay-stack dev</code>) that handles everything in a single process: route scanning, slow rendering, fast rendering, SSR, hydration, action execution, and Vite-based asset serving. This works well for development but isn&#39;t suitable for production:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Vite runs at request time</strong> — every SSR render compiles server elements on-the-fly via <code>vite.ssrLoadModule()</code>, and client assets are served through Vite&#39;s dev middleware</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Slow render runs per-request</strong> — cache-miss requests trigger the full slow pipeline, blocking the response</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No optimized bundles</strong> — client code is served as unbundled ES modules via Vite dev server</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Single process</strong> — a slow render blocking the event loop affects request handling</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The dev server architecture is in <code>packages/jay-stack/dev-server/</code>, with runtime support split between <code>stack-server-runtime/</code> (slow render, fast render, SSR generation) and <code>stack-client-runtime/</code> (hydration, signals, action calls).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>We need a production deployment model where:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Pages are pre-compiled and pre-rendered — no Vite at request time</li>\n' +
      '<li>Client assets are bundled and optimized — tree-shaken, minified, code-split</li>\n' +
      '<li>Slow rendering happens ahead of time (build or data change) — not on the request path</li>\n' +
      '<li>Request handling is fast — just fast phase + SSR with pre-compiled artifacts</li>\n' +
      '<li>Data changes trigger targeted re-rendering without downtime</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Two-Server Architecture</h2>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">┌─────────────────────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n' +
      '│       SLOW RENDER SERVER        │     │          MAIN SERVER             │\n' +
      '│   (build-time / data-change)    │     │      (request-time)              │\n' +
      '│                                 │     │                                  │\n' +
      '│  - Compile jay-html → artifacts │     │  - Route matching                │\n' +
      '│  - Run slow phase per route     │     │  - Run fast phase (SSR)          │\n' +
      '│  - Bundle client JS/CSS (Vite)  │     │  - Execute actions               │\n' +
      '│  - Produce route manifest       │     │  - Serve static assets           │\n' +
      '│  - Watch for data change events │     │  - Read pre-built artifacts      │\n' +
      '│                                 │     │                                  │\n' +
      '│  Output: build/                 │────▶│  Input: build/                   │\n' +
      '│    pre-rendered/                │     │    (reads artifacts from disk     │\n' +
      '│    server-elements/             │     │     or shared storage)           │\n' +
      '│    client-bundles/              │     │                                  │\n' +
      '│    route-manifest.json          │     │                                  │\n' +
      '└─────────────────────────────────┘     └──────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Both servers could be <strong>the same codebase running in different modes</strong> (e.g., <code>jay-stack serve --role=renderer</code> vs <code>jay-stack serve --role=main</code>), sharing:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Service initialization (<code>init.ts</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin loading</li>\n' +
      '<li>Component definitions (<code>page.ts</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Action handlers</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Why Two Servers?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The slow render can be expensive (database queries, API calls, template compilation). Keeping it off the request path means:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Main server startup is instant — just load pre-built artifacts</li>\n' +
      '<li>Request latency is predictable — no cache-miss slow renders</li>\n' +
      '<li>Slow renders can run on different hardware (more CPU, less memory)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Data change re-renders don&#39;t affect serving</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Concern Map</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Concern 1: Build Artifacts — What the Slow Render Server Produces</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The dev server today produces these artifacts on-the-fly:</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Artifact</th>\n' +
      '<th>Dev Server</th>\n' +
      '<th>Production</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Pre-rendered jay-html (slow data baked in)</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>build/pre-rendered/*.jay-html</code> with <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-cache&quot;&gt;</code> metadata</td>\n' +
      '<td>Same format, all routes pre-rendered at build time</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Server element modules (for SSR)</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>.ts</code> files in <code>build/server-elements/</code>, loaded via <code>vite.ssrLoadModule()</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Pre-compiled <code>.js</code> files, loaded via <code>import()</code> — no Vite</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Hydration scripts (client)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Served on-demand via Vite plugin (<code>?jay-hydrate</code> query)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Bundled into client JS by Vite build</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Client JS bundles</td>\n' +
      '<td>Unbundled ES modules via Vite dev server</td>\n' +
      '<td>Vite production build — tree-shaken, minified, code-split</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>CSS</td>\n' +
      '<td>Written to build dir, served via <code>/@fs/</code> prefix</td>\n' +
      '<td>Extracted and optimized by Vite build</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Route manifest</td>\n' +
      '<td>In-memory <code>scanRoutes()</code> result</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>route-manifest.json</code> — static file listing all routes, their params, and artifact paths</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Questions:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Should server element modules be compiled to plain JS or kept as TS loaded through a lightweight transformer?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A1:</strong> Plain JS. No need for a complex runtime architecture — compile everything ahead of time.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: Should the Vite build produce a single entry per page, or a shared chunk strategy?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A2:</strong> Shared chunks for Jay framework and plugin dependencies. Page-specific code is <strong>per slow-rendered instance</strong>, not per route — because slow-phase conditionals can produce different pre-rendered jay-html per param combination, which compiles to different hydration scripts. Two instances of the same route may have structurally different client bundles if a slow conditional evaluates differently.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: Where do pre-rendered files live in deployment — local filesystem, object storage, or embedded in the server?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A3:</strong> Start with local filesystem. Artifact storage should be behind an abstraction (a service) so it can be swapped for object storage or other backends later without changing the server code.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Concern 2: Main Server Runtime — Request Handling Without Vite</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The main server needs to handle requests using only pre-built artifacts:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">HTTP Request\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── /_jay/actions/:name  →  Action Router (same as dev)\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── /static/*            →  Serve bundled client assets\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  └── /*                   →  Page Route\n' +
      '        │\n' +
      '        ├── Match route from manifest\n' +
      '        ├── Load pre-rendered jay-html (slow data baked in)\n' +
      '        ├── Load compiled server element module\n' +
      "        ├── Run fast phase (call component's fastRender)\n" +
      '        ├── Merge fast ViewState into server element\n' +
      '        ├── Execute renderToStream → HTML\n' +
      '        ├── Append client bundle &lt;script&gt; tags\n' +
      '        └── Send response</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Key differences from dev server:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No Vite</strong> — server elements are pre-compiled JS, client assets are static files</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No slow phase on request path</strong> — only fast phase + SSR</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Route manifest</strong> — static JSON instead of filesystem scanning</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No file watching</strong> — artifacts are immutable until slow render server updates them</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Questions:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q4: How does the main server load page components (<code>page.ts</code>) for the fast phase? In dev, Vite&#39;s SSR module loading handles TypeScript + imports. In production, these need to be pre-compiled to JS too.</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A4:</strong> The route manifest (<code>route-manifest.json</code>) includes references to compiled <code>page.js</code> files. The main server loads them via <code>import()</code> at startup or on first use.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q5: Should the main server use Express like the dev server, or something lighter?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A5:</strong> Use whatever makes sense — something lighter than Express is fine since we don&#39;t need Vite middleware.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q5.5: How does the route manifest get updated when data changes?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A5.5:</strong> The route manifest needs to change when param combinations change (new product added, old one removed — <code>loadParams</code> returns different results). The slow render server is responsible for updating it. For the main server to pick up changes without downtime, options:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Atomic file swap</strong> — slow render writes <code>route-manifest.next.json</code>, atomically renames over <code>route-manifest.json</code>. Main server detects the change (poll or filesystem watch).</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Re-read on request</strong> — main server reads the manifest from the artifact store on each request (or with a short TTL cache). Simple and works with any storage backend.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Signal-based reload</strong> — slow render calls an HTTP endpoint on the main server to trigger a manifest reload.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Option 2 fits best with the artifact storage abstraction (A3) — the artifact service can handle caching internally.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Concern 3: Vite Build — Client-Side Bundle Production</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The dev server serves client code through Vite&#39;s dev middleware (unbundled, with HMR). Produc'... 40578 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Production Build","number":134}'
  }
}
[Build] 51/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=134-production-build)
{
  post: {
    title: '134a - Build Pipeline',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #134a — Build Pipeline</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> May 10, 2026\n' +
      '<strong>Status:</strong> Draft\n' +
      '<strong>Parent:</strong> #134 (production build)\n' +
      '<strong>Related:</strong> #94 (SSR streaming), #110 (slow render cache), #52 (code splitting), #118 (jay-html-compiler refactor)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design Log #134 establishes a two-server production architecture where a slow render server produces build artifacts and a main server consumes them. This child design log covers the <strong>build pipeline</strong> — the process of turning source code into production artifacts.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The pipeline must produce, per instance (route + param combination):</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Pre-rendered jay-html (slow data baked in)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Compiled server element JS (for SSR at request time)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Compiled + bundled client JS (hydration script)</li>\n' +
      '<li>CSS</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Plus shared artifacts built once per version:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Jay framework shared chunks</li>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin shared chunks</li>\n' +
      '<li>Compiled server code (page.ts, actions, services, init.ts)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Route manifest</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Current State: What Exists Today</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>compiler-jay-html — Four Compilation Targets</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The compiler produces four targets from a single <code>.jay-html</code> file (<code>jay-html-compiler.ts</code>, <code>jay-html-compiler-server.ts</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Target</th>\n' +
      '<th>Generator</th>\n' +
      '<th>Output</th>\n' +
      '<th>Used By</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Element</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>generateElementFile()</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>render()</code> — creates DOM from scratch</td>\n' +
      '<td>Client-only rendering (no SSR)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Hydrate</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>generateElementHydrateFile()</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>hydrate()</code> — adopts existing DOM</td>\n' +
      '<td>Client after SSR</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Server Element</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>generateServerElementFile()</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>renderToStream(vs, ctx)</code> — writes HTML strings</td>\n' +
      '<td>SSR on server</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Bridge</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>generateElementBridgeFile()</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Worker sandbox communication</td>\n' +
      '<td>Secure mode (not relevant here)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h3>compiler-jay-stack — Vite Plugin Composition</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>jayStackCompiler()</code> returns three Vite plugins (<code>compiler-jay-stack/lib/index.ts</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>jay-stack:code-split</strong> — strips server/client code based on <code>options.ssr</code><ul>\n' +
      '<li>Server build: keeps <code>withSlowlyRender</code>, <code>withFastRender</code>, strips <code>withInteractive</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Client build: strips server phases, keeps <code>withInteractive</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>jay-stack:action-transform</strong> — replaces action imports with <code>createActionCaller()</code> stubs (client only)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>jay:runtime</strong> — the base jay-html compiler plugin</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Plugin Packages — Already Pre-compiled</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins use the same <code>jayStackCompiler</code> for their builds (<code>examples/jay-stack/mood-tracker-plugin/vite.config.ts</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Server build: <code>vite build --ssr</code> → <code>dist/index.js</code> (server code)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Client build: <code>vite build</code> → <code>dist/index.client.js</code> (client code)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Jay framework packages are externalized — they become shared chunks in the consuming project</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Dev Server — How SSR Works Today</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>generate-ssr-response.ts</code> at request time:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">1. parseJayFile(jayHtmlContent)        — parse jay-html YAML\n' +
      '2. generateServerElementFile(jayFile)   — compile to TS\n' +
      '3. fs.writeFile(serverElementPath)      — write .server-element.ts to build/\n' +
      '4. vite.ssrLoadModule(serverElementPath) — Vite compiles TS → JS + loads\n' +
      '5. renderToStream(viewState, ctx)       — execute to produce HTML\n' +
      '6. generateHydrationScript(...)         — inline &lt;script&gt; with imports</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The hydration script is an inline <code>&lt;script type=&quot;module&quot;&gt;</code> that imports:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>hydrateCompositeJayComponent</code> from <code>@jay-framework/stack-client-runtime</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>hydrate</code> from <code>page.jay-html?jay-hydrate</code> (compiled on-demand by Vite plugin)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Each page part&#39;s client export</li>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin/project init modules</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Vite dev server resolves all these imports at request time.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem: Gaps for Production</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 1: Server elements compiled at request time via Vite</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>compileAndLoadServerElement()</code> uses <code>vite.ssrLoadModule()</code> which requires a running Vite dev server. Production needs pre-compiled <code>.js</code> files loadable via <code>import()</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What to change:</strong> The compilation steps (parse → generate → write) are reusable. Replace <code>vite.ssrLoadModule()</code> with a pre-compilation step that produces standalone JS.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 2: Hydration script is an inline module with bare imports</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The hydration script uses bare specifiers (<code>@jay-framework/stack-client-runtime</code>, <code>page.jay-html?jay-hydrate</code>) that Vite resolves at request time. Production needs a bundled JS file with all dependencies resolved.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What to change:</strong> Generate a hydration entry point TS file per instance, then run Vite build on it.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 3: No per-instance Vite build capability</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The existing <code>jayStackCompiler</code> is designed for whole-project builds (all pages at once). We need per-instance builds where each instance has its own entry point referencing pre-rendered jay-html.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What to change:</strong> Create a Vite build configuration that takes a single instance entry point and produces a bundled JS file, referencing pre-built shared chunks.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 4: Client script generation is runtime-only</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>buildScriptFragments()</code> and <code>generateHydrationScript()</code> produce inline script text. Production needs them to produce importable TS/JS entry files.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What to change:</strong> Extract the logic that generates imports and wiring into a file-writing function instead of inline string generation.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 5: CSS handling relies on Vite&#39;s <code>/@fs/</code> URL scheme</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>compileAndLoadServerElement</code> writes CSS to disk and serves it via <code>/@fs/</code> prefix. Production needs CSS as a build artifact with content hashing.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What to change:</strong> CSS becomes part of the per-instance Vite build — imported by the hydration entry, extracted by Vite&#39;s CSS handling.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 6: No shared chunk pre-building</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In dev, shared dependencies are resolved on-demand. Production needs shared chunks built once and referenced by all instances.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What to change:</strong> A separate Vite build step that produces shared chunks from jay framework + plugin packages.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Build Pipeline Overview</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">                        Version Build (jay-stack build)\n' +
      '                        ==============================\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Phase 0: Shared Artifacts\n' +
      '  ├── Compile server code (page.ts, actions, init.ts) → build/v{n}/server/\n' +
      '  ├── Build shared client chunks (jay framework, plugins) → build/v{n}/shared/\n' +
      '  └── Scan routes + load params → route list\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Phase 1: Per-Instance Pipeline (concurrent, bounded parallelism)\n' +
      '  For each (route, params):\n' +
      '    ├── 1. Slow render → slowViewState + carryForward\n' +
      '    ├── 2. Pre-render jay-html → instance-specific jay-html\n' +
      '    ├── 3. Compile server element → .server-element.js\n' +
      '    ├── 4. Generate hydration entry → .hydrate-entry.ts\n' +
      '    ├── 5. Per-instance Vite build → instance-[hash].js + instance-[hash].css\n' +
      '    └── 6. Write instance manifest entry\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Phase 2: Finalize\n' +
      '  └── Write route-manifest.json → build/v{n}/</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 0: Shared Artifacts</h3>\n' +
      '<h4>Server Code Compilation</h4>\n' +
      '<p>Use Vite build in SSR mode to compile all server-side TypeScript:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">await</span> <span class="token function">build</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  plugins<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">jayStackCompiler</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>jayOptions<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  build<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    ssr<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">true</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    outDir<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">`build/v${version}/server`</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    rollupOptions<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '      input<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `        init<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'src/lib/init.ts'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>pageEntries<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// { 'pages/home/page': 'src/pages/home/page.ts', ... }</span>\n` +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>actionEntries<span class="token pun'... 55049 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
