[Build] 52/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=134a-build-pipeline)
{
  post: {
    title: '134b - Main Server',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #134b — Main Server</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> May 10, 2026\n' +
      '<strong>Status:</strong> Draft\n' +
      '<strong>Parent:</strong> #134 (production build)\n' +
      '<strong>Related:</strong> #134a (build pipeline), #134d (server build), #94 (SSR streaming), #63 (server actions), #130 (plugin routes)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The production main server handles HTTP requests using pre-built artifacts — no Vite, no compilation at runtime. It is the production equivalent of the dev server&#39;s <code>handleCachedRequest()</code> path, where slow data is already baked into pre-rendered HTML and only the fast phase runs per-request.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Artifacts come from the build pipeline (DL#134a) and live in a versioned storage bucket (<code>build/v{n}/</code>). The server build (DL#134d) provides compiled page components, actions, and init. The build pipeline provides per-instance artifacts (pre-rendered jay-html, server elements, client bundles).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Request Flow</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">HTTP Request\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── /_jay/actions/:name\n' +
      '  │     → Action Router (parse input, resolve services, execute handler, return JSON)\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── /assets/*\n' +
      '  │     → Static file handler (client bundles, CSS — or CDN redirect)\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  └── /* (page routes)\n' +
      '        │\n' +
      '        1. Match route from manifest\n' +
      '        2. Find instance for request params\n' +
      '        3. Load pre-rendered jay-html (slow ViewState + carryForward from cache metadata)\n' +
      '        4. Load compiled page module, run fast phase\n' +
      '        5. Handle fast phase result (redirect? error? phase output?)\n' +
      '        6. Merge slow + fast ViewState\n' +
      '        7. Load compiled server element, execute renderToStream()\n' +
      '        8. Assemble HTML response (head, SSR body, import map, init script)\n' +
      '        9. Send response</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Route Matching</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The dev server uses <code>scanRoutes()</code> to discover routes from the filesystem and Express route patterns for matching. The production server uses the pre-built route manifest:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface RouteManifest <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  version<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  sourceHash<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  buildTimestamp<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  routes<span class="token operator">:</span> RouteEntry<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  actions<span class="token operator">:</span> ActionEntry<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  plugins<span class="token operator">:</span> PluginEntry<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  sharedManifest<span class="token operator">:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// module name → hashed filename</span>\n' +
      '  publicBasePath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// CDN URL or &quot;/&quot; for self-hosting</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      'interface RouteEntry <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  pattern<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// &quot;/products/[slug]&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  segments<span class="token operator">:</span> RouteSegment<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Parsed segments for matching</span>\n' +
      '  serverModule<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// &quot;pages/products/[slug]/page.js&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  instances<span class="token operator">:</span> InstanceEntry<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  isPlugin<span class="token operator">?:</span> boolean<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  pluginName<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      'interface InstanceEntry <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  params<span class="token operator">:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// { slug: &quot;blue-widget&quot; }</span>\n' +
      '  preRenderedPath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// &quot;instances/products/[slug]/page_abc123.jay-html&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  serverElementPath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// &quot;instances/products/[slug]/page_abc123.server-element.js&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  clientBundlePath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// &quot;instances/products/[slug]/page_abc123-a1b2c3.js&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  clientCssPath<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// &quot;instances/products/[slug]/page_abc123-d4e5f6.css&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Route matching reuses the same segment-matching logic from <code>route-scanner</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Sort routes by specificity (static &gt; single param &gt; catch-all)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Match URL path against route segments</li>\n' +
      '<li>Extract param values</li>\n' +
      '<li>Find instance with matching params</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">matchRequest</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>manifest<span class="token operator">:</span> RouteManifest<span class="token punctuation">,</span> pathname<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> MatchResult <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token keyword">undefined</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">for </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token keyword">const</span> route <span class="token keyword">of</span> manifest<span class="token punctuation">.</span>routes<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">const</span> params <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">matchSegments</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>route<span class="token punctuation">.</span>segments<span class="token punctuation">,</span> pathname<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>params<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token keyword">const</span> instance <span class="token operator">=</span> route<span class="token punctuation">.</span>instances<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">find</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>i<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token function">paramsMatch</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>i<span class="token punctuation">.</span>params<span class="token punctuation">,</span> params<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> route<span class="token punctuation">,</span> instance<span class="token punctuation">,</span> params <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token keyword">undefined</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>If no instance matches the params (e.g., new product added but not yet built), the server returns 404. The slow render server is responsible for building new instances when data changes.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Artifact Storage Service</h3>\n' +
      '<p>All artifact reads go through an abstraction (DL#134 Q3):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface ArtifactStore <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">readManifest</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>RouteManifest<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">readPreRenderedHtml</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>path<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PreRenderedEntry<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">loadServerElement</span><span cl'... 56320 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"134b - Main Server"}'
  }
}
[Build] 53/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=134b-main-server)
{
  post: {
    title: '134c - Slow Render Server',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #134c — Slow Render Server &amp; Data Change</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> May 10, 2026\n' +
      '<strong>Status:</strong> Draft\n' +
      '<strong>Parent:</strong> #134 (production build)\n' +
      '<strong>Related:</strong> #134a (build pipeline), #134b (main server), #134d (server build), #110 (slow render cache), #86 (workflow lifecycle)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The slow render server is responsible for producing the build artifacts that the main server consumes. It runs in two modes:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>One-shot build</strong> (<code>jay-stack build</code>) — builds everything for a new version, then exits. Used in CI/CD pipelines and deployments.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Long-running renderer</strong> (<code>jay-stack serve --role=renderer</code>) — stays alive after the initial build, listening for data change webhooks and re-rendering affected instances.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>The slow render server is the production equivalent of the dev server&#39;s <code>handlePreRenderRequest()</code> path + file watcher invalidation. The key difference: it runs the pipeline eagerly for all instances instead of lazily on first request.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Build Mode (<code>jay-stack build</code>)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>One-shot execution that produces a complete versioned bucket:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">jay-stack build --version=2\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── Phase 0: Shared Artifacts (DL#134a, DL#134d)\n' +
      '  │     ├── Scan routes + merge plugin routes\n' +
      '  │     ├── Compile server code (Vite SSR build)\n' +
      '  │     ├── Build shared client chunks\n' +
      '  │     └── Discover all param combinations (loadParams)\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── Phase 1: Per-Instance Pipeline (concurrent)\n' +
      '  │     For each (route, params):\n' +
      '  │       ├── Slow render → pre-rendered jay-html\n' +
      '  │       ├── Compile server element (esbuild)\n' +
      '  │       ├── Generate hydration entry\n' +
      '  │       └── Per-instance Vite build\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── Phase 2: Finalize\n' +
      '  │     ├── Write route-manifest.json\n' +
      '  │     └── Write build-metadata.json\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  └── Exit</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Output: <code>build/v2/</code> — a complete, self-contained bucket ready for deployment.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The version number is provided as a CLI argument or derived automatically (git commit hash, CI build number, incrementing counter). The build metadata records:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface BuildMetadata <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  version<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  sourceHash<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Hash of source files at build time</span>\n' +
      '  buildTimestamp<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  nodeVersion<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  instanceCount<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Renderer Mode (<code>jay-stack serve --role=renderer</code>)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Long-running process that:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>On startup, verifies/builds the current version bucket</li>\n' +
      '<li>Listens for data change webhooks</li>\n' +
      '<li>Re-renders affected instances on data change</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">jay-stack serve --role=renderer --version=2\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── Startup\n' +
      '  │     ├── Check build-metadata.json in build/v2/\n' +
      '  │     ├── If source hash matches → skip rebuild, artifacts valid\n' +
      '  │     ├── If source hash differs → full rebuild (Phase 0 + 1 + 2)\n' +
      '  │     └── Initialize services (same as main server)\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── Start HTTP Server (webhook endpoints)\n' +
      '  │     ├── POST /_jay/webhooks/:pluginName → data change handler\n' +
      '  │     ├── POST /_jay/render/:route → manual re-render trigger\n' +
      '  │     └── GET  /_jay/status → health check + build info\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  └── Listen for webhooks...</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Data Change Flow</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">External system (CMS, database, etc.)\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── Sends webhook to slow render server\n' +
      '  │   POST /_jay/webhooks/wix-stores.product-change\n' +
      '  │   Body: { &quot;type&quot;: &quot;product.updated&quot;, &quot;itemId&quot;: &quot;prod-123&quot; }\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── Plugin webhook handler (makeWebhook) executes:\n' +
      '  │   1. Parses event, resolves itemId to slug\n' +
      "  │   2. Calls invalidate('product-page', { slug: 'blue-widget' })\n" +
      '  │      (plugin invalidates by its own contract name, not route)\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── Framework resolves contract → routes:\n' +
      "  │   Finds all routes using the 'product-page' contract\n" +
      '  │   (could be /products/[slug], /shop/[id], etc.)\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  ├── Framework invalidation runs per-instance pipeline:\n' +
      '  │   1. Slow render (with fresh data from plugin service)\n' +
      '  │   2. Compare new pre-rendered jay-html with existing\n' +
      '  │   3. If unchanged → skip remaining steps\n' +
      '  │   4. If changed → compile server element + hydration entry + Vite build\n' +
      '  │   5. Atomic update of route-manifest.json\n' +
      '  │\n' +
      '  └── Main server picks up changes on next request\n' +
      '      (timestamp-based caching detects file changes)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Plugin Webhook Registration</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins register webhooks using a builder pattern similar to <code>makeJayAction</code>:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In plugin's actions or init file</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> makeWebhook<span class="token punctuation">,</span> type InvalidateContract <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> '@jay<span class="token operator">-</span>framework<span class="token operator">/</span>fullstack<span class="token operator">-</span>component<span class="token string">';\n` +
      '\n' +
      'export const onProductChange = makeWebhook(\n' +
      `  '</span>wix<span class="token operator">-</span>stores<span class="token punctuation">.</span>product<span class="token operator">-</span>change<span class="token string">',\n` +
      '  async (req: HttpRequest, invalidate: InvalidateContract): Promise&lt;HttpResponse&gt; =&gt; {\n' +
      '    const event = await req.json();\n' +
      '    const { type, itemId } = event;\n' +
      '    const slug = await resolveProductSlug(itemId);\n' +
      '\n' +
      `    // Re-render pages using '</span>product<span class="token operator">-</span>page<span class="token string">' contract with this specific slug\n` +
      `    await invalidate('</span>product<span class="token operator">-</span>page<span class="token string">', { slug });\n` +
      '\n' +
      `    // Re-render all pages using '</span>search<span class="token operator">-</span>results<span class="token string">' contract\n` +
      '    // (any product change could affect search results)\n' +
      `    await invalidate('</span>search<span class="token operator">-</span>results'<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> status<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">200</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> body<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> ok<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">true</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>invalidate</code> API is contract-based — plugins invalidate by their own contract name, not by route patterns. The framework resolves which routes use each contract.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">type InvalidateContract <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>contractName<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> params<span class="token operator">?:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token keyword">void</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>invalidate(&#39;product-page&#39;, { slug: &#39;blue-widget&#39; })</code> — find all routes using the <code>product-page</code> contract, re-render the instance with matching params. If no instance exists (new product), build a new one.</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>invalidate(&#39;search-results&#39;)</code> — find all routes using the <code>search-results</code> contract, re-render <strong>all instances</strong> of those routes.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Why contract-based, not route-based:</strong> A plugin defines contracts, not routes. The plugin <code>wix-stores</code> knows it provides the <code>product-page</code> contract, but doesn&#39;t know (and shouldn&#39;t know) that the project mapped it to <code>/products/[slug]</code> or <code>/shop/[id]</code>. The framework knows the mapping because the route manifest tracks which contracts each route uses.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Future: reverse dependency map.</strong> A more fine-grained approach would track which data items each instance depends on during slow render (e.g., instance <code>/search?q=shoes</code> consumed products A, B, C). On product A change, only instances that consumed product A are re-rendered. This is an optimization that can be added later without changing the <code>invalidate</code> API — it would refine the paramless <code>invalidate(&#39;search-results&#39;)</code> to only rebuild affected instances instead of all.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Webhooks are automatically exposed at <code>/_jay/webhooks/{webhookName}</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>POST /_jay/webhooks/wix-stores.product'... 57086 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"134c - Slow Render Server"}'
  }
}
[Build] 54/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=134c-slow-render-server)
{
  post: {
    title: '134d - Server Build',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #134d — Server Build</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> May 10, 2026\n' +
      '<strong>Status:</strong> Draft\n' +
      '<strong>Parent:</strong> #134 (production build)\n' +
      '<strong>Related:</strong> #134a (build pipeline), #52 (code splitting), #63 (server actions), #65 (makeJayInit)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The production build pipeline (DL#134a Phase 0) needs to compile all server-side TypeScript into production JS. The main server loads these compiled modules via <code>import()</code> to run fast-phase rendering and action execution — no Vite at runtime.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Today, the dev server loads server code via <code>vite.ssrLoadModule()</code>, which handles TypeScript transpilation, import resolution, and hot reloading. The <code>jayStackCompiler</code> already supports SSR builds — the <code>jay-stack:code-split</code> plugin strips client code when <code>options.ssr = true</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>The project server build is the same pattern as plugin package builds.</strong> Plugin packages already use <code>jayStackCompiler</code> with <code>vite build --ssr</code> to produce <code>dist/index.js</code> (server) and <code>dist/index.client.js</code> (client). The project server build follows the same process — the difference is that plugins are published packages while the project build is deployment-specific.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>What Needs Compiling</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Server-side modules in a Jay Stack project:</h3>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Module</th>\n' +
      '<th>Source</th>\n' +
      '<th>Exports</th>\n' +
      '<th>Used By</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Page components</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>src/pages/*/page.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>page: JayStackComponentDefinition</code> with <code>slowlyRender</code>, <code>fastRender</code>, <code>loadParams</code>, <code>services</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Slow render server (slow phase), main server (fast phase)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Actions</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>src/actions/*.actions.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Named <code>JayAction</code> constants with <code>handler</code>, <code>services</code>, <code>method</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Main server (action router)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Init</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>src/lib/init.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>init: JayInit</code> with <code>_serverInit</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Both servers (service initialization)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Service markers</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td>Various <code>src/lib/*.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>createJayService()</code> constants</td>\n' +
      '<td>Imported by page.ts and actions</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Plugin server code</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>node_modules/@plugin/*/dist/index.js</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>init</code>, actions, component definitions</td>\n' +
      '<td>Both servers</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h3>What the code-split transform does for server build:</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Strips from <code>makeJayStackComponent</code> chains:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>.withInteractive(constructor)</code> — client-side component</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>.withContexts(...)</code> — client-side contexts</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Strips from <code>makeJayInit</code> chains:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>.withClient(fn)</code> — client-side initialization</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Keeps everything else: <code>.withServices()</code>, <code>.withSlowlyRender()</code>, <code>.withFastRender()</code>, <code>.withLoadParams()</code>, <code>.withServer()</code></p>\n' +
      '<h2>Current State: How Dev Server Loads Server Code</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Page components</h3>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="">vite.ssrLoadModule('src/pages/products/[slug]/page.ts')\n` +
      '  → jayStackCompiler code-splits for server\n' +
      '  → returns { page: { slowlyRender, fastRender, loadParams, services, ... } }</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Actions</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">ServiceLifecycleManager.initialize()\n' +
      '  → glob scan: src/actions/*.actions.ts\n' +
      '  → vite.ssrLoadModule(each file)\n' +
      '  → extract JayAction-branded exports\n' +
      '  → actionRegistry.register(action)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Init + services</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">ServiceLifecycleManager.initialize()\n' +
      '  → discover plugin inits (topological sort by dependencies)\n' +
      '  → vite.ssrLoadModule(plugin init path) → run _serverInit()\n' +
      "  → vite.ssrLoadModule('src/lib/init.ts') → run _serverInit()\n" +
      '  → registerService(marker, instance) for each service\n' +
      '  → globalThis.__JAY_SERVICE_RESOLVER__ = resolveServices</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Single Vite SSR Build</h3>\n' +
      '<p>All server-side code compiles in one <code>vite build --ssr</code> invocation:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> build <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'vite'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">await</span> <span class="token function">build</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  plugins<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">jayStackCompiler</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>jayOptions<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  build<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    ssr<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">true</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    outDir<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">`build/v${version}/server`</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    rollupOptions<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '      input<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token comment">// Init</span>\n' +
      `        init<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'src/lib/init.ts'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '        <span class="token comment">// Pages (one entry per route, not per instance)</span>\n' +
      `        <span class="token string">'pages/home/page'</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'src/pages/home/page.ts'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        <span class="token string">'pages/products/[slug]/page'</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'src/pages/products/[slug]/page.ts'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '        <span class="token comment">// Actions</span>\n' +
      `        <span class="token string">'actions/cart'</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'src/actions/cart.actions.ts'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        <span class="token string">'actions/search'</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'src/actions/search.actions.ts'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '      external<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token comment">// Jay framework server packages — available at runtime via node_modules</span>\n' +
      `        <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/fullstack-component'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/stack-server-runtime'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/ssr-runtime'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/view-state-merge'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/compiler-jay-html'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/compiler-shared'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '        <span class="token comment">// Plugin packages — pre-compiled, loaded from node_modules</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>pluginPackageNames<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">// Preserve module structure for predictable import paths</span>\n' +
      '    output<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `      entryFileNames<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'[name].js'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `      chunkFileNames<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'chunks/[name]-[hash].js'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `      format<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'es'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Output:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">build/v{n}/server/\n' +
      '  init.js\n' +
      '  pages/\n' +
      '    home/page.js\n' +
      '    products/[slug]/page.js\n' +
      '  actions/\n' +
      '    cart.js\n' +
      '    search.js\n' +
      '  chunks/\n' +
      '    shared-services-[hash].js    # Shared code between pages/actions</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Entry Point Discovery</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Before running the build, scan the project to find all entries:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface ServerBuildEntries <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  init<span class="t'... 24020 more characters,
