[Build] 55/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=134d-server-build)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Display Contents For Wrapper Elements',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #134 — <code>display:contents</code> for Wrapper Elements</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay&#39;s compiler wraps component content in container <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> elements for coordinate tracking and hydration. These wrappers exist at two levels:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Page root</strong> — the first element inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> in the page template, assigned coordinate <code>S0/0</code> by <code>assignCoordinates</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Headfull FS component wrappers</strong> — the <code>&lt;jay:ComponentName&gt;</code> tag that receives injected body content via <code>injectHeadfullFSTemplates</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Multi-child headless instance wrappers</strong> — synthetic <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> created in <code>assignCoordinates</code> (line 222-228) when a headless instance has multiple children</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>All three wrapper types serve the same purpose: provide a DOM node for <code>jay-coordinate</code> so the hydration target can find and adopt elements. They are structural scaffolding, not layout elements.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>These wrapper elements participate in CSS layout, creating an intermediate containing block between the component&#39;s children and their intended layout parent. This breaks:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>position: sticky</code> — the wrapper is only as tall as its content, leaving no room to stick</li>\n' +
      '<li>Flex/grid layout — children of the wrapper don&#39;t participate in the parent&#39;s flex/grid context</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>z-index</code> stacking — the wrapper creates an unnecessary stacking context boundary</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Example (headfull FS component):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">jay-coordinate</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;S0/0&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- page root --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">jay-coordinate</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;S1/0&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- component wrapper --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;sticky-nav&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>...<span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- sticky broken — parent too short --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Example (multi-child headless instance):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">jay-coordinate</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;S0/0&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">jay-coordinate</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;S2/0&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- synthetic wrapper div --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>child 1<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>child 2<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- layout doesn't match parent grid/flex --&gt;</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Fix</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Add <code>style=&quot;display:contents&quot;</code> to all wrapper elements. <code>display:contents</code> removes the element from the layout tree while keeping it in the DOM — <code>jay-coordinate</code>, hydration adoption, and event delegation continue to work, but the element no longer creates a containing block.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Where to Apply</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Headfull FS component wrappers (Approach A from golf agent)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-html-parser.ts</code>, line 876</p>\n' +
      '<p>After <code>jayTag.set_content(jayHtmlBody.innerHTML)</code>, set the style attribute on the <code>jayTag</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-ts">jayTag<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">set_content</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>jayHtmlBody<span class="token punctuation">.</span>innerHTML<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      `jayTag<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">setAttribute</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'style'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'display:contents'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>The style flows through both server and hydrate targets automatically because both render attributes from the element.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>2. Multi-child headless instance wrappers</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/assign-coordinates.ts</code>, line 223</p>\n' +
      '<p>After creating the synthetic wrapper <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>, set <code>display:contents</code>:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-ts"><span class="token keyword">const</span> wrapper <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">parse</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">querySelector</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'div'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">!</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `wrapper<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">setAttribute</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'style'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'display:contents'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>No hydrate target change needed — <code>adoptElement</code> finds the server-rendered element by coordinate and adopts it in place. The <code>display:contents</code> style is already on that DOM element from SSR. The <code>adoptBase</code> function only processes dynamic attributes (those with <code>valueFunc</code>), so static strings in the attributes object would be ignored anyway.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>3. Page root element</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The page root is the actual first element inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> in the jay-html template — it&#39;s authored by the user, not synthesized by the compiler. The user controls its styles directly, so no compiler change is needed here.</p>\n' +
      '<p>However, if the page root is a <code>&lt;jay:ComponentName&gt;</code> tag (a headfull FS component used as the root), it falls under case #1 above and gets <code>display:contents</code> automatically.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Headfull FS component with <code>position: sticky</code> on an inner element sticks correctly on scroll</li>\n' +
      '<li>Multi-child headless instance inside a flex/grid parent — children participate in parent layout</li>\n' +
      '<li>Hydration still works — interactive refs inside wrapped components respond to events</li>\n' +
      '<li>Coordinate-based adoption works — dynamic content updates correctly</li>\n' +
      '<li>Existing style attributes on <code>&lt;jay:Name&gt;</code> tags are not clobbered (check if any exist)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p>Can <code>&lt;jay:Name&gt;</code> tags have user-specified <code>style</code> attributes that we&#39;d overwrite? If so, we need to merge rather than replace.\n' +
      '<strong>Answer:</strong> Grep shows no <code>&lt;jay:...</code> tags with <code>style=</code> in the codebase. Since <code>&lt;jay:Name&gt;</code> tags are component insertion points (not regular HTML), users don&#39;t style them directly. Safe to use <code>setAttribute(&#39;style&#39;, ...)</code> without merging.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p>Does <code>adoptElement</code> in the runtime support a <code>style</code> property in the attributes object? Need to verify the runtime API.\n' +
      '<strong>Answer:</strong> <code>adoptBase</code> (hydrate.ts:176-197) only processes dynamic attributes (objects with <code>valueFunc</code>). Static string attributes are ignored — the element already exists in the DOM from SSR with the correct style. No hydrate target change needed.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Display Contents For Wrapper Elements","number":135}'
  }
}
