{
  post: {
    title: 'LoadParams Route Context',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #136 — loadParams Route Deduplication</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> May 14, 2026\n' +
      '<strong>Status:</strong> Implementing\n' +
      '<strong>Related:</strong> #134a (build pipeline), #130 (plugin routes)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p><code>loadParams</code> is a component method that enumerates all param combinations for a dynamic route at build time. Its current signature:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">type LoadParams<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>Services<span class="token punctuation">,</span> Params<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>contexts<span class="token operator">:</span> Services<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> AsyncIterable<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>Params<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>It receives resolved services but <strong>no information about the route it&#39;s being called for</strong>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Problem 1: Duplicate builds across routes sharing a component</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In the golf project, <code>wix-stores</code> product-page component is used by two route trees:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">/kitan/products/[category]/[slug]     inferredParams: { prefix: &quot;kitan&quot; }\n' +
      '/polgat/products/[category]/[slug]    inferredParams: { prefix: &quot;polgat&quot; }</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Both routes share the same <code>loadParams</code>. The build runs it twice (once per route), and merges <code>inferredParams</code> via <code>Object.assign</code> — overwriting each product&#39;s own <code>prefix</code>. Every product is built twice under the wrong prefix.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Problem 2: Static override duplication</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">/products/[slug]              ← dynamic, loadParams returns all products\n' +
      '/products/ceramic-flower-vase ← static override, inferredParams: { slug: &quot;ceramic-flower-vase&quot; }</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The dynamic route&#39;s <code>loadParams</code> also returns <code>ceramic-flower-vase</code>, so it&#39;s built twice.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Problem 3: Cross-product of multiple loadParams</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When a route has two headless components each with <code>loadParams</code> (e.g., i18n providing <code>lang</code> and product-page providing <code>slug</code>), the current code concatenates results instead of computing the cross product.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Approach: Materialize → Dedupe → Build</h3>\n' +
      '<p>No API changes. Three pipeline steps, each a pure testable function:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Step 1 — Collect unique <code>loadParams</code> and run each once</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>Multiple routes may reference the same headless component with <code>loadParams</code> (by function identity). Run each unique <code>loadParams</code> once and cache the results. When a route has multiple parts with <code>loadParams</code> providing disjoint param keys, compute the cross product.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Step 2 — Materialize URLs</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>For each route, generate all <code>(url, params, route)</code> tuples:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Static routes</strong> (no dynamic segments, has <code>inferredParams</code>): one tuple from the inferred params</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Dynamic routes</strong>: for each cached <code>loadParams</code> result compatible with the route&#39;s <code>inferredParams</code>, generate a tuple. Compatibility = all <code>inferredParams</code> keys match the result&#39;s values.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>This naturally splits kitan/polgat — a product with <code>prefix: &quot;polgat&quot;</code> is incompatible with the kitan route&#39;s <code>inferredParams: { prefix: &quot;kitan&quot; }</code>, so it only materializes under polgat.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Step 3 — Dedupe by URL</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>When multiple routes produce the same URL, the most specific route wins:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>More <code>inferredParams</code> keys = more specific</li>\n' +
      '<li>Fewer dynamic segments = more specific</li>\n' +
      '<li>Static override &gt; dynamic route</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Step 4 — Build the deduplicated list</strong></p>\n' +
      '<h3>Example</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Routes:\n' +
      '  /kitan/products/[category]/[slug]    inferredParams: { prefix: &quot;kitan&quot; }\n' +
      '  /polgat/products/[category]/[slug]   inferredParams: { prefix: &quot;polgat&quot; }\n' +
      '  /products/ceramic-flower-vase        inferredParams: { slug: &quot;ceramic-flower-vase&quot; } (static)\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Step 1: Run loadParams ONCE → 3800 products with { slug, category, prefix }\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Step 2: Materialize:\n' +
      '  static override → (&quot;/products/ceramic-flower-vase&quot;, { slug: &quot;ceramic-flower-vase&quot; })\n' +
      '  kitan route + params where prefix=&quot;kitan&quot; → 1900 tuples\n' +
      '  polgat route + params where prefix=&quot;polgat&quot; → 1900 tuples\n' +
      "  (products with prefix=&quot;kitan&quot; don't materialize under polgat — incompatible)\n" +
      '\n' +
      'Step 3: Dedupe:\n' +
      '  ceramic-flower-vase appears twice (static + dynamic) → static wins\n' +
      '  No other duplicates\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Step 4: Build 1 + 1900 + 1900 - 1 = 3800 instances (not 7600)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Testable Functions</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>1. <code>collectLoadParams(routes, loadParamsFn) → Map&lt;route, params[]&gt;</code></strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>Runs each unique <code>loadParams</code> once (deduped by identity). Cross-products params from multiple parts on the same route. Returns cached results per route.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Input: routes with their loadParams function references</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Output: map of route → all param combinations</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Mockable: loadParamsFn is injected, not imported</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>2. <code>materializeRouteParams(routes, loadParamsResults) → MaterializedEntry[]</code></strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>For each route, generates <code>{ url, params, route, specificity }</code> tuples. Filters by <code>inferredParams</code> compatibility. Includes static override routes.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Test: dynamic route + matching params → materialized</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Test: dynamic route + incompatible inferredParams → filtered out</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Test: static override → one entry</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Test: route without loadParams or inferredParams → one entry with empty params</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>3. <code>dedupeByUrl(entries) → MaterializedEntry[]</code></strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>Groups by URL, picks most specific route per URL.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Test: unique URLs → pass through</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Test: same URL from static + dynamic → static wins</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Test: same URL from specific + catch-all → specific wins</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Each function is pure — takes data in, returns data out. No filesystem, no Vite, no services.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Cross-Product</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When a route has multiple parts with <code>loadParams</code> providing disjoint keys:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Route: /[lang]/products/[slug]\n' +
      'Part A (i18n):    yields [{ lang: &quot;en&quot; }, { lang: &quot;fr&quot; }]\n' +
      'Part B (products): yields [{ slug: &quot;shirt&quot; }, { slug: &quot;hat&quot; }]\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Cross product → [\n' +
      '  { lang: &quot;en&quot;, slug: &quot;shirt&quot; },\n' +
      '  { lang: &quot;en&quot;, slug: &quot;hat&quot; },\n' +
      '  { lang: &quot;fr&quot;, slug: &quot;shirt&quot; },\n' +
      '  { lang: &quot;fr&quot;, slug: &quot;hat&quot; },\n' +
      ']</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>If two parts provide overlapping keys, warn and use the first provider&#39;s value.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>What Stays the Same</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>LoadParams</code> type signature — unchanged</li>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin <code>loadParams</code> implementations — unchanged</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>runLoadParams</code> in <code>stack-server-runtime</code> — unchanged</li>\n' +
      '<li>Dev server — doesn&#39;t use <code>loadParams</code> at all</li>\n' +
      '<li>Agent-kit docs — unchanged</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Optional Segment Defaults</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When a route has an optional segment (<code>[[category]]</code>) and declares an inferred param for it, the inferred value is a <strong>default</strong>, not a filter.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Route: /polgat/products/[[category]]\n' +
      'jay-params:\n' +
      '  prefix: polgat\n' +
      '  category: polgat      ← default value for the optional segment</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Filtering:</strong> Inferred params for required segments (like <code>prefix</code>) are strict filters — <code>loadParams</code> results must include the key with a matching value. Inferred params for optional segments (like <code>category</code>) are skipped during filtering — all values pass.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>URL building:</strong> When an optional segment&#39;s param value equals its inferred default, the segment is omitted from the URL:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>{ prefix: &quot;polgat&quot;, category: &quot;shoes&quot; }</code> → <code>/polgat/products/shoes</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>{ prefix: &quot;polgat&quot;, category: &quot;polgat&quot; }</code> → <code>/polgat/products</code> (category matches default → omitted)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Param merging:</strong> <code>loadParams</code> values take precedence. Inferred params only fill in keys not provided by <code>loadParams</code>. This prevents the inferred <code>category: &quot;polgat&quot;</code> from overwriting <code>category: &quot;shoes&quot;</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Plugin requirement:</strong> <code>loadParams</code> must return the inferred default value as one of its entries to build the root page. E.g., <code>loadSearchParams</code> must yield <code>{ prefix: &quot;polgat&quot;, category: &quot;polgat&quot; }</code> to produce <code>/polgat/pr'... 1520 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"LoadParams Route Context","number":136}'
  }
}
[Build] 57/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=136-loadparams-route-context)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Headfull Component Stripping In Pre-Rendered Jay-Html',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #137 — Production Build Self-Containment</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>When deploying to production (Docker/Cloud Run), only <code>build/</code>, <code>config/</code>, and <code>node_modules/</code> are in the container — no source files (<code>src/</code>). The production server fails in multiple places because it tries to read source files that don&#39;t exist. The build output should be fully self-contained.</p>\n' +
      '<p>DL#134b states the main server&#39;s design principle: <strong>no compilation at runtime, all code is pre-compiled JS</strong>. The &quot;What the Main Server Does NOT Do&quot; section explicitly excludes dynamic contract materialization and compilation. Yet the current serve-time code violates this by re-parsing jay-html and loading contracts from source files.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Related Design Logs</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>#134 — Production build (two-server architecture, artifact directory as contract)</li>\n' +
      '<li>#134b — Main server (stateless request handling, pre-built artifacts only)</li>\n' +
      '<li>#111 — Nested headfull full-stack components (template injection, headless pipeline)</li>\n' +
      '<li>#123 — Deeply nested headfull and headless components (recursive hoisting)</li>\n' +
      '<li>#94 — SSR streaming renderer (server element compilation)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The production server requires source files that don&#39;t exist in the container. Four gaps were discovered during Cloud Run deployment of the golf project.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Root Cause</h3>\n' +
      '<p>All four gaps stem from one root cause: <strong>the production server re-parses jay-html at serve time</strong>. <code>loadProductionPageParts</code> calls <code>parseJayFile</code> and <code>injectHeadfullFSTemplates</code> to discover headless imports, load contracts, and resolve component modules — work that was already done at build time. This triggers file reads against source paths that don&#39;t exist in the container.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The fix is to <strong>pre-compute the page configuration at build time</strong> and load it directly at serve time, eliminating jay-html parsing entirely.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 1: Headfull component source files (ENOENT)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Two serve-time operations try to read headfull component source files:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>parseJayFile</code></strong> (load-production-parts.ts:61) encounters <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headfull&quot; src=&quot;../../components/header&quot;&gt;</code> and calls <code>importResolver.readJayHtml()</code> — fails with ENOENT</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>injectHeadfullFSTemplates</code></strong> (load-production-parts.ts:154) also reads the same source file — fails with ENOENT</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Subtlety: <strong>headfull components can declare children</strong> that are also needed at serve time:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Nested headfull components</strong> (DL#123 Scenario B) — headfull A contains headfull B</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Keyed headless components</strong> — headfull component imports a plugin with a <code>key</code> attribute for page-level data binding</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Instance headless components</strong> — headfull component imports a plugin used as <code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code> instances</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>All three types are hoisted into the page&#39;s <code>headlessImports</code> during <code>parseHeadfullFSImports</code>, but only in memory — not persisted in the pre-rendered HTML.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 2: CSS files referenced by headfull components (ENOENT)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>parseJayFile</code> resolves CSS <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> tags from headfull components&#39; jay-html against source paths. The CSS is already compiled into the build output. This gap goes away when we stop parsing jay-html at serve time.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 3: Materialized contracts needed at serve time (ENOENT)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>parseJayFile</code> → <code>parseHeadlessImports</code> calls <code>importResolver.loadPluginContract()</code> to load contracts at serve time. For NPM plugins, contracts resolve from <code>node_modules</code> (fine). For materialized contracts, the resolver looks in <code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code> (doesn&#39;t exist in container). This gap goes away when we stop parsing jay-html at serve time — the contract data needed for fast rendering is pre-computed.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Gap 4: Absolute paths in route manifest</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>route-manifest.json</code> bakes in the build machine&#39;s absolute path as <code>projectRoot</code>. The production server passes this to <code>scanPlugins()</code> and <code>loadProductionPageParts</code>. Inside the container, that path doesn&#39;t exist.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: After slow rendering and template injection, is a headfull component semantically equivalent to a headless component?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Yes. At that point:</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Contribution</th>\n' +
      '<th>Where it lives after slow rendering</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Template content</td>\n' +
      '<td>Inlined in <code>&lt;jay:Name&gt;</code> tags in the body</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Slow-phase bindings</td>\n' +
      '<td>Resolved into static HTML</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Component module</td>\n' +
      '<td>Referenced by compiled server-element/hydrate output</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>What remains is a component with a contract, a module, and <code>&lt;jay:Name&gt;</code> instances — exactly what a headless component is. The <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headfull&quot;&gt;</code> tag is leftover metadata.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: Why does the production server parse jay-html at serve time?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>It shouldn&#39;t. <code>loadProductionPageParts</code> calls <code>parseJayFile</code> to produce <code>ProductionPageParts</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-ts">interface ProductionPageParts <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  parts<span class="token operator">:</span> DevServerPagePart<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// page + keyed headless component definitions</span>\n' +
      '  headlessContracts<span class="token operator">:</span> HeadlessContractInfo<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// build-time only (for slowRenderTransform)</span>\n' +
      '  headlessInstanceComponents<span class="token operator">:</span> HeadlessInstanceComponent<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// instance component definitions</span>\n' +
      '  discoveredInstances<span class="token operator">:</span> DiscoveredHeadlessInstance<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// build-time only (for slow render)</span>\n' +
      '  forEachInstances<span class="token operator">:</span> ForEachHeadlessInstance<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// forEach instance metadata</span>\n' +
      '  keyedPartModules<span class="token operator">:</span> KeyedPartModule<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// build-time only (for hydration entry)</span>\n' +
      '  serverTrackByMap<span class="token operator">?:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// build-time only</span>\n' +
      '  clientTrackByMap<span class="token operator">?:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// build-time only</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>At serve time, <code>handlePageRequest</code> only uses a subset: <code>parts</code>, <code>headlessInstanceComponents</code>, and <code>forEachInstances</code>. All of these are known at build time.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: What does <code>renderFastChangingData</code> actually need from each component?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Traced through <code>fast-changing-runner.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>From <code>parts</code> (page + keyed headless):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
