[Build] 58/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=137-headfull-component-stripping-in-pre-rendered-jay-html)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Safe Refs Stubs For Unused Contract Refs',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #138 — Safe Ref Stubs for Unused Contract Refs</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>A headless component&#39;s contract declares refs (e.g., <code>addToCartButton</code>, <code>productImage</code>, <code>wishlistButton</code>). The component code uses these refs to wire up interactivity. But the actual template is written by the page designer, who may not include all declared refs — a minimal product card template might only use <code>productImage</code> and skip <code>addToCartButton</code> entirely.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, accessing a ref not present in the template returns <code>undefined</code>, causing a runtime crash:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In plugin component code (shared across many templates)</span>\n' +
      'refs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>addToCartButton<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">onclick</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> coordinate <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token comment">// TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'onclick')</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>The workaround is optional chaining (<code>refs.addToCartButton?.onclick(...)</code>), but this is fragile — every ref access in every shared utility must remember to use <code>?.</code>, and TypeScript won&#39;t warn about missing <code>?.</code> since the type says the ref exists.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Related Design Logs</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>#84 — Headless component props and repeater support</li>\n' +
      '<li>#111 — Nested headfull full-stack components</li>\n' +
      '<li>#123 — Deeply nested headfull and headless components</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>There are two kinds of &quot;missing ref&quot; at runtime:</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Scenario</th>\n' +
      '<th>Ref object</th>\n' +
      '<th>Behavior</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Ref in template, element conditionally hidden (<code>if=&quot;false&quot;</code>)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Proxy exists</td>\n' +
      '<td>Safe — listeners accumulate, auto-attach when element renders</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Ref in contract but not in template at all</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>undefined</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Crash on any property access</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>The inconsistency is the problem. A conditional ref is safe because <code>ReferencesManager.for()</code> creates an entry for it (the element just has no target yet). A missing ref is <code>undefined</code> because <code>ReferencesManager.for()</code> only receives refs that appear in the template — the compiler scans <code>ref=&quot;...&quot;</code> attributes, not the contract.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This matters specifically for <strong>instance-based headless components</strong> (<code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code> tags with inline templates):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Instance headless components</strong> — the inline template is written by the page designer per-page, who may use only a subset of the contract&#39;s refs. The plugin&#39;s component code expects all contract refs to exist.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Repeated instances (forEach)</strong> — same problem, but with collection refs. A <code>&lt;jay:product-card&gt;</code> inside <code>forEach=&quot;products&quot;</code> declares <code>ProductCardRepeatedRefs</code> with collection proxies for each ref, but the template may only use <code>ref=&quot;products.productLink&quot;</code> and skip <code>ref=&quot;products.addToCartButton&quot;</code>.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Headfull components with headless instances</strong> — a headfull component&#39;s template includes <code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code> instances where the same mismatch occurs.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Keyed headless components</strong> (with <code>key=&quot;...&quot;</code> in the <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tag) are NOT affected — even though they also use the page template (not their own), the compiler already handles this correctly. <code>processImportedHeadless()</code> adds ALL contract refs to the page&#39;s ref tree, and <code>optimizeRefs()</code> preserves them in the <code>ReferencesManager.for()</code> call regardless of whether they appear in the template. The <code>autoRef</code> flag only controls TypeScript type generation, not runtime ref creation. This is effectively the same fix that this design log proposes for inline instances.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Real-world example (golf project)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>related-products</code> headless component contract declares 6 refs in <code>ProductCardRepeatedRefs</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>productLink</code>, <code>addToCartButton</code>, <code>cardContainer</code>, <code>viewOptionsButton</code>, <code>quickOption</code>, <code>secondQuickOption</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>But the page&#39;s inline template only provides <code>ref=&quot;products.productLink&quot;</code>. The shared <code>setupCardInteractions()</code> utility accesses all 5 missing refs — currently guarded with <code>?.</code> everywhere, which is fragile and verbose.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Approach: contract-aware ref stubs in ReferencesManager</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When a contract declares refs, ALL declared ref names should have entries in the refs object — not just those matched by <code>ref=&quot;...&quot;</code> in the template. Refs without a template match behave like conditional refs with no target: a proxy exists, method calls are no-ops, listeners accumulate (and would auto-attach if the ref were ever populated, though in this case it won&#39;t be).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Where to create stubs</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>ReferencesManager.for()</code> call is generated by the compiler. It receives arrays of ref names extracted from the template:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Generated by compiler (only refs found in template)</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>refManager<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>productImageRef<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> ReferencesManager<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token keyword">for</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  options<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'productImage'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// Only this ref is in the template</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>But the contract declares <code>productImage</code>, <code>addToCartButton</code>, <code>wishlistButton</code>. The component receives <code>refs</code> from <code>refManager.getPublicAPI()</code>, which only has <code>productImage</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Fix: pass contract ref names to <code>ReferencesManager.for()</code></strong> so it can create stub entries for all declared refs, not just template-matched ones.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">const</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>refManager<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>productImageRef<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> ReferencesManager<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token keyword">for</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  options<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'productImage'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">undefined</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// childRefManagers</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'productImage'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'addToCartButton'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'wishlistButton'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// contract ref names</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>For any contract ref name not in the template ref arrays, <code>ReferencesManager</code> creates a stub <code>PrivateRef</code> that:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Has an <code>HTMLElementProxy</code> public API (same type as a real ref)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Has no element target (same as a conditional ref that hasn&#39;t rendered)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Accepts event listener registration (listeners accu'... 12936 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Safe Refs Stubs For Unused Contract Refs","number":138}'
  }
}
