{
  post: {
    title: 'Wix Deployment Separation',
    content: '<h1>DL#139: Wix Deployment — Build Separation &amp; Fetch Handler Package</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The production server (DL#134b) currently uses Node.js <code>http.createServer</code> with <code>IncomingMessage</code>/<code>ServerResponse</code>. All build artifacts live in a single <code>build/v{n}/</code> folder. For Wix backend-as-a-service deployment:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>The runtime calls a <strong>fetch function</strong> (<code>(Request) → Response</code>) exported from a module — similar to how <code>@wix/runtime-fetch-adapter</code> wraps Astro for BaaS (see <code>tmp/cloud-runtime-baas/packages/wix-runtime-fetch-adapter</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Frontend assets</strong> (JS, CSS, images) are uploaded to <strong>Wix statics CDN</strong> — they don&#39;t live on the server</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Backend artifacts</strong> (server modules, pre-rendered HTML, manifests) stay on the server</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The public folder (<code>./public</code> in project root) contains media files (images, fonts, etc.) and is currently only served by the dev server — the production build ignores it.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p>The main server uses <code>node:http</code> types (<code>IncomingMessage</code>, <code>ServerResponse</code>) throughout all handlers. The serve-time API should be a standard <code>fetch(request: Request): Response</code> function exported from a module — the same interface used by BaaS runtimes, Cloudflare Workers, and other platforms. The HTTP server is just one consumer of this function.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p>Build artifacts are interleaved in one folder. The browser-facing files (<code>shared/</code> chunks, instance <code>.js</code> bundles, <code>.css</code> files) must be separated from server-only files (<code>server/</code> modules, <code>pre-rendered/</code> HTML + cache + server-elements, manifests) so frontend assets can be uploaded to CDN independently.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p>The <code>public/</code> folder contents need to be included in the frontend output.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Should we use Node.js native <code>Request</code>/<code>Response</code> (available since Node 18) or a polyfill?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A1: Node 18+ has native Web API support. Since we require Node &gt;= 20, we can use native <code>Request</code>/<code>Response</code>/<code>ReadableStream</code> directly. No polyfill needed.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: How should streaming SSR work with Fetch API <code>Response</code>?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A2: Use <code>new Response(ReadableStream)</code> with a <code>TransformStream</code> or manual <code>ReadableStream</code> controller. The current <code>res.write()</code> calls become <code>controller.enqueue()</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: Should the build produce two separate root folders or two subfolders?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A3: Subfolders under <code>build/v{n}/</code> — <code>frontend/</code> and <code>backend/</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q4: Should the route manifest live in both folders or just backend?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A4: Just backend. The manifest is only consumed by the server. The CDN folder is dumb static hosting.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q5: What about <code>pre-rendered/</code> files — some are server-only (jay-html, cache.json, server-element.js) and some are browser-facing (instance .js bundles, .css)?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A5: Currently each instance produces these files in the same directory:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>page_{hash}.jay-html</code> → backend</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>page_{hash}.cache.json</code> → backend</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>page_{hash}.server-element.js</code> → backend</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>page_{hash}-{viteHash}.js</code> → frontend</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>page_{hash}.css</code> → frontend</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The build pipeline needs to write these to different output trees.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q6: Do we need to handle the public folder during rebuilds (slow render server)?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A6: No. Public folder contents are static project assets — they don&#39;t change during data invalidation rebuilds. They&#39;re only copied during the initial build.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q7: How does the main server currently serve static files, and what changes?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A7: Currently <code>handleStaticRequest</code> serves <code>shared/</code> and <code>pre-rendered/</code> files from the build folder via filesystem. After separation, static file serving becomes optional — controlled by whether <code>frontendDir</code> is passed to the fetch handler. When provided, the handler serves static files from <code>frontend/</code> (for local/standalone deployments). When omitted, all browser-facing URLs use the CDN base path via <code>staticBaseUrl</code>. This way the same fetch handler works for Wix BaaS deployment, standalone, and local testing.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q8: What about the import map URLs — they currently point to <code>/shared/filename.js</code>?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A8: They need to point to the CDN URL. Currently <code>publicBasePath</code> in the manifest is hardcoded to <code>/</code>. After this change, <code>publicBasePath</code> is removed from the manifest — the fetch handler receives <code>staticBaseUrl</code> as a creation-time option and prepends it when generating import maps, CSS links, and script tags. The import map builder and link generation keep the same logic, but read the base URL from the handler options instead of the manifest.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Fetch Handler Package</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A new package <code>@jay-framework/jay-fetch-handler</code> that exports a <code>fetch(request: Request) → Promise&lt;Response&gt;</code> function. This is the primary serve-time API — not an HTTP server.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The package:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Imports internals from <code>@jay-framework/production-server</code> (artifact store, route matcher, page handler, action handler)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Composes them into a single fetch function</li>\n' +
      '<li>Is consumed directly by BaaS runtimes (Wix, Cloudflare) or wrapped in an HTTP server by <code>jay-stack serve</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n' +
      '│  BaaS runtime / jay-stack serve                     │\n' +
      '│                                                     │\n' +
      '│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n' +
      '│  │  @jay-framework/jay-fetch-handler             │  │\n' +
      '│  │  createJayFetchHandler(options) → fetch        │  │\n' +
      '│  │                                               │  │\n' +
      '│  │  (Request) → Response                         │  │\n' +
      '│  │  • page requests → SSR streaming              │  │\n' +
      '│  │  • actions → JSON responses                   │  │\n' +
      '│  │  • static files (optional) → from frontend/   │  │\n' +
      '│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n' +
      '└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Package API:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface JayFetchHandlerOptions <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  backendDir<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      `  staticBaseUrl<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// defaults to '/'</span>\n` +
      '  frontendDir<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// when set, serves static files from this dir</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">createJayFetchHandler</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  options<span class="token operator">:</span> JayFetchHandlerOptions<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>request<span class="token operator">:</span> Request<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>Response<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Usage — Wix BaaS deployment:</strong></p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> createJayFetchHandler <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/jay-fetch-handler'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> handler <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">createJayFetchHandler</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  backendDir<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'./build/v1/backend'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `  staticBaseUrl<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'https://static.parastorage.com/services/jay-app/1.0.0/'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">default</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> fetch<span class="token operator">:</span> handler <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Usage — self-hosted (jay-stack serve):</strong></p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> createJayFetchHandler <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/jay-fetch-handler'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token keywor'... 35159 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Wix Deployment Separation","number":139}'
  }
}
