{
  post: {
    title: 'References API',
    content: '<h1>Reference API</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>References are used by components to reference internal <code>JayElements</code> and <code>JayComponents</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The consideration with the API are</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Elements may be in the main window, while the component in a worker sandbox. This implies that\n' +
      'we cannot have direct references to DOM elements, but we can have direct reference to components</li>\n' +
      '<li>internal elements and components can be single or a dynamic list</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>The proposed API:</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Shared Declarations for Elements:</h2>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> type JeyEventHandler<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>viewState<span class="token operator">:</span> ViewState<span class="token punctuation">,</span> coordinate<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token keyword">void</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
