[Build] 63/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=141-fast-phase-request-context)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Plugin Cli Commands',
    content: '<h1>DL#142: Plugin CLI Commands</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins need to run administrative operations that don&#39;t belong in the rendering pipeline or the dev server request cycle. Example: a media plugin that uploads files from the project&#39;s <code>public/</code> folder to Wix Media, or a stores plugin that syncs product data from an external CMS.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Today plugins can declare:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Services</strong> — initialized at startup, available to components and actions</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Actions</strong> — request-scoped server functions (<code>makeJayAction</code>/<code>makeJayQuery</code>) for client-server communication</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Setup handlers</strong> — run via <code>jay-stack setup</code>, create config files, validate credentials (DL#87)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>References</strong> — run via <code>jay-stack agent-kit</code>, generate discovery data for AI agents (DL#87)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>None of these fit &quot;upload media files&quot; or &quot;sync products&quot;:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Actions are request-response — they need a running server and an HTTP caller</li>\n' +
      '<li>Setup handlers are for config creation and validation, not arbitrary operations</li>\n' +
      '<li>References are for generating data files, not side effects</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>There&#39;s no mechanism for a plugin to expose a CLI command that:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Runs as a one-shot terminal operation (not a server endpoint)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Has access to initialized services (e.g., Wix Media API client)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Can accept arguments (e.g., folder path, flags)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Can show progress and output in the terminal</li>\n' +
      '<li>Is discoverable — the user knows what commands are available</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Use cases</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Media upload</strong>: <code>jay-stack run media/upload-public</code> — uploads all files from <code>public/</code> to Wix Media, returns a URL mapping</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Product sync</strong>: <code>jay-stack run stores/sync-catalog</code> — pulls product data from external CMS into local reference files</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Schema migration</strong>: <code>jay-stack run data/migrate --dry-run</code> — runs database migrations declared by a plugin</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Cache clear</strong>: <code>jay-stack run cdn/purge --all</code> — purges CDN cache for the site</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Cloud deployment</strong>: <code>jay-stack run wix/deploy --env production</code> — deploys the built application to a cloud provider (uploads frontend to CDN, pushes backend container, runs health checks)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Should this be a new CLI command or extend an existing one?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A1: New subcommand <code>jay-stack run &lt;plugin&gt;/&lt;command&gt;</code>. This parallels the existing <code>jay-stack action &lt;plugin&gt;/&lt;action&gt;</code> pattern but makes the distinction clear: actions are HTTP endpoints, commands are CLI operations. The <code>run</code> verb communicates &quot;execute this thing once.&quot;</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: Should commands be declared in plugin.yaml or auto-discovered?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A2: Declared in <code>plugin.yaml</code>. This is consistent with how actions, services, webhooks, and setup handlers are declared. Explicit declaration provides discoverability (<code>jay-stack run --list</code>) and documentation (description field).</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: Should command handlers get the same context as setup handlers?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A3: Similar but not identical. Commands need services (like setup), but they also need typed input parsed from CLI arguments, and they don&#39;t need configDir. The handler uses a <code>makeCliCommand</code> builder with <code>.withServices()</code>, just like <code>makeJayAction</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q4: How do commands declare their arguments?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A4: In a <code>.jay-command</code> YAML file (same pattern as <code>.jay-action</code>). The file declares <code>inputSchema</code> with typed parameters. The CLI reads the schema and auto-generates commander flags — <code>--folder &lt;string&gt;</code>, <code>--dry-run</code> (boolean), etc. This means the CLI natively validates and parses arguments before calling the handler. No raw passthrough needed.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q5: Should commands run in a Vite context (for TypeScript loading)?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A5: Yes. Same as <code>jay-stack setup</code> and <code>jay-stack action</code> — the handler module is loaded via <code>viteServer.ssrLoadModule()</code> so plugins can be authored in TypeScript. Services are initialized the same way.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q6: How does this relate to dev-time actions?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A6: They&#39;re complementary. A dev-time action would be an HTTP endpoint available only during <code>jay-stack dev</code> — useful for UI-driven admin tools (editor panels, dashboards). A CLI command is for terminal-driven batch operations. Both have access to services. This design log covers CLI commands only. Dev-time actions can be added later if needed, likely as a <code>scope: dev</code> flag on <code>makeJayAction</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q7: Should commands have access to the project&#39;s public folder path?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A7: Yes. The <code>publicFolder</code> path (from project config or default <code>./public</code>) should be in the context. The media upload use case needs this directly.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q8: Can a command return structured data (like actions do)?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A8: Yes. The handler returns a result object. The CLI renders it as JSON or YAML (with <code>--yaml</code> flag), same as <code>jay-stack action</code>. For progress output during execution, the handler uses the logger directly.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Console context service</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A framework-provided service that gives CLI commands access to project info and a logger. Commands request it via <code>.withServices()</code> like any other service:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> createJayService <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/fullstack-component'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> interface ConsoleContext <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  projectRoot<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  publicFolder<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  build<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    frontend<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    backend<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  verbose<span class="token operator">:</span> boolean<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  log<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>message<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token keyword">void</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  warn<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>message<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token keyword">void</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  error<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>message<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token keyword">void</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">const</span> CONSOLE_CONTEXT <span class="token operator">=</span> createJayService<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ConsoleContext<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'ConsoleContext'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>The CLI registers this service before executing the command. Commands that don&#39;t need project info simply don&#39;t request it.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>2. <code>makeCliCommand</code> builder</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Follows the same builder pattern as <code>makeJayAction</code> — declares services, accepts typed input, returns success/failure:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> makeCliCommand <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/fullstack-component'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> MEDIA_SERVICE <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./services'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> CONSOLE_CONTEXT <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/fullstack-component'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">const</span> uploadPublic <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">makeCliCommand</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'upload-public'</span><sp`... 25234 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Plugin Cli Commands","number":142}'
  }
}
[Build] 64/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=142-plugin-cli-commands)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Ui-Kit-Add-Menu-Contribution',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #142 — ui-kit Add Menu contribution</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Status</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Done (U1–U3)</strong> — 2026-06-02. Parent: <a href="../../jay-aiditor/design-log/19%20-%20aiditor-add-menu">jay-aiditor #19</a>. <strong>Does not block</strong> M19.1 (aiditor + wix-stores).</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> ui-kit lives in <strong>jay</strong> monorepo (<code>packages/plugins/ui-kit</code>), not wix. <strong>wix-media out of scope.</strong></p>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Numbering:</strong> <strong>#142</strong> avoids collision with jay <strong>#134</strong> (production build) and <strong>#134a–d</strong>.</p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Release coordination</h2>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Package</th>\n' +
      '<th>M19.1 coupling</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>@jay-framework/aiditor</code> + <code>@jay-framework/wix-stores</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Ship together for Add Menu smoke</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>@jay-framework/ui-kit</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Independent; after M19.1 scanner (aiditor A2)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design log <strong>#132</strong> introduced <code>@jay-framework/ui-kit</code> headless primitives. AIditor Add Menu (#19) lets users attach <strong>prompt fragments</strong> at request time. ui-kit has <strong>no <code>setup</code> handler today</strong> — must add one to write <code>agent-kit/aiditor/add-menu/ui-kit.yaml</code> per the AIditor agreement.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>ui-kit is invisible in Add Menu until a project yaml exists.</li>\n' +
      '<li>Designers cannot attach structured catalog items for scroll-carousel, popover-menu, etc.</li>\n' +
      '<li>Effect/skill-style items in #19 examples need a pattern: static items + optional skill markdown referenced from <code>prompt</code> (U4 defer).</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Output path (locked by aiditor #19)</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">&lt;project&gt;/agent-kit/aiditor/add-menu/ui-kit.yaml</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Items — M19.3 v1 (all static contracts)</h3>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Contract</th>\n' +
      '<th><code>id</code></th>\n' +
      '<th><code>category</code> / <code>subCategory</code></th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>popover-menu</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>ui-kit:popover-menu</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>UI Kit / Components</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>scroll-carousel</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>ui-kit:scroll-carousel</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>UI Kit / Components</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>clipboard-copy</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>ui-kit:clipboard-copy</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>UI Kit / Components</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>word-split</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>ui-kit:word-split</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>UI Kit / Typography</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>letter-split</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>ui-kit:letter-split</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>UI Kit / Typography</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>No URL <code>params:</code> on typical ui-kit contracts → no Q8 route UI for these items.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Setup handler (new)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Register <code>setupUiKit</code> in <code>plugin.yaml</code>; export from <code>lib/index.ts</code> for stack-cli (jay #87 pattern).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Cross-repo test validation (locked)</h2>\n' +
      '<p>ui-kit and aiditor are <strong>separate packages</strong>. <strong>Do not</strong> import <code>@jay-framework/aiditor</code> validator in ui-kit tests.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Approach (same as wix #20 W2):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Canonical shape: <code>jay-aiditor/packages/aiditor/test/fixtures/add-menu/valid-item.yaml</code> (committed in aiditor repo).</li>\n' +
      '<li>ui-kit tests: after setup, parse written <code>ui-kit.yaml</code> and assert each item has required keys (<code>id</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>category</code>, <code>prompt</code>) and <strong>lacks</strong> rejected keys (<code>kind</code>, <code>parameters</code>, <code>component</code>, <code>allowedScopes</code>) via inline checks or duplicated ~20-line helper in ui-kit test — <strong>no cross-repo import</strong>.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation plan</h2>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>ID</th>\n' +
      '<th>Deliverable</th>\n' +
      '<th>Priority</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>U1</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>setupUiKit</code> + plugin.yaml registration</td>\n' +
      '<td>P0</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>U2</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>add-menu.template.yaml</code> with 5 contract items</td>\n' +
      '<td>P0</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>U3</td>\n' +
