{
  post: {
    title: 'Artifact Store Abstraction For BaaS',
    content: '<h1>DL#143: Artifact Store Abstraction for BaaS Deployment</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The production server (DL#134b, DL#139) uses <code>FilesystemArtifactStore</code> to read build artifacts — manifests, pre-rendered HTML, server elements, page modules. The fetch handler (<code>createJayFetchHandler</code> in <code>@jay-framework/jay-fetch-handler</code>) creates this store from a <code>backendDir</code> path and passes it through the serve pipeline.</p>\n' +
      '<p>For Wix BaaS deployment, the entry file (<code>entry.mjs</code>) runs in a container where backend files are not on the local filesystem — they&#39;re stored in Wix data collections and fetched on demand, cached to <code>/tmp</code>. The current architecture assumes filesystem everywhere: <code>fs.readFile</code>, <code>fs.stat</code> for mtime, <code>import()</code> with filesystem paths.</p>\n' +
      '<p>See Wix design log #21 (baas-entry-framework-requirements) for the full requirements from the Wix side.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Six filesystem assumptions block BaaS deployment:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><code>FilesystemArtifactStore</code> is a concrete class, not an interface — serve functions type it concretely</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>createJayFetchHandler</code> creates the store internally from <code>backendDir</code> — no way to inject a custom store</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>production-server</code> exports build-time dependencies (Vite, compilers) alongside serve functions — bundling pulls in 50+ MB of unnecessary code</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>initializeServices</code> discovers init modules from filesystem paths (<code>buildDir/server/plugins/...</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>registerActionsFromManifest</code> imports action modules from filesystem paths (<code>buildDir/serverModule</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>loadPagePartsFromConfig</code> reads <code>page-parts.json</code> and imports modules from filesystem paths</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. ArtifactStore interface</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Extract from <code>FilesystemArtifactStore</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// production-server/lib/serve/artifact-store.ts</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> interface ArtifactStore <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">readManifest</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>RouteManifest<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">readPreRenderedHtml</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>relativePath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PreRenderedEntry<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">loadServerElement</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>relativePath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ServerElementModule<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">getAssetPath</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>relativePath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">getBuildDir</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">class</span> FilesystemArtifactStore implements ArtifactStore <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Existing implementation unchanged</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// loadPageModule and readRawFile removed — unused by the serve pipeline</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Update <code>fetchPageRequest</code> and <code>getPageParts</code> to accept <code>ArtifactStore</code> (the interface) instead of <code>FilesystemArtifactStore</code> (the class):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">async</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">fetchPageRequest</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  match<span class="token operator">:</span> MatchResult<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  manifest<span class="token operator">:</span> RouteManifest<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  requestUrl<span class="token operator">:</span> URL<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  artifacts<span class="token operator">:</span> ArtifactStore<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// ← interface, not class</span>\n' +
      '  staticBaseUrl<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  cookies<span class="token operator">?:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>Response<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>2. createJayFetchHandler accepts custom ArtifactStore</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> interface JayFetchHandlerOptions <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Option A: filesystem (existing)</span>\n' +
      '  backendDir<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Option B: custom store (new)</span>\n' +
      '  artifactStore<span class="token operator">?:</span> ArtifactStore<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  staticBaseUrl<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  frontendDir<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>When <code>artifactStore</code> is provided, use it directly. When <code>backendDir</code> is provided, create <code>FilesystemArtifactStore</code> as before. Exactly one must be present.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>3. Serve-only export</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add a <code>/serve</code> entry point to production-server that re-exports only serve functions — no build-time dependencies:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-json">// production-server/package.json exports\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;.&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/index.js&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;./serve&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/serve.js&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong><code>lib/serve-index.ts</code></strong> (new entry point):</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> type <span class="token punctuation">{</span> ArtifactStore <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./serve/artifact-store'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> FilesystemArtifactStore <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./serve/artifact-store'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> fetchPageRequest <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./serve/fetch-page-handler'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  fetchActionRequest<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  isActionRequest<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  registerActionsFromManifest<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./serve/fetch-action-handler'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> fetchStaticFile <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./serve/fetch-static-handler'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> matchRequest <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./serve/route-matcher'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> initializeServices <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./shared/init-services'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> type <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  RouteManifest<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  Route'... 30959 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Artifact Store Abstraction For BaaS","number":143}'
  }
}
[Build] 66/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=143-artifact-store-abstraction-for-baas)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Per-Route Server Elements',
    content: '<h1>DL#144: Per-Route Shared Artifacts (Server Element, Hydrate Script, CSS)</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Server-element files, hydrate scripts, and CSS are compiled from jay-html templates into per-instance artifacts. For a product page with 10 SKUs, that&#39;s 10 server-element.js, 10 hydrate JS bundles, and 10 CSS files. For the golf project with 163 category/product instances, that&#39;s 489 nearly-identical files.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The problem: these files are 95%+ identical. They differ only in baked-in slow-phase data values. The template structure, bindings, and rendering logic are the same across all instances of a route.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Golf project measurements</h3>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Asset</th>\n' +
      '<th>Instances</th>\n' +
      '<th>Total Size</th>\n' +
      '<th>Actual differences</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>server-element.js</td>\n' +
      '<td>163</td>\n' +
      '<td>~18MB</td>\n' +
      '<td>Product name, options, descriptions, sizes</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>hydrate JS</td>\n' +
      '<td>163</td>\n' +
      '<td>6.8MB</td>\n' +
      '<td>Product ID, choice IDs, swatch colors</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>CSS</td>\n' +
      '<td>163</td>\n' +
      '<td>copies</td>\n' +
      '<td>Zero — all identical</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>The hydrate scripts are even more &quot;samey&quot; than the server-element files. The baked-in data (product ID, choice IDs, color codes) could trivially come from <code>cache.json</code> at hydration time.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Root cause: <code>slowForEach</code> and pre-rendering</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The current system unrolls slow-phase <code>forEach</code> at build time via <code>slowRenderTransform</code>, baking slow data values into the jay-html. This produces per-instance jay-html with:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Slow binding values resolved to literals (<code>{productName}</code> → <code>&quot;Widget A&quot;</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>forEach</code> unrolled into concrete <code>slowForEach</code> items (one element per array item)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Slow conditionals resolved (false branches removed)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>All three compilation targets (server-element, hydrate, element) then compile from this per-instance pre-rendered jay-html, producing per-instance artifacts.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Per-instance artifacts cause:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Build size bloat</strong> — 59 MB pre-rendered content in the golf project. 163 near-identical server elements (18MB) + 163 near-identical hydrate scripts (6.8MB) + 163 identical CSS copies.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Wasted V8 resources</strong> — 163 separate modules parsed and compiled per artifact type. Each function called ~1x, runs interpreted (never JIT-optimized).</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Slow BaaS cold starts</strong> — each instance requires separate file fetches from cloud storage. Hundreds of <code>import()</code> calls with I/O latency.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Slow rebuilds</strong> — when a product changes, server-element AND hydrate script AND CSS must be recompiled. With per-route artifacts, only <code>cache.json</code> needs updating.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Browser can&#39;t cache</strong> — each product page loads a unique hydrate script. Navigating between products forces a fresh parse of nearly-identical JS. A shared script would be cached after first load.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Eliminate slowForEach, compile everything from original jay-html</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Instead of pre-rendering jay-html per instance and compiling from it, compile all artifacts (server-element, hydrate script, CSS) <strong>once per route</strong> from the <strong>original jay-html</strong>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The slow render phase still runs per instance and produces <code>cache.json</code> (slowViewState + carryForward). But it no longer transforms the jay-html. The pre-rendered jay-html is eliminated as a compilation input.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Current flow (per-instance):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Build:\n' +
      '  For each instance (route + params):\n' +
      '    1. Slow render → slow ViewState\n' +
      '    2. slowRenderTransform: bake slow values, unroll forEach → pre-rendered jay-html\n' +
      '    3. Compile pre-rendered HTML → per-instance server-element.js\n' +
      '    4. Compile pre-rendered HTML → per-instance hydrate-entry.js\n' +
      '    5. Extract CSS → per-instance page.css\n' +
      '    6. Write cache.json (slowViewState, carryForward)\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Serve:\n' +
      '  1. import(instance-specific server-element.js)\n' +
      '  2. Read cache.json → get carryForward\n' +
      '  3. Fast render → fast ViewState\n' +
      '  4. Merge slow + fast ViewState\n' +
      '  5. Server-element renders fast+interactive bindings only (slow already baked)\n' +
      '  6. Client loads instance-specific hydrate script</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Proposed flow (per-route):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Build:\n' +
      '  Once per route:\n' +
      '    1. Compile original jay-html → route server-element.js (ALL bindings dynamic)\n' +
      '    2. Compile original jay-html → route hydrate-entry.js (phase-aware)\n' +
      '    3. Extract CSS → route.css\n' +
      '  For each instance (route + params):\n' +
      '    4. Slow render → slow ViewState\n' +
      '    5. Write cache.json (slowViewState, carryForward)\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Serve:\n' +
      '  1. import(route server-element.js) — cached after first load\n' +
      '  2. Read cache.json → slowViewState + carryForward\n' +
      '  3. Fast render → fast ViewState\n' +
      '  4. Merge slow + fast ViewState\n' +
      '  5. Server-element renders ALL bindings from merged ViewState\n' +
      '  6. Client loads shared hydrate script (cached across instances)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>What changes</h3>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Artifact</th>\n' +
      '<th>Current</th>\n' +
      '<th>Proposed</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>server-element.js</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Per instance, bakes slow data</td>\n' +
      '<td>Per route, all data from ViewState</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>hydrate script</td>\n' +
      '<td>Per instance, bakes slow data</td>\n' +
      '<td>Per route, phase-aware</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>CSS</td>\n' +
      '<td>Per instance (all identical)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Per route (single copy)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>cache.json</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Stores slowViewState + carryForward</td>\n' +
      '<td>Same (no change)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Pre-rendered <code>.jay-html</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Input for all compilers</td>\n' +
      '<td>Eliminated</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>slowRenderTransform</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Bakes values + unrolls forEach</td>\n' +
      '<td>No longer needed for compilation</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h3>Coordinate consistency</h3>\n' +
      '<p>With all compilers reading the same original jay-html, coordinate assignment is naturally consistent:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>assignCoordinates</code> runs on the same DOM for both server-element and hydrate</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>forEach</code> gets a single shared scope (S1) — same in SSR output and hydrate adoption</li>\n' +
      '<li>No <code>slowForEach</code> means no per-item scope divergence</li>\n' +
      '<li>No coordinate shifts from conditional removal — conditionals are runtime <code>if</code> checks</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase-aware hydrate compilation</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The hydrate compiler must become phase-aware when compiling from original jay-html:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Interactive bindings</strong> (<code>interactivePaths</code>): emit coordinates, create adoption code, wire reactive updates. This is what the hydrate compiler already does for fast+interactive bindings.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Slow/fast-only bindings</strong>: skip coordinate emission, no adoption code. The server-rendered content stays as-is in the DOM. The hydrate compiler already skips these via the <code>interactivePaths</code> check.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The hydrate compiler already has this logic — it uses <code>interactivePaths</code> (built from the contract) to decide coordinate emission. The change is that it now receives original jay-html (where slow bindings are still <code>{productName}</code>) instead of pre-rendered jay-html (where they&#39;re <code>&quot;Widget A&quot;</code>). Since slow bindings are not in <code>interactivePaths</code>, the compiler correctly ignores them.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>slowForEach → regular forEach</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Slow-phase <code>forEach</code> becomes regular <code>forEach</code> in the compiled output:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Server element: <code>for (const vs1 of vs.products) { ... }</code> — iterates at render time</li>\n' +
      '<li>Hydrate script: <code>forEach(accessor, creator, trackBy)</code> — standard forEach adoption</li>\n' +
      '<li>Element target: same <code>forEach</code> — no <code>slowForEachItem</code> needed</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>slowForEachItem</code> runtime function, <code>isSlowForEach</code> compiler handlers, and forEach unrolling in <code>slowRenderTransform</code> become dead code.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Headless instances in slow forEach</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, headless component instances inside <code>slowForEach</code> are discovered and slow-rendered during pre-rendering (Pass 2 in <code>instance-pipeline.ts</code>). With the new approach:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Headless instances inside <code>forEach</code> are discovered at build time from the original jay-html</li>\n' +
      '<li>Their slow render still runs per instance (producing instance-specific ViewState)</li>\n' +
      '<li>The ViewState is stored in <code>cache.json</code> under <code>carryForward.__instances</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>At serve time, the server element reads instance ViewState from <code>__headlessInstances</code> (existing mechanism)</li>\n' +
      '<li>The hydrate script wires interactive bindings on the headless instance&#39;s template</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Does this break the slow render cache?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>No. <code>cache.json</code> still stores <code>slowViewState</code> and <code>carryForward</code>. The only change is that we no longer generate pre-rendered jay-html alongside it.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: What about slow conditionals (<code>if</code> blocks on slow data)?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>The server element evaluates them at render time from the merged ViewState. The hydrate script ignores them if they&#39;re not interactive (no coordinate emitted). If a slow conditional wraps interactive content, the hydrate compiler emits a conditional adoption — this already works for fast-phase conditionals.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: How does the hydrate script get slow data for initial render?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>Same as today: the hydrate en'... 27077 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Per-Route Server Elements","number":144}'
  }
}
