{
  post: {
    title: 'Pluggable Jay-Html Validation',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #145 — Pluggable Jay-HTML Validation</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Wix media URLs (<code>https://static.wixstatic.com/media/HASH.jpg</code>) return full-size unoptimized images. Wix supports image resize and optimization by appending parameters like <code>/v1/fit/w_300,h_200,q_90/file.jpg</code>. However, the wix plugins cannot apply this because they don&#39;t know the target size — that information lives in the jay-html template (width/height from styles or attributes).</p>\n' +
      '<p>Similarly, accessibility rules (images must have <code>alt</code> attributes, inputs must have associated labels) need to be checked at the template level, not the plugin level.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Both use cases require validation that runs against parsed jay-html files, and both need to provide <strong>agent-friendly feedback</strong> explaining how to fix issues — since AI agents are the primary authors of jay-html templates.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>There is no mechanism for plugins to provide validation rules that run against jay-html files in consuming projects. The existing <code>jay-stack validate</code> command validates contracts, route params, ref types, headless instance props, and tag coverage — all built-in to the framework. Plugins have no extension point to add their own checks.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: What data do validators need access to?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Validators operate on the already-parsed jay-html DOM tree (<code>HTMLElement</code> from node-html-parser). They need:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>The element tree (to walk and inspect elements, attributes, text)</li>\n' +
      '<li>File path (for context in error messages)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Headless imports (to know which plugins are used in this file)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Page contract (to understand the data model)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>They do <strong>not</strong> need to load external files, run compilation, or access runtime state.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: How are validator handlers loaded?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Since validators work purely on parsed jay-html data, they need no special TypeScript loader. Handlers are loaded via standard <code>import()</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>NPM plugins</strong>: handler is pre-compiled JS in the package&#39;s dist</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Local plugins</strong>: handler is a relative path to the compiled JS file</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: Should accessibility validation be built-in or pluggable?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Pluggable — implemented as a framework-provided plugin in <code>packages/plugins/</code>. Projects opt in by adding the plugin. This keeps the core validation focused on structural correctness and allows accessibility rules to evolve independently.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: Per-file or batch validation?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Per-file. Each validator receives one parsed jay-html file and returns findings for that file. This matches the existing validation pattern in <code>validateJayFiles()</code>. Cross-file validators can be added later if needed.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q5: How does the agent consume validation feedback?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Validation findings include a <code>suggestion</code> field with actionable, agent-friendly instructions. When <code>jay-stack validate</code> runs (either by the agent or in CI), findings are printed with their suggestions. The <code>--json</code> output mode already exists and will include suggestion text, making it easy for agents to parse and act on.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Validator Declaration in plugin.yaml</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins declare validators alongside contracts, actions, and services:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> wix<span class="token punctuation">-</span>data\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">validators</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> wix<span class="token punctuation">-</span>media<span class="token punctuation">-</span>optimization\n' +
      '    handler<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ./validators/media<span class="token punctuation">-</span>validator\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Ensures wix media URLs use resize parameters for performance</code></pre>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>name</code>: kebab-case identifier for the validation rule</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>handler</code>: module path — relative path (local plugins) or export subpath (NPM plugins)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>description</code>: human-readable purpose (shown in verbose output)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>2. Type Definitions</h3>\n' +
      '<p>New file <code>packages/compiler/compiler-shared/lib/plugin-validators.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> type <span class="token punctuation">{</span> HTMLElement <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'node-html-parser'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> interface JayHtmlValidationContext <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Parsed jay-html DOM tree root */</span>\n' +
      '  body<span class="token operator">:</span> HTMLElement<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Relative file path (from project root) */</span>\n' +
      '  filePath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Absolute project root path */</span>\n' +
      '  projectRoot<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> interface JayHtmlValidationFinding <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  severity<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'error'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'warning'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Human-readable problem description */</span>\n' +
      '  message<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Agent-friendly instruction on how to fix the issue */</span>\n' +
      '  suggestion<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Element context (tag name or ref) */</span>\n' +
      '  element<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Which attribute is problematic */</span>\n' +
      '  attribute<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      `<span class="token comment">/** Function signature for a validator handler module's default export */</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> type JayHtmlValidatorFn <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>context<span class="token operator">:</span> JayHtmlValidationContext<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> JayHtmlValidationFinding<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>3. PluginManifest Extension</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add to <code>PluginManifest</code> in <code>packages/compiler/compiler-shared/lib/plugin-resolution.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">/** Jay-HTML validation rules provided by this plugin (DL#145) */</span>\n' +
      'validators<span class="token operator">?:</span> Array<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">/** Kebab-case rule name */</span>\n' +
      '    name<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">/** Module path: relative (local) or export subpath (NPM) */</span>\n' +
      '    handler<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">/** Human-readable description */</span>\n' +
      '    description<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>4. Validation Flow</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Extend <code>validateJayFiles()</code> in <code>packages/jay-stack/stack-cli/lib/validate.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">validateJayFiles()\n' +
      '    ├── [existing] Parse and validate .jay-contract files\n' +
      '    ├── [existing] Parse and validate .jay-html files\n' +
      '    │   ├── Route param checks\n' +
      '    │   ├── Ref type checks\n' +
      '    │   ├── Headless instance props\n' +
      '    │   ├── Tag coverage\n' +
      '    │   └── Code generation test\n' +
      '    └── [new] Plugin validator phase\n' +
      '        ├── scanPlugins() to discover all plugins\n' +
      '        ├── Filter plugins with validators\n' +
      '        ├── Load validator handlers via import()\n' +
      '        └── For each already-parsed jay-html file:\n' +
      '            ├── Build JayHtmlValidationContext from the parsed file\n' +
      '            ├── Run each validator function\n' +
      '            └── Collect findings into errors[] and warnings[]</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Key implementation detail: the jay-html files are <strong>already parsed</strong> by the core validation phase. The plugin validator phase reuses those parsed results — no re-parsing needed. We need to retain the parsed <code>JayHtmlSourceFile</code> objects from the core phase and pass them to validators.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>5. Handler Module Contract</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A validator handler module exports a <code>validate</code> function:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// validators/media-validator.ts</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">import</span> type <span class="token punctuation">{</span> JayHtmlValidatorFn <span class="token '... 58540 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Pluggable Jay-Html Validation","number":145}'
  }
}
