{
  post: {
    title: 'Css Performance Fixes',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #146 — CSS Performance Fixes</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Lighthouse flags two CSS performance issues on production builds:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>CSS not minified</strong> — Route CSS files are extracted as raw text from jay-html and written to disk without minification. JS bundles go through Vite with <code>minify: true</code>, but CSS bypasses this entirely.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Font loading waterfall</strong> — Three sequential network hops after HTML:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>HTML → route.css (261ms) → Google Fonts CSS (342ms) → woff2 files (420ms each)</li>\n' +
      '<li>route.css has no preload hint, so the browser discovers it during HTML parsing</li>\n' +
      '<li>Font files can&#39;t start loading until Google Fonts CSS response arrives with <code>@font-face</code> declarations</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix 1: Minify CSS at build time</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In <code>server-element-compile.ts</code>, minify the extracted CSS string before writing to disk. Use <code>esbuild.transform</code> (already a Vite dependency) with <code>{ loader: &#39;css&#39;, minify: true }</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File</strong>: <code>packages/jay-stack/production-server/lib/builder/server-element-compile.ts</code> (line 76)</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix 2: Preload route CSS</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In <code>fetch-page-handler.ts</code>, add <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;preload&quot; as=&quot;style&quot;&gt;</code> for the route CSS so it starts loading in parallel with the importmap and module preloads, instead of being discovered later.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File</strong>: <code>packages/jay-stack/production-server/lib/serve/fetch-page-handler.ts</code> (line 123)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Add <code>esbuild.transform</code> CSS minification in <code>server-element-compile.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Add CSS preload link in <code>fetch-page-handler.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Extract <code>@import</code> URLs from CSS at build time for preload hints</li>\n' +
      '<li>Verify with production build</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Results</h2>\n' +
      '<p>All 85 production-server tests passing.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>CSS minification</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>server-element-compile.ts</code>: added <code>esbuild.transform(css, { loader: &#39;css&#39;, minify: true })</code> before writing route CSS to disk</li>\n' +
      '<li>Respects <code>--no-minify</code> flag via <code>minifyCss</code> parameter threaded from <code>build-pipeline.ts</code> → <code>compileRouteServerElement</code> → <code>compileServerElement</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Dev server unaffected — it doesn&#39;t use this code path (CSS is inlined via Vite dev pipeline)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>CSS preload hint</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>fetch-page-handler.ts</code>: emits <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;preload&quot; href=&quot;...route.css&quot; as=&quot;style&quot; /&gt;</code> at the top of <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, before the importmap</li>\n' +
      '<li>Browser starts fetching CSS immediately instead of discovering it during HTML parsing</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>CSS @import preload hints</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>server-element-compile.ts</code>: <code>extractCssImportUrls()</code> scans CSS for external <code>@import</code> URLs (e.g., Google Fonts) at build time. Handles all syntax forms: <code>@import url(&quot;...&quot;)</code>, <code>@import url(&#39;...&#39;)</code>, <code>@import &quot;...&quot;</code>, and minified <code>@import&quot;...&quot;</code> (no space)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Extracted URLs stored in <code>RouteEntry.cssImports</code> in the route manifest</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>fetch-page-handler.ts</code>: emits <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;preload&quot; as=&quot;style&quot;&gt;</code> for each <code>cssImports</code> URL at the top of <code>&lt;head&gt;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>The <code>@import</code> stays in the CSS file — the preload just ensures the browser starts the fetch early, and the <code>@import</code> hits the cache</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Resulting <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> order</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">&lt;link rel=&quot;preload&quot; href=&quot;...route.css&quot; as=&quot;style&quot; /&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;link rel=&quot;preload&quot; href=&quot;https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?...&quot; as=&quot;style&quot; /&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;script type=&quot;importmap&quot;&gt;...&lt;/script&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;!-- head tags (preconnect, Google Fonts stylesheet, SEO) --&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;!-- module preloads --&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;...route.css&quot; /&gt;</code></pre>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Css Performance Fixes","number":146}'
  }
