[Build] 69/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=146-css-performance-fixes)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay-Html Validation Rules Catalog',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #147 — Jay-HTML Validation Rules Catalog</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>DL#145 introduced pluggable jay-html validation — a mechanism for plugins to provide validation rules that run against parsed jay-html templates during <code>jay-stack validate</code>. Three validator plugins now exist:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>wix-media</strong> — Wix-specific media optimization rules (external package)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>seo-validator</strong> — SEO best practices (<code>packages/plugins/seo-validator</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>a11y-validator</strong> — WCAG accessibility rules (<code>packages/plugins/a11y-validator</code>)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>This design log catalogs all validation rules across all plugins as a single reference.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Validator Plugins</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>wix-media / media-optimization</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Package: <code>@jay-framework/wix-media</code> (external, dev dependency)</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Rule</th>\n' +
      '<th>Severity</th>\n' +
      '<th>Element</th>\n' +
      '<th>What it checks</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Hardcoded Wix URL without optimization</td>\n' +
      '<td>error</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;source&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Static URLs from <code>static.wixstatic.com/media/</code> missing <code>/v1/</code> transform params</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Wix-image binding without optimization</td>\n' +
      '<td>error</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;source&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Template bindings to tags with <code>meta.mediaType: wix-image</code> without <code>/v1/</code> suffix appended</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Local image reference</td>\n' +
      '<td>error</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;source&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Local file paths (<code>/images/*.png</code>) that should be uploaded to Wix Media Manager</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>All three rules check <code>src</code> and <code>poster</code> attributes. Rule B uses <code>walkElements</code> + <code>resolveBinding</code> to resolve bindings through contracts and headless imports.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>seo-validator / seo</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Package: <code>@jay-framework/seo-validator</code> (monorepo, dev dependency)</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Rule</th>\n' +
      '<th>Severity</th>\n' +
      '<th>Element</th>\n' +
      '<th>What it checks</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Image missing alt</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>No <code>alt</code> attribute (hurts SEO and accessibility)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Image missing dimensions</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>No <code>width</code>/<code>height</code> attributes, inline style dimensions, or <code>srcset</code> — causes CLS</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Image missing loading</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>No <code>loading</code> attribute — should use <code>loading=&quot;lazy&quot;</code> or <code>loading=&quot;eager&quot;</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Empty anchor</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;a&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Anchor with <code>href</code> but no visible text, no <code>aria-label</code>, and no child <code>&lt;img&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Missing h1</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;h1&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Page has no <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> element</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Multiple h1</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;h1&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Page has more than one <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> element</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Skipped heading level</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;h2&gt;</code>–<code>&lt;h6&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Heading level skips (e.g., <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> followed by <code>&lt;h3&gt;</code>)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Missing main landmark</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;main&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Page body has no <code>&lt;main&gt;</code> element</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Missing fetchpriority</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Page has images but none with <code>fetchpriority=&quot;high&quot;</code> — LCP image should be prioritized</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Missing title</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;title&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>No <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> (via <code>ctx.head</code>)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Missing meta description</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;meta&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>No <code>&lt;meta name=&quot;description&quot;&gt;</code> in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Missing canonical</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;link&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>No <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;canonical&quot;&gt;</code> in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Noindex robots</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;meta&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;meta name=&quot;robots&quot;&gt;</code> contains <code>noindex</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>| Missing preconnect | warning | <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> | External stylesheet <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> without a preceding <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;preconnect&quot;&gt;</code> for that domain |\n' +
      '| Font missing display=swap | warning | <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> | Google Fonts / Typekit stylesheet URL missing <code>display=swap</code> parameter |</p>\n' +
      '<p>The dimensions rule accepts three forms of sizing: <code>width</code>/<code>height</code> attributes, inline <code>style</code> with <code>width:</code> and <code>height:</code>, or <code>srcset</code> (responsive images).</p>\n' +
      '<p>The head metadata rules use <code>ctx.head</code> — a parsed representation of the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> section added to the validation context.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Render-blocking resource rules (added DL#147a)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Missing preconnect:</strong> For each <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;https://...&quot;&gt;</code> in <code>ctx.head</code>, extract the origin (scheme + host). If no <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;preconnect&quot; href=&quot;https://that-host&quot;&gt;</code> exists earlier in <code>ctx.head.links</code>, flag it. Only applies to external origins (different from the page&#39;s own domain). Suggestion: <code>Add &lt;link rel=&quot;preconnect&quot; href=&quot;https://fonts.googleapis.com&quot;&gt; before the stylesheet</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Font missing display=swap:</strong> Match stylesheet <code>href</code> against known font service domains (<code>fonts.googleapis.com</code>, <code>use.typekit.net</code>). If the URL doesn&#39;t contain <code>display=swap</code> (Google) or equivalent, flag it. Suggestion: <code>Add &amp;display=swap to the Google Fonts URL to avoid render-blocking text</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>a11y-validator / accessibility</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Package: <code>@jay-framework/a11y-validator</code> (monorepo, dev dependency)</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Rule</th>\n' +
      '<th>Severity</th>\n' +
      '<th>Element</th>\n' +
      '<th>WCAG</th>\n' +
      '<th>What it checks</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Image missing alt</td>\n' +
      '<td>error</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>1.1.1</td>\n' +
      '<td>No <code>alt</code> attribute</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Form input without label</td>\n' +
      '<td>error</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;input&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>1.3.1</td>\n' +
      '<td>No <code>&lt;label for&gt;</code>, no wrapping <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>, no <code>aria-label</code>/<code>aria-labelledby</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Button without accessible name</td>\n' +
      '<td>error</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;button&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>4.1.2</td>\n' +
      '<td>No text, no <code>aria-label</code>, no <code>aria-labelledby</code>, no child <code>&lt;img alt&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Media autoplay without muted</td>\n' +
      '<td>error</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;video&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;audio&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>1.4.2</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>autoplay</code> attribute present without <code>muted</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Invalid ARIA role</td>\n' +
      '<td>error</td>\n' +
      '<td>any</td>\n' +
      '<td>4.1.2</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>role</code> attribute value not in WAI-ARIA role list</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Viewport disables zoom</td>\n' +
      '<td>error</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;meta&gt;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>1.4.4</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>user-scalable=no</code> or <code>maximum-scale</code> &lt; 2 in viewport meta (via <code>ctx.head</code>)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Positive tabindex</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td>interactive + <code>[role]</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>2.4.3</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>tabindex</code> &gt; 0 disrupts natural tab order</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Focusable without role</td>\n' +
      '<td>warning</td>\n' +
      '<td>non-interactive</td>\n' +
      '<td>4.1.2</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;div tabindex=&quot;0&quot;&gt;</code> or similar without <code>role</code> — screen readers don&#39;t know what it is</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>The form label rule skips <code>type=&quot;hidden&quot;</code>, <code>type=&quot;submit&quot;</code>, <code>type=&quot;button&quot;</code>, and <code>type=&quot;reset&quot;</code> inputs.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Rule Overlap</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Image alt</strong> is checked by both SEO (warning) and a11y (error). This is intentional:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Different severity reflects different impact framing</li>\n' +
      '<li>A project using both plugins sees both findings — the fix is the same</li>\n' +
      '<li>Projects may use only one of the two plugins</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>No other rules overlap between plugins.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Validation Context: Head Metadata</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>JayHtmlValidationContext</code> includes a <code>head?: JayHtmlHeadMeta</code> field parsed from the jay-html <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> section:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface JayHtmlHeadMeta <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  title<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  meta<span class="token operator">:</span> Array<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> name<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> property<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> content<span class="token operator">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class='... 1784 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Jay-Html Validation Rules Catalog","number":147}'
  }
}
[Build] 70/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=147-jay-html-validation-rules-catalog)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Head Tag Bindings',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #148 — Head Tag Bindings</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>DL#127 added component-driven head injection — components return <code>HeadTag[]</code> from <code>phaseOutput()</code> to render <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;meta&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> during SSR. A later extension added static head tags from the jay-html <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> section (<code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;meta&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;canonical&quot;&gt;</code>), rendered via <code>headMetaToHeadTags()</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>However, the static head tags don&#39;t support <code>{binding}</code> expressions. A page with <code>&lt;title&gt;{productName} | Store&lt;/title&gt;</code> renders literally as <code>{productName} | Store</code>. The only way to get dynamic head content is via component <code>phaseOutput({ headTags })</code>, which requires writing a component just to set a title.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>For pages that already have ViewState from contracts/headless components, there&#39;s no simple way to bind head metadata to that data without writing explicit component code. Common cases:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;title&gt;{productName} | My Store&lt;/title&gt;</code> — product name from ViewState</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;meta name=&quot;description&quot; content=&quot;{description}&quot; /&gt;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;link rel=&quot;canonical&quot; href=&quot;https://mystore.com/products/{slug}&quot; /&gt;</code> — slug from route params</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The component <code>phaseOutput({ headTags })</code> approach works but is heavy for simple interpolation. Designers authoring jay-html should be able to use the same <code>{binding}</code> syntax in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> that they use in <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Canonical URL issue</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Additionally, <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;canonical&quot;&gt;</code> requires an absolute URL (<code>https://...</code>), but the validator doesn&#39;t check this. The default should be no canonical — only rendered if explicitly declared.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Binding resolution at SSR time</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Head meta values (<code>title</code>, <code>meta.content</code>, <code>link.href</code>) are stored as raw strings with <code>{...}</code> intact by <code>parseHeadMeta()</code>. At SSR time, when the merged ViewState is available, resolve bindings before converting to <code>HeadTag[]</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Resolution function</strong> (<code>resolveHeadValue</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">resolveHeadValue</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>template<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> viewState<span class="token operator">:</span> object<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> parts <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">parseTemplateParts</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>template<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>parts<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">every</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>p<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> p<span class="token punctuation">.</span>kind <span class="token operator">===</span> <span class="token string">'static'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token keyword">return</span> template<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> parts\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">map</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>p<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `      <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>p<span class="token punctuation">.</span>kind <span class="token operator">===</span> <span class="token string">'static'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token keyword">return</span> p<span class="token punctuation">.</span>value<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token keyword">const</span> resolved <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">getByPath</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>viewState<span class="token punctuation">,</span> p<span class="token punctuation">.</span>value<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token keyword">return</span> resolved <span class="token operator">!==</span> <span class="token keyword">undefined</span> <span class="token operator">?</span> <span class="token function">String</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>resolved<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">`{${p.value}}`</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">join</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">''</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Uses <code>parseTemplateParts</code> from <code>compiler-jay-html</code> (already handles nested braces, ternaries). Simple dot-path resolution against ViewState — no compiler changes needed.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Updated signature:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">headMetaToHeadTags</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  headMeta<span class="token operator">:</span> JayHtmlHeadMeta <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token keyword">undefined</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  viewState<span class="token operator">?:</span> object<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> HeadTag<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Priority chain (template wins)</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Slow phase <code>phaseOutput({ headTags })</code> — component defaults</li>\n' +
      '<li>Fast phase <code>phaseOutput({ headTags })</code> — overrides slow</li>\n' +
      '<li>Jay-html <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> tags with bindings resolved — <strong>highest priority, template wins</strong></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>The template writer (designer) has final control over head content, matching Jay&#39;s philosophy that templates control output. Components provide sensible defaults (e.g., product name as title); the template overrides when it needs customization (e.g., <code>{productPage.name} | My Store</code> instead of just the product name).</p>\n' +
      '<p>In practice, most pages will only use one source — either the component provides head tags, or the template declares them. When both exist, the template takes precedence.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Static validation challenge</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When the template doesn&#39;t declare <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;meta description&gt;</code>, the SEO validator warns about missing head tags. But a component might provide them dynamically via <code>phaseOutput({ headTags })</code> — the validator can&#39;t know this statically without running the component.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Solution: <code>headTags</code> declaration in plugin.yaml</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins declare which head tags their components provide:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> wix<span class="token punctuation">-</span>stores\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">contracts</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> product<span class="token punctuation">-</span>page\n' +
      '    headTags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">-</span> title\n' +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">-</span> meta<span class="token punctuation">:</span>description\n' +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">-</span> link<span class="token punctuation">:</span>canonical</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The validator checks: &quot;this page imports <code>product-page</code> from <code>wix-stores</code>, which declares it handles <code>title</code>, <code>meta:description</code>, and <code>link:canonical</code> — skip warnings for those.&quot; If the template also declares a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, no conflict — the template wins at runtime, and the validator knows a title exists from either source.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This declaration is optional — plugins without <code>headTags</code> declarations don&#39;t affect validation. The validator falls back to checking the jay-html <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> only.</p>\n' +
