{
  post: {
    title: 'Script Tags In Jay-Html',
    content: '<h1>DL#149 — Script Tags in Jay-HTML</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay-HTML pages use <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-*&quot;&gt;</code> tags in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> for framework declarations (headless imports, headfull imports, data contracts). The SSR output is built from scratch — it constructs a new <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> document containing only the rendered body and a hydration script. Any non-jay script tags in the original jay-html are silently dropped.</p>\n' +
      '<p>An AI agent was observed writing inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tags for animation logic instead of using <code>page.ts</code>. The silent drop meant no error feedback — the script simply didn&#39;t work, and the agent didn&#39;t know why.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Separately, there are legitimate use cases for script tags: marketing/analytics snippets (Google Analytics, GTM, Meta Pixel), third-party widget embeds, and consent management scripts. These are often provided as inline snippets (GTM gives an inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> that bootstraps the external tag manager with site-specific parameters) or external <code>&lt;script src=&quot;...&quot;&gt;</code> includes.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No validation feedback</strong> — arbitrary <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tags are silently dropped, confusing both agents and developers</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No mechanism for third-party scripts</strong> — legitimate external and inline marketing scripts have no supported path into the rendered HTML</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Agent misdirection</strong> — without guardrails, agents write inline JS instead of using the component API</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Should we ever allow inline JS in jay-html?</strong>\n' +
      'Not by default. Inline JS bypasses the component model, can&#39;t participate in rendering phases, and breaks SSR. All page behavior should go through <code>page.ts</code> / <code>makeJayStackComponent</code>. However, some third-party tools (e.g., Google Tag Manager) provide inline snippets that bootstrap their external script with site-specific parameters. These need to be supported via an explicit opt-in (<code>jay-script</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: Should we allow local script imports (<code>&lt;script src=&quot;./local.js&quot;&gt;</code>)?</strong>\n' +
      'No, not even with <code>jay-script</code>. Local scripts should be part of <code>page.ts</code>. Only inline snippets and external URLs are supported.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: Where can third-party scripts be placed?</strong>\n' +
      'In <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> or in <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> (top or bottom). Placement matters for performance:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;head&gt;</code> with <code>async</code> or <code>defer</code> — loads without blocking rendering</li>\n' +
      '<li>End of <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> — loads after page content</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;head&gt;</code> without <code>async</code>/<code>defer</code> — blocks rendering (discouraged)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The agent-kit guide should advise on placement and loading strategies.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q4: What about <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tags with attributes like <code>async</code>, <code>defer</code>, <code>type=&quot;module&quot;</code>?</strong>\n' +
      'These should be preserved on included scripts. They&#39;re meaningful for loading behavior.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q5: Could <code>jay-script</code> carry values for future extensibility?</strong>\n' +
      'Yes. Using <code>jay-script=&quot;allow&quot;</code> (instead of a boolean <code>jay-allow</code>) leaves room for future modes like <code>jay-script=&quot;sandbox&quot;</code> (run in isolated context) without introducing new attributes.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>The <code>jay-script</code> attribute</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A value-carrying attribute that marks a script for inclusion. Currently supports one value:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-script=&quot;allow&quot;</code> — include this script as-is in the rendered output</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Future values (not implemented now):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-script=&quot;sandbox&quot;</code> — run in an isolated context</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-script=&quot;defer&quot;</code> — framework-managed deferred loading</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Validation rules</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When the jay-html parser encounters a <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tag that is not a <code>type=&quot;application/jay-*&quot;</code> declaration:</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Script type</th>\n' +
      '<th>Without <code>jay-script</code></th>\n' +
      '<th>With <code>jay-script=&quot;allow&quot;</code></th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Inline</strong> (has body)</td>\n' +
      '<td><strong>error</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td>Allowed, included in output</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Local src</strong> (<code>./</code>, <code>../</code>, relative path)</td>\n' +
      '<td><strong>error</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td><strong>error</strong> (never allowed)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>External src</strong> (<code>https://...</code>)</td>\n' +
      '<td><strong>error</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td>Allowed, included in output</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>Error message (inline without <code>jay-script</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>&quot;Inline scripts are not supported in jay-html. Use page.ts with makeJayStackComponent for page behavior. If this is a third-party script that must be included as-is, add jay-script=&quot;allow&quot;. See designer/script-tags.md.&quot;</p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>Error message (local src):</p>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>&quot;Local script imports are not supported in jay-html. Move the script logic into page.ts with makeJayStackComponent. See designer/script-tags.md.&quot;</p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>Error message (external without <code>jay-script</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>&quot;External scripts should be explicitly marked. If this script is required (e.g., analytics or tag manager), add jay-script=&quot;allow&quot;. Prefer page.ts for page behavior. See designer/script-tags.md.&quot;</p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h3>Script passthrough</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Scripts marked with <code>jay-script=&quot;allow&quot;</code> are collected during parsing and included in the SSR output. They can appear in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> — their position is preserved. The <code>jay-script</code> attribute itself is stripped from the output.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;head</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- External script: loads GTM library --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-XXXXX&quot;</span>\n' +
      '    async\n' +
      '    <span class="token attribute">jay-script</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;allow&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Inline script: GTM bootstrap with site parameters --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">jay-script</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;allow&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    window.dataLayer <span class="token punctuation">=</span> window.dataLayer || [];\n' +
      '    function gtag() {\n' +
      '      dataLayer.push(arguments);\n' +
      '    }\n' +
      `    gtag(<span class="token string">'js'</span>, new Date());\n` +
      `    gtag(<span class="token string">'config'</span>, <span class="token string">'G-XXXXX'</span>);\n` +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Framework declaration: no jay-script needed --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token attribute">plugin</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;wix-stores&quot;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token attribute">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;product-page&quot;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token attribute">key</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;product&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/head</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token comment">&lt;!-- End-of-body placement for non-critical scripts --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;main</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>...<span class="token tag">&lt;/main</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;https://cdn.example.com/chat-widget.js&quot;</span> defer <span class="token attribute">jay-script</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;allow&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Agent-kit guidance</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Create a new agent-kit guide <code>designer/script-tags.md</code> (referenced from designer INSTRUCTIONS.md) covering:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Default rule</strong>: use <code>page.ts</code> with <code>makeJayStackComponent</code> for all page behavior</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>When scripts are needed</strong>: th'... 4175 more characters,
