{
  post: {
    title: 'Build Content Hash',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #150 — Build Content Hash</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>When deploying to Wix BaaS, we need client (CDN) and server (backend worker) artifacts to stay in sync. Today the build version comes from <code>package.json</code> and doesn&#39;t change between deploys unless manually bumped. If a developer rebuilds and redeploys without bumping the version, the CDN and backend can serve mismatched artifacts.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>We need a content-derived identifier that changes whenever the build output changes, regardless of the semver version string. This hash can serve as a deployment cache key to guarantee client/server consistency.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>What to hash</h3>\n' +
      '<p>All files under the build directory (<code>build/v{version}/</code>) — both <code>frontend/</code> and <code>backend/</code> — excluding <code>build-metadata.json</code> itself (since it contains the hash).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Hash algorithm</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>SHA-256 over a deterministic stream: sort file paths lexicographically, then for each file feed <code>relativePath + content</code> into the hash</li>\n' +
      '<li>Truncate to first 12 hex characters — short enough for URLs/keys, long enough to avoid collisions in practice</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Where to store</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>BuildMetadata</code> type already has a <code>sourceHash: string</code> field (currently set to <code>&#39;&#39;</code>). Populate it.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Where to compute</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In <code>build-pipeline.ts</code>, after all build artifacts are written (route manifest, server elements, client bundles, public folder copy) but before writing <code>build-metadata.json</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Single file change</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>packages/jay-stack/production-server/lib/builder/build-pipeline.ts</code></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p>Add a <code>computeBuildHash(dir: string): Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> function:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Recursively collect all file paths under <code>dir</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Filter out <code>build-metadata.json</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Sort paths lexicographically</li>\n' +
      '<li>Create a SHA-256 hash, update with each file&#39;s relative path and content</li>\n' +
      '<li>Return first 12 hex chars</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p>Call it at ~line 546 (after <code>writeRouteManifest</code> and public folder copy, before metadata write):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-ts"><span class="token keyword">const</span> sourceHash <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token keyword">await</span> <span class="token function">computeBuildHash</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>buildDir<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p>Set <code>sourceHash</code> in the metadata object (replacing <code>&#39;&#39;</code>).</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>No type changes needed — <code>BuildMetadata.sourceHash</code> already exists.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification</h2>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-stack-cli build</code> on an example project → <code>build-metadata.json</code> has non-empty <code>sourceHash</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Two identical builds → same hash</li>\n' +
      '<li>Change a source file, rebuild → different hash</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Results</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Hash computation — implemented as designed</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>computeBuildHash()</code> added to <code>build-pipeline.ts</code>, called after all artifacts written</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>sourceHash</code> removed from <code>RouteManifest</code> (only lives in <code>BuildMetadata</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>buildTimestamp</code> removed from <code>RouteManifest</code> (moved to <code>BuildMetadata</code> only) to ensure the manifest is deterministic — same source produces same hash</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Public folder duplication fix (discovered during implementation)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>All Vite build calls in the production pipeline used <code>root: projectRoot</code> without <code>publicDir: false</code>. Vite&#39;s default behavior copies <code>public/</code> into every build output directory. This caused ~190 images duplicated across <code>backend/server/</code> and every <code>backend/pre-rendered/{route}/</code> directory.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Fix: added <code>publicDir: false</code> to all 5 Vite build calls (server-code-build, server-element-compile x2, instance-client-build, shared-chunks-build). The build pipeline already explicitly copies <code>public/</code> to <code>frontend/public/</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Hydration flattening bug fix</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Discovered and fixed during this work — see DL#106 &quot;Bug I&quot; for details.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
