{
  post: {
    title: 'Phase-Aware Contract Props',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #152 — Phase-Aware Contract Props</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Headless component contracts define <code>props</code> — typed inputs passed via <code>&lt;jay:component prop=&quot;value&quot;&gt;</code> attributes. Unlike <code>tags</code> (which have explicit <code>phase</code> annotations like <code>slow</code>, <code>fast+interactive</code>), props have no phase information. The framework doesn&#39;t know when a prop value needs to be available.</p>\n' +
      '<p>PR #182 added support for resolving <code>{binding}</code> expressions in instance props — e.g., <code>&lt;jay:category-products categorySlug=&quot;{p.categorySlug}&quot;&gt;</code>. The binding is resolved against the page&#39;s ViewState at render time. But there&#39;s a gap: if the binding references a fast-phase field, the slow render receives an empty string.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Related</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>DL#84 — Headless component props and repeater support</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#124 — Contract props and params consistency</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#50 — Rendering phases in contracts</li>\n' +
      '<li>PR #182 — Resolve jay params values for headless instances</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token comment"># category-products.jay-contract</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">props</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> categorySlug\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string</code></pre>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Page uses a keyed component `p` that provides categorySlug at fast phase --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;jay</span>:category-products <span class="token attribute">categorySlug</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;{p.categorySlug}&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span> ... <span class="token tag">&lt;/jay</span>:category-products<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>category-products</code> component has <code>slowlyRender(props)</code> that queries the database by <code>categorySlug</code>. But <code>p.categorySlug</code> is only available after the page&#39;s fast render. During slow render:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><code>slowRenderInstances</code> resolves <code>{p.categorySlug}</code> → <code>p</code> has no <code>categorySlug</code> yet → returns <code>&quot;&quot;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Component&#39;s <code>slowlyRender({ categorySlug: &quot;&quot; })</code> queries with empty slug → wrong/empty results</li>\n' +
      '<li>Fast render later resolves correctly, but the slow data is already cached with wrong results</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>No error or warning is produced. The designer has no way to know that this binding won&#39;t work at slow time.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions &amp; Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1:</strong> Should props have a <code>phase</code> annotation like tags?</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A1:</strong> Yes. Same system as tags.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2:</strong> What phases make sense for props? Tags use <code>slow</code>, <code>fast</code>, <code>fast+interactive</code>. Props are inputs from the template, not rendered outputs — do the same phases apply?</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A2:</strong> Same phases as tags. <code>slow</code> (default), <code>fast</code>, <code>fast+interactive</code>. In practice <code>fast</code> === <code>fast+interactive</code> because interactive-phase props can change on the client.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3:</strong> Should the phase on a prop indicate when the VALUE is expected to be available, or when the component USES it?</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A3:</strong> These are the same thing — the expectation that a value is available is defined by when the component uses it.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q4:</strong> How should the framework validate that a prop binding provides data at the right phase?</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A4:</strong> The binding&#39;s source tag phase must be ≤ the prop&#39;s phase. A slow tag can bind to a fast prop. A fast tag cannot bind to a slow prop.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q5:</strong> Should this be a compile-time validation error, a runtime warning, or both?</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A5:</strong> Compile error, like any other tag phase mismatch.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q6:</strong> What about literal props like <code>limit=&quot;4&quot;</code> — are they always available at all phases?</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A6:</strong> Yes. Literal values and route params are always available at all phases.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Prop Phase Annotation</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add a <code>phase</code> field to contract prop definitions, following the same rules as tag phases:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">props</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> categorySlug\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '    phase<span class="token punctuation">:</span> slow <span class="token comment"># Default — must be available at build time</span>\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Category slug to filter products by\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> productId\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '    phase<span class="token punctuation">:</span> fast <span class="token comment"># Only needs to be available at request time</span>\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Product ID to exclude from results</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Phase values for props (same as tags):</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Phase</th>\n' +
      '<th>Default</th>\n' +
      '<th>Meaning</th>\n' +
      '<th>Binding source must be</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>slow</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Yes</td>\n' +
      '<td>Available at build time</td>\n' +
      '<td>Literal, route param, or slow-phase tag</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>fast</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>No</td>\n' +
      '<td>Available at request time</td>\n' +
      '<td>Any of above, or fast-phase tag</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>fast+interactive</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>No</td>\n' +
      '<td>Can also change on client</td>\n' +
      '<td>Same as fast (fast === fast+interactive in practice)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Default is <code>slow</code></strong> — same as tags. This means existing contracts without <code>phase</code> on props will now be validated as slow, which may surface binding mismatches that were previously silent. This is a <strong>regression fix</strong> — the empty-prop-at-slow-time bug was always there, just undetected.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>What Can Provide Slow-Phase Props</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A <code>phase: slow</code> prop binding must resolve to a value available during slow render:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Literal values</strong> — always available: <code>categorySlug=&quot;best-sellers&quot;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Route params</strong> — always available: <code>categorySlug=&quot;{category}&quot;</code> (from URL segments)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Slow-phase keyed ViewState</strong> — available if the keyed component has <code>slowlyRender</code>: <code>categorySlug=&quot;{p.categorySlug}&quot;</code> where <code>p.categorySlug</code> is a slow tag</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Page slow ViewState</strong> — available: <code>slug=&quot;{pageSlug}&quot;</code> where <code>pageSlug</code> has <code>phase: slow</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>A <code>phase: slow</code> prop binding to a fast-phase field should produce a validation error.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>What Can Provide Fast-Phase Props</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A <code>phase: fast</code> prop can bind to anything available at request time — slow or fast ViewState, route params, query params, literals.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Validation</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Compile-time error in <code>jay-stack validate</code>, same as tag phase mismatches.</p>\n' +
      '<p>When a <code>&lt;jay:component&gt;</code> instance has a prop binding, the validator:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Resolves the binding path (e.g., <code>p.categorySlug</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Finds the source tag in the page&#39;s contract or keyed component&#39;s contract</li>\n' +
      '<li>Checks: source tag phase must be ≤ prop phase</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Phase ordering: <code>slow</code> &lt; <code>fast</code> ≤ <code>fast+interactive</code></p>\n' +
      '<p>A slow source can bind to any prop phase. A fast source cannot bind to a slow prop.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">❌ &lt;jay:category-products&gt; prop &quot;categorySlug&quot; (phase: slow) bound to\n' +
      '   {p.categorySlug} which is phase: fast+interactive.\n' +
      '   Suggestion: Use a slow-phase binding, a route param, or a literal value.</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Literal values and route params are always considered <code>slow</code> (always available).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Default Behavior</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Props default to <code>phase: slow</code>, same as tags. Existing contracts without explicit <code>phase</code> on props will now be validated — bindings to fast-phase fields that were silently producing empty values at slow render will surface as compile errors.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Contract Example</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> category<span class="token punctuation">-</span>products\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">description</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> Shows products filtered by category\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">props</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> categorySlug\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '    phase<span class="token punctuation">:</span> slow\n' +
      '    required<span class="token punctuation">:</span> true\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Category slug — must be available at build time for SSG\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> productId\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Product to exclude (no phase — works '... 3158 more characters,
