[Build] 77/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=153-npm-create-jay)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Plugin Package Shipping Validation',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #154 — Plugin Package Shipping Validation</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins ship NPM packages with <code>package.json</code> controlling what files are included. The <code>plugin-validator</code> already checks that contracts appear in <code>exports</code>, but doesn&#39;t verify that <code>agent-kit/</code> directories are included in the <code>files</code> array. This caused the <code>design-system-validator</code> plugin&#39;s <code>agent-kit/designer/design-system.md</code> to be silently excluded from the published package.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Related: #39 (Plugin package), #73 (validate command), #85 (agent-kit), #124 (contract consistency), #125 (plugin agent-kit).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>A plugin can have an <code>agent-kit/</code> directory with designer/developer guidance files, but if it&#39;s not listed in <code>package.json</code> <code>files</code>, those files won&#39;t be in the npm tarball. There&#39;s no validation catching this.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Concrete example: design-system-validator</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-json">// package.json — agent-kit/ NOT listed\n' +
      '<span class="token string">&quot;files&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">&quot;dist&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">&quot;plugin.yaml&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">agent-kit/\n' +
      '  designer/\n' +
      '    design-system.md    ← not shipped</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Add a check in <code>validatePackageJson()</code> (in <code>plugin-validator</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>If <code>agent-kit/</code> directory exists in the plugin root</li>\n' +
      '<li>Check that <code>&quot;agent-kit&quot;</code> appears in <code>packageJson.files</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>If missing → emit warning with suggestion</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Warning (not error) because the plugin still functions without agent-kit — it&#39;s a documentation/discoverability issue.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Add check in <code>validatePackageJson()</code> after existing exports checks</li>\n' +
      '<li>Add tests for the three cases (missing, present, no agent-kit dir)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Fix <code>design-system-validator</code> <code>package.json</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification</h2>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin-validator tests pass</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>yarn validate</code> in <code>design-system-validator</code> produces no warnings about agent-kit</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Plugin Package Shipping Validation","number":154}'
  }
}
