{
  post: {
    title: 'Markdown Plugin',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #155 — Markdown Plugin</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack needs a markdown rendering plugin for content-driven pages — blogs, documentation, changelogs, knowledge bases. The plugin should integrate with the three-phase rendering model, support code highlighting and mermaid diagrams, and work with both static directories of markdown files and dynamic markdown values.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Related</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>DL#39 — Plugin package requirements</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#60 — Plugin system refinement, dynamic contracts</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#84 — Headless component props</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#85 — Rendering phases and agent kit</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#130 — Plugin routes and templates</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#152 — Phase-aware contract props</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>No built-in way to render markdown content in Jay Stack pages. Projects that need blog posts, documentation, or markdown-driven content must implement their own parsing, rendering, and routing. This is a common enough need to warrant a plugin.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions &amp; Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: How should the directory-to-pages component know which markdown directory to scan?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A1: Via props on the headless component script tag. This requires a framework change — currently <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;&gt;</code> supports <code>plugin</code>, <code>contract</code>, and <code>key</code> attributes but no <code>props</code>. See &quot;Framework Gap&quot; section below.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: Should code highlighting use a JS library (Shiki, Prism) or CSS-only?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A2: CSS-only with pre-tagged HTML. The marked renderer extension tokenizes code into <code>&lt;span class=&quot;token keyword&quot;&gt;</code> etc. A shipped CSS file provides colors. No client JS needed, theme-able via CSS custom properties.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: Should mermaid render at build time or client-side?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A3: Build-time SVG in the slow phase. No client JS, no layout shift, diagrams are part of the static HTML. Mermaid is a build-time dependency only.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q4: What markdown parser?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A4: <code>marked</code> — fast, lightweight, extensible via tokenizer/renderer extensions.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q5: Should the single-value renderer support interactive updates?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A5: Yes — two components. <code>markdown-content</code> renders at slow phase (static). <code>markdown-live</code> renders at fast+interactive (dynamic, re-parses on client when value changes).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Components</h3>\n' +
      '<h4>1. <code>markdown-pages</code> — Directory to pages</h4>\n' +
      '<p>A headless component that scans a directory of <code>.md</code> files and provides page data. The page&#39;s <code>page.jay-html</code> references it, and it contributes a <code>slug</code> param via <code>loadParams</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Usage in page.jay-html:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;html</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;head</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token attribute">plugin</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;@jay-framework/markdown&quot;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token attribute">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;markdown-pages&quot;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token attribute">key</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;post&quot;</span>\n' +
      `      <span class="token attribute">props</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">'{ &quot;contentDir&quot;: &quot;./content&quot; }'</span>\n` +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/head</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;article</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;h1</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{post.title}<span class="token tag">&lt;/h1</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;time</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{post.date}<span class="token tag">&lt;/time</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{post.content}<span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;/article</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/html</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Directory structure:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">src/pages/blog/[slug]/\n' +
      '  page.jay-html          ← references markdown-pages\n' +
      '  page.jay-contract      ← optional, for page-level data\n' +
      '  content/\n' +
      '    getting-started.md\n' +
      '    advanced-topics.md\n' +
      '    changelog.md</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Markdown file format:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-markdown">---\n' +
      'title: Getting Started\n' +
      'date: 2026-07-15\n' +
      'description: Learn how to set up the project\n' +
      'tags: [tutorial, beginner]\n' +
      '---\n' +
      '\n' +
      '# Getting Started\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Your content here...\n' +
