{
  post: {
    title: 'Keyed Headless Component Props',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #156 — Keyed Headless Component Props</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack has three mechanisms for passing data into headless components, each covering a different case:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Route params</strong> via <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-params&quot;&gt;</code> (DL#113) — static YAML values that flow as <code>pageParams</code> to all components. Used for static route overrides like <code>/products/ceramic-flower-vase</code> providing <code>{ slug: &#39;ceramic-flower-vase&#39; }</code>.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Instance props</strong> via <code>&lt;jay:component-name attrName=&quot;value&quot;&gt;</code> — attributes on inline instances, resolved against the page&#39;s binding context. Used for per-instance configuration.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Keyed headless components</strong> via <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headless&quot; key=&quot;name&quot;&gt;</code> — no props mechanism. The component receives only <code>pageProps</code> (route params). Its ViewState merges into the page namespace.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Related</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>DL#84 — Headless component props and repeater support</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#113 — Explicit route params for static overrides</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#124 — Contract props and params consistency</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#152 — Phase-aware contract props</li>\n' +
      '<li>DL#155 — Markdown plugin (motivating use case)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Keyed headless components cannot receive per-component configuration from the page. The <code>markdown-pages</code> component (DL#155) needs a <code>contentDir</code> prop to know which directory to scan. Today, the only way to pass data is through route params (<code>jay-params</code>), but those are page-wide — not scoped to a specific component.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Current mechanisms side by side</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">                        jay-params           instance props          keyed headless\n' +
      'Where declared:         &lt;script&gt; in head     &lt;jay:xxx attr=&quot;val&quot;&gt;    &lt;script&gt; in head\n' +
      'Scope:                  page-wide            per-instance            per-component (but no props)\n' +
      'Format:                 YAML body            HTML attributes         —\n' +
      'Flows to component as:  pageParams           normalizedProps         pageProps only</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The gap: keyed headless components (<code>key=&quot;name&quot;</code>) have no way to receive component-specific props.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Observation: jay-params is a special case of headless props</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>jay-params</code> provides static values for route param matching. But conceptually it&#39;s the same as &quot;static props for the page component.&quot; If keyed headless components had props, <code>jay-params</code> would be the props for the page component itself (which is implicitly keyed).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions &amp; Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Should we add a <code>props</code> attribute to <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;&gt;</code>, or extend <code>jay-params</code> to be per-component?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A1: Extend the headless script tag with a YAML body for props. This mirrors <code>jay-params</code> (YAML in a script tag) and <code>jay-data</code> (YAML contract in a script tag). The YAML body is more readable than a JSON attribute for multi-line values.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: Should we consolidate <code>jay-params</code> into this mechanism?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A2: Yes. <code>jay-params</code> becomes props on the page&#39;s implicit headless component. Instead of a separate <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-params&quot;&gt;</code>, the params are declared directly in <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-data&quot;&gt;</code> (the page&#39;s contract script tag), or we keep <code>jay-params</code> as sugar for backward compatibility but treat it as page-level props internally.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: What about the contract&#39;s <code>props</code> section — how does it validate?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A3: The contract already has a <code>props</code> section that declares expected prop names and types. The validate command (DL#124) should check that props provided in the headless script tag match the contract&#39;s declaration.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Props on keyed headless components via YAML body</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add YAML body support to <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;&gt;</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;script</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">plugin</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;@jay-framework/markdown&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;markdown-pages&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">key</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;post&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  contentDir: .<span class="token punctuation">/</span>content\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The YAML body contains prop values. These flow to the component&#39;s <code>withSlowlyRender</code> / <code>withFastRender</code> as part of <code>props</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Multi-value example:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;script</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">plugin</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;@jay-framework/markdown&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;markdown-pages&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">key</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;post&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  contentDir: .<span class="token punctuation">/</span>content<span class="token punctuation">/</span>blog\n' +
      '  defaultAuthor: Jane Doe\n' +
      '  dateFormat: YYYY-MM-DD\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Consolidating jay-params</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The page component has its own <code>page.ts</code> — it doesn&#39;t need external values from the template.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The only components that need template-provided values are <strong>reusable headless components</strong> — they&#39;re generic and can&#39;t hardcode per-page configuration. This includes both props (like <code>contentDir</code> for the markdown plugin) and params (like <code>slug</code> for a product page override).</p>\n' +
      '<p><code>jay-params</code> (DL#113) was a page-wide mechanism, but the values it provides actually belong to a specific headless component. A static override page at <code>/products/ceramic-flower-vase/</code> provides <code>slug: ceramic-flower-vase</code> for the <code>wix-stores/product-page</code> component — not for the page itself.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Before (jay-params — page-wide, no component association):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-params&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  slug: ceramic-flower-vase\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;script</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">plugin</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;@jay-framework/wix-stores&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;product-page&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">key</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;productPage&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>After — values on the component that needs them:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;script</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">plugin</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;@jay-framework/wix-stores&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;product-page&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">key</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;productPage&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  slug: ceramic-flower-vase\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Props example — same mechanism:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;script</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">plugin</span><span class="token punctuation">=<'... 15864 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Keyed Headless Component Props","number":156}'
  }
}
