{
  post: {
    title: 'Staged Npm Publish',
    content: '<h1>DL#158 — Staged npm Publish</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The monorepo has ~40 publishable <code>@jay-framework/*</code> packages. Previously, publishing required passing an OTP to every <code>yarn npm publish</code> call. With 2FA enabled, OTPs expire in 30 seconds — not enough time for sequential publishing of all packages. The old scripts either failed mid-way or required disabling 2FA.</p>\n' +
      '<p>npm introduced a <strong>staging</strong> workflow (npm 11+ / Node 22+, Yarn 4.17+): packages are uploaded without 2FA, then bulk-approved with a single OTP after all uploads complete.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>OTP expires before all packages are published</li>\n' +
      '<li>Partial publish leaves the registry in an inconsistent state (some packages updated, others not)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Old <code>publish.cjs</code> script required <code>NPM_OTP</code> env var upfront — wasted if staging took too long</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Two-phase publish</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Phase 1: Stage (no OTP)          Phase 2: Approve (single OTP)\n' +
      '┌─────────────────────┐          ┌─────────────────────┐\n' +
      '│ yarn npm publish    │          │ yarn npm stage      │\n' +
      '│   --staged          │  ──────► │   approve &lt;id&gt;      │\n' +
      '│   --access public   │          │   --otp &lt;otp&gt;       │\n' +
      '│   (per workspace)   │          │   (per staged pkg)  │\n' +
      '└─────────────────────┘          └─────────────────────┘</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Resumable flow</h3>\n' +
      '<p>On start, check for already-staged packages. If found, skip directly to approve. This handles:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Ctrl-C after staging but before OTP entry</li>\n' +
      '<li>OTP entered incorrectly — re-run picks up staged packages</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>OTP prompt timing</h3>\n' +
      '<p>OTP is requested interactively right before the approve step, not as a CLI argument. This maximizes the time window for the OTP to remain valid.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Script: <code>scripts/publish-staged.mjs</code></h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">1. yarn npm whoami          — verify npm login\n' +
      '2. yarn npm stage list      — check for existing staged packages\n' +
      '   ├── found → skip to step 4\n' +
      '   └── empty → continue\n' +
      '3. yarn workspaces foreach -A --no-private --topological-dev\n' +
      '     exec &quot;yarn npm publish --staged --access public --tolerate-republish&quot;\n' +
      '4. yarn npm stage list --json  — collect stage IDs\n' +
      '5. prompt: Enter OTP\n' +
      '6. yarn npm stage approve &lt;id&gt; --otp &lt;otp&gt;  — for each staged package</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>package.json scripts</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;publish&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;node scripts/publish-staged.mjs&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;publish:legacy&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;node scripts/publish.cjs&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Old <code>publish:interactive</code> and <code>publish:manual</code> removed — the staged flow replaces both.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Requirements</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Node 22+ (<code>nvm use v22</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Yarn 4.17+ (supports <code>--staged</code>, <code>yarn npm stage list/approve</code>)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Key flags</h3>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Flag</th>\n' +
      '<th>Purpose</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>--staged</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Upload without 2FA, defer to approve step</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>--access public</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Required for <code>@jay-framework/*</code> scoped packages</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>--tolerate-republish</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Skip already-published versions without error</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>--topological-dev</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Publish dependencies before dependents</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>--json</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>NDJSON output from <code>stage list</code> for script parsing</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h2>Trade-offs</h2>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Choice</th>\n' +
      '<th>Pro</th>\n' +
      '<th>Con</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Interactive OTP prompt vs CLI arg</td>\n' +
      '<td>OTP entered at last moment, maximizes validity window</td>\n' +
      '<td>Cannot be fully non-interactive</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Resume from staged vs always re-stage</td>\n' +
      '<td>Handles interruptions gracefully</td>\n' +
      '<td>Stale staged packages could surprise if left from a previous session</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Yarn <code>--staged</code> vs <code>yarn pack</code> + <code>npm stage publish</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Single tool, resolves <code>workspace:*</code> automatically</td>\n' +
      '<td>Requires Yarn 4.17+</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Staged Npm Publish","number":158}'
  }
}
