{
  post: {
    title: 'Deprecate Editor Packages',
    content: '<h1>DL#160 — Deprecate Editor Packages</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Three packages exist from the original editor integration (DL#42):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>@jay-framework/editor-client</code> — client-side editor communication</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>@jay-framework/editor-protocol</code> — shared types for editor ↔ server messages</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>@jay-framework/editor-server</code> — WebSocket server for editor connections</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>These were designed for the Figma design tool integration. The AIditor has since replaced this workflow — it operates directly on jay-html files without the editor protocol layer.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Current Usage</h2>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Package</th>\n' +
      '<th>Dependents</th>\n' +
      '<th>Actual code usage</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>editor-client</td>\n' +
      '<td>none</td>\n' +
      '<td>none</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>editor-protocol</td>\n' +
      '<td>stack-cli, plugin-validator</td>\n' +
      '<td>stack-cli: Figma vendor types (<code>FigmaVendorDocument</code>, <code>ProjectPage</code>, <code>Plugin</code>, <code>ContractTag</code>). plugin-validator: vite external only, no code imports</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>editor-server</td>\n' +
      '<td>stack-cli</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>stack-cli/lib/server.ts</code>: <code>createEditorServer()</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p>All usage is in stack-cli&#39;s Figma vendor integration (<code>lib/vendors/figma/</code>, <code>lib/editor-handlers.ts</code>, <code>lib/server.ts</code>). The dev-server has no editor dependencies.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Move packages</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Move <code>packages/jay-stack/editor-client</code> → <code>packages/_deprecated/editor-client</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Move <code>packages/jay-stack/editor-protocol</code> → <code>packages/_deprecated/editor-protocol</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Move <code>packages/jay-stack/editor-server</code> → <code>packages/_deprecated/editor-server</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Remove from stack-cli</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Remove <code>@jay-framework/editor-server</code> dependency from stack-cli</li>\n' +
      '<li>Remove <code>lib/server.ts</code> (editor WebSocket server)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Remove <code>lib/editor-handlers.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Remove <code>lib/vendors/</code> directory (Figma vendor converters) — or keep if vendor types can be inlined</li>\n' +
      '<li>Remove editor-related tests (<code>test/vendors/</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Remove <code>@jay-framework/editor-protocol</code> external from <code>vite.config.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 3: Remove from plugin-validator</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Remove <code>@jay-framework/editor-protocol</code> dependency</li>\n' +
      '<li>Remove from <code>vite.config.ts</code> externals</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 4: Stop publishing</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Remove editor packages from publish scripts / CI</li>\n' +
      '<li>Mark as deprecated on npm if already published</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><code>yarn build</code> succeeds without editor packages</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>yarn test</code> passes</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-stack dev</code> works without editor server</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-stack validate</code> works without editor types</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Deprecate Editor Packages","number":160}'
  }
}
