{
  post: {
    title: 'Markdown Image Url Resolution',
    content: '<h1>DL#161 — Markdown Image URL Resolution</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The markdown plugin (<code>@jay-framework/markdown</code>) renders <code>.md</code> files via the <code>markdown-pages</code> component. When markdown content contains relative image references like <code>![Diagram](22 - flow.svg)</code>, the rendered HTML produces <code>&lt;img src=&quot;22%20-%20flow.svg&quot;&gt;</code> relative to the page URL — but no static file exists at that route. The dev server interprets it as a markdown page request and fails:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">GET /design-log/22%20-%20serialized%20mutable%20flow%202.svg\n' +
      "Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open 'content/22 - serialized mutable flow 2.svg.md'</code></pre>\n" +
      '<p>The images sit alongside the <code>.md</code> files in the content directory, but that directory isn&#39;t served as static files.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Relative image paths in markdown resolve against the page URL, not the content directory</li>\n' +
      '<li>The content directory isn&#39;t exposed as a public-accessible path</li>\n' +
      '<li>No mechanism to rewrite image URLs to externally hosted versions (e.g., CDN)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Three layers. Layers 1+2 work together as the zero-config default. Layer 3 replaces both when provided.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Layer 1: Rewrite relative URLs to content directory path</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In the markdown parser, intercept <code>&lt;img src=&quot;...&quot;&gt;</code> tags. If <code>src</code> is relative (not <code>http://</code> or <code>https://</code>), rewrite it to be served from the public folder where layer 2 copies the files.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Use marked&#39;s <code>renderer.image</code> override with an <code>imageBaseUrl</code> computed from the content directory&#39;s public-relative path.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Layer 2: Copy media files to public directory (default)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>During <code>loadParams</code> (build time), scan the content directory for non-<code>.md</code> files (images, SVGs, diagrams) and copy them to the project&#39;s <code>public/</code> folder under a matching path. The public folder path is read from the <code>.jay</code> config (<code>devServer.publicFolder</code>, defaults to <code>./public</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<p>This is the <strong>default behavior</strong> — no props needed. Images alongside markdown files are automatically made available as static assets.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">contentDir: design-log/content/\n' +
      'public folder: ./public/\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Copy: design-log/content/22 - flow.svg\n' +
      '  →   public/design-log/content/22 - flow.svg\n' +
      '\n' +
      'URL rewrite: &lt;img src=&quot;/design-log/content/22%20-%20flow.svg&quot;&gt;</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Layer 3: Media mapping file (replaces layers 1+2)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Optional <code>mediaMap</code> prop pointing to a YAML file that maps local filenames to CDN URLs with responsive variants:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token comment"># media-map.yaml — generated by an upload script</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token string">'22 - flow.svg'</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n` +
      '  width<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token number">800</span>\n' +
      '  height<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token number">600</span>\n' +
      `  src<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/abc123/v1/fill/w_800,h_600/flow.webp'</span>\n` +
      '  srcset<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> url<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/abc123/v1/fill/w_400,h_300/flow.webp'</span>\n` +
      '      width<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token number">400</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> url<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/abc123/v1/fill/w_800,h_600/flow.webp'</span>\n` +
      '      width<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token number">800</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token string">'diagram.png'</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n` +
      '  width<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token number">1200</span>\n' +
      '  height<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token number">900</span>\n' +
      `  src<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/def456/v1/fill/w_1200,h_900/diagram.webp'</span>\n` +
      '  srcset<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> url<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/def456/v1/fill/w_400,h_300/diagram.webp'</span>\n` +
      '      width<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token number">400</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> url<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/def456/v1/fill/w_800,h_600/diagram.webp'</span>\n` +
      '      width<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token number">800</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> url<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/def456/v1/fill/w_1200,h_900/diagram.webp'</span>\n` +
      '      width<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token number">1200</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;</span> ...<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  contentDir: .<span class="token punctuation">/</span>content\n' +
      '  mediaMap: .<span class="token punctuation">/</span>media-map.yaml\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>When <code>mediaMap</code> is provided:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Mapped images use the external URL — no file copying, no local serving</li>\n' +
      '<li>Unmapped images fall back to layers 1+2</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>width</code> and <code>height</code> from the mapping are added to the <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> tag (prevents CLS)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>srcset</code> variants produce responsive <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> with <code>srcset</code> and <code>sizes</code> attributes</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Rendered output for a mapped image with srcset:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;img</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;https://cdn.../w_800/flow.webp&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">srcset</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;\n' +
      '    https://cdn.../w_400/flow.webp   400w,\n' +
      '    https://cdn.../w_800/flow.webp   800w,\n' +
      '    https://cdn.../w_1200/flow.webp 1200w\n' +
      '  &quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">sizes</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;(max-width: 600px) 400px, (max-width: 1024px) 800px, 1200px&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">width</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;800&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">height</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;600&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">loading</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;lazy&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">alt</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;Diagram&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Without srcset (just <code>src</code> + dimensions):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;https://cdn.../w_800/flow.webp&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">width</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;800&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">height</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;600&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">loading</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;lazy&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">alt</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;Diagram&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h4>Upload script responsibilities</h4>\n' +
      '<p>The upload script is external tooling (not part of the markdown plugin). It:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Scans the content directory for image files</li>\n' +
      '<li>Reads original dimensions (e.g., using <code>sharp</code> or <code>image-size</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Uploads to CDN (e.g., wix-media API) requesting responsive variants at configured breakpoints</li>\n' +
      '<li>Writes/updates the <code>media-map.yaml</code> file</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>The script decides what responsive widths to generate. Typical breakpoints: <code>[400, 800, 1200]</code>. For each image, it generates variants up to the original width (no upscaling).</p>\n' +
      '<p>Input configuration (script-specific, not part of the plugin):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token comment"># upload-config.yaml (example)</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">breakpoints</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token number">400</span>, <span class="token number">800</span>, <span class="token number">1200</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">format</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> webp\n' +
      '<span '... 4281 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Markdown Image Url Resolution","number":161}'
  }
}
[Build] 86/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=161-markdown-image-url-resolution)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Structural Headfull Components',
    content: '<h1>DL#162 — Structural Headfull Components (No Code File)</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Headfull full-stack components currently require three files: <code>.jay-html</code>, <code>.jay-contract</code>, and <code>.ts</code>. The <code>.ts</code> file provides the component definition via <code>makeJayStackComponent</code>, including render phase implementations.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Many headfull components are purely <strong>structural</strong> — shared headers, footers, layout wrappers. They have props but no data logic, no services, no render phases. Their <code>.ts</code> file is boilerplate:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">const</span> header <span class="token operator">=</span> makeJayStackComponent<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>HeaderContract<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span>withProps<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>HeaderProps<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withFastRender</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token function">async </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>props<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token function">phaseOutput</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> logoUrl<span class="token operator">:</span> props<span class="token punctuation">.</span>logoUrl <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This creates a role boundary problem: the designer creates the template and contract, but needs the developer to write trivial passthrough code before the component works.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Structural headfull components require boilerplate <code>.ts</code> files</li>\n' +
      '<li>The designer role cannot create a complete headfull component independently</li>\n' +
      '<li>Agents frequently get the <code>.ts</code> wrong (missing <code>.withProps()</code>, wrong types)</li>\n' +
      '<li>The contract already declares everything needed — props and their types</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Allow headfull imports without <code>src</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>When a headfull import has <code>contract</code> but no <code>src</code>, treat it as a structural component. The framework generates a passthrough component automatically:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token comment">&lt;!-- No src attribute — structural component --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;script</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headfull&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;../components/site-header/site-header&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">names</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;SiteHeader&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token attribute">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;../components/site-header/site-header.jay-contract&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Wait — the <code>src</code> currently points at the <code>.ts</code> file AND identifies the component&#39;s jay-html directory. We need <code>src</code> for the jay-html location. The question is whether <code>src</code> must resolve to a <code>.ts</code> file.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Approach: auto-generate component when <code>.ts</code> is missing</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Keep <code>src</code> required (it locates the component directory and jay-html). But when the <code>.ts</code> file doesn&#39;t exist at that path:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Parser</strong> — skip <code>analyzeExportedTypes()</code>, derive types from contract only</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Compiler</strong> — generate an inline passthrough component instead of importing from the module</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Dev server</strong> — create a synthetic component definition that passes props → ViewState</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Production build</strong> — same synthetic component</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>The synthetic component behaves as:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">makeJayStackComponent<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>Contract<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span>withProps<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>Props<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withFastRender</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token function">async </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>props<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token function">phaseOutput</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>props<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>All contract props become ViewState fields at fast phase. No slow phase, no interactive phase, no services.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>What the designer creates (two files only)</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">src/components/site-header/\n' +
      '  site-header.jay-html       # template\n' +
      '  site-header.jay-contract   # props declaration</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>No <code>.ts</code> file needed. The <code>src</code> attribute in the import still points to <code>../components/site-header/site-header</code> — the framework looks for <code>.ts</code> there, and when it&#39;s absent, generates the passthrough automatically.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Parser</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong><code>compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-html-parser.ts</code></strong> — in <code>parseHeadfullFSImports()</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>When resolving <code>src</code>, check if the <code>.ts</code> file exists</li>\n' +
      '<li>If missing, skip <code>analyzeExportedTypes()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Create a synthetic <code>codeLink</code> with a generated component name</li>\n' +
      '<li>Derive ViewState type from contract props (all props → fast phase data tags)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Dev server loading</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong><code>stack-server-runtime/lib/load-page-parts.ts</code></strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>When loading headfull component module, check if file exists</li>\n' +
      '<li>If missing, create a synthetic <code>compDefinition</code> with fast render that passes props through</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 3: Production build</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong><code>production-server/lib/builder/load-production-parts.ts</code></strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Same synthetic component fallback</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 4: Compiler code generation</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong><code>compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-html-compiler.ts</code></strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>When no code module exists, generate inline component definition instead of import statement</li>\n' +
      '<li>The generated code creates a passthrough component in-place</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 5: Validation</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong><code>stack-cli/lib/validate.ts</code></strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Don&#39;t error when headfull component has no <code>.ts</code> file (if contract exists)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Validate that structural components don&#39;t declare render phases they can&#39;t have</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Should the developer be able to add a <code>.ts</code> later to upgrade a structural component to a full component? (Yes — if <code>.ts</code> exists, use it; if not, use passthrough)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Should we support interactive refs in structural components? (No — refs require component code to handle events. Structural components are render-only.)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Trade-offs</h2>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Choice</th>\n' +
      '<th>Pro</th>\n' +
      '<th>Con</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Auto-generate from contract</td>\n' +
      '<td>Designer-independent, zero boilerplate</td>\n' +
      '<td>Less explicit, &quot;magic&quot; behavior</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Keep requiring <code>.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Explicit, no special cases</td>\n' +
      '<td>Role boundary problem, boilerplate</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Generate <code>.ts</code> on <code>agent-kit</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>File exists for inspection</td>\n' +
      '<td>Generated code to maintain</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Results</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Key insight: structural = template fragment, not component</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The original design proposed a synthetic passthrough component (props → ViewState). This was wrong. A structural component has <strong>no props, no tags, no ViewState</strong>. It&#39;s a reusable template fragment — the <code>&lt;jay:&gt;</code> tag is unwrapped and its content becomes plain HTML in the parent.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Data inside a structural component comes from <strong>headless imports declared in its own <code>&lt;head&gt;</code></strong>, not from the parent via props.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>What changed (simplified from original plan)</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Parser</strong> (<code>jay-html-parser.ts</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Check if <code>.ts</code> file exists after resolving <code>src</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>If missing: inject the co'... 2222 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Structural Headfull Components","number":162}'
  }
}
[Build] 87/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=162-structural-headfull-components)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Main And Sandbox Secure Contexts',
    content: '<h1>Main and Sandbox secure Contexts</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>This design log captures the modeling of the <code>Context</code> as in Content API used to derive the\n' +
      'communication between the main and sandbox environments.</p>\n' +
      '<p>We denote in this section</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Context - the Context API</li>\n' +
      '<li>main environment - the main running context, as the main window, running elements</li>\n' +
      '<li>sandbox environment - the secure running context, as worker or iframe, running components</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>the problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The problem to solve is the mapping of</p>\n' +
      '<p>[1] <code>(component bridge in main.compId) === (element bridge in sandbox.compId)</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>To derive this identity, we use the positional relation to create a mapping</p>\n' +
      '<p>[2] <code>(parent comp.compId + coordinate) ==&gt; (comp.compId)</code></p>\n' +
      '<p>Once the mapping [2] is created, we communicate the mapping between environments to ensure\n' +
      'the same the first identity [1] above.</p>\n' +
      '<p>It is important to note that [2] happens in both environments</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>static elements and components are first created in the main environment</li>\n' +
      '<li>dynamic elements and components (children of forEach) are first created in the sandbox environment</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Creating the mapping [2] in main environment</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The regular element structure (non secure) with a child component looks like</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">return</span> ConstructContext<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withRootContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  viewState<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token function">e</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'div'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token function">childComp</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '        Basic<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      `        <span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> safe<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">''</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> firstName<span class="token operator">:</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token operator">:</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>lastName <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        <span class="token string">'comp1'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  options<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>To derive the <code>{compId, coordinate}</code> we note that</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>the element parent component bridge has the parent compId -\n' +
      'which can be provided as a <code>SecureComponentContext</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>if the element is the root of the secure environment (it&#39;s parent is a regular component)\n' +
      'we add to the element root the <code>SecureRootMain</code> which can provide the <code>SecureComponentContext</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>the <code>childComp</code> has the <code>coordinate</code> of the child component within the element\n' +
      '(the <code>coordinate</code> is computed by the <code>ConstructionContext</code> using the <code>refName</code> parameter)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>The same running in a secure mode, in the main environment,</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">return</span> ConstructContext<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withRootContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  viewState<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token function">SecureRootMain</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      `      <span class="token function">e</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'div'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>\n` +
      '        <span class="token function">childCompMain</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '          Basic<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      `          <span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> safe<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">''</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> firstName<span class="token operator">:</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token operator">:</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>lastName <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `          <span class="token string">'comp1'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  options<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>at which (for a component at the root of the secure environment)</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">  SecureRootMain                                    -- provides SecureComponentContext (compId)\n' +
      '  |-- element\n' +
      '      |-- childCompMain                             -- provides SecureCoordinateContext (coordinate)\n' +
      '          |-- makeJayComponentBridge                -- Consumes SecureComponentContext, SecureCoordinateContext\n' +
      '                                                    -- provides new SecureComponentContext (compId, endpoint)\n' +
      '              |-- makeJayComponent\n' +
      '                  |-- makeComponentBridgeConstructor\n' +
      '</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>and for a child component of another component in a secure environment</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">  makeComponentBridgeConstructor                    -- provides SecureComponentContext\n' +
      '  |-- element\n' +
      '      |-- childCompMain                             -- provides SecureCoordinateContext\n' +
      '          |-- makeJayComponentBridge                -- Consumes SecureComponentContext, SecureCoordinateContext\n' +
      '                                                    -- provides new SecureComponentContext (compId, endpoint)\n' +
      '              |-- makeJayComponent\n' +
      '                  |-- makeComponentBridgeConstructor\n' +
      '</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Creating the mapping [2] in sandbox environment</h2>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">  workerRoot                                        -- provides SandboxComponentContext\n' +
      '  | -- workerChildComp                              -- provides SandboxCoordinateContext\n' +
      '       | -- makeJayComponent\n' +
      '            | -- elementBridge                      -- Consumes SecureComponentContext, SecureCoordinateContext\n' +
      '                                                    -- provides new SecureComponentContext (compId, endpoint)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Main And Sandbox Secure Contexts","number":17}'
  }
}
