{
  post: {
    title: 'Update On Conditional',
    content: '<h1>Update on Conditional</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>Conditional, as implemented today, creates the condition child elements\n' +
      'immediately on creation, even if the condition is <code>false</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This imposes a potential performance impact, as we may be doing\n' +
      'unneeded work on creation time.</p>\n' +
      '<p>However, this design also simplifies <code>refs</code> as the <code>refs</code> to static\n' +
      'elements as children of a condition are just static refs.</p>\n' +
      '<p>If we change condition to create the children lazily on first turning to <code>true</code>,\n' +
      'it means that <code>refs</code> to children of a condition has to support the case of children not created yet,\n' +
      'and turn into a construct similar to <code>refs</code> for a collection.</p>\n' +
      '<p>For now, we vote to keep the design decision as is.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Update On Conditional","number":18}'
  }
}
