{
  post: {
    title: 'Component Compiler',
    content: '<h1>Component Compiler</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>Once we open the door for a component compiler in Jay, we should consider what other\n' +
      'component compilations we want to introduce.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Secure Events transformation</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The first transformation comes from security point of view, transforming</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// component file</span>\n' +
      'refs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>input\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span>$<span class="token function">oninput</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> event <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>event<span class="token punctuation">.</span>target as HTMLInputElement<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>value<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">then</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> event <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token function">setText</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>event<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>into</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// component file</span>\n' +
      `refs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>input<span class="token punctuation">.</span>$<span class="token function">oninput</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>$handler<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>Event<span class="token punctuation">,</span> CompViewState<span class="token punctuation">,</span> any<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'1'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">then</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> event <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token function">setText</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>event<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// native-funcs.ts</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">const</span> funcRepository<span class="token operator">:</span> FunctionsRepository <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token string">'1'</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> event<span class="token operator">:</span> Event <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>event<span class="token punctuation">.</span>target as HTMLInputElement<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>value<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Jay Element transformation</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The second potential transformation is the extraction of JSX from the component file\n' +
      'to create the Jay Element.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The potential is to extract the Jay Element DOM structure from the JSX and auto generate\n' +
      'the data script.</p>\n' +
      '<p>It does create a challenge of handling JSX fragments and code lists of fragments, which can be modelled\n' +
      'as internal JayElements.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Consider the component with JSX</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript jsx">export interface CounterProps {\n' +
      '    title: string\n' +
      '    initialCount: number\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function CounterConstructor({title, initialCount}: Props&lt;CounterProps&gt;, refs: CounterElementRefs) {\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    let [count, setCount] = createState(initialCount)\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    refs.subtracter.onclick(() =&gt; setCount(count() - 1));\n' +
      '    refs.adder.onclick(() =&gt; setCount(count() + 1));\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    return {\n' +
      '        render: () =&gt; (&lt;div&gt;\n' +
      '            &lt;div&gt;{title}&lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '            &lt;div&gt;\n' +
      '                &lt;button onclick={() =&gt; setCount(count() - 1)}&gt;-&lt;/button&gt;\n' +
      '                &lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0 16px&quot;&gt;{count}&lt;/span&gt;\n' +
      '                &lt;button onclick={() =&gt; setCount(count() + 1)}&gt;+&lt;/button&gt;\n' +
      '            &lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '        &lt;/div&gt;),\n' +
      '    }\n' +
      '}</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>which can be compiled into</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript jsx">// componnet file\n' +
      'export interface CounterProps {\n' +
      '    title: string\n' +
      '    initialCount: number\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function CounterConstructor({title, initialCount}: Props&lt;CounterProps&gt;, refs: CounterElementRefs) {\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    let [count, setCount] = createState(initialCount)\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    refs.r1.onclick(() =&gt; setCount(count() - 1));\n' +
      '    refs.r2.onclick(() =&gt; setCount(count() + 1));\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    return {\n' +
      '        render: () =&gt; ({title, count}),\n' +
      '    }\n' +
      '}\n' +
      '\n' +
      '// element file\n' +
      '&lt;html&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;head&gt;\n' +
      '        &lt;script type=&quot;application/yaml-jay&quot;&gt;\n' +
      '    data:\n' +
      'title: string | number\n' +
      'count: string | number\n' +
      '&lt;/script&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;/head&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;body&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;div&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;div&gt;{title}&lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;div&gt;\n' +
      '        &lt;button ref=&quot;r1&quot;&gt;-&lt;/button&gt;\n' +
      '        &lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0 16px&quot;&gt;{count}&lt;/span&gt;\n' +
      '        &lt;button ref=&quot;r2&quot;&gt;+&lt;/button&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;/body&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Astro Style syntax</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Another option is to use Astro style API instead of React / JSX like API, which turns into</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html typescript">---\n' +
      'export interface CounterProps {\n' +
      '    title: string\n' +
      '    initialCount: number\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function CounterConstructor({title, initialCount}: Props&lt;CounterProps&gt;, refs: CounterElementRefs) {\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    let [count, setCount] = createState(initialCount)\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    refs.r1.onclick(() =&gt; setCount(count() - 1));\n' +
      '    refs.r2.onclick(() =&gt; setCount(count() + 1));\n' +
      '    \n' +
      '    return {\n' +
      '      render: () =&gt; ({title, count})\n' +
      '    }\n' +
      '}\n' +
      '---\n' +
      '\n' +
      '&lt;div&gt;\n' +
      '  &lt;div&gt;{title}&lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '  &lt;div&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;button ref=&quot;sub&quot;&gt;-&lt;/button&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0 16px&quot;&gt;{count}&lt;/span&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;button ref=&quot;add&quot;&gt;+&lt;/button&gt;\n' +
      '  &lt;/div&gt;\n' +
      '&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Client - Server splitting / transformation</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Another potential is to split the component code for server and client bundles,\n' +
      'addressing the needs to</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>start rendering the component on the server using server only code,\n' +
      'potentially creating initial state</li>\n' +
      '<li>continue running the component on the client, continuing using state</li>\n' +
      '<li>creating calls from the client to the server</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>An example of how such a component syntax can look like</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> interface CounterProps <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  title<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  initialCount<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  dbConnection$<span class="token operator">:</span> DBConnection<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">CounterConstructor</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">{</span> title<span class="token punctuation">,</span> initialCount<span class="token punctuation">,</span> dbConnection$ <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Props<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>CounterProps<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  refs<span class="token operator">:</span> CounterElementRefs<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">let</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>count<span class="token punctuation">,</span> setCount<span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">createState</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>initialCount<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">initTask$</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token function">async </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token keyword">let</span> dbCount <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token keyword">await</span> dbConnection$<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">query</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'select count from counters where title = ?'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token function">title</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span'... 23088 more characters,
