{
  post: {
    title: 'Alternative To Context API',
    content: '<h1>Alternative to Context API</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>The React context API is a great tool to prevent property drilling. Lets first understand\n' +
      'the problem and the React Context solution, and why React Context is still a tradeoff.\n' +
      'We then suggest a better alternative, with the tradeoff that it has to be built into framework.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>What is property drilling?</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Property Drilling is the pattern of passing data via multiple nested components or function\n' +
      'calls (remember that JSX is actually function calls to <code>React.createElement</code>).\n' +
      'In Short, property drilling can be expressed as functions or react elements, and looks like</p>\n' +
      '<p>manifestation for functions</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">f</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">//....</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">g</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">g</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">//....</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">h</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">h</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">//....</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">i</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">i</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>manifestation for React components</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript jsx">function f(firstName, lastName) {\n' +
      '    return (&lt;&gt;&lt;g firstName={firstName} lastName={lastName}/&gt;&lt;/&gt;)\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function g(firstName, lastName) {\n' +
      '    return (&lt;&gt;&lt;h firstName={firstName} lastName={lastName}/&gt;&lt;/&gt;)\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function h(firstName, lastName) {\n' +
      '    return (&lt;&gt;&lt;i firstName={firstName} lastName={lastName}/&gt;&lt;/&gt;)\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function i(firstName, lastName) {\n' +
      '    return (&lt;span&gt;{firstName} {lastName}&lt;/span&gt;)\n' +
      '}</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>In both cases, it is clear that the functions <code>g</code> and <code>h</code>, or components <code>g</code> and <code>h</code> do not need\n' +
      'to know about the properties <code>firstname</code> and <code>lastName</code>, they are only passing those around\n' +
      'from <code>f</code> to <code>i</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>The React Context solution</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The react context solution enables to pass the properties <code>firstName</code> and <code>lastName</code> almost magically\n' +
      'from <code>f</code> to <code>i</code>. Lets see it in action first</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript jsx">let context = React.createContext(null);\n' +
      'function f(firstName, lastName) {\n' +
      '    return (&lt;context.Provider value = {{firstName, lastName}}&gt;\n' +
      '        &lt;g/&gt;\n' +
      '    &lt;/context.Provider&gt;)\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function g() {\n' +
      '    return (&lt;&gt;&lt;h/&gt;&lt;/&gt;)\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function h() {\n' +
      '    return (&lt;&gt;&lt;i/&gt;&lt;/&gt;)\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function i() {\n' +
      '    const { fName, lName } = useContext(context);\n' +
      '    return (&lt;span&gt;{firstName} {lastName}&lt;/span&gt;)\n' +
      '}</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>as we can see, the context API has solved one problem - we do not need to pass the <code>firstName</code>\n' +
      'and <code>lastName</code> properties via <code>g</code> and <code>h</code> - both of those components do not depends on those properties.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Before talking about the downside of the context API, lets consider how to do the same for pure functions -</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">f</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">//....</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">provideContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token function">g</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">g</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">//....</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">h</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">h</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">//....</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">i</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">i</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">let</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> firstName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> lastName <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> _context<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>a very simplistic implementation of <code>provideContext</code> can be (not really production grade)</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">let</span> _context<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">provideContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>context<span class="token operator">:</span> any<span class="token punctuation">,</span> func<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token keyword">void</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">try</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    _context <span class="token operator">=</span> context<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token function">func</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">finally</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    _context <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token keyword">undefined</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>What are the problems with a Context API?</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The main problem with the Context API is that it has modelled the dependency of component\n' +
      'or function <code>i</code> as a hidden dependency - the dependency is not clear from the signature of\n' +
      'the function or component.</p>\n' +
      '<p>If we want to reuse the <code>i</code> function or component, we need to provide the context, and the\n' +
      'only three ways to find out about the dependency are 1. to read the code of <code>i</code>,\n' +
      'which can be long and complex. 2. to read the docs of <code>i</code> and 3. to run <code>i</code> and start debugging for errors.</p>\n' +
      '<p>As we can see, all three are far from ideal.</p>\n' +
      '<p>What if we can create a different context API, one such that prevents property drilling while\n' +
      'explicitly defines the dependencies of &#39;i&#39;?</p>\n' +
      '<h1>Alternative Context API - prop cascading</h1>\n' +
      '<p>The idea of property cascading is that given a component, the component inputs should only be using properties.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>When using the component, it is not required to provide all the properties.\n' +
      'Any unprovided properties of the component become properties of '... 1746 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Alternative To Context API","number":21}'
  }
}
