{
  post: {
    title: 'JSON Compare And Patch',
    content: '<h1>JSON Compare and Patch</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>Given the work in <a href="22-serialized-mutable">Serialization Mutable</a> it is clear we need algorithms for\n' +
      'computing the JSON Patch and applying the JSON Patch. We need those algorithms to be small (code wise), efficient\n' +
      'and such that we can extend with our specifics (<code>immer</code>, <code>jay mutable</code>, <code>list-compare</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<p>A good resource of available work is <a href="https://jsonpatch.com/">jsonpatch</a>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="https://github.com/streamich/json-joy">json-joy</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>Very solid and well written library, yet not really browser ready. License is Apache 2.0.\n' +
      'Includes</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>JSON patch apply algorithm</li>\n' +
      '<li>great starter code for <a href="https://github.com/streamich/json-joy/tree/master/src/json-equal">json-equals</a> which can be a base\n' +
      'for comparing two JSON objects for a JSON patch</li>\n' +
      '<li>serialization benchmarks in <a href="https://github.com/streamich/json-joy/tree/master/src/json-pack">json-pack</a> from which we learn\n' +
      '<code>JSON.stringify</code> and <code>JSON.parse</code> are great</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="https://github.com/dharmafly/jsonpatch.js">jsonpatch.js</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>old library to just apply a patch on objects.</p>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="http://bruth.github.io/jsonpatch-js/">jsonpatch-js</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>old library to just apply a patch on objects.\n' +
      'can also generate a function that given a patch, generates a function to apply it to objects.</p>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="https://github.com/cujojs/jiff">jiff</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>old library, does both diff and patch. looks like solid and fast implementation. MIT license.\n' +
      'It does an <code>O(N^2)</code> array comparison algorithm by first serializing all array elements, then creating a comparison\n' +
      'matrix.</p>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="https://github.com/Starcounter-Jack/JSON-Patch">JSON-Patch</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>recently active, MIT.\n' +
      'Does diff and patch.</p>\n' +
      '<p>It has a solid compare algorithm at <a href="https://github.com/Starcounter-Jack/JSON-Patch/blob/master/src/duplex.ts#L143">duplex.ts</a>,\n' +
      'which does not take into account moved array items.</p>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="https://github.com/sonnyp/JSON8">JSON8</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>has the <a href="https://github.com/sonnyp/JSON8/tree/main/packages/patch">patch</a> library, which is a bit old, ISC license.\n' +
      'Very efficient and concise diff and apply algorithm, not compliant to JSON-patch, does not take into account moved array items</p>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="https://github.com/rubeniskov/mutant-json">mutant-json</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>Only applies patches. 3 years old, MIT license</p>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="https://github.com/josdejong/immutable-json-patch">immutable-json-patch</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>active. Only applies patches. ISC license.</p>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="https://github.com/chbrown/rfc6902">rfc6902</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>MIT license, does both diff and patch.\n' +
      'has an interesting dynamic programming diff algorithm. However, the algorithm does not do move operations.\n' +
      'Instead, it does work to optimize for small insert / remove operations of items, making it a good candidate algorithm.</p>\n' +
      '<p>has also a good apply algorithm which updates in place</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Candidate algorithm</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>NO</strong> - simple validation on a 100x100 matrix with 100 updates shows seconds of runtime!!!\n' +
      'see <a href="../exploration/rfc6902">/exploration/rfc6902</a></p>\n' +
      '<h2><a href="https://github.com/immerjs/immer">immer</a></h2>\n' +
      '<p>Immer has a json patch algorithm that is not decoupled from immer, can only be used as part of immer.\n' +
      'The algorithm does a comparison between objects that does not handle array added, removed or moved items.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"JSON Compare And Patch","number":23}'
  }
}
