{
  post: {
    title: 'Refactor Refs',
    content: '<h1>Refactor Refs</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>First of all, lets understand why.</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p>today, references are created as part of the <code>JayElement</code> creation, which is done\n' +
      'as part of the render function <code>render: (vs: ViewState) =&gt; JayElement</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>However, we have a cycling problem with <code>JayComponent</code>, that requires <code>refs</code> to run\n' +
      'the initial function to create the <code>ViewState</code> which is used for the render function which\n' +
      'creates the <code>refs</code>...</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p>We have two implementations of <code>Refs</code> - for main and sandbox, and those are different</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p>We have 4 types of <code>Refs</code> for each environment - HTML element, collection of HTML Elements\n' +
      'Component and collection of components. In effect, we also need to have 2 additional types for\n' +
      'conditional HTML Element and conditional component</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p>We have inconsistencies in declaring <code>Refs</code> - for the main environment, we declare the dynamic\n' +
      'refs. For the sandbox environment, we declare dynamic elements and components</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>All of the above &quot;smalls&quot; like we need a new pattern</p>\n' +
      '<h1>The new Pattern</h1>\n' +
      '<p>We want a pattern at which when creating the <code>JayElement</code>, the <code>refs</code> are created first, allowing\n' +
      'the component to be created, generate the <code>ViewState</code>, then render the <code>JayElement</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>In essence, it is moving from</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">render</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token operator">:</span> ViewState<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> JayElement<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>into</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">mkElement</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> JayElement<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> refs<span class="token operator">:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> Ref<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token keyword">const</span> title <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>refs<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'title'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token keyword">const</span> name <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>refs<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'name'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token comment">// ... declare refs</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token function">publicRefsAPI</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>refs<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">render</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token operator">:</span> ViewState<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> JayElement<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Using this pattern we will create all refs - static, conditional or collection (denoted dynamic above)\n' +
      'in the first section, transform all to their public API and return both the <code>refs</code> and <code>render</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h1>lets explore the Refs API</h1>\n' +
      '<h2>private API</h2>\n' +
      '<p>looking at <code>element.ts/mkRef</code> before this refactor -</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">mkRef</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  refName<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  referenced<span class="token operator">:</span> HTMLElement <span class="token operator">|</span> JayComponent<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>any<span class="token punctuation">,</span> any<span class="token punctuation">,</span> any<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  updates<span class="token operator">:</span> updateFunc<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>any<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  mounts<span class="token operator">:</span> MountFunc<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  unmounts<span class="token operator">:</span> MountFunc<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  isComp<span class="token operator">:</span> boolean<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">let</span> context <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">currentConstructionContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">let</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>ref<span class="token punctuation">,</span> update<span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> context<span class="token punctuation">.</span>refManager<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">mkRef</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>referenced<span class="token punctuation">,</span> context<span class="token punctuation">,</span> refName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> isComp<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  updates<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">push</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>update<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>context<span class="token punctuation">.</span>forStaticElements<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    context<span class="token punctuation">.</span>refManager<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">addStaticRef</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>refName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> ref<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">else</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">let</span> refManager <span class="token operator">=</span> context<span class="token punctuation">.</span>refManager<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    mounts<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">push</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> refManager<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">addDynamicRef</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>refName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> ref<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    unmounts<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">push</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> refManager<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">removeDynamicRef</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>refName<span class="token punctuation">,</span> ref<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>we see that the interaction of the <code>element.ts</code> structure with refs is contained within a simple contract -</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>when we have an element, static or dynamic, we create a ref in'... 9855 more characters,
