{
  post: {
    title: 'Guiding Principles Of Jay',
    content: '<h1>Guiding principles of Jay</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>1. no magic</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay tries to be as <code>Typescript</code> compatible as possible.</p>\n' +
      '<p>A few examples -</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>for the <code>.jay.html</code> files we generate <code>.d.ts</code> files that represent what those files are compiled into</li>\n' +
      '<li>Jay components are defined using the <code>makeJayComponent</code> function</li>\n' +
      '<li>the Jay state management library is explicit, not relaying on compiler magic</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>2. Make decisions as early as possible, no dead code</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Any decision that can be done by the compiler has to be done by the compiler, not at runtime.\n' +
      'We strive to have a runtime condition free - without <code>if</code>, <code>?</code> or <code>switch</code> statements.\n' +
      'The only valid <code>if</code> is to check <code>if (oldValue !== newValue)</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>We consider a site rendering as having 4 stages</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>compiler - at which we compile and build the application based on the application code</li>\n' +
      '<li>SSG - at which we compile and optimize the application based on additional inputs.</li>\n' +
      '<li>SSR - at which we render the application on a server</li>\n' +
      '<li>CSR - at which we make the application interactive on the client</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Each stage can make decisions that render some of the code &quot;dead&quot; for the next phase. Such dead code has to be eliminated\n' +
      'and not shipped to the next phase.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>3. Reactive</h2>\n' +
      '<p>All updates are fine grained reactive, based on states (signals) and computed values.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>4. immutable data</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay is built with the assumption that data is immutable.</p>\n' +
      '<p>(denote version of a value with a subscript like a<sub>1</sub> or a<sub>2</sub>)</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>If a<sub>1</sub> !== a<sub>2</sub> we assume &#39;a&#39; has changed, and will trigger DOM update.</li>\n' +
      '<li>if a<sub>1</sub> === a<sub>2</sub> we assume &#39;a&#39; has not changed, and will not trigger DOM update.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>same goes for deep objects</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>If a.b.c<sub>1</sub> !== a.b.c<sub>2</sub> we assume &#39;c&#39; has changed, but only if also a.b<sub>1</sub> !== a.b<sub>2</sub> and a<sub>1</sub> !== a<sub>2</sub>.</li>\n' +
      '<li>if any of a.b.c<sub>1</sub> === a.b.c<sub>2</sub> a.b<sub>1</sub> === a.b<sub>2</sub> and a<sub>1</sub> === a<sub>2</sub>, we assume &#39;c&#39; has not changed.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The only exception is for collections (arrays of objects) at which case</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>we only update the DOM if the array itself has changed --&gt; arr<sub>1</sub> !== arr<sub>2</sub></li>\n' +
      '<li>for the array items, we check correlation using <code>trackBy</code> id or key - while still requiring the object has been updated.\n' +
      'We require arr[x]<sub>1</sub> !== arr[x]<sub>2</sub>, and then using <code>trackBy</code> we decide if we have a new item or an updated item.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>5. DOM updated based on reconciliation on Data, not Virtual DOM or real DOM.</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Reconciliation on data means we do not reconcile DOM structures that are static in nature, like static attributes,\n' +
      'wrapper semantic / structural / layout elements, etc. We only reconcile on what the application can actually change on runtime.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>6. All components are 3rd party security ready</h2>\n' +
      '<p>All jay components can run as secure / sandboxed 3rd party components.\n' +
      'There is special syntax for 3rd party components to ensure security.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>7. Zero Trust</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay is based on the zero trust principle, meaning we consider all 3rd party code (any component code) as untrusted.\n' +
      'We only run selective code extracted from the component in the main environment (trusted environment), based on\n' +
      'models of trusted code extraction from untrusted code.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Those include</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>extracting declarative code, like Jay Files or JSX declarative statements</li>\n' +
      '<li>extracting code matching declared patterns</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>In the future, also 3. AI Based models</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Guiding Principles Of Jay","number":27}'
  }
}
