{
  post: {
    title: 'Runtime Compiler',
    content: '<h1>Runtime compiler</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Intro</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Runtime compiler is one of the most different aspects of Jay compared to other web frameworks.\n' +
      'It does not only transforms code to JavaScript, but also splits the logic into main and worker flows.\n' +
      'The first version of Jay runtime compiler only handles client side, it does not tackle SSR and SSG yet.\n' +
      'On high level, the compiler splits trusted code from secure - one to be run on the browser thread, the other on the worker thread.</p>\n' +
      '<p>It&#39;s a first version of the compiler, so the implementation details will change.\n' +
      'Currently, compilation is done by a single plugin.\n' +
      'It&#39;s simple to reason about, but it does not provide the ability to scan all the imported dependencies code\n' +
      'and use the collected information in the transformation step.\n' +
      'Multiple plugins will be introduced to solve this problem.\n' +
      'They will be packaged as a single plugin for the user convenience.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation details</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Let&#39;s take the counter application example.\n' +
      'It defines typescript config, and Vite build.\n' +
      'Typescript config is required, as Jay only supports typescript.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Bundler</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Vite is used as a bundler: it&#39;s easy to configure and supports HMR out of the box.\n' +
      'Currently, Jay runtime compiler supports Rollup and Vite.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Vite configuration:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> resolve <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'path'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> Inspect <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'vite-plugin-inspect'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> defineConfig <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'vitest/config'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> JayRollupConfig<span class="token punctuation">,</span> jayRuntime <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'jay-vite-plugin'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
