{
  post: {
    title: '4 - Jay Stack - Using Builder',
    content: '<h1>Jay Stack - using builder</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>This option defines the component as a builder, to create the most tight jay stack component definition\n' +
      'which includes full type completion.</p>\n' +
      '<p>While all 3 previous API attempts have failed to capture in the type system how the different stages affect\n' +
      'each other, the builder pattern has potential to solve it.</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>introducing a url parameter in the load parameters stage should enter the type signature for later stages</li>\n' +
      '<li>introducing context should enter the type signature of later stages</li>\n' +
      '<li>introducing slowly rendered data should reduce the dynamic rendered data to what was not slowly rendered.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>However, a builder pattern has one inherit problem, that it is not ordered by default. One can call the\n' +
      'builder pattern functions in any order, including multiple times. Yes, we can check that one runtime, but the type\n' +
      'system by default does not guarantee it. However, using a simple trick we can also support builder pattern ordering.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">const</span> productPage <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">makeJayStackComponent</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>render<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span>withProps<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PropsType<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withServerContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>CONTEXT_1<span class="token punctuation">,</span> CONTEXT_2<span class="token punctuation">,</span> CONTEXT_3<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withClientContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>CONTEXT_1<span class="token punctuation">,</span> CONTEXT_2<span class="token punctuation">,</span> CONTEXT_3<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withLoadParams</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>loadParams<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withSlowly</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>renderSlowly<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withfast</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>renderFast<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withInteractive</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>interactive<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This pattern allows us to refine types as we proceed calling builder functions, while giving developer feedback from\n' +
      'type inference. This pattern allows a developer using inline functions to not define any types for carry forward or\n' +
      'the static and dynamic view states, having them inferred by Typescript.</p>\n' +
      '<p>To solve the inherit ordering problem we define a type based state machine which we use to define for each builder\n' +
      'function when it is available.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Such a pattern looks like</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Define the state progression</span>\n' +
      `type State <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">'Initial'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'NameSet'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'ValueSet'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'FlagSet'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'Built'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Builder type based on state</span>\n' +
      `type Builder<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>S <span class="token keyword">extends</span> State<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> S <span class="token keyword">extends</span> <span class="token string">'Initial'</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">?</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token function">setName</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>name<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Builder<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token string">'NameSet'</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">:</span> S <span class="token keyword">extends</span> <span class="token string">'NameSet'</span>\n` +
      `    <span class="token operator">?</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token function">setValue</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>value<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Builder<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token string">'ValueSet'</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n` +
      `    <span class="token operator">:</span> S <span class="token keyword">extends</span> <span class="token string">'ValueSet'</span>\n` +
      `      <span class="token operator">?</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token function">setFlag</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>flag<span class="token operator">:</span> boolean<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Builder<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token string">'FlagSet'</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n` +
      `      <span class="token operator">:</span> S <span class="token keyword">extends</span> <span class="token string">'FlagSet'</span>\n` +
      '        <span class="token operator">?</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token function">build</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Product <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      `        <span class="token operator">:</span> S <span class="token keyword">extends</span> <span class="token string">'Built'</span>\n` +
      '          <span class="token operator">?</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token function">getProduct</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Product <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '          <span class="token operator">:</span> never<span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>We can utilize the same for our full stack component builder.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The steps we have are</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">type State <span class="token operator">=</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'Props'</span> <span class="token comment">// requires setting the props type. Next allowed states are &quot;ServerContexts&quot;, &quot;ClientContexts&quot;, &quot;UrlLoader&quot;, &quot;Slowly&quot;, &quot;Fast&quot;, &quot;Interactive&quot;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'ServerContexts'</span> <span class="token comment">// allowing to set server contexts. Next allowed states are &quot;ClientContexts&quot;, &quot;UrlLoader&quot;, &quot;Slowly&quot;, &quot;Fast&quot;, &quot;Interactive&quot;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'ClientContexts'</span> <span class="token comment">// allowing to set client contexts. Next allowed states are &quot;UrlLoader&quot;, &quot;Slowly&quot;, &quot;Fast&quot;, &quot;Interactive&quot;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'UrlLoader'</span> <span class="token comment">// allowing to set the urlLoader function. Next allowed states are &quot;Slowly&quot;, &quot;Fast&quot;, &quot;Interactive&quot;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'SlowlyRender'</span> <span class="token comment">// allowing to set slowly render function. Next allowed states are &quot;Fast&quot;, &quot;Interactive&quot;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'FastRender'</span> <span class="token comment">// allowing to set slowly render function. Next allowed states is only &quot;Interactive&quot;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'InteractiveRender'</span> <span class="token comment">// allowing to set the slowly render function. Next step is a placeholder for done</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'Done'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// does not allow setting anything more</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>The full builder is then (before implementing the state machine above)</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> ComponentConstructor<span class="token punctuation">,</span> ContextMarkers<span class="token punctuation">,</span> JayComponentCore <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'jay-component'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> JayElement<span class="token punctuation">,</span> PreRenderElement <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span cla'... 18407 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"4 - Jay Stack - Using Builder","number":34}'
  }
}
