{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay Stack',
    content: '<h1>Jay Stack</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack is the name of the full stack framework for Jay.\n' +
      'Like anything else in Jay, it is first designed to enable a design tool to create designs with collaboration\n' +
      'with a developer building features.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>The requirements for the Jay Stack</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Integrated with a design tool, such that<ol>\n' +
      '<li>A design tool can create new pages</li>\n' +
      '<li>A design tool can add functionality with pre-made contracts to a page</li>\n' +
      '<li>A design tool can use a project defined functionality with project defined contract on a page</li>\n' +
      '<li>A design tool can use pre-made components or project defined components on a page</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li>Support page routing, including<ol>\n' +
      '<li>page url</li>\n' +
      '<li>page url with parameters</li>\n' +
      '<li>page url with optional and catch all parameters</li>\n' +
      '<li>support different error pages</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li>support rendering model for website, including<ol>\n' +
      '<li>url / param loading for pages with params</li>\n' +
      '<li>slowly changing data support and pre-rendering</li>\n' +
      '<li>routing hook to redirect and choose pre-rendered page</li>\n' +
      '<li>fast changing data support and rendering</li>\n' +
      '<li>async data rendering</li>\n' +
      '<li>client hydration and rendering</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li>support an application model, pre-made functionalities that can be installed at the design tool, including<ol>\n' +
      '<li>pre-made page functionality</li>\n' +
      '<li>application global context for setting</li>\n' +
      '<li>application pre-made components to be added to pages</li>\n' +
      '<li>application navigation, how to navigate from one application page to another</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h1>The Key concepts of Jay Stack are</h1>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Pages - similar to any other meta framework, a page is a definition file that generates one or more website pages</li>\n' +
      '<li>Page Component - the Jay Component of the page. A Page can have more then one Page Component (due to applications).</li>\n' +
      '<li>Application - an entity to be installed at the design tool. An application consists of Designed Pages, Page Components,\n' +
      'General application context and settings and Application Components.</li>\n' +
      '<li>Jay Components - including the Jay component and Jay element.</li>\n' +
      '<li>Backend code</li>\n' +
      '<li>Frontend code</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>File-system layout</h2>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">/src\n' +
      '  /pages\n' +
      '    /page.jay-html           -- index page on route /\n' +
      '    /products\n' +
      '      /[slug]/page.jay-html        -- product page on route /products/[slug], where slug is a parameter\n' +
      '    /[[lang]]/shop            -- optional parameter\n' +
      '      /[...slugs]/page.jay-html    -- catch all route\n' +
      '      /[[...slugs]]/page.jay-html  -- optional catch all route\n' +
      '  /components\n' +
      '  /node_modules\n' +
      '    /app-1                    -- application functionality, including pages and components\n' +
      '      /manifest.json          -- file describing the content of the application\n' +
      '        /page-1\n' +
      '          /page.ts            -- the page component</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>rendering process</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The Jay rendering process has 3 steps - of which all are optional.</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>slowly changing data rendering (similar to SSG in other frameworks)</li>\n' +
      '<li>fast changing data rendering (similar to SSR in other frameworks)</li>\n' +
      '<li>client rendering</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>This section presents the flow and ideas for the rendering process.\n' +
      'Next we will explore different APIs to package those ideas.</strong></p>\n' +
      '<h3>Slowly changing Data Rendering</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The slowly changing data rendering is used to load param values for pages with url parameters, as well as loading\n' +
      'system parameter values (languages). The rendering continues by loading data for each set of params and pre-rendering the page.</p>\n' +
      '<div class="md-mermaid"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1034.308 435" width="1034.308" height="435">\n' +
      '<style>\n' +
      '  svg {\n' +
      '    /* Derived from --bg and --fg (overridable via --line, --accent, etc.) */\n' +
      '    --_text:          var(--fg);\n' +
      '    --_text-sec:      var(--muted, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 60%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_text-muted:    var(--muted, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 40%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_text-faint:    color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 25%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '    --_line:          var(--line, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 50%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_arrow:         var(--accent, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 85%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_node-fill:     var(--surface, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 3%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_node-stroke:   var(--border, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 20%, var(--bg)));\n' +
      '    --_group-fill:    var(--bg);\n' +
      '    --_group-hdr:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 5%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '    --_inner-stroke:  color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 12%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '    --_key-badge:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 10%, var(--bg));\n' +
      '  }\n' +
      '</style>\n' +
      '<defs>\n' +
      '  <marker id="seq-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="5" refX="8" refY="2.5" orient="auto-start-reverse">\n' +
      '    <polygon points="0 0, 8 2.5, 0 5" fill="var(--_arrow)" />\n' +
      '  </marker>\n' +
      '  <marker id="seq-arrow-open" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="5" refX="8" refY="2.5" orient="auto-start-reverse">\n' +
      '    <polyline points="0 0, 8 2.5, 0 5" fill="none" stroke="var(--_arrow)" stroke-width="1" />\n' +
      '  </marker>\n' +
      '</defs>\n' +
      '<line class="lifeline" data-actor="page" x1="445.33399999999995" y1="70" x2="445.33399999999995" y2="405" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />\n' +
      '<line class="lifeline" data-actor="comp" x1="604.8694999999999" y1="70" x2="604.8694999999999" y2="405" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />\n' +
      '<line class="lifeline" data-actor="child" x1="777.3725" y1="70" x2="777.3725" y2="405" stroke="var(--_line)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />\n' +
      '<g class="message" data-from="page" data-to="comp" data-label="link (import page comp.) +\n' +
