{
  post: {
    title: 'Partial And Complementary Types',
    content: '<h1>Partial and Complementary Types</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>Partial type is, give a type <code>T</code>, getting a type <code>P</code> at which all properties of <code>T</code> are set as optional.\n' +
      'Typescript has a built in utility type for partial - <code>type P = Partial&lt;T&gt;</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Complementary type is, give a type <code>T</code> and a specific incarnation of the partial type <code>P</code>, denoted as <code>P1</code>,\n' +
      'the complementary type <code>C</code> is the subset of <code>T</code> with all other properties of <code>T</code>, such that\n' +
      '<code>T === P &amp; C</code>. Typescript has a built in utility to generate the complementary using <code>Omit</code> - <code>type C = Omit&lt;T, keyof P1&gt;</code>;</p>\n' +
      '<h2>why do we need it?</h2>\n' +
      '<p>With Jay Stack, we split the <code>ViewState</code> into <code>StaticViewState</code> created by slowly changing rendering, and\n' +
      '<code>DynamicViewState</code> created by fast changing and interactive rendering.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Both are partials of the <code>ViewState</code>, but setting a value in <code>StaticViewState</code> means we delete it from the <code>jay-html</code>,\n' +
      'turning it into static, and if this value will repeat in the <code>DynamicViewState</code> it will be ignored. We want to capture this\n' +
      'behavior with the type system.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Infer the partial and complementary as function parameters</h2>\n' +
      '<p>What if we want to create a function who accepts two parameters who must complement to a joined type?</p>\n' +
      '<p>The naive way to define it is using</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">function</span> combineValues<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>P <span class="token keyword">extends</span> Partial<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>T<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> C <span class="token keyword">extends</span> Omit<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>T<span class="token punctuation">,</span> keyof P<span class="token operator">&gt;&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  partial<span class="token operator">:</span> P<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  complement<span class="token operator">:</span> C<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> T <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>partial<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>complement <span class="token punctuation">}</span> as T<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>However, the above will not work.\n' +
      'First, the original type <code>T</code> is not explicitly defined on the function, and those cannot be inferred.\n' +
      'Second, the above does not insure a type cannot have extra properties, which allows to have overlapping properties\n' +
      'or extra properties.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>full solution</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Here is a full solution that works</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Utility types an error message (instead of never)</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Ensures keys of U are a subset of the keys of T, ensuring no extra keys</span>\n' +
      'type ExactSubset<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>T<span class="token punctuation">,</span> U<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> keyof U <span class="token keyword">extends</span> keyof T\n' +
      '  <span class="token operator">?</span> U\n' +
      `  <span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> error<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'Object contains properties not in target type'</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Ensures the keys of A and the Keys of B do not have any overlap</span>\n' +
      'type DisjointKeys<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>A<span class="token punctuation">,</span> B<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> keyof A <span class="token operator">&amp;</span> keyof B <span class="token keyword">extends</span> never\n' +
      '  <span class="token operator">?</span> A\n' +
      `  <span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> error<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'Overlapping properties detected'</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// The generic example function</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> combineValues2<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>\n' +
      '  T <span class="token keyword">extends</span> object<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  P <span class="token keyword">extends</span> Partial<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>T<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  C <span class="token keyword">extends</span> Partial<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>T<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">&amp;</span> Omit<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>T<span class="token punctuation">,</span> keyof P<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>base<span class="token operator">:</span> T<span class="token punctuation">,</span> partial<span class="token operator">:</span> ExactSubset<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>T<span class="token punctuation">,</span> P<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> complement<span class="token operator">:</span> ExactSubset<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>T<span class="token punctuation">,</span> C<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">&amp;</span> DisjointKeys<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>C<span class="token punctuation">,</span> P<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  console<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">log</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>partial<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>complement <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Example usage</span>\n' +
      'interface Person <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  name<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  age<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  id<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">const</span> base<span class="token operator">:</span> Person <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> name<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'default'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> age<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">0</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> id<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'0'</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">const</span> partialResult <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> name<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'Alice'</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">const</span> complementResult <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> age<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">30</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> id<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'12345'</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> result <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">combineValues2</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>base<span class="token punctuation">,</span> partialResult<span class="token punctuation">,</span> complementResult<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      'console<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">log</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>result<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// { name: &quot;Alice&quot;, age: 30, id: &quot;12345&quot; }</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Test cases with improved errors</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Error: Extra property</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">const</span> extraPartial <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> name<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'Bob'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> extra<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token str`... 3097 more characters,
