{
  post: {
    title: 'Partial Rendering',
    content: '<h1>Partial Rendering</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>Partial Rendering is when we have <code>jay-html</code> file and a <code>jay-stack</code> component has a slowly changing phase.\n' +
      'The slowly changing phase generates <code>Partial&lt;ViewState&gt;</code> which we can use to partially render the <code>jay-html</code> file.</p>\n' +
      '<p>What it means is that</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>We inline all the slowly <code>Partial&lt;ViewState&gt;</code> into the <code>jay-html</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>If we have multiple <code>UrlParams</code>, that is we have multiple result HTML pages for a route, we inline into\n' +
      'each result HTML separately</li>\n' +
      '<li>If we have conditions that are bound to an inline member of <code>Partial&lt;ViewState&gt;</code>, we resolve the condition\n' +
      '(delete false branches)</li>\n' +
      '<li>If we have forEach that are bound to an inline member of <code>Partial&lt;ViewState&gt;</code>, it is rendered as a static list</li>\n' +
      '<li>The inlined <code>jay-html</code> is used for fast rendering phase and for interactive rendering.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>how it works</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The component Slowly rendering phase generates a <code>Partial&lt;ViewState&gt;</code>.\n' +
      'Given this partial view state, the jay compiler transforms the jay-html into the inlined jay html.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The jay-html includes bindings to the <code>ViewState</code> of different types, and each is handled in the appropriate way.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>text, property and attribute bindings</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Such bindings are written as <code>{field}</code> or <code>{field.a.b.c}</code> or <code>word {field} words {fields2}...</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The normal compiling generates <code>dt(vs =&gt; vs.field)</code> or <code>dt(vs =&gt; vs.field?.a?.b?.c)</code>, using <code>dp</code>, <code>da</code> or <code>dt</code> for\n' +
      'property, attribute or text.</p>\n' +
      '<p>It is compiled as a template of values.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Given a value, we compile the expression into a value by inlining the value. If the expression becomes static,\n' +
      'it is handled as a static text and not a function. If there are any unbound values, it remains a function.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Given a value for <code>field=world</code>, the expression <code>{field}</code> turns into <code>world</code>\n' +
      'Given a value for <code>field=world</code>, the expression <code>hello {field}</code> turns into <code>hello world</code>\n' +
      'Given a value for <code>field=world</code>, the expression <code>hello {field} from {geo}</code> turns into <code>dt(vs =&gt; &#39;hello world from ${vs.geo}&#39;)</code></p>\n' +
      '<h2>conditions</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Such expressions are written as <code>member</code> or <code>member.a.b.c</code>, and are normally compiled into\n' +
      '<code>vs =&gt; vs.member</code> or <code>vs =&gt; vs.member.a.b.c</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>It is compiled as a condition.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Condition expressions can also use <code>!</code> for not expressions, or equals to enum values, such as\n' +
      '<code>!member</code> which turns into <code>vs =&gt; !vs.member</code> and <code>anEnum === one</code> which turns into <code>vs =&gt; vs.anEnum === AnEnum.one</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Given a value for member, the condition can be resolved to a <code>true</code> or <code>false</code> value, which is then used to decide if\n' +
      'to include the condition element tree or not.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>forEach</h2>\n' +
      '<p>For each iteration member, which returns the item to iterate over, normally looks like\n' +
      '<code>member</code> or <code>member.a</code></p>\n' +
      '<p>It is normally compiled into a function such as <code>(member: MemberType) =&gt; member</code> or <code>(member: MemberType) =&gt; member?.a</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>It is compiled as an accessor.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Given a value for the accessed iteration items, we can remove the forEach and instead just render the forEach items\n' +
      'into the jay-html.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>class expressions</h2>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Partial Rendering","number":36}'
  }
}
