{
  post: {
    title: 'Contract File',
    content: '<h1>Contract File</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>The Jay Contract file is needed to create library components and applications who specify a contract, but do not\n' +
      'specify a specific UI. For instance, a service page component can specify the contract of the services page, without\n' +
      'specifying the actual UI.</p>\n' +
      '<p>An Application Package is an NPM package that includes a Jay Application that can be installed into a site.\n' +
      'An editor environment can use the information in the Jay Application package to read the list of contracts, default\n' +
      'design for pages and components, application settings and page settings, as well as other things we will add later.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>The Contract File</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The contract file is used</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>by design tools to create UI connected to the contract, including indicators like required and descriptions.</li>\n' +
      '<li>generate the <code>ViewState</code> and <code>Refs</code> types the component is using.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>The format selected for the Jay Contract File is a <code>YAML</code> formal, with a hierarchical structure capturing the\n' +
      'contract hierarchical structure.</p>\n' +
      '<p>To set the syntax of the <code>YAML</code> file, we take as an example the <a href="..%2Fexamples%2Fjay%2Ftodo-one-flat-component">todo-one-flat-component</a>\n' +
      'contract.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Todo List\n' +
      '  tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> dynamic data<span class="token punctuation">:</span> newTodo\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> the new todo item text as it is edited in the newTodo input\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> interactive<span class="token punctuation">:</span> newTodo\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLInputElement\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> an input to type in the new todo item.\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> variant<span class="token punctuation">:</span> hasItems\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> what to display when there are items to show in the list, or not\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> variant<span class="token punctuation">:</span> filter\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> enum (all <span class="token punctuation">|</span> active <span class="token punctuation">|</span> completed)\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> variant of the selected filter applied to the list of todo items\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> interactive<span class="token punctuation">:</span> filterAll\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLAnchorElement <span class="token punctuation">|</span> HTMLButtonElement\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> clears any other filter\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> interactive<span class="token punctuation">:</span> filterActive\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLAnchorElement <span class="token punctuation">|</span> HTMLButtonElement\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> filters the list of todo items to show only the active items\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> interactive<span class="token punctuation">:</span> filterCompleted\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLAnchorElement <span class="token punctuation">|</span> HTMLButtonElement\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> filters the list of todo items to show only the completed items\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> sub contract<span class="token punctuation">:</span> shownTodos\n' +
      '      tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> dynamic data<span class="token punctuation">:</span> id\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> dynamic data<span class="token punctuation">:</span> title\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> the todo item itself\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> interactive<span class="token punctuation">:</span> title\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLInputElement\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> an input used for editing the todo item\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> dynamic data<span class="token punctuation">:</span> isCompleted\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> indicating if the todo item is active or completed\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> variant<span class="token punctuation">:</span> isCompleted\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> is the todo item completed?\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> interactive<span class="token punctuation">:</span> completed\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLInputElement\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> an input element used to toggle the todo item between active and completed\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> variant<span class="token punctuation">:</span> isEditing\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> is the todo item in editing state, or display state?\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> interactive<span class="token punctuation">:</span> label\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLLabelElement\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> a label element that when clicked, enables the editing of the todo item\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> interactive<span class="token punctuation">:</span> button\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLButtonElement\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> a button used to remove the todo item from the list of todo items</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>We can see in the above example that when focusing on tag types, we have duplicate tags\n' +
      '(<code>newTodo</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>isCompleted</code> and <code>completed</code>). Lets try and create a more coherent format</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-YAML"><span class="token keyword">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Todo List\n' +
      '  tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> newTodo\n' +
      '      data type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '      interactive type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLInputElement\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> the new todo item text data and interactive element to edit it\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> filter\n' +
      '      data type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> enum (all <span class="token punctuation">|</span> active <span class="token punctuation">|</span> completed)\n' +
      '      variant<span class="token punctuation">:</span> enum (all <span class="token punctuation">|</span> active <span class="token punctuation">|</span> completed)\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> variant of the selected filter applied to the list of todo items\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> sub contract<span class="token punctuation">:</span> shownTodos\n' +
      '      tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> title\n' +
      '          data type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '          interactive type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLInputElement\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> the todo item text and interactive element to edit it\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> isCompleted\n' +
      '          data type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean\n' +
      '          variant<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean\n' +
      '          interactive type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLInputElement\n' +
      '          description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> indicating if the todo item is active or completed, and the interactive element to toggle between active and completed</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The above is better, yet still raises two questions -</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>should the description be one or two? it seems very clear that the description of data and interactive tags are different</li>\n' +
      '<li>using <code>data type</code> we understand it is data, using <code>interactive type</code> we understand it is interactive tag.\n' +
      'how to indicate a variant? when a tag is both data and variant, the definition looks redundant.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-YAML"><span class="token keyword">contract</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
