{
  post: {
    title: 'Plugin Package',
    content: '<h1>Plugin Package</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>The Plugin package is a tool to create reusable Jay Components and Contracts to be installed\n' +
      'from a design tool, and used &quot;no coding&quot;, or used and extended with coding.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Requirements for the Plugin Package</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Ability to install a plugin package from a design tool</li>\n' +
      '<li>Ability of a package to have one or more contracts, used by the design tool to build pages</li>\n' +
      '<li>Ability of each contract to have implementing Jay component</li>\n' +
      '<li>Support different types of contracts<ol>\n' +
      '<li>page contract, which defines a page, such as a product page or cart page</li>\n' +
      '<li>Sub-component contract, which defines a component who can be positioned on any page, such as promoted product</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li>Support dependencies between contracts and plugins<ol>\n' +
      '<li>A plugin <code>B</code> can expand plugin <code>A</code>, requiring it to be installed to function</li>\n' +
      '<li>A Plugin <code>B</code> contract can expand plugin <code>A</code> in the contract of a specific page contract,\n' +
      'requiring to use <code>B</code>&#39;s contract on the <code>A</code>&#39;s contract page</li>\n' +
      '<li>Ability to hand over data from the <code>A</code> plugin contract jay component to <code>B</code>s jay component</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin package should optionally include design tool assets to be used for seeding design tool designs on plugin installation</li>\n' +
      '<li>Plugins with pages should get a facility to map logical pages to actual URLs, enabling creating links between pages.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Requirement for the Jay Application using Plugins</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Ability to install multiple plugin contracts on each page</li>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin contracts installed on a page should work <code>no coding</code> on the application page</li>\n' +
      '<li>Application page code should be able to define page contract and write an application page component</li>\n' +
      '<li>Application page code should be able to override the <code>ViewState</code> of plugins installed in the page</li>\n' +
      '<li>Application page code should be able to use APIs of plugins installed on the page</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h1>Modeling a Application &amp; Plugin Package</h1>\n' +
      '<h2>Runtime Dependencies</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>modeling on refs</h3>\n' +
      '<p>We can model the runtime dependencies between the <code>Page</code> and plugin <code>A</code>, and between plugin <code>B</code> and plugin <code>A</code>\n' +
      'as a <code>ref</code> from the dependant to the dependency. Using a Jay <code>component ref</code> we gain access to the dependent plugin\n' +
      'APIs, including functions and events.</p>\n' +
      '<p>However, refs are only available on the interactive stage, and not in the slowly / fast stages.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>modeling on context</h3>\n' +
      '<p>We can model the runtime dependencies between the <code>Page</code> and plugin <code>A</code>, and between plugin <code>B</code> and plugin <code>A</code>\n' +
      'as a <code>Context</code> that plugin <code>B</code> publishes (using a new API / same API?) and both <code>Page</code> and plugin <code>A</code> consume (using the regular context API).</p>\n' +
      '<p>Context API supports reactive getters and API functions.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>runtime dependencies - selection</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Modeling on Context looks like a superior option because of the support for backend using server contexts.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Overriding plugin ViewState</h2>\n' +
      '<p>One way to model the overriding of a plugin ViewState is to use it as part of the <code>Props</code> and <code>ViewState</code> of the <code>Page</code> component.\n' +
      'For each installed plugin, we add to the <code>PageViewState</code> a member of the <code>PluginViewState</code></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface PageViewState <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// page members</span>\n' +
      '  plugin<span class="token operator">?:</span> PluginViewState<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>To ensure when coding the page component, one does not have to return all the time the <code>PluginViewState</code> we set it as optional.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Now, we add to the page component <code>Props</code> the <code>PluginViewState</code>. As the system is reactive, we set the <code>PluginViewState</code>\n' +
      'value to be the <code>render</code> value from the plugin. If the developer of the page component decides to override the <code>PluginViewState</code>,\n' +
      'they just have to read it from the <code>prop</code>, change it, and return it as part of the component <code>render</code> function.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Page Component vs Sub-Component</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Page Component is a component that defines a page. On a page, there can only be a single page component of a plugin.\n' +
      'Page Components cannot be explicitly placed in a <code>jay-html</code> template, and cannot be under <code>forEach</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>A Page may have multiple page components of different plugins.</p>\n' +
      '<p>A Sub Component is a component that defines an area on the page with an encapsulated logic. Sub-Components can appear multiple\n' +
      'times in a page, including under <code>forEach</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The plugin package is assumed to define which is a page component and which is a sub-component.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>jap-html representation</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Sub-component in <code>jay-html</code> (as defined in the <code>compiler</code> package)</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;header</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;title</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>Todo element<span class="token tag">&lt;/title</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;link</span> <span class="token attribute">rel</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;import&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">href</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;./item&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">names</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;Item&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/header</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- some markup structure --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;Item</span> <span class="token attribute">title</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;{title}&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">isCompleted</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;{isCompleted}&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;shownTodos&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">trackBy</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;id&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;items&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>For a page component, we propose to use the <code>script</code> tag with <code>src</code> as it is more appropriate for a page code.\n' +
      'Unlike regular script loading, the <code>src</code> is understood as a link to code, following Typescript <code>import</code> logic.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;header</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;title</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>Todo element<span class="token tag">&lt;/title</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;stores/product-page&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">name</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;page&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">key</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;productPage&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/header</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>where</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>type=&quot;application/jay&quot;</code> tells us it is a Jay Page Component</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>src</code> the location of the Jay Page Component to load, using the typescript <code>import</code> convention</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>name</code> the name of the parameter to import</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>key</code> the namespace used within the page, which is used as the key for the <code>ViewState</code>, <code>Refs</code> and <code>Props</code>.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>page Refs, Props and ViewState</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In the Page <code>jay-html</code>, the <code>data</code> section defines the <code>ViewState</code> type and the <code>ref</code>s defines the <code>Refs</code> type.\n' +
      'When a jay-html imports a Page Component, the page component <code>ref</code>s and <code>data</code> are prefixed with the <code>key</code> from the script import.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;html</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;head</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;appli'... 4436 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Plugin Package","number":39}'
  }
}
