{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay Package',
    content: '<h1>Jay Package</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>This design doc discusses how to include Jay headless components in an NPM Package,\n' +
      'so that Jay dev server can tell about them to an editor, and an application can use them as defined in\n' +
      '<a href="40-changing-jay-html-format">40 - changing jay-html format.md</a></p>\n' +
      '<h2>why not Headfull components?</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Simply put, headfull components have a jay-html, and restrict editing of the UI.\n' +
      'Headless components are equivalent logic, and the package can include headless component default or template design,\n' +
      'which make them fully equivalent with full design customization options.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Jay Package Structure</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Package is an NPM package that has to include, at the very least, the contract files and exported\n' +
      'code for the headless components.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Technically, for an NPM package to export additional files to <code>main</code>, it has to define a <code>files</code> member\n' +
      'to know what to package and an <code>exports</code> member to know what is accessible from those package files</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;main&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;dist/index.js&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;files&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">&quot;dist&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;exports&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;.&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/index.js&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;./mood-tracker.jay-contract&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;./dist/mood-tracker.jay-contract&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The suggested</p>\n' +
      '<p>// todo - define how to work with meta contracts, such as CMS and A/B tests</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Jay Package","number":43}'
  }
}
