{
  post: {
    title: 'Recursive Jay-Html',
    content: '<h1>Design Log 46 - Recursive Jay-HTML</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay-HTML currently doesn&#39;t support recursive HTML structures natively. To create recursive UIs like trees, developers must create separate components and import them into themselves. This approach works but has limitations:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Forces component extraction</strong>: Even for a single large HTML structure with one recursive section, you must extract it into a separate component</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Requires explicit component import</strong>: Components must import themselves using <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headfull&quot; src=&quot;./self&quot; names=&quot;Self&quot;&gt;</code>, which feels unnatural</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Type complexity</strong>: The recursive type structure requires careful TypeScript type definitions</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Design tool challenges</strong>: Design tools would need to understand and generate these self-imports, which is not intuitive for a single HTML structure</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Verbosity</strong>: Extra boilerplate is needed for what should be a natural recursive pattern within a single HTML document</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Workaround Example</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The current tree example (<code>jay/examples/jay/tree/lib/tree-node.jay-html</code>) requires splitting into a separate component:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;html</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;head</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Component imports itself --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-headfull&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;./tree-node&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">names</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;TreeNode, Node&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="token attribute">type</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;application/jay-data&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      data:\n' +
      '        headChar: string\n' +
      '        node: Node\n' +
      '        open: boolean\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;/script</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/head</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;head&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token tag">&lt;span</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;tree-arrow&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{headChar}<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token tag">&lt;span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{node.name}<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;ul</span> <span class="token attribute">if</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;open&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token tag">&lt;li</span> <span class="token attribute">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;node.children&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">trackBy</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;id&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '          <span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Uses itself as a component --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '          <span class="token tag">&lt;TreeNode</span> <span class="token attribute">props</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;{.}&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token tag">&lt;/li</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;/ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/body</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/html</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>The Challenge</strong>: You can&#39;t define a single component with a large HTML structure where just one subtree is recursive. You&#39;re forced to extract that subtree into a separate component.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Goals</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design a native recursive jay-html syntax that:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Allows marking HTML subtrees as recursive</strong>: A specific section of HTML can repeat recursively without extracting it into a separate component</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Prevents infinite recursion</strong>: Requires a conditional or forEach to guard recursion</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Works with design tools</strong>: Can be easily generated and understood by design tools</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Maintains type safety</strong>: Generates correct TypeScript types for recursive structures</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Keeps HTML structure intact</strong>: The entire HTML hierarchy stays in one file</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design Proposal</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The key insight is to define <strong>recursive regions</strong> - marked sections of HTML that should repeat for nested data structures. The recursion happens at the HTML subtree level, not at the component level.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Syntax Option 1: <code>recursive-region</code> with Named Regions</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Define a named recursive region that can be referenced within itself.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;html</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
