[Build] 121/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=46-recursive-jay-html)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Recursive Html Context Switching',
    content: '<h1>Design Log 47 - Recursive HTML Context Switching</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The current recursive HTML design (Design Log 46) has a fundamental limitation when the recursive structure needs to operate on a nested type that differs from the root context type.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>The Core Issue</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Consider this data structure:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">data</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  tree<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> id<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '      name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '      hasChildren<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean\n' +
      '      isOpen<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean\n' +
      '      children<span class="token punctuation">:</span> $/data/tree <span class="token comment"># References the tree array type</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>When we try to create a recursive region, we encounter a context mismatch:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;ul</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;menu-list&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;menuItem&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;li</span> <span class="token attribute">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;tree&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">trackBy</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;id&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="token attribute">href</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;#&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;span</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;name&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{name}<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;/a</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">if</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;hasChildren &amp;&amp; isOpen&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;recurse</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;menuItem&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/li</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>The Problem:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>The <code>ref=&quot;menuItem&quot;</code> is at the root context where <code>tree</code> is a property</li>\n' +
      '<li>The <code>forEach=&quot;tree&quot;</code> iterates over the tree items</li>\n' +
      '<li>When we recurse, we need to iterate over <code>children</code>, not <code>tree</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>But <code>children</code> is not accessible at the root context</li>\n' +
      '<li>The recursive region needs to work with both <code>tree</code> (initially) and <code>children</code> (on recursion)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Why This Fails:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>At the <code>ref=&quot;menuItem&quot;</code> level, the ViewState type is <code>IndirectRecursion2ViewState</code> (which has <code>tree</code> property)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Inside <code>forEach=&quot;tree&quot;</code>, the ViewState type is <code>TreeOfIndirectRecursion2ViewState</code> (which has <code>children</code> property)</li>\n' +
      '<li>The recursive region function needs a consistent type to operate on</li>\n' +
      '<li>We can&#39;t write <code>forEach=&quot;tree&quot;</code> AND <code>forEach=&quot;children&quot;</code> in the same template</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Workaround Attempts</h3>\n' +
      '<h4>Attempt 1: Put ref inside forEach</h4>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;ul</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;menu-list&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;li</span> <span class="token attribute">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;tree&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">trackBy</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;id&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;menuItem&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="token attribute">href</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;#&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;span</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;name&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{name}<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/a</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">if</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;hasChildren &amp;&amp; isOpen&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;recurse</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;menuItem&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/li</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Problem</strong>: The ref is now on a <code>forEach</code> element, which creates a collection of refs instead of a single ref. The recursive region would need to iterate, but we&#39;re already in an iteration context.</p>\n' +
      '<h4>Attempt 2: Use accessor on recurse</h4>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;ul</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;menu-list&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;menuItem&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;li</span> <span class="token attribute">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;tree&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">trackBy</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;id&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="token attribute">href</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;#&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;span</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;name&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{name}<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/a</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">if</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;hasChildren &amp;&amp; isOpen&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token tag">&lt;recurse</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;menuItem&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">accessor</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;children&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/li</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Problem</strong>: The <code>accessor=&quot;children&quot;</code> would use <code>withData</code> to switch to the children array, but the recursive function still expects to receive <code>tree</code> initially and <code>children</code> on recursion. The mismatch persists.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Root Cause Analysis</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The fundamental issue is a <strong>context type mismatch between initialization and recursion</strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Initialization Phase</strong>: The recursive region is called with the root ViewState type</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Needs to access <code>tree</code> array</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>forEach=&quot;tree&quot;</code> makes sense here</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Recursion Phase</strong>: The recursive region is called with the tree item type</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Needs to access <code>children</code> '... 48568 more characters,
    description: '',
