{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay Stack Services',
    content: '<h1>Jay Stack Services</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>The Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack pages need access to server-side singletons like database connections, API clients, configuration services, and other infrastructure services. Currently, the <code>serverContexts</code> array in the jay-stack-builder is used to pass dependencies to page rendering functions (<code>loadParams</code>, <code>slowlyRender</code>, <code>fastRender</code>), but:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>The naming is confusing - &quot;context&quot; implies hierarchical parent-child relationships (like client contexts), but server dependencies are actually global singletons</li>\n' +
      '<li>There&#39;s no clear pattern for initializing and providing these services</li>\n' +
      '<li>The dev-server has no mechanism to load service definitions on startup or reload them during development</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>The Solution: Services Pattern</h2>\n' +
      '<p>We introduce a <strong>Services</strong> pattern for server-side dependency injection, distinct from the hierarchical client-side <strong>Context</strong> pattern.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Key Differences from Client Contexts</h3>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Aspect</th>\n' +
      '<th>Client Contexts</th>\n' +
      '<th>Server Services</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Scope</td>\n' +
      '<td>Hierarchical (parent→child)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Flat (global singletons)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Lifecycle</td>\n' +
      '<td>Component tree lifetime</td>\n' +
      '<td>Application/request lifetime</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Updates</td>\n' +
      '<td>Reactive (can trigger re-renders)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Static per request</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Runtime</td>\n' +
      '<td>Browser</td>\n' +
      '<td>Server (Node.js)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h3>Naming Convention</h3>\n' +
      '<p>We propose renaming to clarify intent:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Current naming:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>serverContexts</code> - confusing, implies hierarchy</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>clientContexts</code> - redundant &quot;client&quot; prefix</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Proposed naming:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>services</code> (or <code>serverServices</code> if clarity needed) - server-side singletons</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>contexts</code> - client-side hierarchical contexts</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Alternative considered: <code>serverDependencies</code>, but &quot;services&quot; is more idiomatic.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Service Marker Pattern</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Similar to client <code>ContextMarker&lt;T&gt;</code>, we create a <code>ServiceMarker&lt;T&gt;</code> in the stack-server-runtime package:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In @jay-framework/stack-server-runtime</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> interface ServiceMarker<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ServiceType<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> createJayService<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ServiceType <span class="token operator">=</span> unknown<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>name<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> ServiceMarker<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ServiceType<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token function">Symbol</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>name<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Benefits:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Optional <code>name</code> parameter for better error messages</li>\n' +
      '<li>Symbol description helps identify which service is missing</li>\n' +
      '<li>Type-safe marker carries type information</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Key differences from <code>ContextMarker</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>No hierarchical lookup needed (flat structure)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Services are registered globally, not in a stack</li>\n' +
      '<li>Services are initialized once at startup</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>2. Service Registry &amp; Lifecycle Hooks</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The stack-server-runtime provides a global service registry and lifecycle management:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Service registry</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> serviceRegistry <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token keyword">new</span> Map<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>symbol<span class="token punctuation">,</span> any<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> registerService<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ServiceType<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
