{
  post: {
    title: 'Full Stack Component Rendering Manifest',
    content: '<h1>Full Stack Component refinement for gradual rendering</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>The Jay full stack component, created using the Syntax below, is based on the <code>ViewState</code> type for page rendering,\n' +
      'where <code>renderSlowlyChanging</code> renders part of the <code>ViewState</code> members and both <code>renderFastChanging</code> and <code>ProductsPageConstructor</code>\n' +
      'render the rest of the <code>ViewState</code> members.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The current API is at <a href="packages/jay-stack/full-stack-component/lib/jay-stack-builder.ts">jay-stack-builder.ts</a>,\n' +
      'and an example usage is</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">const</span> page <span class="token operator">=</span> makeJayStackComponent<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token keyword">typeof</span> render<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span>withProps<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PageProps<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withServices</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>PRODUCTS_DATABASE_SERVICE<span class="token punctuation">,</span> INVENTORY_SERVICE<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withLoadParams</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>urlLoader<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withSlowlyRender</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>renderSlowlyChanging<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withFastRender</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>renderFastChanging<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withInteractive</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>ProductsPageConstructor<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The above has a problem that it does not capture the relationship between the rendering phases accurately.\n' +
      'We need to extend the above with</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>ability to define for nested properties (under objects and arrays) which is rendered at which phase.</li>\n' +
      '<li>ability to define when an array elements are set, and elements cannot be added / removed / moved in the array.</li>\n' +
      '<li>support for 3 rendering modes 4. slow rendering 5. fast rendering 6. fast and interactive rendering</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Note:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>it does not make sense to combine (for the same attribute) slow and fast rendering,\n' +
      'as fast rendering will override the slow rendered value</li>\n' +
      '<li>it does not make sense to render only interactive value, as what will be rendered for it on SSR?</li>\n' +
      '<li>when an array is interactive (as we can add elements on the client), all the array child attributes have to be\n' +
      'also interactive, as we can add a new item and we need all the data.</li>\n' +
      '<li>when an array is rendered slowly or fast, it means that array items cannot be added or removed in the interactive phase.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>direction of the solution</h2>\n' +
      '<p>We suggest to add another builder phase at which we provide a schema, additional metadata for the product state type\n' +
      'as a constant (that can be used in runtime) and as a type (that can be used to define the Slowly, Fast and Interactive ViewState)</p>\n' +
      '<p>We want the schema to define, for each attribute of the view state, what rendering phase it is rendered at.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Proposed Solution: Rendering Manifest Schema</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Overview</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The ViewState type is defined by the contract (from <code>.jay-contract</code> files or <code>render</code> function in <code>.jay-html</code>).\n' +
      'The rendering manifest schema provides <strong>metadata</strong> for properties in the ViewState, declaring:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Which rendering phase sets each property&#39;s value (slow, fast, or fast+interactive)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Whether arrays are frozen (cannot be modified in interactive phase) or mutable</li>\n' +
      '<li>Type-level narrowing of ViewState per rendering phase</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Key Principle</strong>: The schema doesn&#39;t define ViewState - it annotates it. The schema should either:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Be inferred from the ViewState type with explicit annotations</li>\n' +
      '<li>Be validated against the ViewState type to ensure consistency</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Core Concepts</h3>\n' +
      '<h4>Rendering Phases</h4>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">/**\n' +
      ' * Defines the three rendering phases in Jay Stack components\n' +
      ' */</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> enum RenderingPhase <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/**\n' +
      '   * Slow rendering phase - executed at build time or data change time\n' +
      "   * For semi-static data that doesn't change often\n" +
      '   */</span>\n' +
      `  SLOW <span class="token operator">=</span> 'slow<span class="token string">',\n` +
      '\n' +
      '  /**\n' +
      '   * Fast rendering phase - executed at request time\n' +
      '   * For dynamic data that can be cached\n' +
      '   */\n' +
      `  FAST = '</span>fast<span class="token string">',\n` +
      '\n' +
      '  /**\n' +
      '   * Interactive rendering phase - executed on the client\n' +
      '   * For reactive, user-interactive data\n' +
      '   */\n' +
      `  INTERACTIVE = '</span>interactive'<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h4>Rendering Mode</h4>\n' +
      '<p>A rendering mode defines when a property&#39;s value is SET. The valid modes are:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">/**\n' +
      ' * Valid rendering modes for a property\n' +
      ' *\n' +
      ' * Note: These are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE for when the value is SET:\n' +
      " * - 'slow' means the value is set at build time and remains static\n" +
      " * - 'fast' means the value is set at request time (not set in slow)\n" +
      " * - 'fast+interactive' means the value is set at request time and can be MODIFIED on client\n" +
      ' *\n' +
      ' * Invalid combinations and why:\n' +
      " * - 'slow+fast' - Fast would override slow, so this is redundant\n" +
      " * - 'slow+interactive' - Interactive needs a request-time value to hydrate properly\n" +
      " * - 'interactive' only - SSR needs an initial value, can't be client-only\n" +
      ' */</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> type RenderingMode <span class="token operator">=</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> 'slow<span class="token string">' // Set in slow phase (static, never changes)\n` +
      `  | '</span>fast<span class="token string">' // Set in fast phase (dynamic, but not interactive)\n` +
      `  | '</span>fast<span class="token operator">+</span>interactive<span class="token string">'; // Set in fast phase, modifiable in interactive phase\n` +
      '\n' +
      '/**\n' +
      ' * Type-level validation of rendering mode constraints\n' +
      ' */\n' +
      `type ValidateRenderingMode&lt;Mode extends string&gt; = Mode extends '</span>slow<span class="token string">' | '</span>fast<span class="token string">' | '</span>fast<span class="token operator">+</span>interactive'\n` +
      '  <span class="token operator">?</span> Mode\n' +
      '  <span class="token operator">:</span> never<span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h4>Schema Node Types</h4>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">/**\n' +
      ' * Base interface for all schema nodes\n' +
      " * The 'type' property acts as a discriminator for the union type\n" +
      ' */</span>\n' +
      'interface BaseSchemaNode <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Discriminator property for schema node types */</span>\n' +
      `  type<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'primitive'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'object'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'array'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">/**\n' +
      ' * Schema node for primitive values (string, number, boolean, enum)\n' +
      ' */</span>\n' +
      'interface PrimitiveSchemaNode <span class="token keyword">extends</span> BaseSchemaNode <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  type<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'primitive'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** The rendering mode for this property */</span>\n' +
      '  mode<span class="token operator">:</span> RenderingMode<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">/**\n' +
      ' * Schema node for array properties\n' +
      ' */</span>\n' +
      'interface ArraySchemaNode<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ItemViewState <span class="token keyword">extends</span> object <span class="token operator">=</span> any<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token keyword">extends</span> BaseSchemaNode <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  type<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'array'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** The rendering mode for the array itself, not including child objects */</span>\n' +
      '  mode<span class="token operator">:</span> RenderingMode<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">/** Schema for array item properties */</span>\n' +
      '  itemSchema<span class="token operator">:</span> RenderingManifestSchema<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ItemViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">/**\n' +
      ' * Schema node for object properties\n' +
      ' */</span>\n' +
      'interface ObjectSchemaNode<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>NestedViewState <span class="token k'... 139222 more characters,
