{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay Stack - Headless Configuration',
    content: '<h1>Jay Stack - Headless Configuration for Missing <code>jay-html</code></h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Context</h2>\n' +
      '<p>We have a scenario where <code>jay-html</code> files might not exist (e.g., during early stages of generation from external tools like Figma), but the folder structure and <code>jay-contract</code> files are present. We need a way to define &quot;used components&quot; (headless components) without relying on the <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;&gt;</code> tags inside <code>jay-html</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, <code>getContracts</code> and <code>getProjectConfiguration</code> rely on parsing <code>jay-html</code> files to find which components from installed apps are used on a page. If <code>jay-html</code> is missing, we lose this information, even if we know the page exists (via folder structure and contract).</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Decision: Localized <code>page.conf.yaml</code> (Option B)</h2>\n' +
      '<p>We have decided to adopt <strong>Option B: Localized <code>page.conf.yaml</code></strong>. This allows a page to be fully defined by its folder contents, even without the view template (<code>jay-html</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Implementation Details</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A page directory is recognized if it contains at least one of:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>page.jay-html</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>page.jay-contract</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>page.conf.yaml</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Configuration Logic</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>getContracts</code> API follows this precedence rules for determining page properties:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Page Existence:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>If a directory in the pages tree contains any of the above files, it is treated as a page.</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>pageUrl</code> is derived from the directory structure.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Contract Tags:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>If <code>page.jay-contract</code> exists: Tags are read from this file.</li>\n' +
      '<li>If <code>page.jay-contract</code> is missing: The page has an empty contract schema (no tags).</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Used Components (Headless Components):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Priority 1 (<code>page.jay-html</code>):</strong> If <code>page.jay-html</code> exists, the system parses it for <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/jay-headless&quot;&gt;</code> tags. This is considered the source of truth for the view.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Priority 2 (<code>page.conf.yaml</code>):</strong> If <code>page.jay-html</code> is <strong>missing</strong>, the system checks for <code>page.conf.yaml</code>.<ul>\n' +
      '<li>It reads the <code>used_components</code> list from the YAML file.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Fallback:</strong> If neither exists, the list of used components is empty.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>File Structure Example</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">src/pages/\n' +
      '  home/\n' +
      '    page.jay-contract      # Defines page data interface\n' +
      '    page.conf.yaml         # Defines used components (when HTML is missing)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3><code>page.conf.yaml</code> Format</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">used_components</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> product<span class="token punctuation">-</span>list <span class="token comment"># Component name in the installed app</span>\n' +
      '    src<span class="token punctuation">:</span> wix<span class="token punctuation">-</span>stores <span class="token comment"># App module name</span>\n' +
      '    key<span class="token punctuation">:</span> products <span class="token comment"># Key to bind data to</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Superseded Options</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Option A: Centralized <code>project.conf.yaml</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>Rejected due to scalability issues and merge conflict risks.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Option C: Extend <code>page.jay-contract</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>Rejected to maintain separation of concerns between interface (contract) and implementation (dependencies).</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Jay Stack - Headless Configuration","number":50}'
  }
}
