{
  post: {
    title: 'Rendering Phases In Contracts',
    content: '<h1>Rendering Phases in Contracts - Code Generation Approach</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>From Design Log #49, we learned that TypeScript&#39;s type narrowing has fundamental limitations with nested structures. We need a different approach: <strong>extending the contract format to declare rendering phases and generating phase-specific ViewState types at build time</strong>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay full-stack components render in three phases:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Slow (build-time)</strong>: Static data set at build time</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Fast (request-time)</strong>: Dynamic data set per request, not interactive</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Interactive</strong>: Data that can be modified on the client</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, there&#39;s no way to declare which phase each property belongs to, making it impossible for TypeScript to enforce type safety across rendering phases.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Proposed Solution: Rendering Phase Metadata in Contracts</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Core Idea</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Extend the <code>.jay-contract</code> format to include rendering phase metadata for each tag. The compiler will then generate three distinct ViewState types:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;ComponentName&gt;SlowViewState</code> - properties available at build time</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;ComponentName&gt;FastViewState</code> - properties available at request time</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>&lt;ComponentName&gt;InteractiveViewState</code> - properties that can be modified on client</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Design Principles</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Source of Truth</strong>: The contract is already the source of truth for ViewState - extend it to include phase information</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Sensible Defaults</strong>: Most properties are slow (build-time), so that&#39;s the default</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Simple Syntax</strong>: Minimal additional syntax - leverage existing contract structure</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Type Safety</strong>: Generated types provide exact, compiler-enforced type safety</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No Runtime Overhead</strong>: Pure build-time code generation</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Leverages Existing Patterns</strong>: Interactive elements already go into <code>Refs</code> type - we&#39;re just adding phase-specific ViewState types</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Key Semantic Rules</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Objects (Grouping Only)</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Object&#39;s <code>phase</code> attribute is <strong>only a default</strong> for child properties</li>\n' +
      '<li>Object itself has <strong>no semantic meaning</strong> - it&#39;s just a grouping</li>\n' +
      '<li>Object appears in a phase&#39;s ViewState if it has <strong>any child property</strong> in that phase</li>\n' +
      '<li>Object&#39;s phase attribute is <strong>optional</strong> - children can declare their own phases</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Arrays (Structure Control)</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Array&#39;s <code>phase</code> attribute controls <strong>when the array structure is set</strong> (which items exist)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>phase: slow</code> → Array structure frozen at build time (items cannot be added/removed later)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>phase: fast</code> → Array structure set at request time, frozen during interactive phase</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>phase: fast+interactive</code> → Array is mutable on client (can add/remove items)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Array&#39;s child properties can have <strong>later phases</strong> than the array itself<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Example: <code>slow</code> array can have <code>fast</code> or <code>fast+interactive</code> child properties</li>\n' +
      '<li>Constraint: Child <code>phase &gt;= array.phase</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Interactive Elements</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Tags with <code>type: interactive</code> go into <code>&lt;Component&gt;Refs</code> type (existing pattern)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Interactive elements are <strong>NOT</strong> part of any ViewState - they&#39;re element references</li>\n' +
      '<li>No changes to existing interactive element handling</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Rendering Phase Rules</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Based on contract tag types:</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Tag Type</th>\n' +
      '<th>Default Phase</th>\n' +
      '<th>Can Override?</th>\n' +
      '<th>Notes</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>interactive</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>interactive</td>\n' +
      '<td>❌ No</td>\n' +
      '<td>Always interactive (by definition)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>data</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>slow</td>\n' +
      '<td>✅ Yes</td>\n' +
      '<td>Can be slow, fast, or fast+interactive</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>variant</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>slow</td>\n' +
      '<td>✅ Yes</td>\n' +
      '<td>Can be slow, fast, or fast+interactive</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>repeated</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>slow</td>\n' +
      '<td>✅ Yes</td>\n' +
      '<td>Can be slow, fast, or fast+interactive</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Phase Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>slow</code> (default): Rendered at build time</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>fast</code>: Rendered at request time (SSR), not interactive</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>fast+interactive</code>: Rendered at request time, can be modified on client</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Contract Syntax Extension</h3>\n' +
      '<h4>Option A: Inline Phase Annotation (Recommended)</h4>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-jay-contract">contract ProductPage\n' +
      '  - {tag: name, type: data, dataType: string}                           # Default: slow\n' +
      '  - {tag: sku, type: data, dataType: string}                            # Default: slow\n' +
      '  - {tag: price, type: data, dataType: number, phase: slow}             # Explicit slow\n' +
      '  - {tag: inStock, type: data, dataType: boolean, phase: fast}          # Fast rendering\n' +
      '  - {tag: quantity, type: variant, dataType: number, phase: fast+interactive}  # Interactive\n' +
      '\n' +
      "  # Interactive tags don't need phase (always interactive)\n" +
      '  - {tag: addToCart, type: interactive}\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  # Repeated contracts\n' +
      '  - {tag: images, type: repeated, phase: slow}\n' +
      '    - {tag: url, type: data, dataType: string}\n' +
      '    - {tag: alt, type: data, dataType: string}\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  # Nested objects with mixed phases\n' +
      '  - {tag: discount, type: data, dataType: object, phase: slow}\n' +
      '    - {tag: type, type: data, dataType: string}              # Inherits slow from parent\n' +
      '    - {tag: amount, type: data, dataType: number, phase: fast}  # Override to fast\n' +
      '    - {tag: applied, type: variant, dataType: boolean, phase: fast+interactive}  # Interactive</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Clear and explicit</li>\n' +
      '<li>Easy to see phase at a glance</li>\n' +
      '<li>Follows existing contract syntax patterns</li>\n' +
      '<li>IDE can autocomplete phase values</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Cons:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Slightly more verbose</li>\n' +
      '<li>Need to repeat <code>phase:</code> keyword</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Option B: Shorthand Suffix (Alternative)</h4>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-jay-contract">contract ProductPage\n' +
      '  - {tag: name, type: data, dataType: string}           # Default: slow\n' +
      '  - {tag: inStock, type: data:fast, dataType: boolean}  # Fast rendering\n' +
      '  - {tag: quantity, type: variant:fast+interactive, dataType: number}  # Interactive</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>More concise</li>\n' +
      '<li>Reads naturally</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Cons:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Less explicit</li>\n' +
      '<li>Harder to parse</li>\n' +
      '<li>Doesn&#39;t follow existing syntax patterns</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Recommendation: Use Option A (inline phase annotation)</strong> - it&#39;s more explicit and follows Jay&#39;s existing syntax patterns.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Generated TypeScript Types</h3>\n' +
      '<p>From the contract above, the compiler would generate:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Generated from ProductPage.jay-contract</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">/** Full ViewState (for reference) - data and variant properties only */</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> interface ProductPageViewState <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  name<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  sku<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  price<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  inStock<span class="token operator">:</span> boolean<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  quantity<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  images<span class="token operator">:</span> Array<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
