      '<p>Both define contracts (<code>.jay-contract</code> files) and serve as integration points. They should have parallel identification schemes.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>2. Component Organization Limitations</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The current flat scanning approach prevents natural organization:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">src/components/\n' +
      '  ├── buttons/\n' +
      '  │   ├── submit-button.jay-html       ← name: &quot;submit-button&quot;\n' +
      '  │   └── cancel-button.jay-html\n' +
      '  └── forms/\n' +
      '      └── submit-button.jay-html       ← COLLISION! Also &quot;submit-button&quot;</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Without unique identifiers, components cannot be organized hierarchically.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>3. Current Scanning Implementation</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>scanProjectComponents()</code> function only scans the top level:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// packages/jay-stack/stack-cli/lib/editor-handlers.ts:493-522</span>\n' +
