{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay-Stack Environment Query Parameter Handling',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #53: Jay Stack Environment Query Parameter Handling</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>@jay-framework/compiler-jay-stack</code> plugin adds <code>?jay-client</code> and <code>?jay-server</code> query parameters to local imports to propagate the transformation environment through the import chain. However, this breaks the <code>jay-plugin</code> (jay:runtime) because:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Contract file detection fails</strong>: Files like <code>mood-tracker.jay-contract?jay-client</code> are not recognized as contract files because <code>hasExtension(source, JAY_CONTRACT_EXTENSION)</code> looks for <code>.jay-contract</code> at the end.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Jay-html file detection fails</strong>: Same issue with <code>.jay-html</code> files.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Potential collision with sandbox parameters</strong>: The <code>jay-plugin</code> already uses similar query parameters (<code>?jay-main-sandbox</code>, <code>?jay-worker-trusted</code>, <code>?jay-worker-sandbox</code>) for security transformations. These could collide or interfere with the new <code>?jay-client</code>/<code>?jay-server</code> parameters.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Example of the Problem</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In mood-tracker-plugin/lib/index.ts</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> MoodTrackerContract <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./mood-tracker.jay-contract'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// After jay-stack-compiler transformation:</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> MoodTrackerContract <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./mood-tracker.jay-contract?jay-client'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      `<span class="token comment">// jay-plugin sees: 'mood-tracker.jay-contract?jay-client'</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token comment">// jay-plugin checks: hasExtension(source, '.jay-contract') → FALSE ❌</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token comment">// Contract file is NOT processed!</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Options Analysis</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Option 1: Post-Processing Plugin to Strip Query Parameters</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add a third plugin that runs after <code>jay-stack:code-split</code> but before <code>jay:runtime</code> to strip the <code>?jay-client</code>/<code>?jay-server</code> suffixes.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Implementation:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">jayStackCompiler</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>jayOptions<span class="token operator">:</span> JayRollupConfig <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Plugin<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `      name<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'jay-stack:code-split'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `      enforce<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'pre'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token function">transform</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>code<span class="token punctuation">,</span> id<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token comment">/* ... add ?jay-client/server to imports */</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `      name<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'jay-stack:strip-query-params'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `      enforce<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'pre'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token function">transform</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>code<span class="token punctuation">,</span> id<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token comment">// Strip ?jay-client and ?jay-server from import paths</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token comment">// before jay:runtime sees them</span>\n' +
      `        <span class="token keyword">return</span> code<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">replace</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token operator">/</span>\\<span class="token operator">?</span>jay<span class="token operator">-</span>client<span class="token operator">/</span>g<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">''</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">replace</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token operator">/</span>\\<span class="token operator">?</span>jay<span class="token operator">-</span>server<span class="token operator">/</span>g<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">''</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token function">jayRuntime</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>jayOptions<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Simple to implement</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Minimal changes to existing code</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Quick fix for the immediate problem</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Cons:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>❌ Feels like a workaround, not a proper solution</li>\n' +
      '<li>❌ Plugin chain becomes more complex (3 plugins instead of 2)</li>\n' +
      '<li>❌ Fragile - relies on plugin ordering</li>\n' +
      '<li>❌ Doesn&#39;t solve the underlying architectural issue</li>\n' +
      '<li>❌ Code does a lot of work adding query params just to remove them immediately</li>\n' +
      '<li>❌ The <code>resolveId</code> hook still sees the query params - only <code>transform</code> is fixed</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Option 2: Universal Utility for Environment Metadata on Imports</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Create a shared utility in <code>@jay-framework/compiler-shared</code> that:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Provides a consistent API for adding/removing/detecting environment query parameters</li>\n' +
      '<li>Works for both <code>?jay-client</code>/<code>?jay-server</code> AND <code>?jay-main-sandbox</code>/<code>?jay-worker-*</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Is used by both <code>jay-stack-compiler</code> and <code>jay-plugin</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Implementation:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In @jay-framework/compiler-shared</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> enum JayEnvironment <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  Client <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">'client'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `  Server <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">'server'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `  MainSandbox <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">'main-sandbox'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `  WorkerTrusted <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">'worker-trusted'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `  WorkerSandbox <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">'worker-sandbox'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">const</span> JAY_QUERY_PREFIX <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">'?jay-'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">/**\n' +
      ' * Parse a module specifier to extract the base path and any jay environment\n' +
