{
  post: {
    title: 'Render Result Monads',
    content: '<h1>Render Result Monads - Design Log 54</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The Jay Stack framework uses several result types for server-side rendering phases:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>ServerError5xx</code> - Server errors (database down, internal errors)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>ClientError4xx</code> - Client errors (not found, unauthorized)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>Redirect3xx</code> - Redirects (moved, temporary redirect)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>PartialRender&lt;ViewState, CarryForward&gt;</code> - Successful partial render with data</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, these types are simple discriminated unions that are returned directly from render functions. The challenge is that error handling requires explicit if/else or switch statements, making the code verbose and error-prone.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Usage Pattern</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">async</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">renderSlowlyChanging</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>props<span class="token operator">:</span> PageProps<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>SlowlyRenderResult<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token operator">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">const</span> product <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token keyword">await</span> <span class="token function">getProductBySlug</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>props<span class="token punctuation">.</span>slug<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token operator">!</span>product<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token function">notFound</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>  <span class="token comment">// Must check and return early</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">const</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> id<span class="token punctuation">,</span> name<span class="token punctuation">,</span> description <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> product<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token function">partialRender</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">{</span> id<span class="token punctuation">,</span> name<span class="token punctuation">,</span> description <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token punctuation">{</span> productId<span class="token operator">:</span> id <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Pain Points</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Verbose Error Handling</strong>: Every potential failure requires explicit checks</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No Message Support</strong>: Error types don&#39;t carry human-readable messages or error details</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Chaining is Manual</strong>: Multiple operations require nested conditionals</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Try-Catch Wrapping</strong>: API/database calls need manual try-catch blocks</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Goals</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Functional Composition</strong>: Enable <code>map</code>, <code>flatMap</code> (chain) operations on results</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Error Short-Circuiting</strong>: Errors should automatically propagate through the chain</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Async Support</strong>: Mapping functions can be async</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Message/Details</strong>: Add support for error messages, codes, and details</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Type Safety</strong>: Maintain full TypeScript type inference throughout the chain</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Ergonomic API</strong>: Make common patterns simple and readable</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design Questions &amp; Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: What should the monad type be called?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The monad is <strong>not</strong> the result itself - it&#39;s a pipeline/chain that produces the result. So naming it <code>RenderResult</code> would be confusing:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Confusing: &quot;RenderResult&quot; is not what we're returning</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token keyword">return</span> RenderResult<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token keyword">from</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">map</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">toPhaseOutput</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>RenderPipeline&lt;T&gt;</code> - Emphasizes the pipeline/flow nature ✓</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>PhaseBuilder&lt;T&gt;</code> - Emphasizes building toward a phase output ✓</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>PhaseChain&lt;T&gt;</code> - Chain that produces phase output ✓</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>Render&lt;T&gt;</code> - Short, describes the render operation in progress</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>Pipeline&lt;T&gt;</code> - Generic but clear about purpose</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>DataPipeline&lt;T&gt;</code> - Generic data transformation pipeline</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> <code>RenderPipeline&lt;T&gt;</code> - It clearly communicates:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>It&#39;s about rendering (domain-specific)</li>\n' +
      '<li>It&#39;s a pipeline (operations flow through it)</li>\n' +
      '<li>The result comes out at the end via <code>.toPhaseOutput()</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Clear: A pipeline that produces phase output</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">return</span> RenderPipeline<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token keyword">for</span><span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ProductSlowViewState<span class="token punctuation">,</span> CarryForward<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token keyword">from</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token function">getProduct</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>id<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">map</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">toPhaseOutput</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: Should we rename <code>PartialRender</code> to something else?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The current name &quot;PartialRender&quot; can be confusing because:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>It implies the render is incomplete (but it&#39;s actually complete for that phase)</li>\n' +
      '<li>It&#39;s tied to the multi-phase rendering concept (slow/fast/interactive)</li>\n' +
      '<li>The &quot;partial&quot; refers to the ViewState being partial, not the render</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>PhaseRender</code> - Indicates a phase was rendered</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>RenderSuccess</code> - Generic success indicator</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>Rendered</code> - Simple past-tense</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>PhaseOutput</code> - Describes the output of a phase</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>Ok</code> - Rust-inspired, pairs with error types</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>Success</code> - Clear success indication</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> <code>PhaseOutput&lt;ViewState, CarryForward&gt;</code> - It&#39;s accurate (output of a rendering phase) and doesn&#39;t have the &quot;partial&quot; confusion.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: What message/details structure should error types have?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option A: Simple Message</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface ClientError4xx <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  kind<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'ClientError'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  status<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  message<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option B: Message + Error Code</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface ClientError4xx <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  kind<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'ClientError'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  status<span class="token operator">:</span> number<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  message'... 115327 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Render Result Monads","number":54}'
  }
}
