{
  post: {
    title: 'Full Stack Component Parameter Flow Refinement',
    content: '<h1>Full Stack Component Parameter Flow Refinement</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design logs #34, #48, #50, and #51 established the foundation for full stack components with three rendering phases (slow, fast, interactive) and type-safe phase validation. However, the information passing between phases needed refinement to better support carry-forward data and reactive view state.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>The Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Current implementation has carry-forward mechanisms but with type safety and completeness issues:</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Current State (as of implementation)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What Works:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Runtime correctly passes slow carry forward to fast render (<code>fast-changing-runner.ts</code> line 20-24)</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Fast carry forward is passed to interactive as <code>Signals&lt;CarryForward&gt;</code> (tuple <code>[Getter, Setter]</code> style)</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Builder tracks carry forward types through Services/Contexts arrays</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What Needs Improvement:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Fast View State Missing</strong>: Interactive constructor receives carry forward as signals but NOT fast view state as signals. Since interactive view state is a subset of fast view state, fast properties should be available reactively.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Implicit Carry Forward in Services Array</strong>: Carry forward is prepended to Services array (<code>[CarryForward, ...Services]</code>) making it <code>services[0]</code>, but this is not obvious from the type signature. Could be more explicit.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note on Current Design:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Carry forward is passed as first element of Services array (clever type-level manipulation)</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ <code>Signals&lt;T&gt;</code> using <code>[Getter&lt;T&gt;, Setter&lt;T&gt;]</code> tuple is correct - uses <code>@jay-framework/reactive</code> package</li>\n' +
      '<li>Runtime behavior in <code>fast-changing-runner.ts</code> correctly destructures: <code>compDefinition.fastRender(props, slowCarryForward, ...services)</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>The Solution</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Refine the parameter flow to make carry-forward data explicit, type-safe, and conditionally available based on which rendering phases are implemented.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Key Principles</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Conditional Service Parameters</strong>: Service parameters should only be included if the rendering phase exists</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Reactive View State</strong>: Fast view state should be available as signals in interactive phase</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Explicit Carry Forward</strong>: Each phase explicitly returns carry forward data for the next phase</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Type Safety</strong>: TypeScript enforces correct parameter usage at compile time</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Current vs Proposed Implementation</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Implementation - How Carry Forward Works</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The builder uses <strong>type-level array manipulation</strong> to pass carry forward through the Services array:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// jay-stack-builder.ts line 127-140</span>\n' +
      'withSlowlyRender<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>NewCarryForward <span class="token keyword">extends</span> object<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  slowlyRender<span class="token operator">:</span> RenderSlowly<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>Services<span class="token punctuation">,</span> PropsT<span class="token punctuation">,</span> SlowVS<span class="token punctuation">,</span> NewCarryForward<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Builder<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token string">'FastRender'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '  Refs<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  SlowVS<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  FastVS<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  InteractiveVS<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">[</span>NewCarryForward<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>Services<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>  <span class="token comment">// ✅ Carry forward prepended to Services!</span>\n' +
      '  Contexts<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  PropsT<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  Params<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  JayComponentCore<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PropsT<span class="token punctuation">,</span> InteractiveVS<span class="token operator">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// So RenderFast receives Services where Services[0] = SlowCarryForward</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// fast-changing-runner.ts correctly destructures:</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> fastRenderedPart <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token keyword">await</span> compDefinition<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">fastRender</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>pageProps<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>pageParams <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  partSlowlyCarryForward<span class="token punctuation">,</span>  <span class="token comment">// First element of services array</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>services<span class="token punctuation">,</span>             <span class="token comment">// Rest of services</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>This works correctly</strong> but is implicit - carry forward is hidden in the array type.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Interactive Constructor</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// simple-page/page.ts - Current usage</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">ProductsPageConstructor</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  props<span class="token operator">:</span> Props<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PageProps<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  refs<span class="token operator">:</span> PageElementRefs<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  carryForward<span class="token operator">:</span> Signals<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>FastCarryForward<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// Only carry forward, not view state</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Can access carry forward as signals:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>fastDynamicRendered<span class="token punctuation">,</span> setFastDynamicRendered<span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> carryForward<span class="token punctuation">.</span>fastDynamicRendered<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// ❌ Cannot access fast view state (e.g., fastRendered property)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// even though it was rendered in the fast phase</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Proposed Refinements</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Slow → Fast: Current Approach is Correct</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Current approach works well:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Carry forward is prepended to Services array: <code>[SlowCarryForward, ...Services]</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Runtime correctly destructures it as first parameter</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ Type system tracks it through array manipulation</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>No changes needed</strong> - the current design is elegant. Carry forward IS a service parameter, just passed via array manipulation.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Example (current implementation):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">const</span> productPage <span class="token operator">=</span> makeJayStackComponent<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ProductContract<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span>withProps<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> productId<span class="token operator">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withServices</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>DATABASE_SERVICE<span class="token punctuation">,</span> INVENTORY_SERVICE<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
