{
  post: {
    title: 'Style Binding Support In Jay-Html',
    content: '<h1>Style Binding Support in Jay-HTML</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Current State</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The runtime fully supports dynamic binding into style properties, as evidenced by the test in <code>/packages/runtime/runtime/test/lib/element.test.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token function">e</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'div'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n` +
      '  textContent<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token function">dp</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>text<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  style<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    color<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token function">dp</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>color<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    width<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token function">dp</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>width<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This runtime structure allows individual CSS properties to be bound dynamically using <code>dp()</code> (dynamic property), enabling reactive style updates.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>The Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The jay-html compiler does not support dynamic style bindings. The current implementation in <code>jay-html-compiler.ts</code> (lines 128-133) treats all style attributes as static CSS text:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>attrCanonical <span class="token operator">===</span> <span class="token string">'style'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n` +
      '  renderedAttributes<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">push</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">new</span> <span class="token function">RenderFragment</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">`style: {cssText: \'${attributes[attrName].replace(/\'/g, &quot;\\\\\'&quot;)}\'}`</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This means jay-html cannot express reactive styles like:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">style</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;color: {color}; width: {width}px&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Why This Matters</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Design Tool Integration</strong>: Design tools may want to bind dynamic values to style properties (colors, sizes, visibility, etc.)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Consistency</strong>: Other attributes support binding (class, value, disabled, etc.), but styles do not</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Component Flexibility</strong>: Components need reactive styling based on view state without resorting to class-based workarounds</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>High-Level Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Jay-HTML Syntax</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Support inline binding expressions within style attribute values:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">style</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;color: {color}; width: {width}; background: {bg}&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Mixed static and dynamic:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">style</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;margin: 10px; color: {textColor}; padding: {spacing}px&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Compilation Strategy</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Parse style attribute</strong>: Split CSS text into individual property declarations</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Detect bindings</strong>: For each property, check if the value contains <code>{...}</code> expressions</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Generate runtime code</strong>:<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Static properties: Use plain string values</li>\n' +
      '<li>Dynamic properties: Wrap in <code>dp()</code> with appropriate expression</li>\n' +
      '<li>Generate <code>style: { prop: value, ... }</code> object instead of <code>style: {cssText: &#39;...&#39;}</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Example Transformation</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Input jay-html:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">style</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;color: {color}; width: 100px; opacity: {isVisible?1:0}&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Generated code:</strong></p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token function">e</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'div'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n` +
      '  style<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    color<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token function">dp</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>color<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      `    width<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'100px'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '    opacity<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token function">dp</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>isVisible <span class="token operator">?</span> <span class="token number">1</span> <span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">0</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Edge Cases to Handle</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>All static styles</strong>: Keep current <code>cssText</code> optimization for fully static styles</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>CSS property name normalization</strong>: Convert kebab-case to camelCase (e.g., <code>background-color</code> → <code>backgroundColor</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Units</strong>: Handle cases where units are part of the binding (e.g., <code>{width}px</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Escaping</strong>: Handle quotes and special characters in static portions</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Empty/invalid styles</strong>: Gracefully handle malformed CSS</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Notes</h2>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Reuse existing expression parsing infrastructure (<code>parsePropertyExpression</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>CSS parsing can be simple splitting on <code>;</code> then <code>:</code> (no need for full CSS parser)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Consider performance: fully static styles should use <code>cssText</code> for efficiency</li>\n' +
      '<li>Tests needed in <code>compiler-jay-html</code> package to validate both static and dynamic style compilation</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Status</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Completed</strong> ✅</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Implementation Details</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The implementation adds a new PEG.js parser rule <code>styleDeclarations</code> that properly parses CSS declarations, handling:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Simple accessors: <code>{color}</code>, <code>{width}</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Template strings: <code>{fontSize}px</code> generates <code>`${vs.fontSize}px`</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Complex expressions through the template parser</li>\n' +
      '<li>Kebab-case to camelCase conversion for CSS properties</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Code Changes</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>PEG.js Parser</strong> (<code>/lib/expressions/expression-parser.pegjs</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>styleDeclarations</code> rule - Top-level entry point for parsing style strings</li>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>styleDeclaration</code> rule - Parses individual <code>property: value</code> pairs</li>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>stylePropName</code> rule - Matches CSS property names (including kebab-case)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>styleValueContent<'... 8495 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Style Binding Support In Jay-Html","number":57}'
  }
}
