{
  post: {
    title: 'Json-Patch Typed JSONPointer',
    content: '<h1>JSON Patch Typed JSONPointer</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>json-patch</code> package lacked type safety for JSONPointer paths. When writing a JSON patch operation, there was no autocomplete or type checking on the <code>path</code> property, making it easy to specify invalid paths that don&#39;t exist on the target object.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Before: No type safety - any path accepted</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> patch<span class="token operator">:</span> JSONPatch <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token punctuation">{</span> op<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'replace'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> path<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'nonexistent'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'path'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> value<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">5</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// No error!</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Solution</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Added a <code>Paths&lt;T&gt;</code> utility type that generates all valid path tuples for a given type <code>T</code>, then used it in <code>JSONPointer&lt;T&gt;</code> to provide type-safe path completion.</p>\n' +
