{
  post: {
    title: 'Relocate Deep Merge For Stack-Client-Runtime',
    content: '<h1>Relocate Deep Merge for Stack-Client-Runtime</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Context</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design Log #56 introduced <code>deepMergeViewStates</code> in <code>dev-server/lib/view-state-merger.ts</code> to merge slow and fast view states using <code>trackByMap</code> metadata from contracts. This works correctly on the server side.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>In <code>stack-client-runtime/lib/composite-component.ts</code> (lines 64-74), the render function uses <strong>shallow merge</strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">render<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">let</span> viewState <span class="token operator">=</span> defaultViewState<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    instances<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span>key<span class="token punctuation">,</span> instance<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>key<span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '            viewState<span class="token punctuation">[</span>key<span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '                <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>defaultViewState<span class="token punctuation">[</span>key<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>            <span class="token comment">// shallow</span>\n' +
      '                <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">materializeViewState</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>instance<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">render</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>  <span class="token comment">// shallow</span>\n' +
      '            <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '        <span class="token keyword">else</span> viewState <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>viewState<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>instance<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">render</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">return</span> viewState<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This has the same issue as before: nested objects and arrays are overwritten instead of merged.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Proposed Solution</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Move <code>deepMergeViewStates</code> to a shared location so both dev-server and stack-client-runtime can use it.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions &amp; Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Where should the merge algorithm live?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option A: json-patch library</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Pros: Already handles JSON transformations</li>\n' +
      '<li>Cons: json-patch is about RFC 6902 operations (diff/apply). This merge is semantically different - it&#39;s about combining two partial objects with identity-based array merging.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option B: New shared library (e.g., <code>packages/runtime/view-state-merge</code>)</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Pros: Clear single responsibility, clean dependency</li>\n' +
      '<li>Cons: Another package to maintain</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option C: Move to <code>@jay-framework/component</code> or existing runtime package</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Pros: No new package</li>\n' +
      '<li>Cons: May not be the right conceptual fit</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>✅ Answer:</strong> Option B - new shared library. Clean separation of concerns.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>2. How does trackByMap get to the client?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Currently <code>generateClientScript</code> passes <code>defaultViewState</code> and <code>fastCarryForward</code> to the client:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">const</span> viewState <span class="token operator">=</span> $<span class="token punctuation">{</span>JSON<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">stringify</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>defaultViewState<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> fastCarryForward <span class="token operator">=</span> $<span class="token punctuation">{</span>JSON<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">stringify</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>fastCarryForward<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> pageComp <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">makeCompositeJayComponent</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>render<span class="token punctuation">,</span> viewState<span class="token punctuation">,</span> fastCarryForward<span class="token punctuation">,</span> $<span class="token punctuation">{</span>compositeParts<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>To use deep merge on the client, we&#39;d need to also pass <code>trackByMap</code>. Is this acceptable?</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>✅ Answer:</strong> Yes, the client will also need the trackByMap.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>3. Is trackByMap even needed on the client?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In dev-server, we merge slow + fast view states <strong>before</strong> sending to client. On the client, <code>composite-component.ts</code> merges <code>defaultViewState</code> (which is already the merged slow+fast) with <code>instance.render()</code> results.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Question:</strong> What is <code>instance.render()</code> returning? Is it the interactive component&#39;s state updates? If so, does it also need trackBy-aware merging, or is the shallow merge acceptable for interactive updates?</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>✅ Answer:</strong> Yes, <code>instance.render()</code> returns the interactive part of the view state, which can be partial nested objects. We need trackByMap for proper identification of nested objects in arrays.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>4. Alternative: Generate merged view state with trackBy metadata embedded?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Instead of passing <code>trackByMap</code> separately, could the contract compiler embed trackBy info into the generated code for the client component? This would avoid runtime lookups.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>✅ Answer:</strong> The <code>generate-client-script</code> in stack-server-runtime can embed the trackByMap for the client and pass it to <code>makeCompositeJayComponent</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Create new library:</strong> <code>packages/runtime/view-state-merge</code></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Move <code>deepMergeViewStates</code> and <code>mergeArraysByTrackBy</code> from <code>dev-server/lib/view-state-merger.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Export as <code>@jay-framework/view-state-merge</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Update dev-server:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Import <code>deepMergeViewStates</code> from new library</li>\n' +
      '<li>Remove local implementation</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Update generate-client-script:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Add <code>trackByMap</code> parameter</li>\n' +
      '<li>Embed in generated HTML: <code>const trackByMap = ${JSON.stringify(trackByMap)};</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Pass to <code>makeCompositeJayComponent</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Update stack-client-runtime:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Import <code>deepMergeViewStates</code> from new library</li>\n' +
      '<li>Modify <code>makeCompositeJayComponent</code> to accept <code>trackByMap</code> parameter</li>\n' +
      '<li>Replace shallow merge in render function with <code>deepMergeViewStates</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Lessons Learned During Implementation</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Base Defines Structure</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Overlay-only array items should NOT be added. The base (defaultViewState) defines which items exist; overlay only updates properties on existing items.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>2. Arrays Without trackBy = Full Replacement</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When an array path is not in trackByMap, the overlay array completely replaces the base. This is a feature, not a limitation—useful for dynamic lists like search results.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>3. Server vs Client TrackByMaps</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Contracts require <code>trackBy</code> on all repeated arrays, but not all need identity-based merging on the client:</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Array Phase</th>\n' +
      '<th>Server</th>\n' +
      '<th>Client</th>\n' +
      '<th>Reason</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>slow</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>✅</td>\n' +
      '<td>✅</td>\n' +
      '<td>Structure from slow, updated in fast/interactive</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>fast</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>✅</td>\n' +
      '<td>✅</td>\n' +
      '<td>Structure from fast, updated in interactive</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<'... 891 more characters,
