{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay-Stack Server Actions',
    content: '<h1>Jay Stack Server Actions</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack pages currently support a three-phase rendering model:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Slow Render</strong> (build/data-change time) - Loads static data, pre-renders HTML</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Fast Render</strong> (request time) - Loads dynamic data, completes SSR</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Interactive</strong> (client time) - Handles user interactions with reactive state</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>However, once the page is loaded, <strong>client-side code has no way to call server-side functions</strong>. This is a critical gap for building real applications.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>In real applications, client components need to call server-side code for:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Search</strong>: User types in search box → call server search API</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Mutations</strong>: Add to cart, place order, update profile</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Data fetching</strong>: Load more items, refresh data</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Form submissions</strong>: Submit contact form, checkout</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, developers would need to:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Set up a separate API (Express routes, etc.)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Manually create fetch calls</li>\n' +
      '<li>Handle serialization/deserialization</li>\n' +
      '<li>Lose type safety between client and server</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Example: Current Gap</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// pages/products/[slug]/page.ts</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">ProductsPageConstructor</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  props<span class="token operator">:</span> Props<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PageProps<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  refs<span class="token operator">:</span> PageRefs<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  fastViewState<span class="token operator">:</span> Signals<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PageFastViewState<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  fastCarryForward<span class="token operator">:</span> ProductAndInventoryCarryForward<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  refs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>addToCart<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">onclick</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">// ❌ How do we call the server to add to cart?</span>\n' +
      `    <span class="token comment">// There's no mechanism for this!</span>\n` +
      '    <span class="token function">addToCart</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>fastCarryForward<span class="token punctuation">.</span>productId<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">1</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> render<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span><span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Should actions be defined per-page or globally?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: <strong>Globally as standalone modules.</strong> This enables reuse across pages and components. Actions are developer-to-developer (frontend ↔ backend), not designer-to-developer like contracts.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: How should actions relate to services?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: Actions use the same service injection pattern as render functions via <code>.withServices()</code>.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Should actions be type-safe end-to-end?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: Yes, using a builder pattern with explicit input/output types.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: How does this integrate with the contract system?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: <strong>It doesn&#39;t.</strong> Contracts are for designer ↔ developer communication. Actions are backend API definitions, purely developer concern.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: What about authentication/authorization?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: Actions can optionally receive request context for auth checks.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Where should action modules live?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: In <code>src/actions/</code> directory, organized by domain (e.g., <code>cart.actions.ts</code>, <code>search.actions.ts</code>).</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design Options Considered</h2>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Option</th>\n' +
      '<th>Description</th>\n' +
      '<th>Verdict</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Page-scoped actions</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td>Actions defined in <code>.withActions()</code> on the component builder</td>\n' +
      '<td>❌ Not reusable across pages</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Contract-based actions</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td>Actions defined in <code>.jay-contract</code> files</td>\n' +
      '<td>❌ Contracts are designer↔developer; actions are developer↔developer</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Hybrid (page + standalone)</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td>Both page-scoped and standalone modules</td>\n' +
      '<td>❌ Two ways to do same thing creates confusion</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong><code>&#39;use server&#39;</code> directive</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td>Next.js-style magic directive</td>\n' +
      '<td>❌ Requires complex compiler magic, less explicit</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>RPC-style standalone modules</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td>tRPC-inspired builder pattern</td>\n' +
      '<td>✅ <strong>Chosen</strong></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h3>Why RPC-Style Standalone Modules</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Reusability</strong> - Actions can be imported from any component, page, or context</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Explicit</strong> - Clear what runs on server vs client (no magic directives)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Type-safe</strong> - Full inference from handler function signature</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Familiar pattern</strong> - Builder API consistent with <code>makeJayStackComponent</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Service injection</strong> - Same <code>.withServices()</code> pattern as render phases</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Separation of concerns</strong> - Actions are backend API definitions, not UI contracts</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design: RPC-Style Action Builder</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Actions are defined as standalone modules using a builder pattern similar to <code>makeJayStackComponent</code>. They can be imported and called from any client component or context.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Action Builder API</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Types are <strong>inferred from the handler function</strong> - no need to specify separate Input/Output types:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// @jay-framework/fullstack-component</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      `type HttpMethod <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">'GET'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'POST'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'PUT'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'PATCH'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'DELETE'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// For mutations (default: POST)</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">makeJayAction</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>name<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> JayActionBuilder<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> unknown<span class="token punctuation">,</span> unknown<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'POST'</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// For queries/reads (default: GET)</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">makeJayQuery</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>name<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> JayActionBuilder<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> unknown<span class="token punctuation">,</span> unknown<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'GET'</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      'interface JayActionBuilder<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>\n' +
      '  Services <span class="token keyword">extends</span> any<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  Input<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  Output<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  DefaultMethod <span class="token keyword">extends</span> HttpMethod<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  withServices<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>NewServices <span class="token keywo'... 137256 more characters,
