[Build] 139/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=63-jay-stack-server-actions)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Client Context Initialization And Plugin Init',
    content: '<h1>Client Context Initialization and Plugin Init Files</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>⚠️ SUPERSEDED:</strong> This design log has been largely superseded by <a href="65-makejayinit-builder-pattern">Design Log #65 - makeJayInit Builder Pattern</a>. The core concepts remain valid, but the implementation has evolved to use the <code>makeJayInit()</code> builder pattern instead of separate <code>serverInit</code>/<code>clientInit</code> functions and <code>InitMarker</code> types.</p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack has a server-side initialization pattern via <code>jay.init.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Uses <code>onInit()</code> / <code>onShutdown()</code> hooks to register services</li>\n' +
      '<li>Services are global singletons available during server rendering</li>\n' +
      '<li>Dev-server loads and executes <code>jay.init.ts</code> on startup</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, client-side contexts are:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Created inside component constructors via <code>provideReactiveContext()</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Cannot receive data from the server (like access tokens)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Must be initialized inline, no centralized initialization</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins can declare:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>actions</code> - server-side actions auto-registered</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>contracts</code> - component contracts for pages</li>\n' +
      '<li>No client or server init files</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>No client context initialization pattern</strong> - Unlike server services, there&#39;s no <code>jay.client-init.ts</code> equivalent for initializing client-side contexts before components render.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>No server-to-client data passing</strong> - For auth tokens, user info, config, etc., there&#39;s no standard pattern to pass server-computed data to client contexts.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>No plugin init files</strong> - Plugins cannot define their own initialization logic that runs automatically when the plugin is used.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: What data needs to flow from server to client for context initialization?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Static/slowly-changing application configuration:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Configuration values (e.g., items per page in product search)</li>\n' +
      '<li>OAuth client IDs</li>\n' +
      '<li>Feature flags</li>\n' +
      '<li>A/B test information</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Key constraints:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Data is set at build/application initialization time (slowly changing)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Data does NOT change during the lifecycle of a client page</li>\n' +
      '<li>NOT per-request or per-page dynamic data</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: Should client init run before or after component tree creation?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Before - contexts must be available when components construct.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: How do plugins declare init dependencies on other plugins?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Use <code>package.json</code> dependencies. The framework reads dependency graph from package.json to determine init order.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: Should there be separate init files for server and client in plugins, or one file with both?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Separate files - different concerns with different dependencies (server code should never reach client bundle).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q5: What&#39;s the lifecycle of client contexts - per page load or per SPA navigation?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Per page for now. Future SPA support may change this.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Client Initialization File: <code>jay.client-init.ts</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>Similar to <code>jay.init.ts</code> for server, projects can create a <code>jay.client-init.ts</code> file:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// src/jay.client-init.ts</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> onClientInit<span class="token punctuation">,</span> registerGlobalContext <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/stack-client-runtime'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> APP_CONFIG_CONTEXT <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./contexts/app-config'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> THEME_CONTEXT<span class="token punctuation">,</span> createThemeContext <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'./contexts/theme'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      `<span class="token comment">// Called with only the 'project' namespace data from server</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token function">onClientInit</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'project'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>serverData<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Register app-wide contexts using server config</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">registerGlobalContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>APP_CONFIG_CONTEXT<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    itemsPerPage<span class="token operator">:</span> serverData<span class="token punctuation">.</span>itemsPerPage<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    features<span class="token operator">:</span> serverData<span class="token punctuation">.</span>featureFlags<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">registerGlobalContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>THEME_CONTEXT<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token function">createThemeContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>serverData<span class="token punctuation">.</span>defaultTheme<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>2. Server-to-Client Data via <code>setClientInitData</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>The server provides static application-level data for client initialization. This data is:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Set once at application startup (not per-request)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Slowly changing (configuration, feature flags)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Serializable to JSON</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Namespaced by key</strong> so each client init receives only its own data</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// src/jay.init.ts</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> onInit<span class="token punctuation">,</span> setClientInitData <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/stack-server-runtime'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token function">onInit</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token function">async </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Set static client init data with namespace key</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token function">setClientInitData</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'project'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n` +
      '    oauthClientId<span class="token operator">:</span> process<span class="token punctuation">.</span>env<span class="token punctuation">.</span>OAUTH_CLIENT_ID<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    itemsPerPage<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">20</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    featureFlags<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">await</span> <span class="token function">loadFeatureFlags</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    abTestVariants<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">await</span> <span class="token function">loadABTestConfig</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The data is serialized once and embedded in all page HTML. Each <code>onClientInit</code> callback receives only the data matching its namespace key.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>3. Client Context Registry</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The Jay runtime library already has a context registry infrastructure. We extend it to support pre-registered contexts that are available before component tree construction:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In @jay-framework/runtime (existing infrastructure)</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// We add functions to register contexts at the app level</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> registerGlobalContext<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>T<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>marker<span class="token ope'... 79207 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Client Context Initialization And Plugin Init","number":64}'
  }
}
