{
  post: {
    title: 'Transitive Plugin Dependency Resolution',
    content: '<h1>Transitive Plugin Dependency Resolution</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design Log #65 introduced <code>makeJayInit</code> for plugin initialization. The dev server discovers plugins by scanning the project&#39;s <code>package.json</code> dependencies and executes their init functions in dependency order.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Current discovery in <code>plugin-init-discovery.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Scans ONLY direct dependencies from project's package.json</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> allDeps <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>projectPackageJson<span class="token punctuation">.</span>dependencies<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>projectPackageJson<span class="token punctuation">.</span>devDependencies<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">for </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token keyword">const</span> depName <span class="token keyword">of</span> Object<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">keys</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>allDeps<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Try to find plugin.yaml...</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Two issues arise with transitive plugin dependencies:</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Issue 1: Client Import Resolution in Dev Mode</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When <code>wix-stores</code> depends on <code>wix-server-client</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Source file (<code>wix-stores/lib/contexts/wix-stores-context.ts</code>):</strong></p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> WIX_CLIENT_CONTEXT <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/wix-server-client'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p><strong>Built dist file (<code>wix-stores/dist/index.client.js</code>):</strong></p>\n' +
      `<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> WIX_CLIENT_CONTEXT <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/wix-server-client'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// ❌ Wrong - should be /client</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>The problem: Both in <strong>production</strong> (built dist files) and <strong>dev mode</strong>, the import resolves to the main entry (<code>index.js</code>) instead of the client entry (<code>index.client.js</code>). The Vite build&#39;s <code>external</code> configuration preserves the import as-is without transformation.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Issue 2: Transitive Plugin Discovery</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When a project only has <code>wix-stores</code> as a direct dependency:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-json">// Project package.json\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">&quot;dependencies&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token string">&quot;@jay-framework/wix-stores&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;workspace:^&quot;</span>\n' +
      "    // wix-server-client is NOT listed (it's a transitive dep)\n" +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>discoverPluginsWithInit</code> function only scans <strong>direct dependencies</strong>, so:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>wix-stores</code> is discovered ✅</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>wix-server-client</code> is NOT discovered ❌</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Result: <code>wix-server-client</code>&#39;s server init doesn&#39;t run → <code>WIX_CLIENT_SERVICE</code> is not registered → <code>wix-stores</code> init fails when calling <code>getService(WIX_CLIENT_SERVICE)</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Should plugin dependencies be explicitly declared in plugin.yaml?</strong>\n' +
      'A: No, use existing package.json dependencies. This is already available and avoids redundancy.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: How deep should transitive discovery go?</strong>\n' +
      'A: Recursively discover all plugin dependencies until no new plugins are found. Plugins are identified by having a <code>plugin.yaml</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: For Issue 1, where should the import transformation happen?</strong>\n' +
      'A: In the Jay Stack compiler&#39;s Vite plugin, we should transform imports from plugin packages to use the <code>/client</code> subpath when in client context.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix for Issue 2: Recursive Plugin Discovery</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Modify <code>discoverPluginsWithInit</code> to recursively discover transitive plugin dependencies:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">async</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">discoverPluginsWithInit</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  options<span class="token operator">:</span> PluginInitDiscoveryOptions<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PluginWithInit<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> plugins<span class="token operator">:</span> PluginWithInit<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> visitedPackages <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token keyword">new</span> Set<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Queue of package names to check</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> packagesToCheck<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      `  <span class="token comment">// 1. Seed with project's runtime dependencies (not devDependencies)</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> projectPackageJson <span class="token operator">=</span> JSON<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">parse</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      `    fs<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">readFileSync</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>path<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">join</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>projectRoot<span class="token punctuation">,</span> 'package<span class="token punctuation">.</span>json<span class="token string">'), '</span>utf<span class="token operator">-</span><span class="token number">8</span><span class="token string">'),\n` +
      '  );\n' +
      '  packagesToCheck.push(...Object.keys(projectPackageJson.dependencies || {}));\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  // 2. Process queue, discovering transitive plugin dependencies\n' +
      '  while (packagesToCheck.length &gt; 0) {\n' +
      '    const depName = packagesToCheck.shift()!;\n' +
      '    if (visitedPackages.has(depName)) continue;\n' +
      '    visitedPackages.add(depName);\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    // Check if this package is a Jay plugin\n' +
      '    const pluginInfo = await tryDiscoverPlugin(depName, projectRoot);\n' +
      '    if (!pluginInfo) continue;\n' +
      '\n' +
      '    plugins.push(pluginInfo);\n' +
      '\n' +
      "    // Add this plugin'</span>s dependencies to the queue\n" +
      '    packagesToCheck<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">push</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>pluginInfo<span class="token punctuation">.</span>dependencies<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> plugins<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix for Issue 1: Client Import Transformation</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add a Vite plugin transformation that rewrites plugin package imports in client context.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Important:</strong> Use <code>transform</code> hook, not <code>resolveId</code>, because rollup&#39;s <code>external</code> option is evaluated before <code>resolveId</code> hooks. By transforming the source code, we change the import path before any resolution or external checking happens.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>In <code>jayStackCompiler</code> (via <code>plugin-client-import-resolver.ts</code>):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token function">transform</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>code<span class="token punctuation">,</span> id<span clas'... 17160 more characters,
    description: '',
