{
  post: {
    title: 'Static Route Param Inference',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #70 - Static Route Param Inference</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Following Design Log #69, static override routes now have higher priority than dynamic routes. However, this creates a runtime issue: when a static route matches, Express doesn&#39;t extract URL parameters.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>For <code>/products/ceramic-flower-vase</code> (static override of <code>/products/[slug]</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Express route: <code>/products/ceramic-flower-vase</code> (no <code>:slug</code> param)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>req.params</code> = <code>{}</code> (empty)</li>\n' +
      '<li>The page component still expects <code>params.slug = &#39;ceramic-flower-vase&#39;</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>This breaks pages that use the same headless component as the dynamic route.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Should static overrides share logic with dynamic routes, or be completely independent?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>ceramic-flower-vase</code> page uses <code>productPage</code> headless component which calls <code>wixStores.products.getProductBySlug(props.slug)</code>. If we want this pattern to work, the static route needs access to the same params.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: Where should param inference happen?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>Options:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>At scan time (add inferred params to JayRoute)</li>\n' +
      '<li>At request time (derive from URL and sibling routes)</li>\n' +
      '<li>In the page itself (explicit config)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Option A: Infer Params at Scan Time</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Add <code>inferredParams</code> to <code>JayRoute</code> during scanning by finding sibling dynamic routes.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> type JayRoute <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  segments<span class="token operator">:</span> JayRouteSegment<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  rawRoute<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  jayHtmlPath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  compPath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  inferredParams<span class="token operator">?:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// NEW</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Algorithm:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>After scanning all routes, group by parent path</li>\n' +
      '<li>For each static route, find sibling dynamic routes</li>\n' +
      '<li>Map static segment values to param names from dynamic route</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Routes:\n' +
      '  /products/[slug]              → params from Express\n' +
      "  /products/ceramic-flower-vase → inferredParams: { slug: 'ceramic-flower-vase' }</code></pre>\n" +
      '<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Clean separation - route scanner handles all route logic</li>\n' +
      '<li>Params available immediately without URL parsing</li>\n' +
      '<li>Explicit about what&#39;s inferred</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Cons:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Cross-route analysis during scanning</li>\n' +
      '<li>Adds complexity to route scanner</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Option B: Synthesize Params at Request Time</h2>\n' +
      '<p>In <code>mkRoute</code>, the handler already has access to the route definition. Add a utility to extract params by matching URL segments against sibling dynamic routes.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In dev-server.ts</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">extractParamsFromUrl</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  url<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  currentRoute<span class="token operator">:</span> JayRoute<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  allRoutes<span class="token operator">:</span> JayRoutes<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Find sibling dynamic route that would match this URL</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token comment">// Extract params using that route's structure</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>No changes to route scanner</li>\n' +
      '<li>Params always reflect current URL</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Cons:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Requires passing all routes to each handler</li>\n' +
      '<li>More runtime work per request</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Option C: Use URL Parsing in the Handler</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Extract params directly from the URL path based on the route&#39;s position in the hierarchy.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In dev-server handler</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">const</span> urlSegments <span class="token operator">=</span> url<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">split</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'/'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">filter</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>Boolean<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> routeSegments <span class="token operator">=</span> route<span class="token punctuation">.</span>segments<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> pageParams<span class="token operator">:</span> Record<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> string<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>req<span class="token punctuation">.</span>params <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// For static routes, try to infer params from sibling dynamic routes</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>Object<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">keys</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>req<span class="token punctuation">.</span>params<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>length <span class="token operator">===</span> <span class="token number">0</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Find matching dynamic route and extract params</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Localized change in dev-server</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Cons:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Logic duplicated between scan and request handling</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Option D: Static Overrides Define Their Own Params</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Static pages explicitly declare what params they provide via a config file.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token comment"># page.conf.yaml</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">params</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  slug<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ceramic<span class="token punctuation">-</span>flower<span class="token punctuation">-</span>vase</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Explicit, no magic</li>\n' +
      '<li>Works for any scenario</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Cons:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Extra boilerplate for users</li>\n' +
      '<li>Easy to forget</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Recommendation</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option A (Infer at Scan Time)</strong> seems cleanest because:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Route scanner already analyzes all routes for sorting</li>\n' +
      '<li>Params become part of the route definition</li>\n' +
      '<li>No runtime overhead per request</li>\n' +
      '<li>Clear semantics: &quot;this static route provides these param values&quot;</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Implementation Sketch</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// After sorting, infer params</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">inferParamsForStaticRoutes</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>routes<span class="token operator">:</span> JayRoutes<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> JayRoutes <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Group routes by parent path (all segments except last)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> routesByParent <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">groupByParent</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>routes<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> routes<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">map</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>route<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">// Only process fully-static routes</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>route<span class="token punctuation">.</span>segments<span class="token punctuation">.</span'... 10092 more characters,
