{
  post: {
    title: 'Boolean Attribute Condition Style Parsing',
    content: '<h1>71 - Boolean Attribute Condition-Style Parsing</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>In Jay-HTML, boolean attributes like <code>disabled</code>, <code>hidden</code>, <code>checked</code> need to be conditionally applied based on view state values. Previously, boolean attributes used template-style parsing similar to dynamic attributes.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The expression <code>{categoryPage.sortBy.currentSort == newest}</code> was failing to compile because the template-style parser couldn&#39;t handle enum comparisons in boolean attribute context.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Template-style parsing for boolean attributes:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>❌ Doesn&#39;t support enum comparisons: <code>{status == active}</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>❌ Doesn&#39;t support logical operators: <code>{isEnabled &amp;&amp; status == active}</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>❌ Only works with simple accessor: <code>{isEnabled}</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>We need boolean attributes to support the same condition expressions as class ternaries and other conditional contexts.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Change <code>booleanAttribute</code> rule in the PEG.js parser from template-style to condition-style parsing.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Before (template style)</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-pegjs">booleanAttribute\n' +
      '  = template:template {\n' +
      '  let [renderFragment, isDynamic] = template;\n' +
      '  return isDynamic ?\n' +
      '      renderFragment.map(_ =&gt; `ba(${vars.currentVar} =&gt; ${_})`).plusImport(ba):\n' +
      '      renderFragment;\n' +
      '}</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>After (condition style)</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-pegjs">booleanAttribute\n' +
      '  = cond:condition {\n' +
      '  return cond.map(_ =&gt; `${vars.currentVar} =&gt; ${_}`)\n' +
      '}</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Key Changes</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>No curly braces required</strong>: Conditions are parsed directly</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Before: <code>{isEnabled}</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.isEnabled)</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>After: <code>isEnabled</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.isEnabled)</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Enum comparisons supported</strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>status == active</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.status === Status.active)</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Logical operators supported</strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>isEnabled &amp;&amp; status == active</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; (vs.isEnabled) &amp;&amp; (vs.status === Status.active))</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Nested property access</strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>sortBy.currentSort == newest</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.sortBy.currentSort === CurrentSort.newest)</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Comparison operators supported</strong> (<code>&lt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&gt;=</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>count &gt; 0</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.count &gt; 0)</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>page &lt;= 1</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.page &lt;= 1)</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>current &gt;= total</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.current &gt;= vs.total)</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Equality with numbers</strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>count == 5</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.count === 5)</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>count != 0</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.count !== 0)</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Field-to-field comparisons</strong> (using dotted paths for equality):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>a &gt;= b.value</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.a &gt;= vs.b?.value)</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>current == options.default</code> → <code>ba(vs =&gt; vs.current === vs.options?.default)</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Boolean attributes are always dynamic if present with a value</strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>disabled</code> (bare) → static, always present</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>disabled=&quot;condition&quot;</code> → dynamic, controlled by condition</li>\n' +
      '<li>Omit attribute → never present</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Supported Boolean Attributes</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Extended the list of recognized boolean attributes:</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Category</th>\n' +
      '<th>Attributes</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>Form</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>disabled</code>, <code>readonly</code>, <code>required</code>, <code>autofocus</code>, <code>multiple</code>, <code>novalidate</code>, <code>formnovalidate</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Selection</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>selected</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Visibility</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>hidden</code>, <code>open</code>, <code>inert</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Media</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>autoplay</code>, <code>controls</code>, <code>loop</code>, <code>muted</code>, <code>playsinline</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Other</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>reversed</code>, <code>ismap</code>, <code>defer</code>, <code>async</code>, <code>default</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> <code>checked</code> and <code>value</code> remain as PROPERTY type (using <code>dp()</code> with template-style <code>{expr}</code> syntax) because they reflect DOM property values, not boolean presence.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Parser Update (DONE)</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Update <code>booleanAttribute</code> rule in <code>expression-parser.pegjs</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Add <code>ba()</code> wrapper and import to parsed result</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Unit Test Updates (DONE)</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Update <code>parseBooleanAttributeExpression</code> tests in <code>expression-compiler.unit.test.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Add tests for boolean condition</li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Add tests for nested boolean (dotted path)</li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Add tests for enum comparison</li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Add tests for logical operators (&amp;&amp;, ||)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 3: Fixture Test Updates (DONE)</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Update <code>compiler-jay-html/test/fixtures/basics/attributes/attributes.jay-html</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Update example files: <code>scrum-board/lib/task.jay-html</code>, <code>scrum-board-with-context/lib/task.jay-html</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 4: Compiler Updates (DONE)</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Add empty string handling in <code>jay-html-compiler.ts</code> for empty boolean attributes like <code>&lt;button disabled&gt;&lt;/button&gt;</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Add boolean attribute handling in <code>jay-html-compiler-react.ts</code> for React target</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Results</h2>\n' +
      '<p>All tests pass: <code>yarn confirm</code> succeeds with exit code 0.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 5: Error Handling Improvements (DONE)</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Added <code>getExpressionHelp()</code> function in <code>expression-compiler.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Enhanced error messages with context-specific examples for each expression type</li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Error messages now include:<ul>\n' +
      '<li>The expression that failed to parse</li>\n' +
      '<li>The underlying parse error</li>\n' +
      '<li>Examples of valid syntax with ✓ markers</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 6: Comparison Operators (DONE)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Extended condition expressions to support comparison operators beyond just enum equality.</p>\n' +
      '<h4>Ordering Operators (<code>&lt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&gt;=</code>)</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Added <code>orderingCondition</code> rule in PEG.js parser</li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Supports comparison with numeric literals: <code>count &gt; 0</code>, <code>page &lt;= 1</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Supports comparison with any accessor: <code>current &gt;= total</code>, <code>a.value &lt; b.value</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Equality with Numbers</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Added <code>equalityComparisonCondition</code> rule in PEG.js parser</li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Supports equality with numbers: <code>count == 5</code>, <code>count != 0</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Normalizes <code>==</code> to <code>===</code> and <code>!=</code> to <code>!==</code> in output</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Field-to-Field Comparison</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> Supports comparing two fields using dotted accessors</li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> For equality operators: right side must be dotted path to distinguish from enum values<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>current == options.default</code> → field comparison</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>status == active</code> → enum comparison (unchanged)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> For ordering operators: any accessor allowed (no ambiguity with enums)<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>count &gt;= total</code> → works</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>a.page &lt;= b.page</code> → works</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Documentation Updated</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Added &quot;Boolean Attributes&quot; section to <code>docs/core/jay-html.md</code> with:<ul>\n' +
