{
  post: {
    title: 'Watch Linked Style Files In Dev Server',
    content: '<h1>Watch Linked Style Files in Dev Server</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>When jay-html files reference external CSS files via <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;...&quot;&gt;</code>, the CSS content is extracted and inlined during compilation (see Design Log #44). However, the dev server currently only watches the jay-html file itself, not the referenced CSS files.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>If a developer modifies a linked CSS file (e.g., <code>styles/main.css</code>), the dev server doesn&#39;t detect the change and won&#39;t recompile the jay-html file. The developer must manually touch/save the jay-html file to trigger a rebuild.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Example scenario:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token comment">&lt;!-- page.jay-html --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;link</span> <span class="token attribute">rel</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;stylesheet&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">href</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;styles/main.css&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Editing <code>styles/main.css</code> → No rebuild triggered → Stale CSS served</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q1: Where does CSS extraction happen?</strong>\n' +
      'A1: In <code>compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-html-parser.ts</code>, the <code>extractCss</code> function reads linked CSS files from disk at lines 722-752.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q2: Where is the current watch registration?</strong>\n' +
      'A2: In <code>rollup-plugin/lib/runtime/resolve-id.ts</code> line 78, only the jay-html file is watched via <code>watchChangesFor(context, resolvedBasePath)</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q3: Do we have access to the plugin context during CSS extraction?</strong>\n' +
      'A3: No. The <code>extractCss</code> function in the parser doesn&#39;t have access to Rollup/Vite&#39;s <code>PluginContext</code>. The context is available in the rollup-plugin layer but not passed down to the compiler.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q4: Should we watch CSS files that fail to load?</strong>\n' +
      'A4: Yes - if the file doesn&#39;t exist now, it might be created later. Watching it would trigger a rebuild when created.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Q5: Should external URLs be watched?</strong>\n' +
      'A5: No - external URLs (http://, https://, //) cannot be watched and are already skipped during extraction.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Option A: Return CSS file paths from parser, watch in plugin layer</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Modify <code>extractCss</code> to return the list of resolved CSS file paths alongside the CSS content. The rollup plugin can then add these to the watch list.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In jay-html-parser.ts</span>\n' +
      'interface ExtractCssResult <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  css<span class="token operator">:</span> string <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token keyword">undefined</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  linkedCssFiles<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Resolved absolute paths</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">async</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">extractCss</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  root<span class="token operator">:</span> HTMLElement<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  filePath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>WithValidations<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>ExtractCssResult<span class="token operator">&gt;&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In rollup-plugin, after parsing</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">for </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token keyword">const</span> cssFile <span class="token keyword">of</span> jayFile<span class="token punctuation">.</span>linkedCssFiles<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">watchChangesFor</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>context<span class="token punctuation">,</span> cssFile<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Clean separation of concerns</li>\n' +
      '<li>Parser remains context-agnostic</li>\n' +
      '<li>Easy to test</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Cons:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Requires modifying <code>JayHtmlSourceFile</code> interface</li>\n' +
      '<li>Need to pass linked files up through multiple layers</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Option B: Pass watch callback to parser</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Pass a callback function to the parser that gets called for each file that should be watched.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Minimal interface changes</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Cons:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Mixes concerns (parser shouldn&#39;t know about watching)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Harder to test</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Recommendation</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option A</strong> - cleaner architecture, follows existing patterns.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Extend parser to track linked CSS files</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Add <code>linkedCssFiles: string[]</code> to <code>JayHtmlSourceFile</code> interface in <code>jay-html-source-file.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Modify <code>extractCss</code> in <code>jay-html-parser.ts</code> to collect resolved CSS file paths</li>\n' +
      '<li>Store paths in the returned source file object</li>\n' +
      '<li>Update tests for <code>extractCss</code> to verify file paths are collected</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Add watch registration in rollup plugin</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>In <code>loadCssFile</code> (<code>rollup-plugin/lib/runtime/load.ts</code>), after parsing the jay-html file, iterate over <code>linkedCssFiles</code> and call <code>watchChangesFor</code> for each</li>\n' +
      '<li>Alternatively, add watching in the transform hook if that&#39;s where compilation happens</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 3: Test HMR behavior</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Manual test: modify a linked CSS file and verify rebuild triggers</li>\n' +
      '<li>Verify CSS changes appear in browser without manual refresh</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Files to Modify</h2>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay/packages/compiler/compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-html-source-file.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay/packages/compiler/compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-html-parser.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay/packages/compiler/rollup-plugin/lib/runtime/load.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay/packages/compiler/compiler-jay-html/test/css-extraction.test.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Trade-offs</h2>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Aspect</th>\n' +
      '<th>Current</th>\n' +
      '<th>Proposed</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>DX for CSS changes</td>\n' +
      '<td>Must save jay-html</td>\n' +
      '<td>Auto-rebuild</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Watch count</td>\n' +
      '<td>1 file per jay-html</td>\n' +
      '<td>1 + N CSS files</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Complexity</td>\n' +
      '<td>Simple</td>\n' +
      '<td>Slightly more plumbing</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification Criteria</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Modifying a linked CSS file triggers jay-html recompilation</li>\n' +
      '<li>Creating a previously-missing CSS file triggers recompilation</li>\n' +
      '<li>External URLs are not watched (no errors)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Existing tests continue to pass</li>\n' +
      '<li>No performance regression for pages without linked CSS</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Results</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Changes Made</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>1. <code>jay-html-source-file.ts</code></strong> - Added <code>linkedCssFiles?: string[]</code> property to track absolute paths of referenced CSS files.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>2. <code>jay-html-parser.ts</code></strong> - Modified <code>extractCss</code> function to:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Return <code>ExtractCssResult</code> interface with both <code>css</code> and <code>linkedCssFiles</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Collect resolved CSS file paths before attempting to read them (so missing files are still tracked)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Updated <code>parseJayFile</code> to pass <code>linkedCssFiles</code> to the source file</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>3. <code>rollup-plugin/lib/runtime/load.ts</code></strong> - Added watch registration:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Import <code>watchChangesFor</code> function</li>\n' +
      '<li>In <code>loadCssFile</code>, iterate over <code>linkedCssFiles</code> and register each for watching</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>4. <code>css-extraction.test.ts</code></strong> - Added 4 new tests:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Verify <code>linkedCssFiles</code> contains resolved paths</li>\n' +
      '<li>Verify <code>linkedCssFiles</code> is undefined when no CSS linked</li>\n' +
      '<li>Verify external URLs are excluded</li>\n' +
      '<li>Verify missing files are tracked for watch</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Test Results</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>compiler-jay-html: 406 passed, 4 skipped</li>\n' +
      '<li>rollup-plugin: 47 passed</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Deviations from Design</h3>\n' +
      '<p>None - implementation followed the design exactly.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Watch Linked Style Files In Dev Server","number":74}'
  }
}
