{
  post: {
    title: 'Slow Rendering Jay-Html To Jay-Html',
    content: '<h1>Slow Rendering: Jay-HTML to Jay-HTML</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Summary</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay-html to jay-html slow rendering pre-renders slow-phase bindings at build time, producing a new jay-html file with static data &quot;baked in&quot; while preserving fast/interactive bindings. This enables faster request-time rendering by skipping slow-phase work.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Key features:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Text/attribute bindings with <code>phase: slow</code> are resolved to literal values</li>\n' +
      '<li>Slow conditionals (<code>if</code>) are evaluated and removed or stripped</li>\n' +
      '<li>Slow arrays (<code>forEach</code>) are unrolled to <code>slowForEach</code> elements with <code>jayIndex</code> and <code>jayTrackBy</code> attributes</li>\n' +
      '<li>Fast/interactive bindings remain as template syntax for runtime resolution</li>\n' +
      '<li>Runtime <code>slowForEachItem()</code> function provides correct data context for item-scoped bindings</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Status:</strong> Core transformation engine, runtime support, component handling, and dev server integration implemented (Phase 1-5). Production build pending (Phase 6-7).</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack has three rendering phases (see Design Logs #34, #50):</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Slow (build-time)</strong>: Static data rendered at build time or data-change time</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Fast (request-time)</strong>: Dynamic data rendered per HTTP request (SSR)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Interactive (client-side)</strong>: Client-side interactivity and state management</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, all three phases execute at runtime:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>The dev server runs slow → fast → interactive on each request</li>\n' +
      '<li>Production could pre-render at build time, but the mechanism isn&#39;t defined</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>This design log proposes a <strong>jay-html to jay-html transformation</strong> for the slow phase:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Input: Original <code>*.jay-html</code> file with bindings for all phases</li>\n' +
      '<li>Output: Pre-rendered <code>*.jay-html</code> file with slow data &quot;baked in&quot;</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The generated jay-html can then be used for faster rendering in both dev server and production.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Behavior</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Every page request runs the full rendering pipeline:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Request → Load jay-html → Run slow render → Run fast render → Send HTML\n' +
      '                              ↓\n' +
      '                         (same work repeated every time)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>For pages with slow-phase data (static product info, categories, etc.), this is wasteful.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Desired Behavior</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Pre-render slow data once, reuse for every request:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Build Time:\n' +
      '  jay-html → slow render → pre-rendered jay-html (with slow data embedded)\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Request Time:\n' +
      '  pre-rendered jay-html → fast render → Send HTML\n' +
      '                              ↓\n' +
      '                         (skip slow render)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Use Cases</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Production builds</strong>: Generate pre-rendered jay-html files during build</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Dev server</strong>: Generate on first request, watch for changes, regenerate as needed</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Incremental regeneration</strong>: When slow data changes, regenerate specific pages</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions &amp; Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: What exactly gets &quot;baked in&quot; to the output jay-html?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Properties marked as <code>phase: slow</code> in the contract:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Text content: <code>{productName}</code> → literal value</li>\n' +
      '<li>Attributes: <code>href=&quot;{productUrl}&quot;</code> → literal value</li>\n' +
      '<li>Conditionals: <code>if=&quot;isOnSale&quot;</code> → either present or removed</li>\n' +
      '<li>Loops: <code>forEach=&quot;images&quot;</code> → unrolled to concrete elements</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: How do we identify which bindings are slow vs fast/interactive?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> From the contract&#39;s phase annotations (Design Log #50):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-jay-contract">contract ProductPage\n' +
      '  - {tag: name, type: data, dataType: string, phase: slow}\n' +
      '  - {tag: price, type: data, dataType: number, phase: fast}\n' +
      '  - {tag: quantity, type: variant, dataType: number, phase: fast+interactive}</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The compiler already generates <code>SlowViewState</code>, <code>FastViewState</code>, and <code>InteractiveViewState</code> types.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: How do we handle arrays (<code>forEach</code>) in slow phase?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Two scenarios:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Slow array (structure frozen at build time):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Input --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;li</span> <span class="token attribute">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;images&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">trackBy</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;id&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;{url}&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">alt</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;{alt}&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/li</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Output (unrolled) --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;li</span> <span class="token attribute">data-track-by</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;img1&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;/hero.jpg&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">alt</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;Hero image&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/li</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;li</span> <span class="token attribute">data-track-by</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;img2&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="token attribute">src</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;/detail.jpg&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">alt</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;Detail view&quot;</span> <span class="token punctuation">/</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/li</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Fast array (structure set at request time):</strong>\n' +
      'The <code>forEach</code> is preserved, only child properties with <code>phase: slow</code> are baked in.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: What about conditionals (<code>if</code>) in slow phase?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Slow conditional:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Input --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;span</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;badge&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">if</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;isOnSale&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>On Sale!<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Output (condition evaluated) --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;span</span> <span class="token attribute">class</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;badge&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>On Sale!<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">&lt;!-- or element removed if false --&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Fast conditional:</strong>\n' +
      'The <code>if</code> attribute is preserved for runtime evaluation.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q5: How do we handle nested components (headless/headful)?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Headful components:</strong> Each component&#39;s jay-html is transformed separately. The component reference stays, but the referenced jay-html is pre-rendered.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Headless components:</strong> The component&#39;s slot content may have slow bindings that get baked in. The component structure itself is preserved.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q6: What&#39;s the output file naming/location?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> With <code>loadParams</code>, a single jay-html can generate <strong>multiple pre-rendered files</strong> - one for each combination of URL parameters.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Example</strong>: <code>/products/[slug]/page.jay-html</code> with:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">loadParams<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token function">async </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation'... 128184 more characters,
