{
  post: {
    title: 'AI Agent Integration',
    content: '<h1>AI Agent Integration for Jay Components</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay components have a clear separation between UI (jay-html) and logic (TypeScript). The UI is driven by ViewState, and user interactions are handled through refs and events. This structured approach makes Jay ideal for AI agent automation:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>ViewState</strong> contains all data displayed on the page</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Refs</strong> define interactive elements (buttons, inputs, etc.)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Coordinates</strong> identify elements in collections (forEach items)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Events</strong> are triggered with <code>{event, viewState, coordinate}</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>This design log proposes exposing the page state and interactions to AI agents, enabling them to:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Read current page content (derived from ViewState)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Discover all possible interactions</li>\n' +
      '<li>Trigger events, including those on forEach items (e.g., remove from cart)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Situation</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Jay components are designed for human interaction via DOM events. There&#39;s no programmatic API for:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Querying the current ViewState</li>\n' +
      '<li>Listing available interactions</li>\n' +
      '<li>Triggering events from external code (like an AI agent)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Desired Behavior</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// AI agent can query page state and interactions</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> pageInfo <span class="token operator">=</span> window<span class="token punctuation">.</span>__JAY_AGENT__<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">getPageState</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// → { viewState: {...}, interactions: [...] }</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// AI can trigger events</span>\n' +
      `window<span class="token punctuation">.</span>__JAY_AGENT__<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">triggerEvent</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'click'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'prod-123'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'remove-btn'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token comment">// → Triggers click on remove button for product prod-123</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Use Cases</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>AI Test Automation</strong>: Agent navigates the app, fills forms, validates states</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>AI Assistant</strong>: Understands page context to help users</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Accessibility</strong>: Alternative interaction methods for assistive tech</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>E2E Testing</strong>: Programmatic interaction without DOM selectors</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions &amp; Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: What data should be exposed in the page state?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Three levels of information:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>ViewState</strong>: The current data driving the UI (product names, prices, cart items)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Interactions</strong>: Available actions with their coordinates and event types</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>DOM Elements</strong>: Reference to actual DOM elements with their coordinates (for setting values)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface AIPageState <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  viewState<span class="token operator">:</span> object<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// The current ViewState</span>\n' +
      '  interactions<span class="token operator">:</span> AIInteraction<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      'interface AIInteraction <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  refName<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// e.g., &quot;remove-btn&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  coordinate<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// e.g., [&quot;prod-123&quot;, &quot;remove-btn&quot;]</span>\n' +
      '  element<span class="token operator">:</span> Element<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// The actual DOM element</span>\n' +
      '  elementType<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// e.g., &quot;HTMLButtonElement&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  supportedEvents<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// e.g., [&quot;click&quot;, &quot;focus&quot;]</span>\n' +
      '  itemContext<span class="token operator">?:</span> object<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// ViewState of the forEach item (if applicable)</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>element</code> reference allows the AI to:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Read current input values directly from DOM</li>\n' +
      '<li>Set input values before triggering events (e.g., set text, then trigger <code>input</code> event)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Inspect element attributes and state</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: How do we handle forEach items?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Each item in a collection has a coordinate path. For nested collections:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;li</span> <span class="token attribute">forEach</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;cartItems&quot;</span> <span class="token attribute">trackBy</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;productId&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{productName}<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;remove&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>Remove<span class="token tag">&lt;/button</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;/li</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/ul</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The interactions would be:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-javascript"><span class="token punctuation">[</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">{</span> refName<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;remove&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> coordinate<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">&quot;prod-123&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">&quot;remove&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> itemContext<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> productId<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;prod-123&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">{</span> refName<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;remove&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> coordinate<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">&quot;prod-456&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">&quot;remove&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> itemContext<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> productId<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">&quot;prod-456&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">]</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: How do we keep the runtime package small?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option A: Separate package</strong> (Recommended)</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Create <code>@jay-framework/runtime-ai</code> package</li>\n' +
      '<li>Only imported when AI features are needed</li>\n' +
      '<li>Zero cost when not used</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option B: Conditional import via entry point</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>@jay-framework/runtime/ai</code> separate entry</li>\n' +
      '<li>Tree-shakeable if not imported</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Option C: Runtime flag</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>enableAIAgent()</code> function that adds capability</li>\n' +
      '<li>Still requires bundling the code</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Recommendation</strong>: Option A (separate package) for complete isolation.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: How does the AI trigger events?</h3>\n' +
