{
  post: {
    title: 'Unified Condition Parsing For Code Generation And Evaluation',
    content: '<h1>Unified Condition Parsing for Code Generation and Evaluation</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Summary</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Unify condition expression parsing so the same parser handles both:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Code generation</strong> - JavaScript code strings for the runtime (existing)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Compile-time evaluation</strong> - Evaluating conditions against data during slow rendering (new)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Currently these are handled separately, leading to potential inconsistency and duplicated parsing logic.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The Jay compiler has a PEG-based expression parser (<code>expression-parser.pegjs</code>) that parses condition expressions like:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Simple property access: <code>imageUrl</code>, <code>product.name</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Negation: <code>!imageUrl</code>, <code>!product.isAvailable</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Comparisons: <code>count &lt;= 0</code>, <code>status == pending</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Logical operators: <code>condition1 &amp;&amp; condition2</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The parser currently outputs <strong>JavaScript code strings</strong> via <code>RenderFragment</code> for code generation:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-pegjs">booleanCondition\n' +
      '  = not:bang? head:accessor {\n' +
      '    return not?\n' +
      '      head.render().map(_ =&gt; `!${_}`):\n' +
      '      head.render()\n' +
      '  }</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>For slow rendering (Design Log #75), we need to <strong>evaluate conditions at compile time</strong> against slow-phase data. We added a separate <code>analyzeSimpleCondition()</code> function with regex-based parsing:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">analyzeSimpleCondition</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>expr<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> AnalyzedCondition <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token keyword">null</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> trimmed <span class="token operator">=</span> expr<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">trim</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>trimmed<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">startsWith</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'!'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n` +
      '    <span class="token keyword">const</span> inner <span class="token operator">=</span> trimmed<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">slice</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token number">1</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">trim</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token operator">/^</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span>a<span class="token operator">-</span>zA<span class="token operator">-</span>Z_<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span>a<span class="token operator">-</span>zA<span class="token operator">-</span>Z0<span class="token operator">-</span>9_<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token operator">*</span>$<span class="token operator">/</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">test</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>inner<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> path<span class="token operator">:</span> inner<span class="token punctuation">,</span> isNegated<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">true</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token keyword">null</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token operator">/^</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span>a<span class="token operator">-</span>zA<span class="token operator">-</span>Z_<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span>a<span class="token operator">-</span>zA<span class="token operator">-</span>Z0<span class="token operator">-</span>9_<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token operator">*</span>$<span class="token operator">/</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">test</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>trimmed<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> path<span class="token operator">:</span> trimmed<span class="token punctuation">,</span> isNegated<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">false</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token keyword">null</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Having two separate parsing implementations causes:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Code duplication</strong> - Parsing logic exists in both PEG grammar and TypeScript regex</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Inconsistency risk</strong> - New expression features must be added to both places</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Limited evaluation</strong> - The regex approach only handles simple cases (<code>path</code> or <code>!path</code>)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>As we add more expression features (comparisons, logical operators), maintaining two parsers becomes increasingly problematic.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions &amp; Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: What condition types need evaluation support?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> All condition types should be supported:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Simple property access: <code>isOnSale</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Negation: <code>!imageUrl</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Comparisons: <code>count &gt; 0</code>, <code>price &lt;= 100</code>, <code>status == active</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Logical operators: <code>inStock &amp;&amp; !discontinued</code>, <code>a || b</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Parentheses: <code>(a &amp;&amp; b) || c</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: Can we modify the existing parser to return both?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Yes, but a better approach is to modify the parser to accept slow-phase data and perform partial evaluation inline (see Option D).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: What about complex expressions with mixed phases?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Replace slow properties with their values, then simplify the expression. For example:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Expression: &quot;!imageUrl &amp;&amp; price &gt; 0&quot;\n' +
      'Slow data: { imageUrl: &quot;&quot; }  (price is fast-phase)\n' +
      '\n' +
      "Step 1: Replace imageUrl with &quot;&quot; → &quot;!'' &amp;&amp; price &gt; 0&quot;\n" +
      'Step 2: Evaluate !&quot;&quot; → true\n' +
      'Step 3: Simplify: &quot;true &amp;&amp; price &gt; 0&quot; → &quot;price &gt; 0&quot;\n' +
      'Step 4: Output: Runtime expression for &quot;price &gt; 0&quot;</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The result is a simplified runtime-only expression with slow values already resolved.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Design Options</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Option A: Add AST Output to the PEG Parser</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Modify the grammar to return an intermediate AST that can be:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Rendered to JavaScript code (for code generation)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Evaluated against data (for slow rendering)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// New types</span>\n' +
      'type ConditionNode <span class="token operator">=</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> type<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'property'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> path<span class="token operator">:</span> string <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> type<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'negation'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> operand<span class="token operator">:</span> ConditionNode <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> type<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'comparison'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> left<span class="token operator">:</span> ConditionNode<span class="token punctuation">;</span> op<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> right<span class="token operator">:</span> ConditionNode <span class="token operator">|</span> number <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> type<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'logical'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> op<span class="token operator">`... 47968 more characters,
    description: '',
