[Build] 154/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=78-unified-condition-parsing-for-code-generation-and-evaluation)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Linked Contracts With Mixed Phase Properties',
    content: '<h1>Design Log 79: Linked Contracts with Mixed Phase Properties</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay contracts support <strong>linked sub-contracts</strong> via the <code>link</code> property, allowing contracts to reference reusable component contracts. For example:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token comment"># category-page.jay-contract</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> products\n' +
      '  type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> sub<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contract\n' +
      '  repeated<span class="token punctuation">:</span> true\n' +
      '  trackBy<span class="token punctuation">:</span> _id\n' +
      '  link<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ./product<span class="token punctuation">-</span>card <span class="token comment"># Links to product-card.jay-contract</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Jay also supports <strong>rendering phases</strong> (Design Log #50):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>slow</code>: Build-time rendering</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>fast</code>: Request-time SSR</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>fast+interactive</code>: Client-side mutable</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Design Log #50 establishes that <strong>slow arrays can have fast/interactive child properties</strong>:</p>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>&quot;Array&#39;s child properties can have <strong>later phases</strong> than the array itself&quot;</p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n' +
      '<p>When a slow array links to a contract that has fast/interactive properties, those properties are not properly handled:</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Example</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token comment"># category-page.jay-contract</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> products\n' +
      '  type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> sub<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contract\n' +
      '  repeated<span class="token punctuation">:</span> true\n' +
      '  trackBy<span class="token punctuation">:</span> _id\n' +
      `  link<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ./product<span class="token punctuation">-</span>card <span class="token comment"># No explicit phase = defaults to 'slow'</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment"># product-card.jay-contract</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> name\n' +
      '  type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data\n' +
      '  dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment"># phase: slow (default)</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> isAddingToCart\n' +
      '  type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> variant\n' +
      '  dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> boolean\n' +
      '  phase<span class="token punctuation">:</span> fast+interactive <span class="token comment"># Fast/interactive property!</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Behavior (Broken)</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Type Generation</strong>: <code>CategoryPageFastViewState</code> does NOT include <code>products</code></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Generated - WRONG</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">export</span> type CategoryPageFastViewState <span class="token operator">=</span> Pick<span class="token operator">&lt;</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'loadedProducts'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'hasMore'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '<span class="token comment">// Missing: products array with isAddingToCart</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Slow Render</strong>: Array is unrolled correctly, but expressions like <code>{isAddingToCart ? is-adding}</code> reference undefined values at runtime</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Runtime Error</strong>: <code>vs1.isAddingToCart</code> is undefined because the fast ViewState doesn&#39;t include the products array</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Expected Behavior (Per Design Log #50)</h3>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>&quot;Array appears in phase where it&#39;s set AND all later phases&quot;</p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p>So <code>products</code> should appear in:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>SlowViewState</code>: with slow properties (<code>name</code>, <code>thumbnail.url</code>, etc.)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>FastViewState</code>: with slow + fast properties (including <code>isAddingToCart</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>InteractiveViewState</code>: with all properties</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Root Cause Analysis</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Two components don&#39;t follow linked contracts:</p>\n' +
      '<h3>1. Phase Type Generator (<code>phase-type-generator.ts</code>)</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// extractPropertyPathsAndArrays only checks tag.tags</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>tag<span class="token punctuation">.</span>type<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">includes</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>ContractTagType<span class="token punctuation">.</span>subContract<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">&amp;&amp;</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">.</span>tags<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Processes inline nested tags</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Does NOT handle tag.link!</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>2. Slow Render Transform (<code>slow-render-transform.ts</code>)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>We just fixed this in the previous session - <code>buildPhaseMap</code> now follows <code>tag.link</code> via the import resolver. But the type generation still has the same gap.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Should we resolve linked contracts at contract parse time or at usage time?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: Usage time (lazy resolution) is better because:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Contracts may be used in different contexts</li>\n' +
      '<li>Avoids circular dependency issues</li>\n' +
      '<li>Consistent with how we just fixed slow render</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: How do we handle the runtime ViewState for slow arrays with fast properties?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: The fast phase needs to provide the array with fast properties for each item. The runtime <code>slowForEachItem</code> already supports this - it gets the item from the array and uses it for bindings. The issue is the fast render function isn&#39;t being typed/validated to return the array.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: What about the component&#39;s fast render function - does it need to return the full array?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A: Yes, if a slow array has fast properties, the fast render must return that array with the fast properties populated. The slow properties can be omitted (they&#39;re already rendered).</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Fix Type Generation</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Modify <code>extractPropertyPathsAndArrays</code> in <code>phase-type-generator.ts</code> to resolve linked contracts:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">extractPropertyPathsAndArrays</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '  tags<span class="token operator">:</span> ContractTag<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  targetPhase<span class="token operator">:</span> RenderingPhase<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  parentPath<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  parentPhase<span class="token operator">?:</span> RenderingPhase<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  parentTrackBy<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  importResolver<span class="token operator">?:</span> JayImportResolver<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// NEW</span>\n' +
      '  contractDir<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// NEW</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> paths<span class="token operator">:</span> PropertyPath<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> arrays<span class="token operator">:</span> ArrayInfo<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> asyncProps<span class="token operator">:</span> AsyncInfo<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// ...</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>tag<span class="token punctuation">.</span>type<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">includes</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>ContractTagType<span class="token punctuation">.</span>subContract<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">let</span> childTags<span class="token operator">:</span> ContractTag<span class="tok'... 22194 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Linked Contracts With Mixed Phase Properties","number":79}'
  }
}
