{
  post: {
    title: 'Materializing Dynamic Contracts For Agentic Generation',
    content: '<h1>Materializing Dynamic Contracts for Agentic Page Generation</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> February 1, 2026<br><strong>Status:</strong> Draft<br><strong>Related:</strong> Design Logs #60, #76, #77</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Terminology:</strong> This design uses &quot;materialization&quot; to describe the process of writing dynamic contracts to disk. This follows the database convention where a &quot;materialized view&quot; makes computed/virtual data concrete.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack supports agentic generation of web pages using headless components connected to contracts. When an AI agent has access to contract files, it can:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Understand the available data structure (tags, types, phases)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Use proper data bindings in jay-html templates (<code>{products.name}</code>, <code>{cart.items}</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Connect multiple headless components on a single page</li>\n' +
      '<li>Generate type-safe, working pages</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Current State:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Static contracts</strong>: Exist as <code>.jay-contract</code> files in plugins - agents read these directly</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Dynamic contracts</strong>: Generated at build/dev time via generator functions - <strong>not available as files</strong></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>This works well for static contracts because agents can read <code>.jay-contract</code> files like any other source file. However, dynamic contracts (e.g., CMS-driven schemas) are generated in-memory and never written to disk.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n' +
      '<p>When using headless components with dynamic contracts, the AI agent cannot &quot;see&quot; what contracts are available or their structure. This prevents the agent from:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Knowing which dynamic contracts exist</li>\n' +
      '<li>Understanding the tag structure for data bindings</li>\n' +
      '<li>Generating pages that use dynamic contract data</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Example scenario:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A CMS plugin generates contracts based on collections (BlogPosts, Products, Authors). The developer wants the agent to generate a blog listing page. The agent needs to know:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Contract name: <code>cms/blog-posts-list</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Available tags: <code>items</code> (repeated), <code>totalCount</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Item tags: <code>title</code> (string), <code>content</code> (string), <code>publishedAt</code> (string)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Without access to this information, the agent cannot generate correct jay-html.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: Where should materialized contract files be stored?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A) In the build folder: <code>build/materialized-contracts/</code>\n' +
      'B) In the src folder: <code>src/.materialized-contracts/</code></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Considerations:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Location</th>\n' +
      '<th>Pros</th>\n' +
      '<th>Cons</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>build/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Already gitignored, consistent with <code>slow-render-cache/</code> and <code>jay-runtime/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Must run materialization before agent can access</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>src/.materialized-contracts/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Can optionally commit for read-only agent environments</td>\n' +
      '<td>Adds generated files to src/</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Option A - <code>build/materialized-contracts/</code></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Rationale:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Consistent with existing build artifacts (<code>build/slow-render-cache/</code>, <code>build/jay-runtime/</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Already gitignored by default</li>\n' +
      '<li>Agents running in dev environment can run <code>jay-stack contracts</code> to materialize</li>\n' +
      '<li>Keeps <code>src/</code> clean for actual source files</li>\n' +
      '<li>All contracts (from all plugins) in one place for agent discovery</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: Should we include static contracts in the materialized output?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A) Only dynamic contracts (static ones are already files)\n' +
      'B) All contracts (unified view)\n' +
      'C) Index file pointing to static, materialized dynamic</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Option C - index file with references to static, materialized files for dynamic</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Rationale:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Agents get a single discovery point</li>\n' +
      '<li>No duplication of static contract files</li>\n' +
      '<li>Index provides metadata (plugin, type, path)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: When should contracts be generated?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A) Dev server startup only\n' +
      'B) CLI command only\n' +
      'C) Both dev server startup and CLI command\n' +
      'D) On-demand (lazy, when first requested)</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Option C - both dev server startup and CLI command</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Rationale:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Dev server: automatic, always up-to-date during development</li>\n' +
      '<li>CLI: useful for CI/CD, agent setup scripts, build pipelines</li>\n' +
      '<li>Flexibility for different workflows</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: What format should the generated files use?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A) YAML (<code>.jay-contract</code> format)\n' +
      'B) JSON\n' +
      'C) TypeScript (<code>.d.ts</code> or <code>.ts</code>)</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Option A - YAML (<code>.jay-contract</code> format)</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Rationale:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Consistent with existing static contracts</li>\n' +
      '<li>Agents already know how to read <code>.jay-contract</code> files</li>\n' +
      '<li>Human-readable for debugging</li>\n' +
      '<li>Can be used directly by the compiler if needed</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Q5: How do we handle contract staleness?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Problem:</strong> Dynamic contracts depend on external systems (CMS, databases). They can become stale.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Dev server: re-materialize on startup (no watching)</li>\n' +
