{
  post: {
    title: 'Automatic Server-Side Action Service Injection',
    content: '<h1>Automatic Server-Side Action Service Injection</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack server actions (design log 63) provide a type-safe RPC mechanism for client-server communication. Actions defined with <code>makeJayAction</code>/<code>makeJayQuery</code> can declare service dependencies via <code>.withServices()</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>When an action is called from <strong>client-side code</strong>, the compiler transforms the call to an HTTP request, and the action router on the server resolves services before executing the handler.</p>\n' +
      '<p>However, when an action is called from <strong>server-side code</strong> (e.g., in a render phase), services are NOT automatically injected. The action callable passes an empty array:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// jay-action-builder.ts line 186</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">(</span>input<span class="token operator">:</span> I<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>O<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token function">handler</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>input<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> as unknown as Services<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Backend code calling actions directly fails because services aren&#39;t injected:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// In renderSlowlyChanging - FAILS</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> result <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token keyword">await</span> <span class="token function">queryItems</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span> collectionId<span class="token punctuation">,</span> limit<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">20</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// ❌ WixDataService is undefined because services = []</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Why can&#39;t fullstack-component import resolveServices from stack-server-runtime?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: Circular dependency. <code>stack-server-runtime</code> depends on <code>fullstack-component</code> for types.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Can we detect at runtime if we&#39;re on server vs client?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: Yes, but the service resolver function still needs to be available somehow.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: Should we transform server-side action calls at build time?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: Could work, but adds complexity to the compiler and requires AST analysis of all call sites.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Q: What about using a global resolver?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>A: This is the cleanest approach - <code>fullstack-component</code> checks for a global resolver, <code>stack-server-runtime</code> registers it at startup.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design: Global Service Resolver</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Mechanism</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Define resolver interface</strong> in <code>fullstack-component</code>:</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// jay-action-builder.ts</span>\n' +
      'type ServiceResolver <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>markers<span class="token operator">:</span> any<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> any<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      'declare global <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">var</span> __JAY_SERVICE_RESOLVER__<span class="token operator">:</span> ServiceResolver <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token keyword">undefined</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
