[Build] 160/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=84-headless-component-props-and-repeater-support)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Rendering Phases And Agent Kit For Agentic Generation',
    content: '<h1>Rendering Phases and Agent Kit for Agentic Generation</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> February 6, 2026<br><strong>Status:</strong> Draft<br><strong>Related:</strong> Design Logs #34, #50 (phases &amp; headless), #80, #84, #76</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack agentic generation relies on several existing pieces:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Rendering phases</strong> (Design Logs #34, #50): Slow (build-time), fast (request-time), interactive (client). Contracts declare phase per tag; agents need to know which data is available when.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Contract discovery and materialization</strong> (Design Log #80): We use a single command <strong><code>jay-stack agent-kit</code></strong> (renamed from <code>contracts</code>) that prepares the full agent kit: materializes dynamic contracts, writes contracts-index and plugins-index, and outputs to <strong>agent-kit/</strong> only (no separate <code>build/materialized-contracts/</code>). Agents read from agent-kit to understand data shapes and bindings.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Actions and params discovery via CLI</strong> (Design Log #84): <code>jay-stack action &lt;plugin&gt;/&lt;action&gt;</code>, <code>jay-stack params &lt;plugin&gt;/&lt;contract&gt;</code> (load params), and plugin <code>.action.yaml</code> files let agents discover valid prop/param values.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Today an agent must:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Know to run <code>jay-stack agent-kit</code> and read materialized contracts from <strong>agent-kit</strong></li>\n' +
      '<li>Know to run <code>jay-stack params</code> / <code>jay-stack action</code> for discovery</li>\n' +
      '<li>Know jay-html syntax, headless script tags, <code>jay:</code> instances, phase semantics</li>\n' +
      '<li>Have instructions and context scattered (README, plugin docs, etc.)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>We need a <strong>single, coherent folder</strong> that a coding agent can use to create jay-html files: instructions, contracts index, <strong>plugins index</strong>, and <strong>minimal content</strong> (which components and how to use them). Content is <strong>input for the agent</strong> to generate pages — agent-only, no CLI transform. Metadata (contract shape, phases) lives in the kit; content does not repeat it.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: Where should the agent kit live?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A) <code>src/.agent-kit/</code> — next to source, dot-prefix for “tooling”<br>B) <code>agent-kit/</code> at project root — visible, not mixed with app source<br>C) <code>build/agent-kit/</code> — generated; populated by CLI from contracts + plugin manifests</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Option B — <code>agent-kit/</code> at project root.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Rationale:</strong> Visible to agents and humans; not inside <code>src/</code> so it doesn’t blur app vs instructions. Materialized contracts, contracts index, and plugins index live in agent-kit (single place; no build copy). Can be committed (instructions + content) or partially generated (contracts, plugins index, actions/params refs).</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2b: Should we materialize plugin.yaml files?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A) <strong>Index only</strong> — <code>plugins-index.yaml</code> lists plugin name + path to each plugin (e.g. <code>node_modules/@wix/stores</code>). Agent reads <code>plugin.yaml</code> from that path when needed.<br>B) <strong>Materialize</strong> — Copy each plugin’s <code>plugin.yaml</code> into <code>agent-kit/plugins/&lt;name&gt;.yaml</code> so the kit is self-contained; agent never touches node_modules.<br>C) <strong>Index + optional materialize</strong> — Index always; <code>--materialize-plugins</code> or similar copies plugin.yaml into agent-kit for offline/read-only use.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Option A for v1 (index only). Option B or C if we need a fully self-contained kit (e.g. agent has no filesystem access to node_modules).</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Rationale:</strong> Index is enough for discovery; contract metadata is already in materialized-contracts. Materializing plugin.yaml duplicates data and must be kept in sync. Prefer index-only unless the agent cannot read plugin paths.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: What belongs in the agent kit?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Proposed contents:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Item</th>\n' +
      '<th>Purpose</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>README.md</code> or <code>INSTRUCTIONS.md</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>How to generate jay-html: phases, headless usage, CLI commands, file layout</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>plugin.yaml</code> (or symlink/copy)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Optional: project-level plugin manifest or pointer to plugins in use</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Contracts (materialized)</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code> + <code>contracts-index.yaml</code>; <code>jay-stack agent-kit</code> writes here (no build copy). Agents discover contracts from here.</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Plugins index</td>\n' +
      '<td>Generated by <code>jay-stack agent-kit</code>; lists plugins (name, path, contracts). Single discovery point for which plugins/contracts exist.</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Actions / params reference</td>\n' +
      '<td>Optional: output of <code>jay-stack params …</code>, <code>jay-stack action …</code>, or curated list in <code>references/</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Content as Markdown</td>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Minimal</strong>: which components (plugin/contract) and how to use them. All other metadata (contract shape, phases) lives in the kit; do not repeat here.</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: How do we indicate headless components (including nested) with their properties?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>We need to support <strong>nested components with specific props</strong>, e.g. “3 product cards with specific product IDs” — not only “one list key + forEach”. The content format must express:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Which components</strong> (plugin + contract) to use.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>How to use them</strong>: page-level (key), or nested with <strong>static props</strong> (e.g. three product cards: <code>productId</code>: id1, id2, id3), or <strong>dynamic</strong> (forEach + trackBy + props from context).</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p>A) <strong>Frontmatter (page-level)</strong> + <strong>minimal spec for nested</strong> — e.g. frontmatter: <code>headless: [{ plugin, contract, key }]</code>. Nested: list of <code>{ plugin, contract, props?: { productId: &quot;id1&quot; } | { forEach, trackBy, props } }</code> so we can say “3 product cards, productId = x, y, z” or “product cards from list”.<br>B) <strong>Single minimal spec file per page</strong> — One YAML with <code>page: { headless: [...] }</code> and <code>nested: [{ contract (or plugin/contract), props | forEach/trackBy/props }]</code>. No duplication of contract metadata; just component ref + usage.<br>C) <strong>Block directives in markdown</strong> — e.g. <code>::: wix-stores/product-card productId=&quot;id1&quot;</code> for each instance; or one directive with <code>forEach</code> and <code>props</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> <strong>Minimal information only</strong>: component ref (plugin/contract) + how to use (key for page-level; for nested: either fixed props per instance or forEach + trackBy + props). All metadata (contract shape, phases, valid prop names) lives in the kit (contracts, plugins index); content does not repeat it. Prefer a single minimal spec (frontmatter for page-level, small YAML or inline for nested) so the agent has one clear place to read “what components + how”.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Rationale:</strong> Nested with specific IDs (e.g. 3 product cards) is a core case; the format must support both “list from data” (forEach) and “fixed set of instances with props”. Keeping content minimal avoids drift from contract metadata and keeps the kit as the single source of truth.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: Who transforms content → jay-html?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> <strong>Agent only.</strong> The content (markdown + minimal spec) is <strong>input to help the agent generate the pages</strong>. The agent reads the kit (instructions, contracts index, plugins index, materialized contracts) and the minimal content (which components, how to use them), then produces jay-html. No CLI transform step: content is not “compiled” into jay-html by the stack; it is guidance for the agent.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q5: Should we specify params in the contract (like props) and generate the Params interface?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Background:</strong> Components that use URL/load params (e.g. product page with <code>[slug]</code>) today declare the params type manually, e.g. in <code>product-page.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> interface ProductPageParams <span class="token keyword">extends</span> UrlParams <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  slug<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The contract file (<code>product-page.jay-contract</code>) currently has only <code>tags</code> (ViewState); it has no declaration of params. Design Log #84 describes load params discovery via <code>jay-stack params &lt;plugin&gt;/&lt;contract&gt;</code> and <code>withLoadParams</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Proposal:</strong> Specify params in the contract (similar to props), and <strong>generate</strong> the Params interface from the contract so the contract is the single source of truth. Example:</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Contract (e.g. <code>product-page.jay-contract</code>):</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> product<span class="token punctuation">-</span>page\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">params</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  slug<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string <span class="token comment"># type is ignored; URL pa'... 28815 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Rendering Phases And Agent Kit For Agentic Generation","number":85}'
  }
}
[Build] 161/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=85-rendering-phases-and-agent-kit-for-agentic-generation)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay Stack Full Workflow Lifecycle',
    content: '<h1>Jay Stack Full Workflow Lifecycle</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> February 4, 2026<br><strong>Status:</strong> Draft<br><strong>Related:</strong> Design Logs #50, #80, #84, #85</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay Stack has multiple stages from project setup to runtime. Several pieces exist (CLI commands, rendering phases, plugin system, agent-kit) but the full lifecycle is not tracked as a coherent workflow. Understanding the lifecycle is important for:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Knowing which CLI commands/steps exist or are needed at each stage</li>\n' +
      '<li>Ensuring plugins can hook into the right lifecycle points</li>\n' +
      '<li>Giving agents (and developers) a clear sequence to follow</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Lifecycle Phases</h2>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n' +
      '│ 1. PROJECT SETUP                                        │\n' +
      '│    create project, install plugins                      │\n' +
      '├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│ 2. PLUGIN SETUP                                         │\n' +
      '│    configure plugins, generate reference info            │\n' +
      '├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│ 3. AGENT KIT                                            │\n' +
      '│    materialize contracts, prepare instructions/content   │\n' +
      '├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│ 4. DEVELOPMENT (agent or human coding)                  │\n' +
      '│    generate/write pages, components, contracts           │\n' +
      '├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│ 5. SLOW RENDER (build / dev server start)               │\n' +
      '│    static generation, SSG, slow phase                    │\n' +
      '├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│ 6. FAST RENDER (SSR / request time)                     │\n' +
      '│    per-request data, session-aware rendering              │\n' +
      '├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│ 7. INTERACTIVE (CSR / client-side)                      │\n' +
      '│    hydration, signals, reactive updates                   │\n' +
      '├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│ 8. SLOW REFRESH (data change → re-render)               │\n' +
      '│    incremental slow re-render for specific routes        │\n' +
      '└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Phase Details</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Project Setup</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What happens:</strong> Developer creates a new project, installs plugins.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Existing:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>npm init</code> / project scaffold</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>npm install</code> plugins (e.g., <code>@wix/stores</code>, <code>@wix/data</code>)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>CLI:</strong> None specific to jay-stack yet for project creation.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>No new commands needed</strong> - standard npm workflow.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Plugin Setup</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What happens:</strong> Plugins are configured. Some plugins (like wix-data) need initial configuration and can generate reference files, default configs, or seed data after basic setup.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Example:</strong> After installing <code>@wix/data</code>, the developer runs a setup command. The plugin:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Creates default collection schemas</li>\n' +
      '<li>Generates reference config files</li>\n' +
      '<li>Seeds initial data (if applicable)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Validates plugin prerequisites (API keys, etc.)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Question: Should this be a dedicated CLI command?</strong></p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Yes. Plugins need a lifecycle hook for post-install setup.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Proposed command:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token comment"># Run setup for all installed plugins</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">jay-stack</span> <span class="token function">setup</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment"># Run setup for a specific plugin</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">jay-stack</span> <span class="token function">setup</span> <span class="token function">wix-stores</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment"># Re-run setup (e.g., after config change)</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">jay-stack</span> <span class="token function">setup</span> <span class="token function">wix-data</span> --force</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What <code>jay-stack setup</code> does:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Scans installed plugins for a <code>setup</code> export or <code>setup</code> entry in <code>plugin.yaml</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Runs each plugin&#39;s setup function</li>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin setup can:<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Create/update config files (in <code>src/</code> or project root)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Generate reference data (write to <code>agent-kit/references/</code> or project-level config)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Validate configuration (API keys, connections)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Report status (configured/needs-attention)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Plugin.yaml extension:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token comment"># plugin.yaml</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> wix<span class="token punctuation">-</span>data\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">setup</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  handler<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ./setup.js <span class="token comment"># Setup function entry point</span>\n' +
      '  description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Configure CMS collections and seed data\n' +
      '  creates<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> src/data/collections/ <span class="token comment"># Files/dirs this setup creates</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p><strong>When to run:</strong> After install, before agent-kit. Not automatic - developer explicitly runs it.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 3: Agent Kit</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What happens:</strong> Prepare everything an agent needs to generate pages.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Existing:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-stack contracts</code> - materializes contracts to disk</li>\n' +
      '<li>Design Log #85 defines <code>agent-kit/</code> folder structure</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Proposed:</strong> Rename/extend to <code>jay-stack agent-kit</code> (as in #85):</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Materialize dynamic contracts → <code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Generate contracts-index.yaml and plugins-index.yaml</li>\n' +
      '<li>Ensure INSTRUCTIONS.md is present</li>\n' +
      '<li>Optionally run <code>jay-stack params</code> for all components with load params</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>CLI:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token function">jay-stack</span> <span class="token function">agent-kit</span>          <span class="token comment"># Full agent-kit generation</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">jay-stack</span> <span class="token function">params</span> <span class="token operator">&lt;</span>contract<span class="token operator">&gt;</span>  <span class="token comment"># Discover load param values (from #84 Phase 1b)</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">jay-stack</span> <span class="token function">action</span> <span class="token operator">&lt;</span>action<span class="token operator">&gt;</span>    <span class="token comment"># Run plugin action for data discovery</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 4: Development (Agent or Human Coding)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What happens:</strong> Agent or developer creates/edits pages, components, contracts.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Agent workflow:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Read <code>agent-kit/INSTRUCTIONS.md</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Read contracts-index, plugins-index</li>\n' +
      '<li>Read content files from <code>agent-kit/content/</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Generate <code>src/pages/**/page.jay-html</code>, <code>page.jay-contract</code>, <code>page.conf.yaml</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Human workflow:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Write jay-html templates, TypeScript components</li>\n' +
      '<li>Use <code>jay-stack validate</code> to check files</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Existing CLI:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-stack validate</code> - validates .jay-html and .jay-contract files</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>jay-stack validate-plugin</code> - validates plugin packages</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 5: Slow Render (Build Time)</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What happens:</strong> Static site generation. All slow-phase data is resolved, templates are rendered with slow ViewState, carry-forward data is stored.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Existing:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Dev server runs slow rendering on startup</li>\n' +
      '<li>Build (not yet fully implemented) would do the same</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What runs:</strong></p>\n' +
