[Build] 162/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=86-jay-stack-full-workflow-lifecycle)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay-Stack Setup Command',
    content: '<h1>Jay Stack Setup Command</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> February 9, 2026<br><strong>Status:</strong> Draft<br><strong>Related:</strong> Design Logs #60 (plugin system), #65 (makeJayInit), #85 (agent-kit), #86 (lifecycle)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design Log #86 identifies Phase 2 &quot;Plugin Setup&quot; as a gap: after installing plugins and before running <code>agent-kit</code>, plugins need configuration (credentials, connections) and can generate reference data (collection schemas, category lists). Today:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin init (<code>makeJayInit</code>) registers services but has no mechanism for first-time config setup</li>\n' +
      '<li>No CLI command creates config templates or validates credentials</li>\n' +
      '<li>The agent-kit template docs (<code>cli-commands.md</code>, <code>project-structure.md</code>) already reference <code>jay-stack setup</code> but it doesn&#39;t exist</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>PluginManifest</code> has no <code>setup</code> field</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Plugins like <code>wix-data</code> and <code>wix-stores</code> need credentials (API keys, site URLs) to function. Currently a developer must manually create config files by reading plugin docs. There&#39;s no:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Guided config creation (templates with required fields)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Credential/connection validation before attempting to build</li>\n' +
      '<li>Reference data generation (collection schemas, product lists) that agents need for informed page generation</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Three-Phase Setup Flow</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">jay-stack setup [plugin] [--force]\n' +
      '         │\n' +
      '         ▼\n' +
      '┌──────────────────────────┐\n' +
      '│ 1. CONFIG CHECK          │\n' +
      '│ Does config exist?       │\n' +
      '│ No → create template     │\n' +
      '│ Yes → continue           │\n' +
      '├──────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│ 2. SERVICE INIT + VERIFY │\n' +
      '│ Run plugin init          │\n' +
      '│ Failed → report error    │\n' +
      '│ OK → continue            │\n' +
      '├──────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│ 3. REFERENCE GENERATION  │\n' +
      '│ Call setup hook with      │\n' +
      '│ live services             │\n' +
      '│ Write to agent-kit/      │\n' +
      '│ references/&lt;plugin&gt;/     │\n' +
      '└──────────────────────────┘</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Plugin.yaml Extension</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token comment"># plugin.yaml</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> wix<span class="token punctuation">-</span>stores\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">setup</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  handler<span class="token punctuation">:</span> setupWixStores <span class="token comment"># Export name (NPM) or path (local)</span>\n' +
      '  description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Configure Wix Stores credentials and generate product catalog reference</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>PluginManifest Type Change</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In <code>compiler-shared/lib/plugin-resolution.ts</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">export</span> interface PluginManifest <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// ...existing fields...</span>\n' +
      '  setup<span class="token operator">?:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    handler<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Export name or relative path to setup module</span>\n' +
      '    description<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Human-readable description of what setup does</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Setup Handler Interface</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface PluginSetupContext <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  pluginName<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  projectRoot<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  configDir<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// From .jay configBase, defaults to ./config</span>\n' +
      '  referencesDir<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// agent-kit/references/&lt;plugin&gt;/</span>\n' +
      '  services<span class="token operator">:</span> Map<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>symbol<span class="token punctuation">,</span> unknown<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Registered services (empty if init failed)</span>\n' +
      '  initError<span class="token operator">?:</span> Error<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Present if plugin init failed</span>\n' +
      '  force<span class="token operator">:</span> boolean<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// --force flag</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      'interface PluginSetupResult <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  status<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'configured'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'needs-config'</span> <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token string">'error'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  configCreated<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Config files created (relative paths)</span>\n' +
      '  referencesCreated<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Reference files created (relative paths)</span>\n' +
      '  message<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// Human-readable status message</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Plugin exports this function:</span>\n' +
      'type PluginSetupHandler <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>context<span class="token operator">:</span> PluginSetupContext<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PluginSetupResult<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>How the Handler Works</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The handler gets full context and decides what to do:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Example: wix-stores/lib/setup.ts</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">async</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">setupWixStores</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>ctx<span class="token operator">:</span> PluginSetupContext<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> Promise<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>PluginSetupResult<span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token keyword">const</span> configPath <span class="token operator">=</span> path<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">join</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>ctx<span class="token punctuation">.</span>configDir<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">'wix-stores.yaml'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// Phase 1: Config check</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token operator">!</span>fs<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">existsSync</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>configPath<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token comment">// Create template with placeholders</span>\n' +
      '    fs<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">writeFileSync</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>\n' +
      '      configPath<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '      YAML<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">stringify</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `        apiKey<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'&lt;your-api-key&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `        siteUrl<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'&lt;your-site-url&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">return</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `      status<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'needs-config'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `      configCreated<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'config/wix-stores.yaml'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      `      message<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">'Config template created. Fill in credentials and re-run setup.'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n` +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token pu'... 20228 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Jay-Stack Setup Command","number":87}'
  }
}
[Build] 163/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=87-jay-stack-setup-command)
{
  post: {
    title: 'PR 158 Review Guide',
    content: '<h1>Branch Review Guide: <code>export_import</code></h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Overview</h2>\n' +
      '<p>This branch introduces two major features:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Figma Vendor Integration</strong> - A complete system for converting Figma documents to Jay HTML</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Enhanced Plugin Resolution</strong> - Improved plugin manifest and component resolution with better validation</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Total Changes:</strong> 75 files changed, ~9,893 insertions, ~1,168 deletions</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Recent Updates:</strong> This branch now includes the merge from main (PR #159) which added headless component props and repeater support. This merge introduced important interactions with the vendor system that are documented below.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>How to Review This Branch</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The changes are clustered into <strong>6 logical domains</strong>. We recommend reviewing in this order:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong><a href="#1-plugin-resolution--validation">Plugin Resolution &amp; Validation</a></strong> (Foundation)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><a href="#2-editor-protocol-extensions">Editor Protocol Extensions</a></strong> (API Contract)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><a href="#3-vendor-system-architecture">Vendor System Architecture</a></strong> (Core Infrastructure)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><a href="#4-figma-vendor-implementation">Figma Vendor Implementation</a></strong> (Feature Implementation)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><a href="#5-editor-handlers-integration">Editor Handlers Integration</a></strong> (Feature Integration)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><a href="#6-documentation--tests">Documentation &amp; Tests</a></strong> (Quality &amp; Maintenance)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>1. Plugin Resolution &amp; Validation</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Improve plugin manifest resolution and add better validation for NPM and local plugins.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Changes</h3>\n' +
      '<h4>Core Plugin Resolution</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/compiler/compiler-shared/lib/plugin-resolution.ts</code> (~574 lines total, +172 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>New <code>resolvePluginManifest()</code> - Resolves plugin.yaml from local or NPM paths</li>\n' +
      '<li>New <code>resolvePluginComponent()</code> - Resolves contract files from plugins with validation</li>\n' +
      '<li>Enhanced <code>getPluginsFromConfig()</code> - Better error handling and validation</li>\n' +
      '<li>Added validation responses with detailed error messages</li>\n' +
      '<li>Enhanced with support for headless component resolution</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Compiler Integration</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/compiler/compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-import-resolver.ts</code> (+9 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Export <code>LOCAL_PLUGIN_PATH</code> for consistent plugin path handling</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/compiler/compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-html-parser.ts</code> (+4 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Use exported <code>LOCAL_PLUGIN_PATH</code> constant</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Plugin Validation</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/jay-stack/plugin-validator/lib/validate-plugin.ts</code> (+32 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Added validation for <code>slugs</code> field in contract definitions</li>\n' +
      '<li>Validates slug format (must be valid identifiers)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Validates slugs is an array of strings</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Tests</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/compiler/compiler-shared/test/plugin-resolution.test.ts</code> (~603 lines total, +578 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Tests for <code>resolvePluginManifest()</code> with local and NPM plugins</li>\n' +
      '<li>Tests for <code>resolvePluginComponent()</code> with validation scenarios</li>\n' +
      '<li>Tests for various error cases and edge conditions</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Why These Changes?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The plugin system needed better resolution logic to:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Support both local (<code>src/plugins/</code>) and NPM plugins consistently</li>\n' +
      '<li>Provide detailed validation errors instead of silent failures</li>\n' +
      '<li>Support the vendor system&#39;s need to resolve plugin contracts (for Figma binding analysis)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Add support for dynamic route slugs in plugin contracts</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Key Points for Reviewer</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>✅ <strong>Backward Compatible:</strong> Existing plugins continue to work</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ <strong>Better Errors:</strong> Validation failures now return structured error messages</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ <strong>Test Coverage:</strong> Comprehensive test suite for resolution logic</li>\n' +
      '<li>⚠️ <strong>Breaking Change:</strong> None, but adds new optional <code>slugs</code> field to contract schema</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>2. Editor Protocol Extensions</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Extend the Editor Protocol to support vendor document export/import and improve type definitions.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Changes</h3>\n' +
      '<h4>Protocol Core</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/jay-stack/editor-protocol/lib/protocol.ts</code> (+168 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>ContractTag</code> and <code>Contract</code> types (simplified from compiler types)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>ExportMessage&lt;TVendorDoc&gt;</code> - Message type for exporting vendor documents</li>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>ImportMessage&lt;TVendorDoc&gt;</code> - Message type for importing vendor documents</li>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>ExportResponse</code> and <code>ImportResponse&lt;TVendorDoc&gt;</code> types</li>\n' +
      '<li>Changed <code>ProjectPage.contractSchema</code> → <code>ProjectPage.contract</code> (simplified)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Simplified <code>Plugin</code> interface (removed legacy <code>InstalledApp</code>)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Vendor Document Types</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/jay-stack/editor-protocol/lib/vendor-documents.ts</code> (new file, +12 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Single source of truth for vendor document types</li>\n' +
      '<li>Currently exports <code>FigmaVendorDocument</code> type</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/jay-stack/editor-protocol/lib/vendors/figma.ts</code> (new file, +147 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Complete <code>FigmaVendorDocument</code> type definition</li>\n' +
      '<li>Includes types for frames, text, images, components, variants, etc.</li>\n' +
      '<li>Includes <code>LayerBinding</code> type for contract bindings</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Protocol Constructors</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/jay-stack/editor-protocol/lib/constructors.ts</code> (+71 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>createExportMessage()</code> - Factory for export messages</li>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>createImportMessage()</code> - Factory for import messages</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Client/Server Updates</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/jay-stack/editor-client/lib/editor-client.ts</code> (+18 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>export()</code> method for vendor document export</li>\n' +
      '<li>Added <code>import()</code> method for vendor document import</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/jay-stack/editor-server/lib/editor-server.ts</code> (+38 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Added handlers for <code>export</code> and <code>import</code> messages</li>\n' +
      '<li>Integrated with vendor registry</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h4>Type Simplifications</h4>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>packages/jay-stack/editor-protocol/lib/types.ts</code> (+12 lines)<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Export new protocol types</li>\n' +
      '<li>Remove legacy types</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Why These Changes?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The Editor Protocol needed to support:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Vendor Documents:</strong> A standardized way for editor plugins (Figma, Sketch, etc.) to export their native formats</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Type Safety:</strong> Single source of truth for vendor document types that both plugins and vendors import</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Simplified Types:</strong> Protocol-specific types that are easier to serialize/deserialize than compiler types</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Better DX:</strong> Clear API for plugin developers to export/import designs</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Key Points for Reviewer</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>✅ <strong>Single Source of Truth:</strong> <code>vendor-documents.ts</code> is imported by both plugins and vendors</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ <strong>Type Safety:</strong> Generic <code>ExportMessage&lt;TVendorDoc&gt;</code> ensures type safety per vendor</li>\n' +
      '<li>✅ <strong>Backward Compatible:</strong> Old protocol messages still work</li>\n' +
      '<li>⚠️ <strong>Breaking Change:</strong> <code>ProjectPage.contractSchema</code> renamed to <code>contract</code> with simplified structure</li>\n' +
      '<li>⚠️ <strong>Headless Components Interaction:</strong> <code>usedComponents[].key</code> is typed as <code>string</code>, but the merged headless component feature allows instance-only headless components where <code>key</code> is <code>undefined</code> (see Known Limitations below)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>3. Vendor System Architecture</h2>\n' +
