[Build] 165/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=89-pr-158-merge-concerns)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Headless Instances In Interactive ForEach Without Slow Phase',
    content: '<h1>Headless Instances in Interactive forEach (No Slow Phase)</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Date:</strong> February 11, 2026<br><strong>Status:</strong> Draft<br><strong>Related:</strong> Design Log #84 (headless component props and repeater support), #50 (rendering phases)</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design Log #84 introduced nested headless component instances (<code>&lt;jay:xxx&gt;</code>) with support for <code>forEach</code> and <code>slowForEach</code> repeaters. During implementation, we added a <strong>compile-time restriction</strong>: headless instances cannot appear inside fast-phase (interactive) <code>forEach</code>.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The reason was that headless instances may need server-side <code>slowlyRender()</code> calls, but fast-phase forEach items are only known at request time — after the slow phase has already completed. Since the slow phase runs once (and is cached), we can&#39;t retroactively call <code>slowlyRender()</code> for dynamically-discovered items.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The restriction was implemented as a <strong>compiler error</strong> in <code>renderHeadlessInstance()</code> when <code>insideFastForEach</code> is true.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The restriction is <strong>overly broad</strong>. Not all headless components have a slow phase. A component built with:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">makeJayStackComponent<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>MyContract<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span>withProps<span class="token operator">&lt;</span>MyProps<span class="token operator">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withFastRender</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token function">async </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>props<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>services<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withInteractive</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>MyConstructor<span class="token punctuation">)</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>...has no <code>slowlyRender</code> at all. For such components, the &quot;can&#39;t render slow data for dynamic items&quot; concern doesn&#39;t apply.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Current State</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Compiler: &lt;jay:xxx&gt; inside forEach → always error</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Desired State</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Compiler: &lt;jay:xxx&gt; inside forEach → allowed (defer validation to server)\n' +
      'Server:   &lt;jay:xxx&gt; inside forEach → error ONLY if component has slowlyRender</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Key Insight</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The slow rendering phase already loads all headless component definitions (via <code>loadPageParts</code> → <code>vite.ssrLoadModule</code>). At that point, we have access to <code>compDefinition.slowlyRender</code> and can check if it&#39;s defined. This information is <strong>not available at compile time</strong> (the compiler only sees contracts and jay-html, not runtime component definitions), but <strong>is available at slow render time</strong>.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: Should the validation move from compile-time to server-time?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Yes. The compiler cannot know whether a component has a slow phase — that&#39;s determined by the builder API (<code>withSlowlyRender</code>), not by the contract. The server already loads components and checks <code>compDefinition.slowlyRender</code> (see <code>instance-slow-render.ts</code> line 69). We should:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Remove the compile-time <code>insideFastForEach</code> error</li>\n' +
      '<li>Add a server-time validation when discovering instances inside forEach</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: How do we discover instances inside a preserved forEach at slow-render time?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, <code>discoverHeadlessInstances</code> <strong>skips</strong> instances inside preserved <code>forEach</code> elements (the <code>insidePreservedForEach</code> flag). We need to still discover them, but handle them differently.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Discover them in a separate list. <code>discoverHeadlessInstances</code> should return two lists:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><code>instances</code> — instances with resolved props (existing, outside forEach)</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>forEachInstances</code> — instances inside preserved forEach (new, props may have bindings)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>For <code>forEachInstances</code>, we only need the <code>contractName</code> to look up the component definition and validate it has no slow phase. We don&#39;t need to call <code>slowlyRender</code> for them — they will be rendered entirely in the fast + interactive phases.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: How does the fast phase render these instances?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, the fast phase for instances (<code>renderFastChangingDataForInstances</code>) relies on slow-phase discovery data (<code>InstancePhaseData.discovered</code>). For instances inside forEach, there IS no slow-phase data.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> These instances need a <strong>different rendering path</strong>. Since forEach items are resolved during fast rendering:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>The page&#39;s <code>fastRender()</code> returns the forEach array (e.g., <code>allProducts.items</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>For each item, the props are known (e.g., <code>productId = item._id</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>We can call the nested component&#39;s <code>fastRender(props, {}, ...services)</code> with empty carryForward (no slow phase → no carryForward)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>This happens in the dev server after the page&#39;s fast render completes. The flow becomes:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Page fastRender() → returns forEach array data\n' +
      '  ↓\n' +
      'For each forEach item:\n' +
      '  → Resolve instance props from item data\n' +
      '  → Call component.fastRender(props, {}, ...services)  (empty carryForward)\n' +
      '  → Collect viewStates keyed by dynamic coordinate</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: How do dynamic coordinates work for forEach instances?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Static instances have fixed coordinates (e.g., <code>product-card:0</code>). ForEach instances need <strong>per-item coordinates</strong> since the number of items varies at request time.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Use the existing <code>Coordinate</code> system from the runtime/secure packages. <code>Coordinate = string[]</code> is already defined in <code>element-types.ts</code>. The secure package builds coordinates by accumulating <code>dataIds</code> — each <code>sandboxForEach</code> level pushes <code>item[matchBy]</code> onto the array, and the final segment is the ref/component name:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// secure/lib/sandbox/sandbox-refs.ts</span>\n' +
      'coordinate<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>refName<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>dataIds<span class="token punctuation">,</span> refName<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// secure/lib/sandbox/sandbox-element.ts — forEach extends dataIds:</span>\n' +
