  post: {
    title: 'Webmcp Plugin For Jay-Stack',
    content: '<h1>WebMCP Plugin for Jay-Stack</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>What exists today</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong><code>@jay-framework/runtime-automation</code></strong> (Design Log #76, #77) — wraps Jay components with <code>AutomationAPI</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>getPageState()</code> → <code>{ viewState, interactions, customEvents }</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>triggerEvent(eventType, coordinate)</code> → trigger UI events</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>onStateChange(callback)</code> → subscribe to changes</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>getInteraction(coordinate)</code> → find specific interaction</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Dev server automation integration</strong> — already wraps every page in dev mode:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>wrapWithAutomation(instance)</code> in generated client script</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>window.__jay.automation</code> for console access</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>AUTOMATION_CONTEXT</code> for plugin access via <code>useContext</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong><code>cart-webmcp</code> example</strong> — manually wires 6 hand-written WebMCP tools:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>get-cart-state</code>, <code>get-interactions</code>, <code>add-item</code>, <code>remove-item</code>, <code>update-quantity</code>, <code>clear-cart</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Uses <code>navigator.modelContext.registerTool()</code> to register each</li>\n' +
      '<li>Each tool calls <code>automation.getPageState()</code> or <code>automation.triggerEvent()</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>WebMCP browser API</strong> (<code>navigator.modelContext</code>) supports three primitives:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Tools</strong> — callable functions with JSON Schema input, returning content items</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Resources</strong> — readable data endpoints with URI schemes (static or template)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Prompts</strong> — reusable message templates for AI conversations</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Server actions (Design Log #63)</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Jay-stack exposes server-side RPC via <code>makeJayAction</code>/<code>makeJayQuery</code>:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Actions registered in <code>plugin.yaml</code> or <code>src/actions/*.actions.ts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Served at <code>/_jay/actions/:actionName</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Called from client via <code>createActionCaller(name, method)</code></li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h3>Contract system</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>.jay-contract</code> files declare page structure including interactive refs:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> addToCart\n' +
      '  type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> interactive\n' +
      '  elementType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLButtonElement\n' +
      `  description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token string">'Add the product to cart'</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>The <code>Interaction</code> type at runtime already includes <code>description</code> from contracts.</p>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>cart-webmcp</code> example requires <strong>manual, per-page wiring</strong> of WebMCP tools. Every tool is hand-written with specific knowledge of the component&#39;s data shape. This doesn&#39;t scale.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>What we want:</strong> Any jay-stack page, with zero or minimal configuration, automatically exposes its capabilities to WebMCP-enabled browsers. An AI agent visiting the page can:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Read</strong> the current page state (ViewState)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Discover</strong> all available interactions (buttons, inputs, selects)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Trigger</strong> interactions (click, fill, select)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Call</strong> server actions (if the page uses them)</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Subscribe</strong> to state changes (via resource updates)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: Should we generate generic tools or semantic tools from contracts?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Both, in two layers.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Generic layer</strong> (always available, no contract needed):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Works with any Jay page out of the box</li>\n' +
      '<li>Tools like <code>get-page-state</code>, <code>list-interactions</code>, <code>trigger-interaction</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>The AI agent reads state, discovers what&#39;s available, and acts</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Semantic layer</strong> (auto-generated from runtime <code>Interaction</code> data):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Analyze interactions at runtime → generate named tools</li>\n' +
      '<li>Button refs → <code>click-{refName}</code> tools</li>\n' +
      '<li>Input refs → <code>fill-{refName}</code> tools</li>\n' +
      '<li>forEach refs → tools that accept item identifiers</li>\n' +
      '<li>Use <code>interaction.description</code> from contracts when available</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>The generic layer is always the foundation. The semantic layer enriches it with domain-specific tool names and descriptions. Both can coexist.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: Can we generate semantic tools purely from client-side data?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Yes. The <code>AutomationAPI.getPageState().interactions</code> array already contains everything needed:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface Interaction <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  refName<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// &quot;removeBtn&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  coordinate<span class="token operator">:</span> Coordinate<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// [&quot;item-1&quot;, &quot;removeBtn&quot;]</span>\n' +
      '  element<span class="token operator">:</span> HTMLElement<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// actual DOM element</span>\n' +
      '  elementType<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// &quot;HTMLButtonElement&quot;</span>\n' +
      '  supportedEvents<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// [&quot;click&quot;]</span>\n' +
      '  itemContext<span class="token operator">?:</span> object<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// forEach item data</span>\n' +
      '  description<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// from contract</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>From this, we can derive:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Tool name from <code>refName</code> (e.g., <code>click-remove-btn</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Whether it&#39;s in a forEach (coordinate length &gt; 1 → needs item parameter)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Input type from <code>elementType</code> (button → click, input → fill)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Description from <code>description</code> field (contract-provided)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>No server-side contract metadata transfer needed</strong> for the core use case.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: What about exposing server actions as tools?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Deferred. Start without action-as-tools.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The generic <code>trigger-interaction</code> and semantic tools already cover all UI-driven interactions, which is how users invoke actions (clicking buttons wired to action handlers). Exposing server actions directly as WebMCP tools would require action metadata (inputSchema, description) that doesn&#39;t exist yet — can be added incrementally later.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: How does the plugin get access to AutomationAPI?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> No special hook needed. Use the existing <code>AUTOMATION_CONTEXT</code> with deferred access.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Current client script execution order:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Plugin client inits run (<code>await jayInit._clientInit(data)</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Page component is created</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>wrapWithAutomation(instance)</code> is called</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>registerGlobalContext(AUTOMATION_CONTEXT, wrapped.automation)</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>window.__jay.automation = wrapped.automation</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>The WebMCP plugin&#39;s client init runs at step 1, but automation isn&#39;t ready until step 3-5.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Solution:</strong> The plugin registers <code>AUTOMATION_CONTEXT</code> as a dependency (via plugin ordering or similar). In its client init, it sets up a deferred bridge — subscribing to the context and initializing WebMCP tools once the automation instance is populated:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Plugin client init</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">clientInit</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token comment">// Automation context isn't populated yet, but we can set up</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token comment">// to run when it becomes available (after component mount)</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token function">queueMicrotask</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token keyword">const</span> automation <span class="token operator">=</span> window<span class="token punctuation">.</span>__jay<span class="token operator">?</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>automation<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token function">if </span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>automation<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token function">setupWebMCP</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>automation<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punct'... 154071 more characters,
