{
  post: {
    title: 'Client Hydration',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #93 — Client Hydration</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay currently renders entirely on the client. The server sends an empty <code>&lt;div id=&quot;target&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code> with a <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> that imports <code>render</code> and <code>makeCompositeJayComponent</code>, creates the full DOM via <code>element()</code> calls, and appends to <code>target</code> (see <code>generate-client-script.ts</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<p>With SSR (Design Log #94), the server will generate full HTML. The client runtime needs to <strong>hydrate</strong> — connect to the existing server-rendered DOM instead of creating it from scratch.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Related Design Logs</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>#11 — SSR (original concept)</li>\n' +
      '<li>#34 — Jay Stack (3-phase rendering)</li>\n' +
      '<li>#50 — Rendering phases in contracts</li>\n' +
      '<li>#75 — Slow rendering jay-html to jay-html</li>\n' +
      '<li>#72 — Skip client script for non-interactive components</li>\n' +
      '<li>#94 — SSR streaming renderer (companion to this log)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>When the server renders full HTML, the client must:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Find and connect to existing DOM nodes for dynamic elements (refs, dynamic text, bindings)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Set up reactive updates (signals, conditionals, forEach)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Attach event handlers via refs</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>NOT</strong> recreate static HTML that already exists in the DOM</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, <code>element()</code> always creates new DOM nodes via <code>document.createElementNS</code>. There&#39;s no way to &quot;adopt&quot; existing DOM nodes.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Key Design Guideline</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Do not hydrate static HTML.</strong> The element bridge pattern (see <code>generated-element-bridge.ts</code> in refs fixture) demonstrates this principle:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">// Full element (generated-element.ts) — creates entire DOM tree:\n' +
      "e('div', {}, [\n" +
      "    e('div', {}, [dt((vs) =&gt; vs.text)], refRef1()),\n" +
      "    e('div', {}, [dt((vs) =&gt; vs.text)], refRef()),\n" +
      "    e('div', {}, [e('div', {}, [dt((vs) =&gt; vs.text)], refRef3())]),\n" +
      '])\n' +
      '\n' +
      '// Element bridge (generated-element-bridge.ts) — only refs, skips static structure:\n' +
      'elementBridge(viewState, refManager, () =&gt; [\n' +
      '    e(refRef1()),\n' +
      '    e(refRef()),\n' +
      '    e(refRef3()),\n' +
      '])</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The bridge doesn&#39;t create the wrapper <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> or the nested <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> around ref3. It only knows about dynamic attachment points (refs). Hydration should follow the same principle.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: How does the client find existing DOM nodes to hydrate?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The server can mark dynamic elements with data attributes (e.g., <code>data-jay-h=&quot;0&quot;</code>) to create an index. The client walks the DOM or uses <code>querySelectorAll</code> to locate these markers.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Use a coordinate-based attribute: <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;trackByKey/refName&quot;</code> or <code>jay-coordinate=&quot;trackByKey/index&quot;</code>. This reuses the existing coordinate system from <code>ConstructContext</code> (see Design Log #91 for coordinate usage in automation). Coordinates mark each nested level with a path based on forEach element trackBy keys. Elements with refs use the ref name as the final segment. Elements without refs that still need hydration (e.g., a <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> with dynamic text) use an auto-generated index within the current coordinate scope. The client uses <code>querySelectorAll(&#39;[jay-coordinate]&#39;)</code> to build a lookup map, then resolves each dynamic node by its coordinate path.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: What&#39;s the hydration compilation target?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Similar to how the compiler has <code>generated-element.ts</code> (full DOM) and <code>generated-element-bridge.ts</code> (sandbox), we need a <code>generated-element-hydrate.ts</code> (or a mode flag) that only connects to existing DOM.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Yes, a separate <code>generated-element-hydrate.ts</code> target. However, for Level 3 (interactive forEach and if=false), the hydration code should reuse the same element creation logic from <code>generated-element.ts</code> rather than duplicating it. The hydrate file imports from the element file for creation paths.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: Should hydration be a separate compiler target or a runtime mode?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A separate compiler target is cleaner — the hydration code is structurally different from creation code (no <code>document.createElement</code> calls). It&#39;s closer to the element bridge pattern.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Confirmed — separate compiler target.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: How do we handle the &quot;mismatch&quot; case where server HTML doesn&#39;t match client expectations?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>For now, we can log warnings in dev mode. In production, mismatches would indicate a bug.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Confirmed — dev-mode warnings only.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q5: Does the component lifecycle change?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><code>mount()</code> currently means &quot;start reactive updates.&quot; For hydration, it should also mean &quot;connect to DOM.&quot; The <code>makeJayComponent</code> flow doesn&#39;t change much — instead of calling <code>render(viewState)</code> which creates DOM, we call <code>hydrate(viewState, rootElement)</code> which adopts DOM.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Confirmed — <code>mount()</code> semantics stay the same. Hydration replaces the element construction, not the lifecycle.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Principle: Three Levels of Hydration Complexity</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n' +
      '│  Level 1: Static HTML with dynamic points                     │\n' +
      '│  → Skip static, walk to dynamic nodes via jay-coordinate      │\n' +
      '│  → Like element bridge: only refs/dynamic text matter         │\n' +
      '├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│  Level 2: Interactive if (condition=true at SSR)              │\n' +
      '│  → Children exist in DOM, adopt them (compact form, Level 1)  │\n' +
      '│  → No creation code needed — Jay retains element on toggle    │\n' +
      '├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n' +
      '│  Level 3: Interactive if=false / interactive forEach          │\n' +
      '│  → if=false: nothing in DOM, import creation from             │\n' +
      '│    generated-element.ts                                       │\n' +
      '│  → forEach: adopt existing items + import item creation       │\n' +
      '│    from generated-element.ts for new items                    │\n' +
      '└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Level 1: Static HTML with Dynamic Points</h3>\n' +
      '<p>For jay-html with static structure and dynamic bindings:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token tag">&lt;div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;h1</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{title}<span class="token tag">&lt;/h1</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="token attribute">ref</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;content&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>{text}<span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token tag">&lt;p</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>Static footer<span class="token tag">&lt;/p</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;/div</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The hydration code only needs to:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Find the <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> text node and connect <code>dynamicText</code> to it</li>\n' +
      '<li>Find the <code>&lt;div ref=&quot;content&quot;&gt;</code> and connect the ref + <code>dynamicText</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Ignore <code>&lt;p&gt;Static footer&lt;/p&gt;</code> entirely</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Compiled hydration (conceptual):</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-ts"><span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">hydrate</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>rootElement<span class="token operator">:</span> Element<span class="token punctuation">,</span> viewState<span class="token operator">:</span> ViewState<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> PreRender <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token keyword">const</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>refManager<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>refContent<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> ReferencesManager<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token keyword">for</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>options<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">'content'</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> render <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>viewState<span class="token operator">:</span> ViewState<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">=&gt;</span>\n' +
      '    ConstructContext<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">withHydrationRootContext</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>viewState<span class="token punctuation">'... 75792 more characters,
    description: '',
