{
  post: {
    title: 'Ssr Streaming Renderer',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #94 — SSR Streaming Renderer</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Jay currently does NOT render HTML on the server. The server produces ViewState data (slow + fast phases), then sends an empty <code>&lt;div id=&quot;target&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code> plus a <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> that imports the compiled element and creates the entire DOM on the client (see <code>generate-client-script.ts</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<p>This means:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Users see a blank page until JavaScript loads and executes</li>\n' +
      '<li>Search engines see an empty page (no SEO)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Time to First Contentful Paint is slow</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>We need the server to render the full HTML from compiled jay-html, streaming it directly to the response without materializing the full HTML string in memory.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Related Design Logs</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>#11 — SSR (original concept, mentions stream support)</li>\n' +
      '<li>#34 — Jay Stack (3-phase rendering pipeline)</li>\n' +
      '<li>#50 — Rendering phases in contracts</li>\n' +
      '<li>#75 — Slow rendering jay-html to jay-html</li>\n' +
      '<li>#93 — Client hydration (companion — how client connects to this HTML)</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No server HTML rendering</strong> exists. The compiler produces <code>generated-element.ts</code> which calls <code>document.createElement</code> — browser-only APIs.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>The fast phase only produces data</strong>, not HTML. <code>renderFastChangingData()</code> returns ViewState objects.</li>\n' +
      '<li>We need a new compilation target that renders jay-html to an HTML <strong>stream</strong> on the server, without DOM APIs.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: Should we compile jay-html into a streaming render function, or interpret jay-html at runtime on the server?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Compilation is preferred — it avoids parsing jay-html at request time and produces optimal code.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Confirmed — compile. The compiled output will also be used for production builds later, not just dev server.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: What format should the compiled server render function output?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>A stream of strings (or chunks). The function yields/writes HTML fragments sequentially, allowing the HTTP response to start immediately.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Confirmed — stream of string chunks via <code>write()</code> callback.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: How do slow-rendered (pre-rendered) jay-html templates work with SSR?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>After slow rendering (Design Log #75), we have pre-rendered jay-html with slow data baked in. The SSR compiler should compile this pre-rendered jay-html into the streaming render function, binding only fast + interactive data at request time.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Confirmed.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: Where does the SSR render function live — in the compiler output or in jay-stack server runtime?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In the compiler output. The compiler produces a <code>generated-server-element.ts</code> (or similar) that exports a render function. Jay-stack&#39;s server runtime calls it.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Confirmed — compiler output.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q5: How do headless components render on the server?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Headless components that have slow/fast phases already produce ViewState. The SSR render function needs the merged ViewState to render the HTML. The headless component resolution happens before SSR rendering.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Confirmed.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q6: How do we handle interactive <code>if</code> and <code>forEach</code> in SSR?</h3>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><code>if</code>: evaluate the condition with the current ViewState, render the matching branch. For the client, include hydration markers (see Design Log #93).</li>\n' +
      '<li><code>forEach</code>: iterate the array, render each item. Include markers for hydration.</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Confirmed. Uses <code>jay-coordinate</code> attributes on elements for hydration targeting, consistent with Design Log #93. No comment boundaries needed — the runtime&#39;s <code>Kindergarten</code> handles DOM positioning via offset counting.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q7: How do we handle ViewState with Promise / async data?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>See Design Log #45 for async types (<code>when-resolved</code>, <code>when-loading</code>, <code>when-rejected</code>).</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>A:</strong> Render the <code>when-pending</code> (loading) variant immediately into the stream. Do NOT close the final <code>&lt;/html&gt;</code> tag yet — keep the stream open. Once the promise resolves (or rejects), write inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> that replaces the pending content with the resolved/rejected variant. This is similar to React Suspense streaming.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Flow:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>When SSR hits an <code>async</code> property, render the <code>when-loading</code> variant inline</li>\n' +
      '<li>Mark it with a placeholder: <code>&lt;template jay-async=&quot;p1:pending&quot;&gt;...&lt;/template&gt;</code> wrapper (or similar)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Continue streaming other HTML</li>\n' +
      '<li>When the promise settles, append an inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> at the end of the stream that:<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Contains the resolved/rejected HTML as a string</li>\n' +
      '<li>Swaps the pending placeholder with the resolved/rejected content</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li>Only close <code>&lt;/html&gt;</code> after all promises settle (or after a timeout)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>This means <code>renderToStream</code> becomes <strong>async</strong> — it returns a Promise that resolves when all async ViewState properties have settled.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Architecture Overview</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">                          Build Time                    Request Time\n' +
      '                          ─────────                    ────────────\n' +
      '\n' +
      'jay-html ──→ slow render ──→ pre-rendered jay-html ──→ SSR compiler output\n' +
      '                                                            │\n' +
      '                                                    ┌───────┴────────┐\n' +
      '                                                    │                │\n' +
      '                                            generated-server   generated-element\n' +
      '                                            -element.ts        -hydrate.ts\n' +
      '                                            (server render)    (client hydrate)\n' +
      '                                                    │                │\n' +
      '                                                    ▼                ▼\n' +
      '                                             HTML stream ──→  Client hydration\n' +
      '                                             (to response)    (Design Log #93)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Compilation Target: <code>generated-server-element.ts</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>New compiler target that produces a function rendering HTML to a stream:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-ts"><span class="token comment">// generated-server-element.ts</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token keyword">import</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> escapeHtml<span class="token punctuation">,</span> type ServerRenderContext <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">from</span> <span class="token string">'@jay-framework/ssr-runtime'</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">export</span> <span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">renderToStream</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token operator">:</span> ViewState<span class="token punctuation">,</span> ctx<span class="token operator">:</span> ServerRenderContext<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token keyword">void</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token keyword">const</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> write<span class="token operator">:</span> w <span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> ctx<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      `  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'&lt;div&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'&lt;h1 jay-coordinate=&quot;0&quot;&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token function">escapeHtml</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>title<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'&lt;/h1&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'&lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;content&quot;&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token function">escapeHtml</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs<span class="token punctuation">.</span>text<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      `  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'&lt;/div&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      `  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'&lt;p&gt;Static footer&lt;/p&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n` +
      '  <span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><sp'... 85008 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Ssr Streaming Renderer","number":94}'
  }
}
