{
  post: {
    title: 'Jay-Action Contract References',
    content: '<h1>Design Log #95 — Contract References and Compact Notation in .jay-action Files</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design Log #92 introduced <code>.jay-action</code> files as metadata descriptors for server actions, using JSON Schema-style inline definitions for input/output types. Two problems emerged:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Contract duplication</strong>: Action outputs often reference types from <code>.jay-contract</code> files (e.g., <code>ProductCardViewState</code>), but the schema is duplicated inline — incomplete and fragile.</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Verbose format</strong>: The JSON Schema notation is verbose compared to the compact type notation already used in jay-html data scripts and contract files.</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The <code>.jay-action</code> format should:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Reference contract ViewState types instead of duplicating them</li>\n' +
      '<li>Use the same compact type notation as jay-html (<code>string</code>, <code>number</code>, <code>enum(...)</code>, arrays as YAML lists, <code>?</code> for optional)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Reuse existing infrastructure: <code>resolveType</code>, JayType system, enum parsing</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Revised <code>.jay-action</code> format</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Replace JSON Schema with the compact jay-type notation. Add <code>import:</code> block for contract references.</p>\n' +
      '<h4>Before (JSON Schema — current)</h4>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token keyword">name</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> searchProducts\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">description</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> Search products...\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">inputSchema</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> object\n' +
      '  required<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '    <span class="token punctuation">-</span> query\n' +
      '  properties<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '    query<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '      description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Search query text\n' +
      '    filters<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '      type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> object\n' +
      '      properties<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '        minPrice<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> number\n' +
      '        maxPrice<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> number\n' +
      '        collectionIds<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '          type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> array\n' +
      '          items<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '            type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string\n' +
      '    sortBy<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
