[Build] 171/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=95-jay-action-contract-references)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Consistent Build Folder Structure',
    content: '<h1>Design Log 96: Consistent Build Folder Structure</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The Jay framework generates build artifacts into a <code>build/</code> folder during development and compilation. There are two distinct contexts:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Jay Stack</strong> (full-stack) — dev server generates pre-rendered HTML, compiled templates, client entry points, and contract metadata</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Client-only</strong> (Vite/Rollup plugin) — compiler generates compiled <code>.jay-html.ts</code> files (and optionally secure sandbox variants)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<p>Both contexts write into <code>build/</code>, but the internal structure has grown organically and is inconsistent across examples and between the two contexts.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Additionally, contract metadata is duplicated between <code>build/materialized-contracts/</code> and <code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code>, produced by the same <code>materializeContracts()</code> function. The <code>agent-kit/</code> folder is the intended interface for agents and could also serve the editor integration, making the build copy redundant.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Current Jay Stack build layout</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">build/\n' +
      '├── client-scripts/                     # HTML entry points per route (debug only)\n' +
      '├── slow-render-cache/                  # Pre-rendered .jay-html files\n' +
      '├── jay-runtime/\n' +
      '│   ├── build/slow-render-cache/        # Same templates compiled to .jay-html.ts\n' +
      '│   └── src/pages/                      # Source mirror (inconsistently present)\n' +
      '└── materialized-contracts/             # Contract/plugin YAML indexes</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Current client-only build layout (varies per example)</h3>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">build/\n' +
      '└── jay-runtime/\n' +
      '    ├── lib/                            # Compiled .jay-html.ts (when source is lib/)\n' +
      '    ├── src/                            # Compiled .jay-html.ts (when source is src/)\n' +
      '    └── lib-secure/                     # Sandbox variants (when secure mode)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Specific inconsistencies</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong><code>build/jay-runtime/build/slow-render-cache/</code></strong> — &quot;build inside build&quot; is confusing. The path <code>build/jay-runtime/build/</code> reads as two nested build folders.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong><code>slow-render-cache/</code> exists in two places</strong> — raw <code>.jay-html</code> files in <code>build/slow-render-cache/</code> and compiled <code>.jay-html.ts</code> wrappers in <code>build/jay-runtime/build/slow-render-cache/</code>. Same logical content, duplicated with different formats.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong><code>jay-runtime/src/pages/</code> appears inconsistently</strong> — present in <code>store-light</code> and <code>studio-store</code> examples but absent from <code>store</code>, <code>whisky-exchange</code>, <code>fake-shop</code>, and others. Its purpose vs. the <code>build/slow-render-cache/</code> TS version is unclear.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Client-only source directory leaks into build</strong> — the build folder mirrors whether source is in <code>lib/</code> or <code>src/</code>, making the output structure unpredictable. One example (<code>todo-rollup-build</code>) puts files at <code>build/lib/</code> without the <code>jay-runtime/</code> prefix at all.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong><code>client-scripts/</code> naming inconsistencies</strong> — fake-shop produces trailing dashes (<code>cart-.html</code>, <code>checkout-.html</code>) while other examples don&#39;t (<code>cart.html</code>).</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '<li><p><strong>Folder names describe mechanisms, not content</strong> — <code>slow-render-cache</code> describes a caching strategy, <code>jay-runtime</code> is an overloaded term (also a package name), <code>client-scripts</code> is vague.</p>\n' +
      '</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Where the paths are hardcoded</h3>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Artifact</th>\n' +
      '<th>Source file</th>\n' +
      '<th>Line</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>build/</code> default</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>dev-server/lib/dev-server.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>73</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>client-scripts/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>dev-server/lib/dev-server.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>816</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>slow-render-cache/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>dev-server/lib/dev-server.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>1178</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>materialized-contracts/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>stack-server-runtime/lib/contract-materializer.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>327</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>build/materialized-contracts</code> (resolver fallback)</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-import-resolver.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>91</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>build/jay-runtime</code> (outputDir)</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>stack-cli/lib/server.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>37</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>jay-runtime/</code> (Vite plugin)</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>compiler/rollup-plugin/lib/common/files.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>44</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Vite plugin config</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>compiler/rollup-plugin/lib/runtime/jay-plugin-context.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>26</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Proposed structure</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The build folder mirrors the source layout directly. Compiled <code>.ts</code> files sit alongside their source <code>.jay-html</code> files. No extra <code>compiled/</code> wrapper.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">build/\n' +
      '├── &lt;mirrors source layout&gt;       # Compiled .jay-html.ts (e.g., lib/, src/, lib-secure/)\n' +
      '│\n' +
      '├── pre-rendered/                  # Slow-phase HTML + compiled TS wrappers (Jay Stack only)\n' +
      '│   └── &lt;mirrors route layout&gt;    # e.g., page.jay-html + page.jay-html.ts side by side\n' +
      '│\n' +
      '└── debug/                         # Debug-only artifacts (dev server only)\n' +
      '    └── client-entry/              # Generated HTML entry points per route\n' +
      '        ├── index.html\n' +
      '        └── cart.html</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Contracts are <strong>not</strong> in the build folder. See &quot;Unifying contracts into agent-kit&quot; below.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>What changes and why</h3>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Current</th>\n' +
      '<th>Proposed</th>\n' +
      '<th>Rationale</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>jay-runtime/&lt;lib|src&gt;/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&lt;lib|src&gt;/</code> (no wrapper)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Drop the <code>jay-runtime/</code> prefix; source layout mirrors directly into <code>build/</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>jay-runtime/lib-secure/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>lib-secure/</code> (no wrapper)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Same — no collision since <code>lib/</code> and <code>lib-secure/</code> are distinct source directories</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>jay-runtime/build/slow-render-cache/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>pre-rendered/*.jay-html.ts</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Compiled TS sits alongside pre-rendered HTML; no nested build directories</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>slow-render-cache/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>pre-rendered/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Describes content (pre-rendered HTML), not mechanism (cache)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>build/materialized-contracts/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>Removed from build</td>\n' +
      '<td>Unified into <code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code> (see below)</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>client-scripts/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>debug/client-entry/</code></td>\n' +
      '<td>These exist only for debugging; make that explicit</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td><code>jay-runtime/src/pages/</code> (source mirror)</td>\n' +
      '<td>Removed</td>\n' +
      '<td>Redundant</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h3>Unifying contracts into agent-kit</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Currently, materialized contracts are duplicated:</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>build/materialized-contracts/</code></strong> — written by dev server on startup, read by <code>JAY_IMPORT_RESOLVER</code> for dynamic contract resolution</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code></strong> — written by <code>jay-stack agent-kit</code> command, read by AI agents</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>Both are produced by the same <code>materializeContracts()</code> function and contain identical data. The only runtime consumer of <code>build/materialized-contracts/</code> is <code>JAY_IMPORT_RESOLVER.loadPluginContract()</code> in <code>compiler-jay-html/lib/jay-target/jay-import-resolver.ts:91</code>, which falls back to it when resolving dynamic contracts. The editor integration uses the same resolver indirectly.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Remove <code>build/materialized-contracts/</code> entirely. Both the dev server and the import resolver should use <code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code> as the single location for materialized contracts.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Changes:</strong></p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Dev server startup writes contracts to <code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code> instead of <code>build/materialized-contracts/</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><code>JAY_IMPORT_RESOLVER</code> fallback path changes from <code>build/materialized-contracts</code> to <code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>The <code>jay-stack agent-kit</code> command continues to work as before (it already writes to <code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code>)</li>\n' +
      '<li>The editor integration requires no changes — it uses the resolver, which now points to agent-kit</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<p>This means <code>agent-kit/materialized-contracts/</code> is always kept fresh by the dev server, and agents always see up-to-date contracts without needing to run <code>jay-stack agent-kit</code> separately during development.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Design principles</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Names describe content, not mechanism</strong> — <code>pre-rendered</code> not <code>slow-render-cache</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No nested build directories</strong> — <code>build/pre-rendered/...</code> instead of <code>build/jay-runtime/build/slow-render-cache/...</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>No unnecessary wrapper directories</strong> — compiled output mirrors source layout directly under <code>build/</code></li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Same top-level structure for both contexts</strong> — Jay Stack projects just have more folders than client-only ones</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Debug artifacts are clearly separated</strong> '... 9660 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Consistent Build Folder Structure","number":96}'
  }
}
