{
  post: {
    title: 'Contract-Based Tool Descriptions For Gemini Agent',
    content: '<h1>Contract-Based Tool Descriptions for Gemini Agent</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The gemini-agent plugin auto-generates page automation tools from <code>AutomationAPI</code> interactions. Each tool gets a name from the ref name (<code>toggle-is-selected</code>, <code>click-add-to-cart-button</code>) and a description generated from the ref name:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Toggle is selected for a specific item\n' +
      'Click add to cart button</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>These descriptions are poor signals for the LLM. When asked to &quot;select the Claxton&#39;s category&quot;, the LLM doesn&#39;t know that <code>toggle-is-selected</code> controls category and price range filters — the description just says &quot;Toggle is selected for a specific item&quot;.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Meanwhile, <code>.jay-contract</code> files support a <code>description</code> field on tags:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> isSelected\n' +
      '  type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> interactive\n' +
      '  description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Select or deselect a filter (price range or product category)</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This information is parsed by the contract parser but never reaches the runtime interaction groups.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The LLM needs semantic tool descriptions to make good decisions about which tools to use. Current auto-generated descriptions from ref names are meaningless.</p>\n' +
      '<p>Embedding descriptions in the compiled HTML/JS output would increase bundle size for every page, even when no AI agent is present. The cost should only be paid on the AI path.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Questions and Answers</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Q1: Where do the descriptions live at build time?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The contract parser extracts <code>description</code> fields from <code>.jay-contract</code> tags into <code>ContractTag.description</code>. The agent-kit materializer writes <code>plugins-index.yaml</code> with contract paths but no tag-level detail — tag information is in the individual <code>.jay-contract</code> files referenced by path.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q2: How should descriptions reach the gemini agent at runtime?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Via a server action. The server has access to the materialized contract files. A new action <code>getToolDescriptions</code> returns a map of <code>refName → description</code> by reading the contract YAML at runtime. The client merges these descriptions into the serialized tools before sending to the server.</p>\n' +
      '<p>This keeps the HTML/JS bundle unchanged — the descriptions are fetched only when the gemini-agent component initializes.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q3: Should this be a one-time fetch or per-turn?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Answer:</strong> One-time. Contract descriptions don&#39;t change at runtime. The client fetches them once during the interactive phase init and caches them. The tool definitions sent each turn include the enriched descriptions.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q4: What about nested contracts (sub-contracts)?</h3>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Use the leaf tag description only — no concatenation.</strong> Validated against real wix-stores contracts: leaf descriptions are self-contained (&quot;Category checkbox&quot;, &quot;Radio button for this range&quot;), and concatenating parents produces redundant or worse results (&quot;Category checkbox in categories&quot;, &quot;Button to select this choice in choices in options&quot;). The parent context is already implicit in the coordinate structure the LLM sees (<code>coordinate: &quot;color/red&quot;</code>). If a leaf description is insufficient, the author should write a better one.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q5: What if a contract tag has no description?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Fall back to the current auto-generated description from the ref name. Descriptions are opt-in — existing contracts work unchanged.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Q6: Should <code>plugins-index.yaml</code> include tag descriptions?</h3>\n' +
      '<p>No. Keep <code>plugins-index.yaml</code> as a lightweight discovery index. The action reads the full <code>.jay-contract</code> files directly. This avoids bloating the index and keeps the single-source-of-truth in the contract files.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>New action: <code>getToolDescriptions</code></h3>\n' +
      '<p>A server action registered by the gemini-agent plugin that reads contract files and returns tool descriptions.</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript">interface ToolDescription <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  refName<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '  description<span class="token operator">:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// Returns descriptions for all interactive tags across all contracts</span>\n' +
      'type GetToolDescriptionsOutput <span class="token operator">=</span> ToolDescription<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>The action:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Reads <code>plugins-index.yaml</code> to find all contract paths</li>\n' +
      '<li>Parses each <code>.jay-contract</code> YAML</li>\n' +
      '<li>Walks the tag tree, collecting <code>description</code> fields for interactive tags (leaf description only, no parent concatenation)</li>\n' +
      '<li>Returns the list</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Client-side integration</h3>\n' +
      '<p>In <code>gemini-chat.ts</code>, the interactive phase:</p>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Calls <code>getToolDescriptions</code> once at init</li>\n' +
      '<li>Stores the result as a <code>Map&lt;string, string&gt;</code> (refName → description)</li>\n' +
      '<li>In <code>buildSerializedTools</code>, uses the map to override auto-generated descriptions</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">const</span> description <span class="token operator">=</span>\n' +
      '  toolDescriptionMap<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">get</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>group<span class="token punctuation">.</span>refName<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">||</span>\n' +
      '  group<span class="token punctuation">.</span>description <span class="token operator">||</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token string">`${prefix} ${humanName}${isForEach ? \' for a specific item\' : \'\'}`</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<h3>Contract authoring</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Page authors add descriptions to interactive tags in their contracts:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="token comment"># product-page.jay-contract</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">tags</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> filters\n' +
      '    type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> sub<span class="token punctuation">-</span>contract\n' +
      '    repeated<span class="token punctuation">:</span> true\n' +
      '    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Product filters\n' +
      '    tags<span class="token punctuation">:</span>\n' +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> isSelected\n' +
      '        type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> interactive\n' +
      '        elementType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> HTMLInputElement\n' +
      '        description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> Select or deselect this filter\n' +
      '      <span class="token punctuation">-</span> tag<span class="token punctuation">:</span> filterLabel\n' +
      '        type<span class="token punctuation">:</span> data\n' +
      '        dataType<span class="token punctuation">:</span> string</code></pre>\n' +
      '<h2>Implementation Plan</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 1: Server action</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Create <code>getToolDescriptions</code> action in gemini-agent plugin</li>\n' +
      '<li>Read <code>plugins-index.yaml</code> for contract paths</li>\n' +
      '<li>Parse contracts and extract interactive tag descriptions</li>\n' +
      '<li>Handle nested sub-contracts with description concatenation</li>\n' +
      '<li>Register as a server action (not exposed to the LLM — internal use only)</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 2: Client integration</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Call <code>getToolDescriptions</code> once during interactive phase init</li>\n' +
      '<li>Cache result as a map</li>\n' +
      '<li>Use in <code>buildSerializedTools</code> to enrich tool descriptions</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h3>Phase 3: Add descriptions to example contracts</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li>Add <code>description</code> fields to fake-shop contract tags</li>\n' +
      '<li>Verify enriched descriptions appear in gemini agent tools</li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Trade-offs</h2>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Approach</th>\n' +
      '<th>Pro</th>\n' +
      '<th>Con</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td><strong>Server action (chosen)</strong></td>\n' +
      '<td>Zero bundle cost, descriptions from source of truth</td>\n' +
      '<td>Extra HTTP call at init</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Embed in HTML/JS</td>\n' +
      '<td>No init call needed</td>\n' +
      '<td>Increases bundle for all pages, even without AI agent</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>Materializer writes descriptions</td>\n' +
      '<td>Available without parsing contracts</td>\n' +
      '<td>Bloats plugins-index.yaml, duplicates source of truth</td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Contract-Based Tool Descriptions For Gemini Agent","number":97}'
  }
}
