{
  post: {
    title: 'Route-Based Server-Element Output',
    content: '<h1>Design Log 98 — Route-Based Server-Element Output</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Design Log 96 established a consistent build folder with <code>pre-rendered/</code> mirroring route structure. The SSR hydration branch (DL93 + DL94) later added server-element file generation, but placed them in a flat <code>build/server-elements/</code> directory. This causes name collisions for multi-page sites and is inconsistent with DL96.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>If two routes share a jay-html filename (e.g., <code>pages/about/index.jay-html</code> and <code>pages/shop/index.jay-html</code>), their compiled server-element files collide in the flat <code>build/server-elements/</code> directory.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Server-element files should be written to <code>build/pre-rendered/{routeDir}/</code> instead of <code>build/server-elements/</code>, where <code>routeDir</code> is the route&#39;s directory relative to <code>pagesRootFolder</code>. This mirrors the pre-rendered file structure from DL96.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Changes</h3>\n' +
      '<ol>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>generateSSRPageHtml</code></strong> and <strong><code>compileAndLoadServerElement</code></strong> receive a new <code>routeDir: string</code> parameter</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong><code>sendResponse</code></strong> (dev-server) receives the original <code>sourceJayHtmlPath</code> (always <code>route.jayHtmlPath</code>) and computes <code>routeDir</code> from it relative to <code>pagesRootFolder</code></li>\n' +
      '<li>Output directory changes from <code>path.join(buildFolder, &#39;server-elements&#39;)</code> to <code>path.join(buildFolder, &#39;pre-rendered&#39;, routeDir)</code></li>\n' +
      '</ol>\n' +
      '<h2>Verification</h2>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li>Build passes</li>\n' +
      '<li>Existing dev-server tests pass</li>\n' +
      '<li>Full test suite passes</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<hr>\n' +
      '<h2>Log Methodology Note</h2>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Note:</strong> These design logs are written primarily for AI agents as part of the <a href="/design-log">Design Log methodology</a> and made accessible here for human readers. The language and structure are optimized for machine consumption — expect precise, specification-style prose rather than narrative documentation.</p>\n',
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Route-Based Server-Element Output","number":98}'
  }
}
[Build] 174/1235 /design-log/jay/[slug] (slug=98-route-based-server-element-output)
{
  post: {
    title: 'Hydration Coordinate Alignment Bugs',
    content: '<h1>Design Log 99 — Hydration Coordinate Alignment Bugs</h1>\n' +
      '<blockquote>\n' +
      '<p><em>Written for AI agents. See <a href="#log-methodology-note">Log Methodology Note</a> below for details.</em></p>\n' +
      '</blockquote>\n' +
      '<h2>Background</h2>\n' +
      '<p>DL93 (client hydration) and DL94 (SSR streaming renderer) established a coordinate system using <code>jay-coordinate</code> attributes to link server-rendered DOM with the client hydration code. The runtime tests (e.g., <code>hydrate-for-each.test.ts</code>) define the correct coordinate format. However, the two compiler targets (<code>generated-server-element.ts</code> and <code>generated-element-hydrate.ts</code>) produce <strong>incompatible coordinates</strong>, causing hydration to silently fail for any page with forEach or conditional+ref elements.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The compiler tests only compare generated code text against fixtures — they never verify that the two outputs work together at runtime.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Problem</h2>\n' +
      '<p>The whisky-store products page logs:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">[jay hydration] hydrateForEach: could not find container element</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>Interactive elements (search, filters, add-to-cart) do not work.</p>\n' +
      '<h2>Root Cause Analysis</h2>\n' +
      '<p>Three coordinate bugs in the compilers:</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Bug A: forEach child coordinates lack path prefix</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The runtime expects forEach child coordinates to be prefixed with the item&#39;s trackBy value:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-html"><span class="token comment">&lt;!-- Runtime test (hydrate-for-each.test.ts, line 35): --&gt;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token tag">&lt;li</span> <span class="token attribute">jay-coordinate</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;span</span> <span class="token attribute">jay-coordinate</span><span class="token punctuation">=</span><span class="token string">&quot;a/0&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span>Alice<span class="token tag">&lt;/span</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span><span class="token tag">&lt;/li</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>But the server element compiler emits unprefixed coordinates:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// collections/generated-server-element.ts (current, WRONG):</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">' jay-coordinate=&quot;'</span> <span class="token operator">+</span> <span class="token function">escapeAttr</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token function">String</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>vs1<span class="token punctuation">.</span>id<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">+</span> <span class="token string">'&quot;&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// item root: OK</span>\n` +
      `<span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">' jay-coordinate=&quot;0&quot;&gt;'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// child: WRONG, should be &quot;{id}/0&quot;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<p>The hydrate runtime&#39;s <code>forItem(item, id)</code> sets <code>coordinateBase = [id]</code>, so <code>resolveCoordinate(&quot;0&quot;)</code> looks for <code>&quot;{id}/0&quot;</code> in the coordinate map. Since the server rendered plain <code>&quot;0&quot;</code>, it finds nothing.</p>\n' +
      '<p><strong>Impact</strong>: ALL dynamic content inside forEach items fails to adopt — refs, dynamic text, conditionals are silently broken.</p>\n' +
      '<h3>Bug B: Conditional + ref counter divergence</h3>\n' +
      '<p>When a conditional element has a ref (e.g., <code>&lt;button ref=&quot;addToCartButton&quot; if=&quot;...&quot;&gt;</code>):</p>\n' +
      '<ul>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Hydrate compiler</strong> (<code>renderHydrateElement</code>): ALWAYS increments counter, uses counter value as coordinate</li>\n' +
      '<li><strong>Server compiler</strong> (<code>renderServerElementContent</code>): uses ref name as coordinate, does NOT increment counter</li>\n' +
      '</ul>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">coordinate = refName || String(context.coordinateCounter.count++)\n' +
      '                ↑ server takes this branch     ↑ hydrate takes this branch</code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>This shifts all subsequent coordinates. In the whisky store&#39;s searchResults item:</p>\n' +
      '<table>\n' +
      '<thead>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<th>Element</th>\n' +
      '<th>Server coord</th>\n' +
      '<th>Hydrate coord</th>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</thead>\n' +
      '<tbody><tr>\n' +
      '<td>addToCartButton (ref+if)</td>\n' +
      '<td>ref name</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&quot;10&quot;</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>quick-options-area (if)</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&quot;10&quot;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&quot;11&quot;</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>quick-options-buttons</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&quot;12&quot;</code></td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&quot;13&quot;</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '<tr>\n' +
      '<td>inner forEach container</td>\n' +
      '<td>—</td>\n' +
      '<td><code>&quot;14&quot;</code></td>\n' +
      '</tr>\n' +
      '</tbody></table>\n' +
      '<h3>Bug C: forEach containerCoordinate has no matching element</h3>\n' +
      '<p>The hydrate compiler generates <code>containerCoordinate = counter++</code> for each forEach:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// renderHydrateElement for forEach:</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token keyword">const</span> containerCoordinate <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token function">String</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>context<span class="token punctuation">.</span>coordinateCounter<span class="token punctuation">.</span>count<span class="token operator">++</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>  <span class="token comment">// e.g., &quot;3&quot;</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// ...</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">hydrateForEach</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">&quot;3&quot;</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>But the server element compiler does NOT emit this coordinate. The container IS the parent element (which has its own coordinate). So <code>hydrateForEach</code> resolves a coordinate that doesn&#39;t exist.</p>\n' +
      '<p>The collections fixture demonstrates this:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="">Server:  &lt;div jay-coordinate=&quot;2&quot;&gt;  ← only &quot;2&quot;, no &quot;3&quot;\n' +
      "Hydrate: adoptElement('2', {}, [hydrateForEach('3', ...)])  ← looks for &quot;3&quot;</code></pre>\n" +
      '<p>Compare with the working runtime test:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// No wrapping adoptElement — hydrateForEach uses the container coordinate directly:</span>\n' +
      `<span class="token function">hydrateForEach</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'0'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>  <span class="token comment">// &quot;0&quot; matches &lt;ul jay-coordinate=&quot;0&quot;&gt;</span></code></pre>\n` +
      '<h2>Design</h2>\n' +
      '<h3>Fix A: Prefix forEach child coordinates in server element</h3>\n' +
      '<p>Add <code>coordinatePrefix</code> to <code>ServerContext</code>. When rendering coordinates inside a forEach item, prefix with the trackBy expression:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// ServerContext:</span>\n' +
      'interface ServerContext <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token comment">// ... existing fields</span>\n' +
      '  coordinatePrefix<span class="token operator">?:</span> string<span class="token punctuation">;</span> <span class="token comment">// runtime expression, e.g., `vs1.id`</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>In <code>renderServerElement</code> for forEach, set the prefix on the item context:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token keyword">const</span> itemContext<span class="token operator">:</span> ServerContext <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>\n' +
      '  <span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span>context<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  variables<span class="token operator">:</span> forEachVariables<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  indent<span class="token operator">:</span> itemIndent<span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  coordinateCounter<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> count<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">0</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>\n' +
      '  coordinatePrefix<span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">`${forEachVariables.currentVar}.${trackBy}`</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token comment">// NEW</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></code></pre>\n' +
      '<p>In <code>renderServerElementContent</code>, when emitting a coordinate with a prefix:</p>\n' +
      '<pre class="md-code"><code class="language-typescript"><span class="token comment">// Before (plain):</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">w</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">\' jay-coordinate=&quot;${coordinate}&quot;&gt;\'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span>\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<span class="token comment">// After (prefixed):</span>\n' +
      '<span class="token function">w</span><span'... 31464 more characters,
    description: '',
    date: '',
    tags: [],
    frontmatter: '{"title":"Hydration Coordinate Alignment Bugs","number":99}'
  }
}
